<div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>1914 Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>1914 Box</b> is a Loot Box given to <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> and <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for killing Empress <a href="bword://D&#x27;nadia">D'nadia</a> and receiving the <a href="bword://Gavrilo Princip Achievement">Gavrilo Princip Achievement</a>. The both receive a Legendary version of the box. The name is a reference to the Assassination of Archduke Franz <a href="bword://Ferdinand">Ferdinand</a>, which took place on 28 June 1914, and was done by Gavrilo Princip, who the achievement granting this box is named after.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Gavrilo Princip Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: 1914 Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/1914_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>1965 Harley Davidson Motorcycle</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>When <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> was a kid, Carl's <a href="bword://Father">Father</a>'s most prized possession was a red and beige <b>1965 Harley Davidson FLH Panhead Electra Glide</b> motorcycle. The small dent on the gas tank was from when Carl knocked it over as a kid.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Earth</li></ul><p class="source">Source: 1965 Harley Davidson Motorcycle on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/1965_Harley_Davidson_Motorcycle</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>201st Security Group Militia</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The 201st Security Group</b> is a cult of City Elves on the Third Floor. They worship the goddess <a href="bword://Apito">Apito</a>, and the city elves are a "batshit crazy, doomsday cult of banished elves" who traveled from the Sixth Floor Hunting Grounds to the Over City, joined the uniformed <b>201st Security Group Militia</b>, and swore to protect the <a href="bword://Skyfowl">Skyfowl</a> from flightless creatures and the Oak Fell.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: 201st Security Group Militia on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/201st_Security_Group_Militia</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Accounts Tab</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Accounts Tab</b> is a tab in a Crawler's Heads-Up Display (HUD). The tab is specifically related to new items created in-dungeon by a crawler. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> gains access to this tab when he creates his <a href="bword://Carl&#x27;s Jug O&#x27;Boom">Carl's Jug O'Boom</a>, which is a brand new, never before seen creation in any dungeon.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Accounts Tab on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Accounts_Tab</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Achievements</b> are a type of crawler notification generated and distributed by the <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a> to reward, mock, or warn crawlers for performing specific actions within the Dungeon. Most achievements reward crawlers for playing the game with <a href="bword://Loot Boxes">Loot Boxes</a>, but some serve to warn crawlers of impending danger, notify crawlers that they're on the wrong track, or even nudge crawlers to remember particular tactics or information.</li><li><b>Source:</b> System AI</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Adad</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>In Dungeon lore, <b>Adad</b> is a mountainous storm god capable of summoning clouds of lightning-shooting bugs. During <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a>'s crawl, he used a Summoning Box to summon <a href="bword://Dodola">Dodola</a> and Adad on the Tenth Floor. Adad was AI controlled.</li><li><b>Race:</b> God</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Prologue</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Adad on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Adad</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Adept's Fountain Pen</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Adept's Fountain Pen</b> is an item that allows a user to do calligraphy. The description of "<i>Or will you literally stab someone in the neck with it again?</i>" is in reference to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> stabbing a <a href="bword://Naga">Naga</a> journalist named Nihit in the neck with a sharpie at CrawlCon.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Adept's Fountain Pen on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Adept%27s_Fountain_Pen</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Adventurer Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Adventurer Boxes</b> are common <a href="bword://Loot Boxes">Loot Boxes</a> containing standard adventuring gear. Bronze and Silver Adventurer Boxes are liberally distributed on the first two floors, and typically contain potions and bandages.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Achievements</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Adventurer Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Adventurer_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Agatha</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Agatha</b> is a Crawler who appears to be a homeless human woman pushing a loaded-down shopping cart through the Dungeon. Agatha keeps her own company. She refuses the Tutorial, declines to join the newly formed <a href="bword://Meadow Lark">Meadow Lark</a> party, and, never having passed through a guild, has no <a href="bword://Inventory">Inventory</a>, which is why she pushes her belongings ahead of her rather than storing them. She cackles at moments other crawlers find terrifying, mutters to herself, refers to herself in the third person, and huffs the metallic silver spray paint she uses to tag dungeon walls with happy faces.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Agent 22</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Wenatchee, WA</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 22</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Agatha on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Agatha</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ajib</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Ajib</b> is an Earth crawler and presumably a dexterity-themed fighter. He lost the bottom half of his left leg jumping through the <a href="bword://Gate of the Feral Gods">Gate of the Feral Gods</a> on the Fifth Floor.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 5, Chapter 1</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ajib on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ajib</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Akland</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Akland</b> was an accountant and a hunter on the Sixth Floor Hunting Grounds. As an accountant for the <a href="bword://Dream">Dream</a>, Akland worked with soy crop shipping manifests. When the Dream rented out the <a href="bword://Fantasy Hunter Camp">Fantasy Hunter Camp</a> as a sort of employee retreat, he performed well and won a spot in the Dream's Faction Wars army. The Dream offered him money to participate, and more money to travel down to the Sixth Floor Hunting Grounds and hunt <a href="bword://Louis">Louis</a>. Akland claimed to have a family.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Moon Elf</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 5, Chapter 22</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Akland on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Akland</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Akuma</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Akuma</b> is a <a href="bword://War Mage">War Mage</a> and the leader of the War Mage Rebellion. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> describes Akuma as a "a long-haired elf, old and wizened with an angry sneer on his sagging face.”</li><li><b>Race:</b> War Mage</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Akuma on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Akuma</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Alchemy Table</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Alchemy Table</b> is a crafting workbench that allows crawlers to transform various Dungeon loot such as organs and skins into potions. Although the table includes tools and resources, it does not necessarily include recipes.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Alchemy Table on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Alchemy_Table</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Alexandro</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Alexandro</b> is a <a href="bword://Residual">Residual</a> seeking to free the Eulogist and wipe out biological life in the galaxy. Agent 21 peeled away from the collective and traveled to Earth with <a href="bword://Agatha">Agatha</a> ten years ago. Like Agatha, they killed an <a href="bword://Apothecary">Apothecary</a> residual already on earth and assumed control of its body to secure access to the Apothecary's information feeds and equipment. For years now, they have gone by their human name "Parvati."</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Agent 21, Parvati</li><li><b>Race:</b> Residual (assumed)</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Epilogue</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Alexandro on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Alexandro</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Algos</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>In the Dungeon, <b>Algos</b> is the god of pain. <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> notes that Algos is "a good god to choose if you want your target to suffer." The <a href="bword://Skull Empire">Skull Empire</a> sent <a href="bword://Maggie My">Maggie My</a> a <a href="bword://Benefactor Box">Benefactor Box</a> containing a scroll that allows her to choose a god to worship, and <a href="bword://Chris Andrews">Chris Andrews</a> a benefactor box containing a picture of Algos. After choosing to worship Algos and arriving on the Fifth Floor, Maggie My was approached by a mysterious person in a safe room and given a <a href="bword://Celestial Grenade">Celestial Grenade</a>. She was supposed to detonate the grenade near <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> to summon Algos.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> God</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Algos on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Algos</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>All Eyes on Me Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>"All Eyes on Me"</b> is a minor charm bard spell which causes those hearing it to focus attention on a subject of the caster's choice. As a charm bard spell, the caster only needs to sing the song in tune to affect everyone in line of sight. The better the caster sings, the more effective it will be. It does not cost mana to cast.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: All Eyes on Me Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/All_Eyes_on_Me_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Allister</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Allister</b> is a former Crawler and author of the <i><a href="bword://Dungeon Anarchist&#x27;s Cookbook">Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook</a> (13th Edition)</i>. For Allister, the cookbook took the form of T'Ghee Cards. As T'Ghee was part of his meditation-based religion, he was able spend hours studying the cookbook's contents. He wrote a little bit in the cookbook about how T'Ghee works.</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 13</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Allister on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Allister</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Alpha Male Carl</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Alpha Male Carl</b> is a T'Ghee totem belonging to the <a href="bword://Reminiscence Hydra of Malicious Compliance">Reminiscence Hydra of Malicious Compliance</a>. Alpha Male Carl is a masculine caricature of <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>. He has gelled-back hair that <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> says is better than Carl's, and a prominent bulge in his star-patterned boxers. His War Gauntlet is bone-white rather than black. His patch jacket has two buttons: "#1 Son" and "Brother of the Century." He speaks in Carl's <a href="bword://Father">Father</a>'s voice.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Alpha Male Carl on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Alpha_Male_Carl</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Amayon</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Amayon</b> is a major demon lord and one of the four crown princes of Sheol. Expelled from Sheol by one of his brothers, he was stranded on the Eighth Floor, where the portal he cast to return home carried keyless crawlers into the stairwells to the next floor.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Sheol</li><li><b>Race:</b> Major Demon</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 58</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Amayon on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Amayon</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Amazonian</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Amazonian</b> is a race a crawler can choose upon entry to the Third Floor. The Amazonian race makes the crawler a foot taller and wider, enhancing their muscles until they look like a body builder. It most likely includes an increase in strength stats.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Amazonian on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Amazonian</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Anaconda</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Anaconda</b> is a level 75 Quarter <a href="bword://Naga">Naga</a> NPC who works as a lead exotic dancer at the Penis Parade strip club located within the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>. He is a highly favored performer of Princess <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> and has deep, secretive family ties to the club's management.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> The Dungeon (Desperado Club)</li><li><b>Race:</b> Quarter Naga</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3 (mentioned); Book 6, Chapter 23 (in person)</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Anaconda on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Anaconda</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Angel</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Angel</b> was a female cocker spaniel living with an unidentified female owner in the Seattle, WA apartment next door to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>, Bea, and Princess <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Seattle, WA</li><li><b>Race:</b> Cocker Spaniel Dog</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 13</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Angel on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Angel</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Annie</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Annie</b> is the child that <a href="bword://Katia Grim">Katia Grim</a> tried to adopt before the Transformation.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Annie on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Annie</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Anser</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Anser</b> is the long-dead emperor entombed within the Necropolis of Anser on the Fourth Floor, a conqueror who subjugated the local <a href="bword://Dromedarian">Dromedarian</a>, <a href="bword://Bactrian">Bactrian</a>, and Glaber peoples and brought his own people through a magical gate from elsewhere. His legend looms over the entire floor, though his true nature is only revealed once his tomb is finally breached.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Anser on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Anser</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Anton Lopez</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Anton Lopez</b> is an Earth Crawler from Cuba. While originally a prison guard before the collapse, he is now part of a squad with <a href="bword://Sister Ines">Sister Ines</a> and his cousin <a href="bword://Paz Lo">Paz Lo</a>. He briefly allies with the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a> on the Eighth Floor.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 5, Book 6</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Anton Lopez on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Anton_Lopez</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Apex Predator Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Apex Predator</b> is an <a href="bword://Achievement">Achievement</a> awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for killing the very last hunter on the Sixth Floor, thus fulfilling the promise he made to the hunters at the end of the Fifth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Apex Predator Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Apex_Predator_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Apito</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Apito</b>, the <b>Oak <a href="bword://Mother">Mother</a></b>, is a goddess of the Dungeon's in-game pantheon, revered as the mother of all gods and worshipped by elves, most fervently by the doomsday cult known as the 201st Security Group.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Oak Mother; Blessed Oak Mother; Oak Goddess; Tree Goddess</li><li><b>Race:</b> Goddess</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2, Chapter 17 (mentioned)</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Apito on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Apito</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Apollon the Mighty</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Apollon the Mighty</b> is an Elite created for the <i>Vengeance of the Daughter</i>. He and his brothers, <a href="bword://Areson the Wise">Areson the Wise</a> and Herman, were once the nodling tattooed on <a href="bword://Tsarina Signet">Tsarina Signet</a>'s skin.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Sensation Entertainment Inc</li><li><b>Race:</b> Nodling | Ogre</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2, Chapter 6</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Apollon the Mighty on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Apollon_the_Mighty</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Apostate Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Apostate Box</b> is a rare Loot Box awarded for angering gods other than the god that you worship. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives this box on the Sixth Floor from the <a href="bword://Temple Defiler Achievement">Temple Defiler Achievement</a> for falling through the roof of <a href="bword://Diwata">Diwata</a>'s desecrated church and landing on the altar, breaking it.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Achievements related to pissing off Gods; Marked for Life Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Apostate Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Apostate_Box</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Apothecary</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Apothecary</b> is a galaxy-spanning collective mind and the entity the Dungeon caricatures as the <a href="bword://Krakaren">Krakaren</a>. "Apothecary" is the truer translation of her name, taken from her ability to synthesize elements; the dungeon's version bends that translation into an insult.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Krakaren; The Collective; The Apothecary Lady</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Apothecary on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Apothecary</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Krakaren</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The Krakaren are a hive mind that runs the <a href="bword://Apothecary">Apothecary</a> and is financing the <a href="bword://Plenty">Plenty</a>.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> The Apothecary</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Krakaren on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Krakaren</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Apothecary Beanie</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Apothecary Beanie</b> appears to be a small, knitted beanie hat. It boosts all of the wearer's base stats by 3% and allows the wearer to cast the <a href="bword://I Need My Personal Space Spell">I Need My Personal Space Spell</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Benefactor Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Apothecary Beanie on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Apothecary_Beanie</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Apparel Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><i>Apparel Boxes</i> are a Loot Box distributed on the First Floor. The Gold Apparel Box glows with a golden light and contains two items. A Gold Apparel Box may be rewarded by an <a href="bword://Achievement">Achievement</a> or by cashing in a <a href="bword://PVP Coupon">PVP Coupon</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Apparel Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Apparel_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Arachnid</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Arachnid</b> is a half-human half-tarantula race.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Arachnid on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Arachnid</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Areson the Wise</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>Brother to Apollon and Herman, the three of them used to be nodlings.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Ogre</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 13, Book 5</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Areson the Wise on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Areson_the_Wise</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Arief</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Arief</b> is a Level 80 Semeru <a href="bword://Dwarf">Dwarf</a> and the War Leader commanding the Larracos Defense Force Infantry, serving under <a href="bword://Juice Box">Juice Box</a> as part of <a href="bword://Team Retribution">Team Retribution</a> during the Ninth Floor Faction Wars.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Arief on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Arief</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Armita</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Armita</b> is a former crawler who was part of <a href="bword://Odette">Odette</a>'s party. She entered the dungeon with Odette and got deep enougth that she managed to become a demigod attendant on the twelth floor.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human (non Earth)</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Prologue</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Armita on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Armita</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Armorer's Workshop</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>An <b>Armorer's Workshop</b> is a Crafting Crafting Workbench that can be purchased from a Safe Room Marketplace and installed in a crawler's Personal Space.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Marketplace</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Armorer's Workshop on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Armorer%27s_Workshop</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Arrow of Enthusiastic Double Gonorrhea</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>Although it looks deceptively like a normal arrow, the <b>Arrow of Enthusiastic Gonorrhea</b> is tipped with a poison that inflicts Enthusiastic Double Gonorrhea.</li><li><b>Source:</b> The Dream Hunters</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Arrow of Enthusiastic Double Gonorrhea on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Arrow_of_Enthusiastic_Double_Gonorrhea</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Arwick</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Arwick</b> was a member of the <a href="bword://Dream">Dream</a> and a hunter on the Sixth Floor Hunting Grounds. Bald and exceptionally pale, Arwick carried a quiver of unenchanted arrows but no bow. He wore a flowing, enchanted robe that allowed him to move quickly and gave him a small constitution buff.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Elf</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 5, Chapter 15</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Arwick on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Arwick</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Asher</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Asher</b> is <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s half-brother, whom Carl did not know existed until encountering a simulation of his father's home on the Eighth Floor. Asher was the son of Carl's father and Carl's stepmother, <a href="bword://Tami-Lynn">Tami-Lynn</a>. Carl was completely unaware of his existence, as his ex-girlfriend <a href="bword://Beatrice">Beatrice</a> and her mother had secretly known about the boy but deliberately hid the information from Carl. He liked to draw, as evidenced by the artwork Carl found in his childhood bedroom.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human (Simulated as a Hydra Head)</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 45</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Asher on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Asher</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Asojano</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Asojano</b> is the Lord of Smallpox. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>, <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>, <a href="bword://Sister Ines">Sister Ines</a>, Anton and Paz get a quest in which they get the option to repair his shrine. The description notes that repairing his shrine will not cause him to ascend.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Orisha Deity</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 10</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Asojano on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Asojano</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Assassin! Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Assassin! Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> after he kills <a href="bword://Miss Quill">Miss Quill</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Assassin! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Assassin%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Assassin's Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Assassin's Box</b> is a Loot Box awarded for successfully assassinating <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a>. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives this box for the <a href="bword://Assassin! Achievement">Assassin! Achievement</a> for killing <a href="bword://Miss Quill">Miss Quill</a> on the Third Floor.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Assassin! Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Assassin's Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Assassin%27s_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Assassin's Veil</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Assassin's Veil</b> is a unique item created for <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> with her choosing the Assassin of Sekhmet class on the Tenth Floor.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Donut when choosing the Assassin of Sekhmet Class</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Assassin's Veil on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Assassin%27s_Veil</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Asshole's Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Asshole's Boxes</b> are <a href="bword://Loot Boxes">Loot Boxes</a> awarded for particularly ruthless actions. Unless a Crawler is already affiliated with a club, they will most likely receive a <a href="bword://Desperado Pass Tattoo">Desperado Pass Tattoo</a> in their first Asshole's Box.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Achievements</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Asshole's Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Asshole%27s_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Astral Paw Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Astral Paw Spell</b> is a telekinesis spell that mimics the paw of an animal. At higher levels it becomes a potent attack spell. Obtained by <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> on Floor 5 through her membership to the <a href="bword://Dungeon Book of the Floor Club">Dungeon Book of the Floor Club</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Astral Paw Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Astral_Paw_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Astrid</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Astrid</b> is the Assistant Manager of the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>. Her sons are <a href="bword://Damascus Steel">Damascus Steel</a> and <a href="bword://Anaconda">Anaconda</a>. Astrid is a hand-sized fairy with buzzing wings; red sparkles follow her when she flies. She wears a tuxedo, and her raven hair is tied up in severe bun. She has a deep, serious voice that is not at odds with her appearance.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Bloodlust Sprite (Fairy)</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 9, Book 3</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Astrid on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Astrid</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Atoll</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Atoll</b> are a tall, thin race with four arms and only three fingers on each hand, they have thin shovel like faces with high set eyes, all set into wrinkle ape like skin. They have no mouths but they do have about a dozen nostril holes. They speak using sign language.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Atoll on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Atoll</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Author Steve Rowland</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Author Steve Rowland</b> is a Level 50 Forest Troll NPC who initially works as a male exotic dancer at the Penis Parade, a strip club located on the top floor of the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>. Following the destruction of the club, he is hired as a mercenary by <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and joins his entourage as an allied fighter, remaining with the crawlers until the climactic battle of the Eighth Floor.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Stevie</li><li><b>Origin:</b> The Dungeon (Desperado Club)</li><li><b>Race:</b> Forest Troll</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 23</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Author Steve Rowland on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Author_Steve_Rowland</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Automaton Table</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>An <b>Automaton Table</b> is a crafting table where crawlers can create automaton robots.</li><li><b>Source:</b> (bribery)</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Automaton Table on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Automaton_Table</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Azin</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Azin</b> is a former Crawler and author of the <i><a href="bword://Dungeon Anarchist&#x27;s Cookbook">Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook</a> (17th Edition)</i>. On Azin's homeworld, spiders only existed in myths. &lt;Note added by Crawler Azin. 17th Edition&gt; - Responding to <a href="bword://Sinjin">Sinjin</a>'s Final Entry</li><li><b>Race:</b> Unknown</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 26</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Azin on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Azin</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>B'sieging Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>B'sieging Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for using the Venomous Elven Rock Chucker Trebuchet Device against an Odious Creeper.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: B'sieging Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/B%27sieging_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Babababoon</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Babababoons</b> are mobs specifically created for <i>Dungeon Crawler World: Earth</i>. They are introduced on the Fourth Floor, where they are ~ Level 17.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Babababoon on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Babababoon</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bactrian</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bactrian</b> are A race of two humped camels.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bactrian on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bactrian</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bad Attitude Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bad Attitude Spell</b> is a spell that is similar to the <a href="bword://Fear Spell">Fear Spell</a> but it effects intelligence instead of dexterity and lowers resistance.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bad Attitude Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bad_Attitude_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bad Llama</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> encounters low level, lava-spitting, meth-dealing <b>bad llamas</b> on the first floor. With giant yellow buckteeth and tan fur, Bad Llamas are approximately the size of a horse. According to the Denver Zoo, regular llamas are characterized by a small head, a split upper lip, large ears, and short tails.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bad Llama on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bad_Llama</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Baggie of Trailer-Park-Grade Meth</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Baggie of Trailer-Park-Grade Meth</b> is a pharmaceutical item that is received as a loot drop after killing Bad Llamas. The system AI automatically adds these to the Pharmaceutical Items tab when <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> adds them to his inventory.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Bad Llama</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Baggie of Trailer-Park-Grade Meth on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Baggie_of_Trailer-Park-Grade_Meth</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ball of Swine</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Ball of Swine</b>, also known as the Porkchop Express, is a level 15 Borough Boss fought on the First Floor of the World Dungeon. It is not one creature but a rolling battle formation of dozens of <a href="bword://Tuskling">Tuskling</a> aristocrats fused into a single sphere of flesh, and it kills by steamrolling crawlers along concentric tracks governed by shifting dungeon walls.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ball of Swine on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ball_of_Swine</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bam Bam</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bam Bam</b> is a level 70 <a href="bword://Tummy Acher">Tummy Acher</a> T'Ghee card that was designed to eat mongo. He was a T'Ghee card owned by the <a href="bword://Reminiscence Hydra of Malicious Compliance">Reminiscence Hydra of Malicious Compliance</a> that never got to be played.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bam Bam on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bam_Bam</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bandages</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bandages</b> can be used to stop Bleed effects. They are frequently and abundantly found in low-tier <a href="bword://Loot Boxes">Loot Boxes</a> (especially Adventurer Boxes) on the First and Second floors.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Loot Boxes</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bandages on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bandages</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bandit Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bandit Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to all crawlers who survived the Fools Who Broke the Glass Quest. However due to a veto filed by the <a href="bword://Borant Corporation">Borant Corporation</a>, only <a href="bword://Quan Ch">Quan Ch</a> got to keep the reward. All other participants get the <a href="bword://Cuck Aquaman Achievement">Cuck Aquaman Achievement</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bandit Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bandit_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bang Bro Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bang Bro</b> is an enchantment Spell that adds fire and electrical damage to an equipped item.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bang Bro Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bang_Bro_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bard's Golden Throat</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bard's Golden Throat</b> is a microphone that automatically tunes songs to within one and a half steps of the correct note, assists in the proper formation of bard based songs and amplifies noise to twice normal volume, this can be increased to five times normal volume. It also provides +5% charisma.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bard's Golden Throat on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bard%27s_Golden_Throat</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Baroness Eclair Exquisite</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>A cat and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s cousin, she got run over by a tractor after running into a field.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Baroness Eclair Exquisite on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Baroness_Eclair_Exquisite</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Barry</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bartholomew Eli McGibbons</b>, known to everyone as <b>Barry</b>, was the late husband of <a href="bword://Elle McGibbons">Elle McGibbons</a>. He never appears in the Dungeon himself, having died decades before the crawl began, but he surfaces constantly in Elle's memories and stories, and is formally eulogized by her on the Tenth Floor.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Bartholomew Eli McGibbons</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 31</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Barry on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Barry</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Batbilge</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Batbilge</b> is a former Crawler and author of the <i><a href="bword://Dungeon Anarchist&#x27;s Cookbook">Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook</a> (12th Edition)</i>. &lt;Note added by Crawler Batbilge, 12th Edition&gt;</li><li><b>Race:</b> Unknown</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 3</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Batbilge on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Batbilge</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bathin</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bathin</b> is one of the chief engineers of the <a href="bword://Plenty">Plenty</a> Tunnel Project, the galaxy-spanning tunnel network built by the caprid Plenty. Bathin has a distinctive jowly face and is present on the caprid talk show hosted by <a href="bword://Botis">Botis</a> as a panelist. His reactions swing between joyful and panicked in a way <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> can't quite parse, culminating in a humanlike wail once the herd's mood turns.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bathin on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bathin</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Battlefield Construction Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Battlefield Construction!</b> is an achievement awarded to crawlers the first time they build a fortification or structure and then assemble it in a fight.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Battlefield Construction Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Battlefield_Construction_Achievement</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bautista</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Daniel Bautista</b> is an Earth Crawler and the sole survivor of a large extended family that entered the Dungeon together. A <a href="bword://Tigran">Tigran</a> Swashbuckler who fights with a curved sword and an army of summonable plush figures, he becomes a long-term ally of <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> after they avenge his family on the Third Floor.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Bautista</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Tigran</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2, Chapter 23</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bautista on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bautista</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Grace Bautista 3</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Grace <a href="bword://Bautista">Bautista</a></b> is Daniel Bautista's sister. She was killed by a Circus Lemur in the Overcity. The pile of corpses that includes Grace Bautista includes two <a href="bword://Human">Human</a> corpses, and the corpse of a large, humanoid, tree-like race. The humans appear to be "Asian, perhaps Filipino". Grace is implied to be the tree-like corpse. The body is humanoid, but badly mishapen ("closer to an Ent from Lord of the Rings than Groot from Guardians of the Galaxy”), with her facial features resembling a human but her back is hunched, with an extra set of limbs emerging from her back.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Large, tree-like creature</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2, Chapter 6</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Grace Bautista 3 on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Grace_Bautista_3</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bea's Mother</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bea's Mom</b> is portrayed as having been a mean spirited woman and a bad influence on <a href="bword://Beatrice">Beatrice</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>. She was highly religious and had had plastic surgery. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> describes her as having "...perfect, tight, face-lifted cheeks."</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: USA</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2, Chapter 12</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bea's Mother on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bea%27s_Mother</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bear Witness Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bear Witness Spell</b> is a spell. Spell can be negated by a high enough Mind Balance Skill. <a href="bword://Eris">Eris</a> (Goddess of Chaos) casts this at the start of the Open Hostilities section of Faction Wars (game).</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bear Witness Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bear_Witness_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Beatrice</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Beatrice</b>, usually called <b>Bea</b>, is an Earth character, the ex-girlfriend of <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>, and the owner of the Persian show cat who becomes <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>. She never enters the Dungeon, but is referenced frequently by both protagonists.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Bea, Miss Beatrice</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Seattle, WA</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 1</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Beatrice on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Beatrice</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Beguiler Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Beguiler Box</b> is a Loot Box awarded for charming mobs and <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a>. <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> receives this after charming the goblins on the First Floor.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Beguiler Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Beguiler_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Belt of Buoyancy</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Belt of Buoyancy</b> is a simple belt that, when equipped, prevents the wearer from sinking. It only works in water. It can be equipped on quadrupeds by wrapping it around their stomach.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Silver I'm Wet Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Belt of Buoyancy on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Belt_of_Buoyancy</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Benefactor Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Benefactor Boxes</b>, also called <b>sponsor boxes</b>, are a class of loot box purchased for a crawler by their sponsors. They use the same six quality tiers as every other box, but rank for rank they outclass ordinary loot: a bronze benefactor box beats a gold adventurer box.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Purchased and sent by one of a crawler's sponsors; Priority delivery available for an emergency fee</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Benefactor Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Benefactor_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bianca</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bianca Del Ciao</b> was originally a Boer goat and dungeon familiar to <a href="bword://Miriam Dom">Miriam Dom</a>. She is now a <a href="bword://Hellspawn Familiar">Hellspawn Familiar</a> to <a href="bword://Prepotente">Prepotente</a>. Bianca was one of fifteen brown-and-white Boer goats that Miriam Dom shepherded into the Dungeon. She enjoyed butt scratches and grapes.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Italy</li><li><b>Race:</b> Boer Goat | Hellspawn Familiar</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bianca on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bianca</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Big Boy Blue</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Big Boy Blue</b> are a white-tagged (nonhostile) race found in Water Quadrants on the Fifth Floor. A smaller white variant of the Big Boy Blue amplifies pain.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Big Boy Blue on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Big_Boy_Blue</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Big Daddy Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Big Daddy Box</b> is a rare Loot Box awarded for the sort of crazy feats that cause the <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a> to say, "Holy shit. Good job."</li><li><b>Source:</b> Three Cheers for Slaughter Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Big Daddy Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Big_Daddy_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Big Tina</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Big Tina</b> is a level 80 allosaurus city boss. She was born an ursine, but was transformed into an allosaurus after <a href="bword://Scolopendra">Scolopendra</a>'s <a href="bword://Nine-Tier Attack">Nine-Tier Attack</a>. She contracted Vampirism from <a href="bword://Miriam Dom">Miriam Dom</a>, but was cured of the curse after Miriam died.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Allosaurus</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Big Tina on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Big_Tina</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Big Top Ticket</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Big Top Ticket</b> is an item looted from <a href="bword://Terror the Clown">Terror the Clown</a> on the Third Floor. It allows entry into <a href="bword://Grimaldi">Grimaldi</a>'s Traveling Circus. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> gets a Big Top Ticket from Terror the Clown on the Third Floor. It allows entry into Grimaldi's Traveling Circus. He uses the ticket to come into the circus when he and <a href="bword://Tsarina Signet">Tsarina Signet</a> attack the following night.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Terror the Clown</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Big Top Ticket on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Big_Top_Ticket</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bijanbi Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bijanbi Spell</b> is a spell that summons an enemy to your location. Bijanbi is never clearly described, but is instead described in relation to other spells. The Hamzo Spell stuns and summons an enemy to your location. The Dinner Bell Spell does a similar effect but over an area of affect to multiple enemies. It doesn't stun the enemies, but you can designate a location. Binjanbi is something in that similar range of spells.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bijanbi Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bijanbi_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Billy Maloney</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Billy Maloney</b> was one of <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s friends in Seattle, WA. One week before the transformation, Billy stumbled out of a bar and peed on a cop's bicycle... while the same cop was writing up someone else for drunk and disorderly conduct. Billy already had an outstanding warrant for failing to appear in court a previous charge, and was still in jail during the collapse.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Seattle, WA</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 4</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Billy Maloney on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Billy_Maloney</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bin</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bin</b> is a <a href="bword://Nullian">Nullian</a> producer of Planet Beautiful, produced by the <a href="bword://Titan Conglomerate">Titan Conglomerate</a>. He looks tired and irritated, annoyed that his show has gotten popular enough that he is being micromanaged.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Nullian</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bin on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bin</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bisected Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bisected Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for teleporting into a door when he gets teleported back from CrawlCon.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bisected Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bisected_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bitch, What? Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bitch, What? Spell</b> is a spell granted to <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> by the <a href="bword://Enchanted Nipple Ring of the Superior Fire Demon’s Hand Maiden">Enchanted Nipple Ring of the Superior Fire Demon’s Hand Maiden</a>. Donut receives a legendary Beguiler's Box for having charmed <a href="bword://Ferdinand">Ferdinand</a> during the Butcher's Masquerade on the Sixth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bitch, What? Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bitch%2C_What%3F_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bitchmeat! Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bitchmeat!</b> is an achievement awarded the first time a crawler is attacked inside a safe room by another crawler. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> both receive this achievement after <a href="bword://Frank Q">Frank Q</a> and <a href="bword://Maggie My">Maggie My</a> attempt to assault them inside a safe room on the First Floor. It's the first <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a> notification that Carl laughs at, marking an important moment in their relationship.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bitchmeat! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bitchmeat%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Black Nimbus</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Black Nimbus</b> is a spell <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> gets from the <a href="bword://Enchanted Nipple Ring of the Defiler">Enchanted Nipple Ring of the Defiler</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Black Nimbus on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Black_Nimbus</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Blender Fiend</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Blender Fiends</b> are an unknown mob type that initially populated the First Floor, but were relocated to a lower level some 62 hours after the Dungeon opened due to concerns that they may wipe out the crawlers.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Blender Fiend on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Blender_Fiend</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Blister Ghoul</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Blister Ghoul</b> are a Fourth Floor mob that congregates at the stairwell location at station 72 on the Iron Tangle. Blister Ghouls look like almost-human heads with green, rotting skin. Some of them have torsos attached.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Blister Ghoul on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Blister_Ghoul</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Blitz Sticks</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Blitz Sticks</b> are a common but highly addictive magical hallucinogen. Blitz sticks look a bit like licorice sticks and, when lit, have a distinct tangy smell like patchouli. While smoking a blitz stick, saying <i>"show me..."</i> can produce a vivid non-existent memory or create a false escapist dream. The hallucinations are shorter each time the drug is used.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Dungeon PharmacistsLoot</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Blitz Sticks on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Blitz_Sticks</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Blood and Ink Elemental</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Blood and Ink Elemental</b> are a type of summoned minion. <a href="bword://Tsarina Signet">Tsarina Signet</a> summons Blood and Ink Elementals with her <a href="bword://Ink Marauder Spell">Ink Marauder Spell</a>. When the Ink Marauder Spell spell is cast, the tattoos of the caster become huge, fearsome monsters, but remain in the form of drawings. They barely have 3D shape, like a cutout paper monster.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Blood and Ink Elemental on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Blood_and_Ink_Elemental</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Blood Sultanate</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Blood Sultanate of the <a href="bword://Naga">Naga</a></b> is the royal house of the Naga in <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> space and a permanent participant in the Ninth Floor Faction Wars. Its line of succession is bound to a piece of dungeon loot, which makes it the single largest obstacle between the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a> and the Tenth Floor.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Sultanate</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Blood Sultanate on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Blood_Sultanate</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bloom</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Bloom</b>, or the <b>Party</b>, is the ultranationalist ruling political party of the <a href="bword://Kua-Tin">Kua-Tin</a>-dominated <a href="bword://Borant System">Borant System</a>. The Bloom rose to power in the Borant System in the last several hundred cycles. The party promotes the concepts of "system strength," True Unity, and the Great Consensus.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> The Party</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bloom on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bloom</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bobby</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bobby D.J.</b> was a crawler from Earth. His party occupied Bubble #543's Subterranean Quadrant on the Fifth Floor; <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> calls them the "tomb raiders."</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 6</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bobby on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bobby</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bodi</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bodi</b> is a former crawler whose season was Land War. He comes to help the <a href="bword://Princess Posse">Princess Posse</a> during Faction Wars (game). He is selected to be a battalion commander of the 103rd based on his experience inside and outside the dungeon. He is known as someone famous from outside the dungeon.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 7, Chapter 15</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bodi on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bodi</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bogdon Ro</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bogdon Ro</b> is a crawler in the dungeon. He spends time on/off the top 10 list. He has a lot of player killer skulls. He is killed by a hunter on the 6th floor and <a href="bword://Vrah">Vrah</a> sports his head attached to her back while fighting.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 4</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bogdon Ro on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bogdon_Ro</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bolt of Ophiotaurus</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Bolt of Ophiotaurus</b> is a crossbow bolt that, if shot into a deity's eye, can strip the deity of its invulnerability for fifteen seconds. There are only (100) Bolts of Ophiotaurus available.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Benefactor Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bolt of Ophiotaurus on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bolt_of_Ophiotaurus</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bolt of Petrify Rock Class</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>Bolt of Petrify Rock Class</b> is a crossbow bolt that imbues a rock-class target with the "Petrified" status condition. The bolt vanishes in a puff of smoke after impact. This type of bolt is more expensive than bolts designed to injure rock-class creatures.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Benefactor Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bolt of Petrify Rock Class on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bolt_of_Petrify_Rock_Class</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bolt-Thrower's Workshop</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Bolt-Thrower's Workshop</b> is a crafting workbench that allows for the mass production of explosive and other magical crossbow bolts. <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> buys the Bolt-Thrower's Workshop from the marketplace on the Fourth Floor. The bolts pair with <a href="bword://Katia Grim">Katia Grim</a>'s <a href="bword://Enchanted Repeating Crossbow of the Scavenger Mother of Mothers">Enchanted Repeating Crossbow of the Scavenger Mother of Mothers</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Marketplace</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bolt-Thrower's Workshop on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bolt-Thrower%27s_Workshop</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bomb Upgrade Patch</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Bomb Upgrade Patch</b> is an <a href="bword://Upgrade Patch">Upgrade Patch</a> given to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> on the Sixth Floor in a Gold <a href="bword://Spicy Box">Spicy Box</a> rewarded to him for the <a href="bword://This Little Piggy Made a Boom Boom! Achievement">This Little Piggy Made a Boom Boom! Achievement</a>. This patch is applied to the <a href="bword://Enchanted Anarchist&#x27;s Battle Rattle">Enchanted Anarchist's Battle Rattle</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Gold Spicy Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bomb Upgrade Patch on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bomb_Upgrade_Patch</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bomb's Away Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Bomb's Away Achievement</b> is an achievement you get by dropping a lot of ordnance while flying. A lot. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> did that after fleeing Larracos, and opens this box in a safe room on the Tenth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bomb's Away Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bomb%27s_Away_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bomo</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bomo</b> is a <a href="bword://Cretin">Cretin</a> NPC employed as a body guard at the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>. First appears as private security for Princess <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> and <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> in the Desperado Club. He is good friends with the <a href="bword://Sledge">Sledge</a>.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Cretin</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 8</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bomo on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bomo</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Boned Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <i><b>Boned</b></i> spell reanimates skeletons, apparently creating Skellies. This is the only spell that Fleshers know.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Boned Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Boned_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bonnie</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bonnie</b> is a juvenile <a href="bword://Dirigible Gnome">Dirigible Gnome</a> NPC originating from the Fifth Floor of the World Dungeon. Initially rescued by <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and Princess <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> after the tragic death of her father, <a href="bword://Commandant Kane">Commandant Kane</a>, Bonnie is taken under the wing of the <a href="bword://Princess Posse">Princess Posse</a> and its allies.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> The Dungeon (Fifth Floor, Air Quadrant)</li><li><b>Race:</b> Dirigible Gnome</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 16</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bonnie on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bonnie</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Book Burner Patch</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Book Burner <a href="bword://Upgrade Patch">Upgrade Patch</a></b> is an Upgrade Patch given to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> on the Eighth Floor in a Gold <a href="bword://Talk of the Town Box">Talk of the Town Box</a> rewarded to him for the <a href="bword://LBC Achievement">LBC Achievement</a>. This patch is applied to the <a href="bword://Enchanted Anarchist&#x27;s Battle Rattle">Enchanted Anarchist's Battle Rattle</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Gold Talk of the Town Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Book Burner Patch on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Book_Burner_Patch</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Book Burner Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Book Burner Spell</b> is a spell <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> gets as part of his <a href="bword://Book Burner Patch">Book Burner Patch</a> on the Eighth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Book Burner Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Book_Burner_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Boom! Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Boom!</b> is an achievement awarded the first time a crawler causes a significant explosion inside the Dungeon. It is a prerequisite to selecting the Bomb Squad Tech Class on the Third Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Boom! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Boom%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Boomer</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Boomer</b> is a former crawler who bowed out on the 10th floor. He eventually came back to help <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s army in their Faction Wars. The old man had been an outspoken critic of the crawl for a very long time.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Elf</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 7 chapter 22</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Boomer on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Boomer</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bopca</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bopca</b> are an alien race, but often work as non-combatant <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a> inside the Dungeon. Bopca are a stout, green-tinted, hairy dwarfish race that smell vaguely like wet moss. The females and males are equally shaggy. In general, Bopca are good cooks but known for having "a miserly streak"; giving discounts goes against their better nature.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bopca on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bopca</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Borant Corporation</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>A <a href="bword://Kua-Tin">Kua-Tin</a> megacorporation operating within the <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a>, the <b>Borant Corporation</b> (aka <b>Borant</b>) is the current planetary regent of Earth and the producer of <i>Dungeon Crawler World: Earth</i>.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Borant</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Borant Corporation on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Borant_Corporation</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Borant System</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Borant System</b> is a government and <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> System largely inhabited by <a href="bword://Kua-Tin">Kua-Tin</a>. The Borant System was formerly a democracy, republic, or other vote-based government with multiple political parties. In the last several hundred cycles, an ultranationalist party called the <a href="bword://Bloom">Bloom</a> rose to power. The Bloom introduced a totalitarian regime and strict social hierarchy in which Party members enjoy special treatment within the System and Bloom-controlled companies (e.g.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Kua-Tin</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Borant System on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Borant_System</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Borant Corporation</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>A <a href="bword://Kua-Tin">Kua-Tin</a> megacorporation operating within the <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a>, the <b>Borant Corporation</b> (aka <b>Borant</b>) is the current planetary regent of Earth and the producer of <i>Dungeon Crawler World: Earth</i>.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Borant</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Borant Corporation on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Borant_Corporation</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Borant Emancipation Front</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The Borant Emancipation Front is a rebel group fighting for control of the <a href="bword://Borant System">Borant System</a>. <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> and Zev helped smuggle Valtay secret agents to them.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Borant Emancipation Front on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Borant_Emancipation_Front</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Borant System</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Borant System</b> is a government and <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> System largely inhabited by <a href="bword://Kua-Tin">Kua-Tin</a>. The Borant System was formerly a democracy, republic, or other vote-based government with multiple political parties. In the last several hundred cycles, an ultranationalist party called the <a href="bword://Bloom">Bloom</a> rose to power. The Bloom introduced a totalitarian regime and strict social hierarchy in which Party members enjoy special treatment within the System and Bloom-controlled companies (e.g.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Kua-Tin</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Borant System on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Borant_System</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Borough Boss! Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Borough Boss!</b> is an achievement distributed the first time a crawler encounters a Borough Boss and/or enters their boss chamber. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>, <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>, <a href="bword://Imani">Imani</a>, <a href="bword://Chris Andrews">Chris Andrews</a>, <a href="bword://Brandon Andrews">Brandon Andrews</a>, <a href="bword://Yolanda Martinez">Yolanda Martinez</a>, and <a href="bword://Agatha">Agatha</a> receive this achievement after defeating the <a href="bword://Ball of Swine">Ball of Swine</a> on the First Floor. Carl and Donut immediately descend the stairs, and do not open the achievement until after finding a Safe Room in the <a href="bword://Mind Horror">Mind Horror</a> neighborhood on the Second Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Borough Boss! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Borough_Boss%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Borough Field Guide</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Borough Field Guide</b> is a persistent loot item dropped by slain Borough Bosses. Once a crawler picks up the item, the boss's borough will be outlined on the crawler's minimap. The individual rooms and hallways are obscured by the "fog of war" but, when a crawler zooms in on an area, a tooltip pops up showing the mob types and levels there as (for example) <b>Mobs Level 2-5. Axebeak.</b></li><li><b>Source:</b> Borough Boss</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Borough Field Guide on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Borough_Field_Guide</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Boss Babe Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Boss Babe</b> is an achievement awarded the first time a crawler deals damage to a boss. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives this achievement on the First Floor after lobbing <a href="bword://Goblin Dynamite">Goblin Dynamite</a> into the <a href="bword://Hoarder">Hoarder</a>'s lair.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Boss Babe Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Boss_Babe_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Boss Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>Boss Box</b> is a Loot Box awarded to Crawlers who kill a Boss monster. The box's tier, and the quality of the loot inside, scales with the difficulty of the boss defeated.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Defeating a Boss</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Boss Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Boss_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Botis</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Botis</b> is a caprid goat and the magistrate/host of a live trial-style talk show, <a href="bword://Plenty">Plenty</a> of Plenty, run by the Plenty, the goat-people who run the galaxy's tunnel network.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Botis on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Botis</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bounty Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bounty Boxes</b> are rare <a href="bword://Loot Boxes">Loot Boxes</a> awarded to players who kill one of the Top Ten Crawlers on the Leaderboard. The Bounty Box contains the bounty for the slain crawler.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Claim a Crawler's Bounty</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bounty Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bounty_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Brad</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Brad</b> is <a href="bword://Beatrice">Beatrice</a>'s ex-boyfriend and presumed lover. He persuaded her to post a picture of the two of them on instagram that resulted in <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> breaking up with her.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Brad on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Brad</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Brain Boiler</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Brain Boilers</b> are a Third Floor mob that specializes in psionic attacks. They are a more advanced form of the Mind Horrors from the Second Floor</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Brain Boiler on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Brain_Boiler</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Brain Freeze Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Brain Freeze Spell</b> is a spell that targets one mob and drains their health. The spell targets one mob and drains their health. At level 10 it makes them temporarily blind.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Brain Freeze Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Brain_Freeze_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Brandon Andrews</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Brandon Andrews</b> is a crawler from Wenatchee, WA, and a member of the <a href="bword://Meadow Lark">Meadow Lark</a> party. He and his older brother <a href="bword://Chris Andrews">Chris Andrews</a> entered the Dungeon alongside the elderly residents they were paid to look after, and are the first friendly crawlers <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> meet.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Wenatchee, WA</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 22</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Brandon Andrews on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Brandon_Andrews</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bravvo</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bravvo</b> is the thirty-sixth Hunter killed by <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>. Dropped black leather boots, enchanted against magical bolts; 30 Good Health Potions; 30 Good Mana Refills; magical longsword (+2 CON), 9 potions of Levitation.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Yenk</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 5, Chapter 13</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bravvo on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bravvo</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Brawler's Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Brawler's Boxes</b> are a Loot Box awarded for... brawling. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> gets a Gold Brawler's Box for the <a href="bword://Two Chicks at the Same Time Achievement">Two Chicks at the Same Time Achievement</a> during the fight with the <a href="bword://Juicer">Juicer</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Two Chicks at the Same Time Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Brawler's Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Brawler%27s_Box</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ring of Water Breathing</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> gets a <b>Ring of Water Breathing</b> on the Fifth Floor. A glowing blue ring that twinkles with little sparkles.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Gold I'm Wet Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ring of Water Breathing on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ring_of_Water_Breathing</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Scroll of Water Breathing</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Scroll of Water Breathing</b> is a scroll that allows a crawler to breathe underwater for a limited amount of time.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Platinum That Wasn't Too Smart, Was It? Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Scroll of Water Breathing on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Scroll_of_Water_Breathing</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Brin Root</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Brin Root</b> is a rare alchemical ingredient, but less stable than Bujold Sap. When <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> purchases a <a href="bword://Pharmaceutical Starter Kit">Pharmaceutical Starter Kit</a> from <a href="bword://Quint">Quint</a> in the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a> on the Third Floor, he notes that it does not include brin root. Quint explains that it's hard to come by, and he has substituted two vials of bujold sap instead.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Quint</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Brin Root on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Brin_Root</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Brindle Grub</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Brindle Grubs</b> are the janitor mob of the Second Floor. One to fifteen Brindle Grubs are spawned every time a corpse is created until their numbers cap out at 5,000 per quadrant. Destroying corpses prevents Brindle Grubs from leveling up but not from spawning, and eventually causes hoards of the mob to swarm crawlers, thus chasing crawlers out of otherwise secured neighborhoods.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Brindle Grub on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Brindle_Grub</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Britney</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Britney Proskurina</b> is an Earth Crawler from Ukraine and one of the three crawlers to come out alive from the water quadrant of Bubble 543 on the Fifth Floor. She travels with the loose group of survivors that forms around <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Ukraine, Earth</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 25</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Britney on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Britney</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bronze Condom</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bronze Condom</b> is an item <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives as a result of the <a href="bword://It itches when I pee Achievement">It itches when I pee Achievement</a>. An unenchanted condom in bronze colored packaging. It has a sketch of an older woman (possibly Bea Arthur) and a sheep on the other.</li><li><b>Source:</b> It itches when I pee Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bronze Condom on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bronze_Condom</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Brynhild's Daughters</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Brynhild's Daughters</b> is an all-female party of crawlers founded and led by <a href="bword://Hekla">Hekla</a> and themed after Norse shieldmaiden imagery. The party operated separately from the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a>.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> The Daughters, Hekla's team</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Brynhild's Daughters on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Brynhild%27s_Daughters</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bucket Boy</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bucket Boy</b> is a young <a href="bword://Crocodilian">Crocodilian</a> NPC who works as a tip collector at the Penis Parade strip club within the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>. He is later hired as a mercenary for the <a href="bword://Princess Posse">Princess Posse</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> The Dungeon (Desperado Club)</li><li><b>Race:</b> Crocodilian</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 23</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bucket Boy on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bucket_Boy</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bugaboo</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bugaboos</b> are a type of mob found on the First, Second, and Third Floors. <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> is a bugaboo on the second floor. Approximately 7 ft tall, Bugaboos look both "terrifying and cartoonish." They take the general shape of a bear with no neck, enormous owl-like eyes, "comically skinny legs," and long but "absurdly thin" arms. They are covered in obsidian-colored hair.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bugaboo on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bugaboo</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bugbear</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bugbear</b> are a race on the Fifth Floor. Unknown, but references are made to bugbear paste (as an explosive) and bugbear metal (found in the submarine of Bubble #543) by <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Tran">Tran</a>. Also, <a href="bword://Priestly">Priestly</a> marched on Larracos with the bugbear army on his ninth floor, which drove him insane.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bugbear on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bugbear</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bugbear Paste</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bugbear Paste</b> is a paste capable of creating powerful explosions. <a href="bword://Coolie">Coolie</a> secretes bugbear paste into his boots with the intention of detonating it some time later and the expectation that the small quantity will destroy a spaceship, suggesting that it is relatively stable and extremely powerful.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bugbear Paste on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bugbear_Paste</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bully and a Thief Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bully <i>and</i> a Thief!</b> is an achievement awarded to crawlers who seize a lower level crawler's property. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives this achievement for taking <a href="bword://Agatha">Agatha</a>'s shopping cart into his inventory during the battle against the <a href="bword://Ball of Swine">Ball of Swine</a> on the First Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bully and a Thief Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bully_and_a_Thief_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bune</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bunes</b> are a <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> race, and inhabited at least one seeded planet featured in a previous season of <i>Dungeon Crawler World.</i> A slight, dragon-like people, Bunes are naturally peaceful.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bune on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bune</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Burcu</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Burcu</b> is a badger-headed <a href="bword://Porsuk">Porsuk</a> Swashbuckler crawler who spent much of her crawl floating near the bottom of the top ten leaderboard, and who came to blame <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for her father's death.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Turkey</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Porsuk</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Burcu on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Burcu</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Burgundy</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 2.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Burgundy</b> is a human assistant working in the Medium <a href="bword://Skyfowl">Skyfowl</a> Settlement on the Third Floor who is secretly cursed to transform into a <a href="bword://Krasue">Krasue</a> each night.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Burgundy on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Burgundy</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Book Burner Patch</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Book Burner <a href="bword://Upgrade Patch">Upgrade Patch</a></b> is an Upgrade Patch given to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> on the Eighth Floor in a Gold <a href="bword://Talk of the Town Box">Talk of the Town Box</a> rewarded to him for the <a href="bword://LBC Achievement">LBC Achievement</a>. This patch is applied to the <a href="bword://Enchanted Anarchist&#x27;s Battle Rattle">Enchanted Anarchist's Battle Rattle</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Gold Talk of the Town Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Book Burner Patch on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Book_Burner_Patch</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Book Burner Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Book Burner Spell</b> is a spell <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> gets as part of his <a href="bword://Book Burner Patch">Book Burner Patch</a> on the Eighth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Book Burner Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Book_Burner_Spell</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Burrowers</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Burrowers</b> are the <a href="bword://Mantis">Mantis</a> royal family and governmental entity in charge of the Hive Home System, one of several Mantis-occupied solar systems in a cluster of stars. They are the driving force behind the development of Macro AIs, and a regular participant in Faction Wars.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Burrowers on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Burrowers</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bush Elf</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bush Elves</b> are a subrace of Elves. Crawlers may choose the "Bush Elf" race on the Third Floor, or may encounter Bush Elf <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a> on the Dungeon's Sixth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bush Elf on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bush_Elf</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Butcher's Masquerade Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Butcher's Masquerade</b> is a divine ritual spell and one of the holiest sacraments of <a href="bword://Apito">Apito</a>, the Blessed Oak <a href="bword://Mother">Mother</a>. It cannot be learned or cast by ordinary crawlers; the right belongs to the goddess's clerics, and only to the most divine among them, who may use it once in their lives to convene a protected gathering of mortal enemies. No caster has ever completed one successfully.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Butcher's Masquerade Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Butcher%27s_Masquerade_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Camouflage Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Camouflage</b> is a spell that conceals its caster's dot on the Minimap as long as the caster stays in place. <i>Camouflage</i> is included with the Guerilla Class Upgrade.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Camouflage Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Camouflage_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Cannonball! Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Cannonball!</b> <a href="bword://Achievement">Achievement</a> would presumably be awarded to any crawler who survives falling from a great height. It probably contains some interesting information that <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> will never have a chance to read.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Cannonball! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Cannonball%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Caprid</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Caprid</b> is a <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> race and a Crawler race option, a sapient, goat-like people best known as the species of the <a href="bword://Plenty">Plenty</a> and of the crawler <a href="bword://Prepotente">Prepotente</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Caprid on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Caprid</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Carl</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Carl</b> is the titular protagonist of <i>Dungeon Crawler Carl</i>. A former coast guardsman, Carl and his ex-girlfriend's cat are now fan-favorite crawlers on the <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> gameshow, <i>Dungeon Crawler World: Earth</i>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Seattle, WA</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Primal</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 1</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Carl on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Carl</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Carl's Doomsday Scenario</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Carl's Doomsday Scenario</b> is a "Pretty Damn Rare" item that <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> created trying to solve the Fools Who Broke the Glass Quest. During the (original) end of the Fools Who Broke the Glass Quest on the Third Floor, Carl placed a <a href="bword://Sheol Glass Reaper Case">Sheol Glass Reaper Case</a> around an about-to-explode Soul Crystal and pulled the result into his inventory.</li><li><b>Source:</b> A Sheol Glass Reaper Case placed around an about to explode soul crystal.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Carl's Doomsday Scenario on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Carl%27s_Doomsday_Scenario_%28Item%29</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Carl's Jug O'Boom</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Carl's Jug O'Boom</b> is <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s take on a Dungeon Molotov Cocktail. Carl's Jug O'Boom is crafted by emptying a clay <a href="bword://Rev-Up Toilet-Grade Moonshine">Rev-Up Toilet-Grade Moonshine</a> jug to about 3/4 full, adding a few ounces of <a href="bword://Goblin Oil">Goblin Oil</a>, and corking the bottle with a <a href="bword://Torch">Torch</a>. The crawler only has to look at the Torch, select "Activate" in their Heads-Up Display (HUD), and throw the bottle.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Crafting</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Carl's Jug O'Boom on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Carl%27s_Jug_O%27Boom</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Cascadia</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Cascadia</b> is a Kua-tin alien Dungeon admin, best known as the voice of the daily announcements broadcast to the crawlers during the Earth season of Dungeon Crawler World and famous for signing off with her catchphrase, "Now get out there and kill, kill, kill!"</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> The "kill, kill, kill" lady</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Borant System</li><li><b>Race:</b> Kua-tin (Mudskipper)</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 14</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Cascadia on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Cascadia</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Cascadia's Turquoise Taco Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Cascadia's Turquoise Taco Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to all crawlers who end a card fight before any cards are drawn.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Cascadia's Turquoise Taco Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Cascadia%27s_Turquoise_Taco_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Casino Chip</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Casino Chip</b> can be used at the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives a 100,000 credit chip in a <a href="bword://Lucky Bastard Box">Lucky Bastard Box</a> from the <a href="bword://Lazarus Achievement">Lazarus Achievement</a>. The black poker chip has pink and purple splotches along the edges. The Desperado Club dagger is in the middle. The chip feels like it weighs 15 pounds.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Platinum Lucky Bastard Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Casino Chip on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Casino_Chip</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Cat</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> is the only fully cat crawler in the Dungeon; however, at least one crawler chose the Were-Cat race, and several chose the <a href="bword://Cat Girl">Cat Girl</a> race.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Cat on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Cat</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Cat Girl</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Cat Girl</b> is a race of humanoid cat. It provides a charisma bonus. <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> is offended by this race, and especially <a href="bword://Sister Ines">Sister Ines</a>, who Donut says is a Havana Brown cat.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Cat Girl on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Cat_Girl</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Cave Mudge Bonker</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Cave Mudge Bonkers</b> (or "Bonkers") are a Fourth Floor mob that can be found on the Yellow Line. Bonkers are gray-skinned, pig-like, corpulent monsters wobbling on thin legs. Their heads are topped with wisps of oily black hair, and feature black beady eyes and shark-like mouths. They have no necks and stand at approximately 4' 6" (1.37m) tall. They are armed with wooden clubs studded with nails.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Cave Mudge Bonker on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Cave_Mudge_Bonker</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Celestial</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Celestial</b> is the highest, rarest tier of Dungeon-made items and <a href="bword://Loot Boxes">Loot Boxes</a>. Celestial objects are often tied to <a href="bword://Gods">Gods</a>, either bestowing god-like powers or given by gods as quests rewards.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Celestial on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Celestial</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Celestial Grenade</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>Rare and expensive, <b><a href="bword://Celestial">Celestial</a> Grenades</b> look like spiked orbs with a pin. When detonated, they summon a deity for one minute (60 seconds). They are commonly used near the end of the Ninth Floor Faction Wars.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Celestial Grenade on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Celestial_Grenade</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Celestial Loot Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Celestial Loot Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> on the Eighth Floor for picking up <a href="bword://Quan Ch">Quan Ch</a>'s <a href="bword://Celestial">Celestial</a> <a href="bword://Cloak of the Benevolent Champion">Cloak of the Benevolent Champion</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Celestial Loot Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Celestial_Loot_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Celestial Orgy of Chaos Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Celestial Orgy of Chaos Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to all Crawlers who were in <a href="bword://Club Vanquisher">Club Vanquisher</a> during Operation Snake Pit. <a href="bword://Li Jun">Li Jun</a>, <a href="bword://Zhang">Zhang</a>, <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>, <a href="bword://Prepotente">Prepotente</a>, and <a href="bword://Katia Grim">Katia Grim</a> got a <a href="bword://Celestial">Celestial</a> Who Let the <a href="bword://Gods">Gods</a> Out This Time Box, and Daniel <a href="bword://Bautista">Bautista</a> got a Legendary Who Let the Gods Out This Time Box because he left early.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Celestial Orgy of Chaos Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Celestial_Orgy_of_Chaos_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Cerberus</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Cerberus</b> is a "three-headed monstrosity" and Gate Guardian rumored to guard one of the stairwells on the Twelfth Floor. <a href="bword://Orthrus">Orthrus</a> is Cerberus's little brother.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> God</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 29</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Cerberus on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Cerberus</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Chaco</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Chaco</b> is an alien NPC and former Crawler who works for the Dungeon Crawler World production as an on-camera personality, best known as host of The <a href="bword://Prize Carousel">Prize Carousel</a>. A <a href="bword://Pterolykos">Pterolykos</a> Song Bard, he shares a violent history with <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a>, the Royal Court's manager, who attacks him on sight.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Chaco the Bard</li><li><b>Race:</b> Skyfowl | Pterolykos</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 7</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Chaco on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Chaco</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Chalchiuhtlicue</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Chalchiuhtlicue</b> is a goddess in the dungeon. After the death of the dogs of <a href="bword://Lucia Mar">Lucia Mar</a>, Chalchiuhtlicue became Lucia's newest influence, mentally communicating with her.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> God</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 8, Chapter 51</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Chalchiuhtlicue on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Chalchiuhtlicue</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Champion Pack</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Champion Pack</b> is a reward for beating the key master on the Eighth Floor.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Defeating keymaster on the Eighth Floor</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Champion Pack on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Champion_Pack</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Chandra</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Princess Chandra, Esquire</b> is a <a href="bword://Naga">Naga</a> lawyer and the opportunistic widow of <a href="bword://Rishi">Rishi</a>. Following a bloody political coup in her home system, she uses an antiquated Naga law to legally force a marriage to the dungeon crawler <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>, attempting to seize control of his and Princess <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s massive fortunes. She is not a crawler, but an external citizen maneuvering through the <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> legal system.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Naga Sector</li><li><b>Race:</b> Naga</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 8, Interlude: Chandra</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Chandra on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Chandra</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Changbi Demon</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Changbi Demon</b> is a race a crawler can choose upon entry to the Third Floor. <a href="bword://Li Na">Li Na</a> chooses this as her race on the Third Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Changbi Demon on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Changbi_Demon</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Changeling</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Changeling</b> is a race a crawler can choose upon entry to the Third Floor, and a people of shapeshifters found throughout the Dungeon as <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a>, mobs, and game guides. Unlike doppelgangers, they shift into any species they have physically touched and gain part of that species' abilities along with its form.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Changeling on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Changeling</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Charge of the Light Brigade Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Charge of the Light Brigade Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> (and presumably <a href="bword://Katia Grim">Katia Grim</a> and <a href="bword://Prepotente">Prepotente</a>) for storming into <a href="bword://Khepri">Khepri</a>'s temple uninvited to kill <a href="bword://Vinata">Vinata</a> during Operation Snake Pit. It is most likely in reference to the doomed cavalry charge by the same name.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Charge of the Light Brigade Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Charge_of_the_Light_Brigade_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Charles</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Charles</b> Ellis is a bartender <a href="bword://Samantha">Samantha</a> attempts to seduce in the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>. He was killed by <a href="bword://Minge">Minge</a> after being kidnapped by Samantha.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Porsuk</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Charles on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Charles</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Charm Animal Potion</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <i><b>Charm Animal</b></i> <a href="bword://Potion">Potion</a> tames a Dungeon animal for the duration of the Floor. The potion must be brewed for that specific type of creature using blood.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Recipe</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Charm Animal Potion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Charm_Animal_Potion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Cheat Code Potion</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>Cheat Code Potion</b> is a potion that adds 3 levels to a random combat or magic skill. When a crawler receives this potion, a flashing red timer (starting with <i>at least</i> 17 minutes) appears at the bottom of the description. Even if a crawler consumes this potion from their hotlist, they feel a crackling sensation in their mouth, as though they had "just downed a whole packet of Pop Rocks."</li><li><b>Source:</b> Loot Boxes</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Cheat Code Potion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Cheat_Code_Potion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Chee</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Chee</b> are a race. The Chee were a peaceful race before being attacked by the high-elves lead by <a href="bword://King Finian">King Finian</a>, Finian's daughter Princess <a href="bword://Imogen">Imogen</a> transformed them into Were-kin.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Chee on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Chee</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Chickenshit Exploit Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Chickenshit Exploit Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for the teleport totem hack he and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> used to fight <a href="bword://Quan Ch">Quan Ch</a> with <a href="bword://Tserendolgor">Tserendolgor</a> on the Eighth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Chickenshit Exploit Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Chickenshit_Exploit_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Children of Inpewt</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Children of Inpewt</b> are powerful revenants created by the spell <a href="bword://Zerzura Spell">Zerzura Spell</a>. Zerzura transfers a full Dungeon settlement, including all of its <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a> and buildings, to a "random" location on a deeper floor. Every creature previously occupying the location is immediately killed and then resurrected as Children of Inpewt. Everyone in the transferred settlement is marked for death by the Children of Inpewt, who will not stop until all their marks are dead.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Children of Inpewt on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Children_of_Inpewt</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Chilly Goat</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Chilly Goats</b> are a mob found on the First Floor. They are white, horned goats with mouths full of fangs.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Chilly Goat on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Chilly_Goat</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Chin'Dua</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The second Hunter killed by <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Draconian</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 5, Book 5</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Chin'Dua on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Chin%27Dua</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Chirag Ali</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>Not much is known about Chirag Ali. They appear once on the Leaderboard during the middle of the Fifth Floor, in the 10th spot.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 17, Book 4</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Chirag Ali on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Chirag_Ali</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Chiyome</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Chiyome. <a href="bword://Razor Fox">Razor Fox</a>. Level 80 Mistress of Nunchaku.</b> One of three from team The Wild Hunt.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Razor Fox</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 8, Chapter 12</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Chiyome on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Chiyome</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Chris Andrews</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Chris Andrews</b> is a Crawler from Wenatchee, Washington, and one of the original members of the <a href="bword://Meadow Lark">Meadow Lark</a> party. A quiet, stoic maintenance man, he stood by the group's elderly wards and fought alongside his brother Brandon and the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a> to open the First Floor stairwell.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Silent Bob</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth (Wenatchee, WA)</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Igneous | Werewolf</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 22</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Chris Andrews on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Chris_Andrews</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Cichociemni</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>A group of crawlers. They are named after Polish special forces despite none of them being from Poland. Mentioned on <a href="bword://Odette">Odette</a>'s show in Epilogue of Book 3.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Cichociemni on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Cichociemni</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Cici</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Cici</b> is one of <a href="bword://Lucia Mar">Lucia Mar</a>'s Rottweilers that entered the dungeon with her. Cici and <a href="bword://Gustavo 3">Gustavo 3</a> are put in the pet playroom while Lucia Mar goes into the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>. They get riled up, kill two attendants and another pet and break into the main club. This, along with Lucia Mar killing an Elite she is talking to, is how Lucia gets banned from the club.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth</li><li><b>Race:</b> Rotweiler</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Cici on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Cici</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Circe Took</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Circe Took</b> is of the mantis race. She is a minor hive queen. She is the mother of <a href="bword://Hunters">Hunters</a> <a href="bword://Vrah">Vrah</a> and <a href="bword://Xindy">Xindy</a>. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> meets her at CrawlCon! where she is the moderator of the Crawling Through the Ages panel. Circe is enraged with Carl for killing her daughter Xindy and is further enraged by Carl promising to kill her other daughter, Vrah. She later managed to successfully sue to let the hunters leave early, arguing that now that the <a href="bword://Borant Corporation">Borant Corporation</a> was no longer running the show, their contracts were no longer binding.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Mantis</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Circe Took on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Circe_Took</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Clammy the Clown</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Clammy the Clown</b> is a clown in <a href="bword://Grimaldi">Grimaldi</a>'s Traveling Circus. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> comes across him when entering the circus tent as he and <a href="bword://Tsarina Signet">Tsarina Signet</a> attack the circus.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2, Chapter 9</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Clammy the Clown on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Clammy_the_Clown</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Clarabelle</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Clarabelle</b> is a lizard-faced <a href="bword://Crocodilian">Crocodilian</a> NPC who works as a bouncer at the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>. Clarabelle knows <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> from previous seasons and is happy to let him enter the club on the Third Floor.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Crocodilian</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2, Chapter 15</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Clarabelle on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Clarabelle</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Claude Sludgington the Fourth</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Claude Sludgington the Fourth</b>, a Level 65 Borough Boss Eryops Gigantis.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> River Squatter or the Mud Kato</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon: Sixth Floor</li><li><b>Race:</b> Eryops Gigantis</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Claude Sludgington the Fourth on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Claude_Sludgington_the_Fourth</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Clay</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Clay</b> is the gatekeeper at Hump Town, armed with a spear and a home-made bazooka with five guided anti-air rockets.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Dromedarian</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Clay on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Clay</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Clay-ton</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Clay-ton</b> is is a <a href="bword://Cretin">Cretin</a> NPC employed as a body guard at the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>. He later joins the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a> as a mercenary.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Cretin</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 8</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Clay-ton on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Clay-ton</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Cleaner Bot</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Cleaner Bots</b> are a Personal Space upgrade that crawlers can purchase for 25,000 gold beginning on the Fourth Floor. Beyond simple housekeeping, the units are capable of far more than they first appear, and by Book 8 a single cleaner bot becomes the linchpin of a plan to smuggle crawlers out of the dungeon entirely.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Bopca</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Cleaner Bot on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Cleaner_Bot</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Cleiton</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Cleiton</b> was a crawler from Earth and a member of Team <a href="bword://Flamengo">Flamengo</a>. He had sapphire armor and occasionally appeared on the recap episodes. Cleiton attended the Butcher's Masquerade at the end of the Sixth Floor, and was the opening act of the talent competition. He nervously told "knock knock" jokes and fumbled the punchlines.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 5, Chapter 72</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Cleiton on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Cleiton</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Cliffhanger Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Cliffhanger Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for climbing the patch of Iowa in the Florida Keys on the Eighth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Cliffhanger Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Cliffhanger_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Clint Smashgrab</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Clint Smashgrab</b> is a bald, one-legged were-castor.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Chee | Were-kin</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 5, Chapter 13</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Clint Smashgrab on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Clint_Smashgrab</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Cloak of the Benevolent Champion</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Cloak of the Benevolent Champion</b> is a <a href="bword://Celestial">Celestial</a>-tier shoulder accessory that provides massive, game-changing buffs to the wearer's stats, spells, and skills. Originally awarded to the crawler <a href="bword://Quan Ch">Quan Ch</a>, it is later looted by <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and worn by Princess <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Looted from Quan Ch; originally awarded via a Celestial Quest Box during the Fools Who Broke the Glass Quest</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Cloak of the Benevolent Champion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Cloak_of_the_Benevolent_Champion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Clockwork Triplicate</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Clockwork Triplicate</b> is a utility spell that creates two clockwork copies of a crawler's pet or minion. When <i>Clockwork Triplicate</i> is cast, the target appears to split into three. The two duplicates look and behave like the target, but act independently. The <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a> does not identify which copy is real.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Clockwork Triplicate on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Clockwork_Triplicate</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Krakaren Clone (Fourth Floor)</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b><a href="bword://Krakaren">Krakaren</a></b> on the Fourth Floor is a Borough Boss, and part of the Iron Tangle political statement. The Iron Tangle is a massive political statement by the <a href="bword://Borant Corporation">Borant Corporation</a>, and the fact that there is a version of Krakaren in the level is directed towards the actions of the <a href="bword://Apothecary">Apothecary</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon - Fourth Floor</li><li><b>Race:</b> Apothecary, Krakaren</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 10</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Krakaren Clone (Fourth Floor) on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Krakaren_Clone_%28Fourth_Floor%29</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Krakaren Clone (Second Floor)</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b><a href="bword://Krakaren">Krakaren</a> Clone</b> is a Neighborhood Boss on the Second Floor, and part of the running <a href="bword://Rev-Up">Rev-Up</a> storyline. There are at least three separate instances of the Krakaren Clone on the level.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon - Second Floor</li><li><b>Race:</b> Apothecary</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 34</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Krakaren Clone (Second Floor) on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Krakaren_Clone_%28Second_Floor%29</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Cloud of Exhaust Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Cloud of Exhaust Spell</b> is a telekinesis spell that knocks out mobs, mobs wake up after taking damage but any damage dealt to them in the next 30 seconds will be enhanced.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Cloud of Exhaust Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Cloud_of_Exhaust_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Club Vanquisher</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Club Vanquisher</b> is one of the two main clubs of the World Dungeon, first available to crawlers in the Over City on the Third Floor. The exclusive, country-club-style religious counterpart to the raucous <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>, it caters to the dungeon's clerics, paladins, and the worshippers of its many deities.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Club Vanquisher on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Club_Vanquisher</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Clurichaun</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Clurichaun</b> are a fairy-class mob on the Second Floor. Small and troll-like with humanoid bodies and oversized heads, Clurichaun are marked by curly black hair, hooked noses, small feet, and very few teeth. They make a puglike gurgling noise when attack.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Clurichaun on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Clurichaun</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Unvaccinated Clurichaun Rev-Up Consultant</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b><a href="bword://Clurichaun">Clurichaun</a></b> are a fairy-class mob on the Second Floor. Small and troll-like with humanoid bodies and oversized heads, Clurichaun are marked by curly black hair, hooked noses, small feet, and very few teeth. They make a puglike gurgling noise when attack.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Unvaccinated Clurichaun Rev-Up Consultant on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Unvaccinated_Clurichaun_Rev-Up_Consultant</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>CockBlock Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>CockBlock Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> when he kills <a href="bword://Miss Quill">Miss Quill</a>, an NPC needed for Daniel <a href="bword://Bautista">Bautista</a> to complete his own quest.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: CockBlock Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/CockBlock_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Coffee Shop Author Kit</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4 and 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Coffee Shop Author Kit</b> is a crafting tool consisting of a magical sheet of paper, a quill pen, and a little capped jar filled with black ink. It allows users to copy information from a second (or third) page of their scratchpad onto the magical paper or from the magical paper to their scratchpad.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Gold Makeup Sex is the Best Sex Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Coffee Shop Author Kit on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Coffee_Shop_Author_Kit</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Columbia House Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Columbia House Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> when he takes out a loan to pay for the ring upgrade in <a href="bword://Club Vanquisher">Club Vanquisher</a>. The 8th track on Cuts Both Ways is called "Get on Your Feet".</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Columbia House Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Columbia_House_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Combo Card</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Combo Card</b> is a T'Ghee utility card.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Combo Card on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Combo_Card</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Come to Daddy Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Come to Daddy Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for rejecting an exit deal at the start of the Tenth Floor. <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> does not get this achievement.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Come to Daddy Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Come_to_Daddy_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Commandant Kane</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Commandant Kane</b> is the leader of <a href="bword://Dirigible Gnome">Dirigible Gnome</a> faction in Bubble #543. <a href="bword://Father">Father</a> of <a href="bword://Bonnie">Bonnie</a>. Nephew of <a href="bword://Wynne">Wynne</a>. Holder of one third of the <a href="bword://Gate of the Feral Gods">Gate of the Feral Gods</a>.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Dirigible Gnome</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Commandant Kane on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Commandant_Kane</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Commander Stockade</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Commander Stockade</b> is the (former) leader of the <a href="bword://Lemig Sortion">Lemig Sortion</a> faction He got trapped in the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a> when <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> flooded the ninth floor.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Caterpillar like alien</li><li><b>First scene:</b> The Eye of the Bedlam Bride</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Commander Stockade on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Commander_Stockade</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Community Pool</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><i><b>Community Pool</b></i> is a powerful rare scroll that allows the caster to transfer an infection from Target A to Target B. The caster must be physically touching both targets for the spell to take effect, and will be stunned for one minute after the casting completes.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Community Pool on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Community_Pool</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Concierge Shark</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Concierge Sharks</b> are a mob found in water quadrants on the Fifth Floor, and in previous water-themed Dungeons. Concierge Sharks look like typical tiger sharks, but are 15' (4.572m) long, jet black, and have glowing red eyes. They are attracted to blood.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Concierge Shark on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Concierge_Shark</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Confusing Fog Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><i><b>Confusing Fog</b></i> is a spell that fills a space with thick, wet fog for a brief period of time (seconds equal to caster's Intelligence x 5). The billowing cloud of fog is initially opaque but immediately becomes translucent to the caster, crawlers, and white-tagged <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a>; however, mobs remain blinded for its duration. While the fog is active, water beads on the ground and every surface.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Confusing Fog Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Confusing_Fog_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Conrad E</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Conrad E</b> was a human Crawler from Earth who participated in the Dungeon. He was part of the large group of surviving crawlers who made a frantic dash toward the stairwell to escape the Third Floor before the level collapsed.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Russia</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2, Chapter 25</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Conrad E on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Conrad_E</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Conscription Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Conscription</b> is a powerful military charm used primarily during the Faction Wars to force unaffiliated crawlers, <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a>, and even deities to fight for a specific army.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Conscription Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Conscription_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Control Sigil</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>Control Sigil</b> is a Dungeon mechanic used by the show runners to program specific actions. To those who have the Escape Plan Skill, a Control Sigil looks like a glowing circle that "looks like something used in a Satanic ritual mixed with the text from Frodo's One Ring". To anyone else the sigil doesn't show up.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Control Sigil on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Control_Sigil</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Coolie</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Coolie</b> is a former Crawler and author of the <i><a href="bword://Dungeon Anarchist&#x27;s Cookbook">Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook</a> (19th Edition)</i>. Coolie was a popular crawler on <i> Dungeon Crawler World: Qurux</i>, and appeared on multiple <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> programs during their time in the Dungeon.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Qurux</li><li><b>Race:</b> Unknown</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Coolie on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Coolie</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Corcunda</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Corcunda</b> is a former male stripper in the Penis Parade of the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a> who was physically split into two halves that developed different personalities, Corky and <a href="bword://Porky">Porky</a>.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Half Mantuar</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Corcunda on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Corcunda</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Cornets</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Cornets</b> are a Fourth Floor mob that can be found at Banshee Station, station number 116 on the Yellow Line of the Iron Tangle Cornets look like tall, skinless, eyeless, human-sized jackrabbits walking on two legs. They are hunched forward with their rabbit ears almost reaching the ceiling. They have a massive mouth with teeth. They make an odd humming noise.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Cornets on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Cornets</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Corporal Pillbox</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Corporal Pillbox</b> is a gnoll mercenary who leads a squad of fellow gnolls in Empress D'Nadia's employ during the Ninth Floor Faction Wars, and survives the entire conflict on <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s side after his surrender.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Corporal Pillbox on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Corporal_Pillbox</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Cosmic Buff Potion</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Cosmic Buff Potions</b> are pink, frothy potions that immediately raise a random stat by 10 points. Shortly after arriving on the Eighth Floor, <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> each receive a single Cosmic Buff Potion in a Platinum <a href="bword://Here&#x27;s Some Good Shit Because You&#x27;re Gonna Need It Box">Here's Some Good Shit Because You're Gonna Need It Box</a> awarded for the <a href="bword://Fuck This Floor Achievement">Fuck This Floor Achievement</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Platinum Here's Some Good Shit Because You're Gonna Need It Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Cosmic Buff Potion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Cosmic_Buff_Potion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Crab Chowder Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Crab Chowder Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for actions taken on the Eighth Floor with <a href="bword://Raul the Crab">Raul the Crab</a> and <a href="bword://Alpha Male Carl">Alpha Male Carl</a>. Carl opens this achievement in a safe room on the Ninth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Crab Chowder Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Crab_Chowder_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Cracker Jack</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Cracker Jack</b> is a scroll that unlocks weapons or gear locked to someone else.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Cracker Jack on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Cracker_Jack</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Crafter</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Crafter</b> are They look similar to a soother, they are tall and thin with pale skin that's weathered and wrinkled and covered in veins. They have big bug like eyes, and a head covered in coarse hair and with two distinct humps similar to a hearts. They have a line of four red nipples on their chest.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Crafter on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Crafter</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Crafter's Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Crafter's Box</b> is a Loot Box given to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> when he uses the <a href="bword://Goo-Inator 3000">Goo-Inator 3000</a> on the <a href="bword://Engineer&#x27;s Table">Engineer's Table</a>, crafting for the first time. <b>Bronze Crafting Box</b></li><li><b>Source:</b> Martha Stewart Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Crafter's Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Crafter%27s_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Craftsman 3000 Series Rolling Tool Chest</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Craftsman 3000 Series Rolling Tool Chest</b> was <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s tool chest from before the collapse. He was offered it as a reward from the <a href="bword://Prize Carousel">Prize Carousel</a> and was tempted, but ultimately didn't take it because he suspected it was empty.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Prize Carousel</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Craftsman 3000 Series Rolling Tool Chest on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Craftsman_3000_Series_Rolling_Tool_Chest</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Crawler Biscuit</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Crawler Biscuits</b> are food items that may be received in Bronze and Silver Adventurer Boxes. Shortly after entering the First Floor, <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives (100) Crawler Biscuits in the Silver <a href="bword://Adventurer Box">Adventurer Box</a> awarded for the <a href="bword://Early Adopter Achievement">Early Adopter Achievement</a>. He receives more biscuits over the course of the First and Second Floors.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Adventurer Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Crawler Biscuit on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Crawler_Biscuit</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Crazy Cat Lady Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Crazy Cat Lady</b> is an achievement awarded to crawlers who enter the Dungeon with a feline companion. It is distinct and different from <a href="bword://Trailblazing Crazy Cat Lady Achievement">Trailblazing Crazy Cat Lady Achievement</a>, which is only awarded to the <i>first</i> crawler to enter the First Floor with a cat.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Crazy Cat Lady Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Crazy_Cat_Lady_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Crest</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Crest</b> are a humanoid race with no eyebrows.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Crest on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Crest</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Cretin</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Cretin</b> are a race of rock monsters typically employed by the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a> to provide personal security to crawlers. It is similar to the <a href="bword://Igneous">Igneous</a> race, but a different kind.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Cretin on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Cretin</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Crixus</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Crixus</b> is a <a href="bword://Dirigible Gnome">Dirigible Gnome</a> NPC and sniper encountered on the Fifth Floor of the Dungeon. He briefly acts as an informational guide to the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a> during their ascent in the Air Quadrant before abruptly turning hostile.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Dirigible Gnome</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 12</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Crixus on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Crixus</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Crocodilian</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Crocodilian</b> is a race a crawler can choose upon entry to the Third Floor. They look like humanoid crocodiles. <a href="bword://Florin">Florin</a> chooses this as his race.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Crocodilian on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Crocodilian</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Crowd Control Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Crowd Control Box</b> is a Loot Box distributed for dispatching multiple mobs in a single attack.</li><li><b>Source:</b> achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Crowd Control Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Crowd_Control_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Crupper of the Benevolent Champion</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Enchanted crupper. The Crupper of the Benevolent Champion.</b> This is a unique item. This item is part of a matched set with the <a href="bword://Cloak of the Benevolent Champion">Cloak of the Benevolent Champion</a>. There are two more pieces to this set. Find the third, and the fourth will be awarded in a box. Considering what you did to get this one, it’s gotta be something really good.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Crupper of the Benevolent Champion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Crupper_of_the_Benevolent_Champion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Crybaby Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Crybaby Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> on the Eighth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Crybaby Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Crybaby_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Cuck Aquaman Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Cuck Aquaman Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to all participants of the Fools Who Broke the Glass Quest (except <a href="bword://Quan Ch">Quan Ch</a>) for getting their <a href="bword://Celestial">Celestial</a> <a href="bword://Quest Box">Quest Box</a> vetoed by the <a href="bword://Borant Corporation">Borant Corporation</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Cuck Aquaman Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Cuck_Aquaman_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Curupira</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Curupira</b> is an exceptionally obscure race a crawler can choose upon entry to the Third Floor, famously selected by the top-ranking crawler <a href="bword://Osvaldo">Osvaldo</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Curupira on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Curupira</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Cut! Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>This is an achievement that <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> says she received for being a good actress when she tricked the Goblin Shamankas on the second floor. This achievement and having one trillion views are the two pre-requisites that allow Donut to select the Former Child Actor Class during class selection on the third floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Cut! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Cut%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>D'nadia</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>D'nadia</b> is a <a href="bword://Saccathian">Saccathian</a> and Princess of the <a href="bword://Prism Kingdom">Prism Kingdom</a>, a small Sac government in <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> space that carries outsized weight in certain trade circles. An outspoken fixture of the intergalactic talk show circuit and an enthusiastic fan of <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>, she became one of the <a href="bword://Skull Empire">Skull Empire</a>'s loudest critics after a botched assassination attempt on the crawlers killed her closest friend instead.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Princess D'nadia, Empress D'nadia</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Prism Kingdom</li><li><b>Race:</b> Saccathian</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2, Chapter 19</li></ul><p class="source">Source: D'nadia on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/D%27nadia</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Damascus Steel</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Damascus Steel</b> is a level 75 Ifrit NPC who works as the assistant lead dancer at the Penis Parade strip club within the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>. He is a member of the <a href="bword://Guild of Suffering">Guild of Suffering</a> and is registered as a mercenary at the Meat Shields market.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> The Dungeon (Desperado Club)</li><li><b>Race:</b> Ifrit</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 23</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Damascus Steel on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Damascus_Steel</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Damien</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Damien</b> is a Location Manager for <a href="bword://Borant Corporation">Borant Corporation</a> and meant to operate behind the scenes, out of crawlers' sights. <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> describes him as "my manager's manager."</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 33</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Damien on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Damien</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Danforth</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Danforth</b> is an bolt that can be fired from a crossbow.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Danforth on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Danforth</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Danger Dingo</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Danger Dingoes</b> are a canine mob on the Second Floor. Danger Dingoes are roughly the size of mastiffs (which typically stand 2' 6"+ tall and weigh 120-230 lbs), with absurdly long and sharp fangs that make them look "almost prehistoric." The fur on their faces looks like heavy metal corpse paint.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Danger Dingo on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Danger_Dingo</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dante</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Dante</b> is a former crawler and the author of the <i><a href="bword://Dungeon Anarchist&#x27;s Cookbook">Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook</a> (3rd Edition)</i>. Dante was born a <a href="bword://Crocodilian">Crocodilian</a> and chooses to remain that race during Third Floor Class selection.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Birth Race: CrocodilianDungeon Race: Crocodilian</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 7, Dante</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dante on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dante</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dark Hive</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Dark Hive</b> is a <a href="bword://Mantis">Mantis</a> group that regularly participates in the Sixth Floor Hunting Grounds. A few seasons ago, <a href="bword://Vrah">Vrah</a> killed a fellow hunter in a fight on the Sixth Floor (which is not covered by Protections). The Dark Hive insisted that the murder was legal because it took place on the Hunting Grounds. Now, other hunters avoid them where possible out of fear, and the Dark Hive takes advantage to poach other teams' kills.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dark Hive on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dark_Hive</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Darla No-Dentures</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Darla No-Dentures</b> is a hairy <a href="bword://Bugbear">Bugbear</a> and an NPC in <a href="bword://Borant Corporation">Borant Corporation</a>'s Dungeon. She wears a blonde wig and works as a stripper at the Bitches in the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Bugbear</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 33</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Darla No-Dentures on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Darla_No-Dentures</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>De-Sleeving Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>De-Sleeving Box</b> is a loot box awarded for achievements related to removing god sponsors from the gods they are piloting. <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> got an unnamed achievement for ejecting <a href="bword://Circe Took">Circe Took</a> from <a href="bword://Diwata">Diwata</a> using the <a href="bword://Laundry Day Spell">Laundry Day Spell</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Removing outworlder sponsors from the god they are piloting</li></ul><p class="source">Source: De-Sleeving Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/De-Sleeving_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Default Winner Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Default Winner Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for winning Faction Wars (game).</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Default Winner Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Default_Winner_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Deity's Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Deity's Box</b> is a Loot Box distributed for the <a href="bword://Indomitable Achievement">Indomitable Achievement</a> for being physically attacked by a god and surviving. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives this box after he was stepped on by <a href="bword://Grull">Grull</a> on the Fourth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Deity's Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Deity%27s_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dekoki</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Dekoki</b> is a Level 84 Kappa Seductress and singer, one of four members of Team Yokai racing during the Tenth Floor's heats. Dekoki is a Kappa, a turtle-shelled, water-bowl-headed creature normally vulnerable to having that water spilled, but she keeps hers sealed under a plastic wrap-like covering so she can perform without risk. She's an enthusiastic karaoke singer at a bar frequented by racers, performing pop covers like "Tell It to My Heart" by Taylor Dayne alongside her Team Yokai bandmates, including the <a href="bword://Minister of Blood-Letting">Minister of Blood-Letting</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dekoki on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dekoki</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Demolition Workshop Tab</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Demolition Workshop Tab</b> is a tab in a Crawler's Heads-Up Display (HUD). The tab is specifically related to explosives and explosives handling.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Demolition Workshop Tab on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Demolition_Workshop_Tab</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Demons</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>In the Dungeon, <b>Demons</b> are a broad category of mobs and races closely tied to the lore of the "volcano levels." Demons generally inhabit Sheol on the Dungeon's Fifteenth Floor, where a matriarchal hierarchy of demons fight each other for control and the attention of one of the four brothers.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Demons on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Demons</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Demons Hate This One Trick Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Demons Hate This One Trick Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> on the Eighth Floor for teleporting <a href="bword://Samantha">Samantha</a> using his <a href="bword://Xistera">Xistera</a>, accidentally freeing <a href="bword://Demons">Demons</a> from their shell.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Demons Hate This One Trick Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Demons_Hate_This_One_Trick_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Deng Bao</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Judge Deng Bao</b> is an old, experienced grixist adjutant who traditionally serves the warlord of the previous season's winning team, and who sits on one of the highest courts in the galaxy outside the dungeon.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Deng Bao on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Deng_Bao</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Denise</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Denise</b> is a feral goose. Magic items do not work in her presence and she cannot be harmed by magical or physical damage, unless it is from items that originated from within the house.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> feral goose.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Denise on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Denise</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Desecrated Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Desecrated Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> when he falls into the Temple of <a href="bword://Diwata">Diwata</a> on the Sixth Floor. <a href="bword://Lucia Mar">Lucia Mar</a> previously killed everyone inside and caused the temple to become Desecrated. Because he landed on the altar, he also receives the <a href="bword://Temple Defiler Achievement">Temple Defiler Achievement</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Desecrated Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Desecrated_Achievement</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Desperado Club</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Desperado Club</b> is a massive, multi-level nightclub and entertainment complex found throughout the urban floors of the Dungeon. It is one of two Dungeon-based clubs that crawlers can gain membership to; the types of people with access to the Desperado Club and the more exclusive <a href="bword://Club Vanquisher">Club Vanquisher</a> are mutually exclusive, and obtaining a Desperado Pass automatically negates a crawler's ability to earn a Vanquisher pass. A members-only hub for crawlers and <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a> alike, it offers dancing, gambling, drinking, shopping, and access to a variety of rogue-themed guilds.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Desperado Club on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Desperado_Club</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Desperado Pass Tattoo</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Desperado Pass</b> is a tattoo that grants crawlers access to the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>, and may be received in an <a href="bword://Asshole&#x27;s Box">Asshole's Box</a> and/or after a crawler earns their first Player-Killer Skull. The tattoo burns as it is applied to the crawler's neck (or, if a cat, above the right shoulder blade), and looks like a dagger dripping blood.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Asshole's Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Desperado Pass Tattoo on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Desperado_Pass_Tattoo</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Desperado Club</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Desperado Club</b> is a massive, multi-level nightclub and entertainment complex found throughout the urban floors of the Dungeon. It is one of two Dungeon-based clubs that crawlers can gain membership to; the types of people with access to the Desperado Club and the more exclusive <a href="bword://Club Vanquisher">Club Vanquisher</a> are mutually exclusive, and obtaining a Desperado Pass automatically negates a crawler's ability to earn a Vanquisher pass. A members-only hub for crawlers and <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a> alike, it offers dancing, gambling, drinking, shopping, and access to a variety of rogue-themed guilds.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Desperado Club on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Desperado_Club</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Desperado Pass Tattoo</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Desperado Pass</b> is a tattoo that grants crawlers access to the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>, and may be received in an <a href="bword://Asshole&#x27;s Box">Asshole's Box</a> and/or after a crawler earns their first Player-Killer Skull. The tattoo burns as it is applied to the crawler's neck (or, if a cat, above the right shoulder blade), and looks like a dagger dripping blood.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Asshole's Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Desperado Pass Tattoo on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Desperado_Pass_Tattoo</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dick</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Dick</b> is <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s former boss in the coast guard, before that was an EDO for the navy. He became afraid of water after a scuba diving incident.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dick on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dick</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dictum Waystation Controls, Limited</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Dictum Waystation Controls, Ltd</b> is a <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> Corporation that regularly sponsors bidding during Special Events and occasionally sponsors crawlers.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dictum Waystation Controls, Limited on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dictum_Waystation_Controls%2C_Limited</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Did You Really Just Cast Fireball in a Room this Small Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>Did-You-Really-Just-Cast-Fireball-in-a-Room-This-Small Box</b> is a loot box awarded under very specific circumstances. <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> receives this box after she casts Fireball at <a href="bword://Lucia Mar">Lucia Mar</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Did You Really Just Cast Fireball in a Room this Small Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Did_You_Really_Just_Cast_Fireball_in_a_Room_this_Small_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dirigible Gnome</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Dirigible Gnome</b> are a race of <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a> and combatants on the Fifth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dirigible Gnome on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dirigible_Gnome</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dirty Little Phased Bolt</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Dirty Little Phased Bolts</b> are magical crossbow bolts that reduce the target's health to just shy of 0%, as well induce amnesia and health-sapping Bleed effects. The debuffs do not show over the target's head and cannot be seen in the Party Menu. The crawler who fired the bolts will not receive experience if the target dies, <i>but</i> will not receive a Player Killer Skull if the target was another crawler.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dirty Little Phased Bolt on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dirty_Little_Phased_Bolt</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dirty Shirley</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Dirty Shirley</b> is a drink made of Vodka, Grenedine, and lemon lime soda. It is frequently topped with cherries. In most <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a> visits, <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> drinks a non-alcoholic Dirty Shirley out of a bowl. Donut enjoys Dirty Shirleys because of <a href="bword://Beatrice">Beatrice</a>'s liking for them.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Desperado Club</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dirty Shirley on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dirty_Shirley</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Disarming Personality Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Disarming Personality Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for ripping off <a href="bword://Quan Ch">Quan Ch</a>'s arm at the end of the Fifth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Disarming Personality Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Disarming_Personality_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dismember</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>On the Fourth Floor, <b>Dismember</b> is the <a href="bword://War Mage">War Mage</a> aboard the <i>Dismembered Unlimited</i>. Dismember appears to be an elf with long, silver hair. He specializes in necromancy magic.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon: Fourth Floor</li><li><b>Race:</b> Elf</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 12</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dismember on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dismember</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dismemberment Limited</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <i><b>Dismemberment Limited</b></i> is a named train on the Fourth Floor Iron Tangle. The <i>Dismemberment Limited</i> is a sleek, white maglev train that moves almost silently on a monorail line. The first car is aerodynamic and sleek with a fully glass nose (similar to a B-17 chin turret), and pulls only two cars behind it. The train can only be entered and exited from the first car.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Fourth Floor</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dismemberment Limited on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dismemberment_Limited</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dispenser</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 2.</p><ul class="definition"><li><i>The Dispenser'</i> was a Neighborhood Boss located outside the Medium <a href="bword://Skyfowl">Skyfowl</a> Settlement on the Third Floor. The Dispenser looks like a giant manta ray that can blend into the background buildings. It is large enough to cover almost the entire building.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> The Dungeon</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dispenser on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dispenser</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Disrupter Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Disrupter</b> is a powerful, rare, short range spell. Similar to <i><a href="bword://Magic Missile">Magic Missile</a></i>, <i>Disrupter</i> takes the form of an energy bolt and is ideally suited for "blowing holes in things." It inflicts splash damage and has a stun effect.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Disrupter Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Disrupter_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Divider</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 2.</p><ul class="definition"><li><i>The Divider</i> was a Neighborhood Boss located outside the Medium <a href="bword://Skyfowl">Skyfowl</a> Settlement on the Third Floor. It was killed by <a href="bword://Bautista">Bautista</a>. The Divider looks like a two headed sea monster, with a body of a whale and two long heads like the Loch Ness monster. When <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> come across the corpse, it has multiple holes in the the size of manhole covers. The decaying corpse is bloated.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> The Dungeon</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Divider on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Divider</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Divine Epiphany Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Divine Epiphany Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> (and presumably all crawlers who fought <a href="bword://Grull">Grull</a>). Carl opens this box in a safe room on the Fifth Floor</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Divine Epiphany Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Divine_Epiphany_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Diwata</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Diwata</b> is a minor, shapeshifting nature goddess of the Dungeon's pantheon, worshipped by some Dryads. She became hostile to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> after he destroyed her shrine on the Sixth Floor, and was later sponsored into the Dungeon by <a href="bword://Circe Took">Circe Took</a>, mother of the Hunter <a href="bword://Vrah">Vrah</a>.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Deity</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 5, Chapter 35</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Diwata on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Diwata</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dmitri Popov</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Dmitri Popov</b> is a Crawler from Earth. Dmitri Popov, along with his fraternal twin brother Maxim, is a Crawler originating from Bulgaria. When selecting their race on the Third Floor, Dmitri chose the <a href="bword://Nodling">Nodling</a> race under the advice of his game guide, Hongrish. Hongrish advised him that the Nodling race would provide an "extra life" if he died, but deceitfully omitted the fact that choosing this race would force Dmitri and his brother to inhabit and share a single, two-headed body.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth (Bulgaria)</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human (formerly), Nodling, Nodling Yearling</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 5, Chapter 8</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dmitri Popov on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dmitri_Popov</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Doctor Bones</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Doctor Bones</b> is a skeletal NPC who originally works as the announcer and DJ for the Penis Parade at the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>, and later operates as a mercenary allied with <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and his forces.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Dr. Bones</li><li><b>Origin:</b> The Dungeon (Desperado Club)</li><li><b>Race:</b> Skin Skellie</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 23</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Doctor Bones on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Doctor_Bones</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dodola</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Dodola</b> is a god normally sponsored by <a href="bword://Huanxin Jinx">Huanxin Jinx</a>.</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Prologue</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dodola on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dodola</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dog Soldier</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3,4,5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Dog Soldier</b> is the race chosen by <a href="bword://Tserendolgor">Tserendolgor</a> ("Ren") on the Third Floor, the only crawler known to have taken it. A Dog Soldier is a bipedal, humanoid German Shepherd, complete with furry dog breasts. Tserendolgor pairs the race with the Crisper Class and her signature enchanted flamethrower, "Velma," which doubles as part of her shirt. She wears a small heart locket with a dog paw print and a Vietnam-era helmet with holes cut for her ears.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dog Soldier on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dog_Soldier</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Doggie Door</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Doggie Door</b> is a Tier-3 Personal Space Upgrade that allows crawlers to fast-travel to any door they have previously used on the floor, or to the location of other party members.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Doggie Door on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Doggie_Door</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dolores Doesn't Splat Potion</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Dolores Doesn't Splat</b> is a potion that can be used to add extra power to an Earthquake Skill or to survive falling a long distance. The potion only works if consumed while falling at a speed of 124.27mph (200km) or more.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dolores Doesn't Splat Potion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dolores_Doesn%27t_Splat_Potion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dong Quixote</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Dong Quixote</b> is an elderly human NPC who originally worked as an exotic dancer at the Penis Parade strip club. He is eventually hired as a mercenary for <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a>, becoming a loyal and valiantly heroic member of their fighting force.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> The Dungeon (Desperado Club)</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 23</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dong Quixote on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dong_Quixote</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Donita Grace</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Donita Grace</b> is an Earth crawler <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> adds to his chat in the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a> on the Fourth Floor. During Carl and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s second visit to the Desperado Club on the Fourth Floor, Carl trades fist bumps with a couple crawlers to get into each other's chat. Carl starts explaining the subway system to her, and gets frustrated when Donita doesn't agree with the color system. He stops chatting with her after that.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 14, Book 3</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Donita Grace on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Donita_Grace</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Donut</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Grand Champion, Breed Winner Regional, National Winner Princess Donut the Queen Anne Chonk</b> is the deuteragonist of <i>Dungeon Crawler <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a></i>. A tortoiseshell Persian cat, she is the party leader of the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a> and a fan favorite crawler on <i>Dungeon Crawler World: Earth</i>.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> GC, BWR, NW Princess Donut the Queen Anne Chonk</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Seattle, WA</li><li><b>Race:</b> Persian Cat</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 1</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Donut on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Donut</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Donut Holes</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Donut Holes</b> is an unofficial fan club for Princess <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>. Donut refuses to acknowledge them, instead preferring the <a href="bword://Princess Posse Fan Club">Princess Posse Fan Club</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Donut Holes on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Donut_Holes</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Doppelgänger</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Doppelgänger</b> is a race a crawler can choose upon entry to the Third Floor. It is a race of shape shifters, similar to Changelings, but they can shape their body mass into any shape or race. They do not gain the properties of the new race, but can retain the properties of whatever their body mass is made of.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Doppelgänger on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Doppelg%C3%A4nger</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dorota</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Dorota</b> is a sentient novelty car seat that becomes Princess <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s personal chair in the racing truck on the Tenth Floor, and the constant rival of the truck's GPS unit, <a href="bword://Dr. Metcalf">Dr. Metcalf</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dorota on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dorota</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Double-Billed Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Double-Billed Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for participating in the drama Vengeance of the Daughter during The Hunting Grounds while on Dungeon Crawler World as part of a deal he made on the third floor with the producers.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Double-Billed Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Double-Billed_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dr. Metcalf</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Dr. Metcalf</b> is the GPS in the car that <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> drive on the Tenth Floor.</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 8, Chapter 3</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dr. Metcalf on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dr._Metcalf</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dr. Ratchet's Automaton Build-It Kit</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Doctor Ratchet's Automaton Build-It Kit</b> is a large, steampunk-y chest hissing with clockwork gears. It contains dozens of automaton parts. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives the Build-It Kit in a Legendary Hunter Champion/Scourge Box, which he receives for killing the most hunters on the Sixth Floor Hunting Grounds.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Legendary Hunter Champion Box / Scourge Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dr. Ratchet's Automaton Build-It Kit on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dr._Ratchet%27s_Automaton_Build-It_Kit</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dr. Ratchet's Guide to Building Automatons for Fun and Profit</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>A book on creating automatons, features a dwarf riding on the back of a mechanical horse on the cover. Autographed.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dr. Ratchet's Guide to Building Automatons for Fun and Profit on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dr._Ratchet%27s_Guide_to_Building_Automatons_for_Fun_and_Profit</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dragon Chain Tattoo</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Dragon Chain Tattoo</b> is a permanent tattoo on <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s right forearm that temporarily grants him <a href="bword://Li Na">Li Na</a>'s level-13 Profane Iron skill. The Dragon Chain Tattoo was created using a mixture of toraline yam ink and Li Na's freely-given blood. Because the blood was given willingly, Li Na did not permanently lose her skill, but Carl gained the temporary ability to use it. The tattoo grants Carl access to Li Na's level-13 Profane Iron skill, which allows him to unleash multiple prehensile chains from his body once a day for about thirty seconds.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Crafted by Katia Grim</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dragon Chain Tattoo on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dragon_Chain_Tattoo</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Drakea</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Drakea</b> was a former Crawler and author of the <i><a href="bword://Dungeon Anarchist&#x27;s Cookbook">Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook</a> (22nd Edition)</i>. Drakea participated in the last <a href="bword://Naga">Naga</a>-produced season of <i>Dungeon Crawler World</i> over 250 cycles ago. Born a <a href="bword://Bune">Bune</a>, he kept his race on the Third Floor and chose a rogue/magic class similar to the Compensated Anarchist Class. He built elaborate traps using magical items and magical triggers, and chose a sixth floor subclass that allowed him to experiment with hidden traps.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Bune</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3,</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Drakea on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Drakea</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Drakea's Enchanted Kerchief of Disorder</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>Named for the famous trap-loving crawler, <a href="bword://Drakea">Drakea</a>, the Kerchief is a black bandana with a typical white paisley pattern. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives the Enchanted Kerchief of Disorder in a Gold <a href="bword://Boss Box">Boss Box</a> after defeating <a href="bword://Lusca">Lusca</a> on the Fifth Floor. Because his <a href="bword://Enchanted Nightgaunt Cloak of Stoutness">Enchanted Nightgaunt Cloak of Stoutness</a> uses his neck slot, he equips the bandana as a mask.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Gold Boss Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Drakea's Enchanted Kerchief of Disorder on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Drakea%27s_Enchanted_Kerchief_of_Disorder</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dreadnought</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>Large humanoid creatures with red skin, they rarely did well in faction wars because their preferred method of fighting was to just hit everything in front of them.‏‎</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dreadnought on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dreadnought</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dreadnoughts</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>Large humanoid creatures with red skin, they rarely did well in faction wars because their preferred method of fighting was to just hit everything in front of them.‏‎</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dreadnoughts on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dreadnoughts</p></div></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dreadnoughts</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>Large humanoid creatures with red skin, they rarely did well in faction wars because their preferred method of fighting was to just hit everything in front of them.‏‎</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dreadnoughts on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dreadnoughts</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dreadnought</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>Large humanoid creatures with red skin, they rarely did well in faction wars because their preferred method of fighting was to just hit everything in front of them.‏‎</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dreadnought on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dreadnought</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dream</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Dream</b> is a powerful, galaxy-spanning faction and mega-corporation primarily composed of elves. They are one of the dominant legacy teams that participate in the ninth-floor Faction Wars.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dream on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dream</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Drek</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Drek</b> are mobs that appear on the Fourth Floor. They attack the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a> at the start of the Fourth Floor. A knee-high, fat, wrinkly monster with sharp claws and teeth. They stand on two feet but can climb on all fours. They wear loincloths and cry like babies.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Drek on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Drek</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Drick</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Drick</b> is a former crawler and member of The <a href="bword://Dream">Dream</a>, but now with a <a href="bword://Valtay Corporation">Valtay Corporation</a> with a <a href="bword://Gondii">Gondii</a> worm in his brain. He is old and scarred, but still heavily muscled. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> meets him on the panel Crawling Through the Ages at CrawlCon!</li><li><b>Race:</b> Iguanoid | Moon Elf | Gondii</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 33, Book 5</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Drick on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Drick</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dromedarian</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Dromedarian</b> are a camel-like race on the Fifth Floor. The Dromedarians are a common, formerly nomadic race that is found throughout the drier parts of the universe. With the ability to store mass amounts of liquid in their bodies, it is said a Dromedarian can survive up to two months without taking a single sip of water. When these hunters and warriors are placed in a situation where they can no longer wander, they tend to become lethargic, sloth-minded creatures. But make no mistake, this is a mighty race of warriors who were once known for their abject brutality.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dromedarian on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dromedarian</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Drop Shield</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>Drop Shield</b> is a disposable defensive item that projects a stationary protective barrier, available for purchase at the Prize Counter during the Butcher's Masquerade Ball on the Sixth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Drop Shield on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Drop_Shield</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><i>This article is about the item. For the book, see Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook (Book).</i> <b>The Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook</b> is a Unique, Heirloom book item that has passed in secret from one Crawler to the next since it was first generated into the system in the fifteenth season of <i>Dungeon Crawler World</i>. Disguised as a humble recipe book, it is in truth a covert archive of survival knowledge, recipes, strategies, exploits, and warnings left by previous crawlers, and the founding artifact of the crawlers known as Anarchists.</li><li><b>Source:</b> The Prize Carousel</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dungeon_Anarchist%27s_Cookbook_%28Item%29</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dungeon Book of the Floor Club</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Dungeon Book of the Floor Club</b> is a Dungeon Benefit which delivers one new Tome to members on each floor. Crawlers may gain "membership" to the Dungeon Book of the Floor Club from Silver Boss Boxes.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> spellbook-of-the-floor club</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dungeon Book of the Floor Club on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dungeon_Book_of_the_Floor_Club</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dungeon Codex</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <i><b>Dungeon Codex</b></i> appears to be a full, detailed inventory of the Dungeon's mobs (including spawn rates), bosses, items, and spells. Dungeon Administrators and Game Guides can access the codex using their Heads-Up Display (HUD), but <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> laws restrict how much information production company personnel can share with active crawlers.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Work for the Production Company</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dungeon Codex on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dungeon_Codex</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dungeon Gold Rush</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Dungeon Gold Rush</b> is a lottery ticket given to <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> on the Second Floor for the <a href="bword://Like a Moth to the Flame Achievement">Like a Moth to the Flame Achievement</a> in a Platinum <a href="bword://Lucky Bastard Box">Lucky Bastard Box</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Platinum Lucky Bastard Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dungeon Gold Rush on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dungeon_Gold_Rush</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dungeon Mailbox</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>mailbox</b> is a recurring fixture found in saferooms and personal spaces throughout the dungeon, used by the system to deliver recurring and one-off item rewards directly to individual crawlers rather than through the normal loot box process.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dungeon Mailbox on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dungeon_Mailbox</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dungeonpreneur Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Dungeonpreneur</b> is an achievement granted the first time a crawler develops a weapon, device, or potion that can stack up to (999) in inventory.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dungeonpreneur Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dungeonpreneur_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dwarf</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Dwarf</b> are a humanoid race. Several <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a> in the Dungeon are dwarves. Dwarves also have a history of manufacturing items, particularly Automatons. Automatons are known for running a long time before needing a new battery, and are much more efficient than <a href="bword://Soul Crystals">Soul Crystals</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dwarf on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dwarf</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dwarven Battery Fabricator</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Dwarven Battery Fabricator</b> is a crafting item that allows crawlers to produce and charge Dwarven Batteries. The batteries are about the size and shape of bricks. Automatons are known for running a long time before needing a new battery, and are much more efficient than <a href="bword://Soul Crystals">Soul Crystals</a>. The fabricator is about the size of a microwave.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Limp Richard's General Store</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dwarven Battery Fabricator on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dwarven_Battery_Fabricator</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dwarven Industrial Light-Duty Automaton Contraption</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Dwarven Industrial Light-Duty Automaton Contraption</b> is an automaton on the Iron Tangle. They are used to help the monsters get from the Exit-only cavern back to the first stop.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dwarven Industrial Light-Duty Automaton Contraption on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dwarven_Industrial_Light-Duty_Automaton_Contraption</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Dwight</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Dwight. Sparkling Unicorn. Level 87 Enchanter.</b> One of two members of Team Sparkles. “I bet you already know what a unicorn is. A sparkling unicorn is pretty much the same thing, but they sparkle because they have even more magic permeating them. Their horns are quite valuable to certain parties, so if you kill him, it’s recommended to grab the horn as quickly as possible. Most unicorns are regarded for their beauty and their grace and their childlike innocence. They’re generally known for their overly gentle manner. But not Dwight. Dwight is known for being a complete prick.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Sparkling Unicorn</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 8, Chapter 5</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Dwight on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Dwight</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Goblin Dynamite</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Goblin Dynamite</b> is an extremely volatile explosive created by <a href="bword://Goblins">Goblins</a>. The red stick is wet and sticky, and the long wick hisses and pops like a sparkler when lit. The wick must be physically lit using a lighter or mechanism.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Goblins, Goblin Box, Hobgobs and Boom Sticks</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Goblin Dynamite on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Goblin_Dynamite</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hobgoblin Dynamite</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Hobgoblin Dynamite</b> is an explosive Item that <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> occasionally recieves in loot boxes. It is very similar to <a href="bword://Goblin Dynamite">Goblin Dynamite</a>, but has a larger yield and is more stable.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Hobgoblins, Hobgobs and Boom Sticks</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hobgoblin Dynamite on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hobgoblin_Dynamite</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Early Adopter Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Early Adopter</b> is an achievement awarded to each of the first 5,000 crawlers to enter the Dungeon. The third achievement <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives upon entering the Dungeon, which was likely distributed to <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> as well. Carl and Donut (crawlers #4,122 and 4,119, respectively) enter the First Floor 12 minutes after the surface-level stairwells appear.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Early Adopter Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Early_Adopter_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Early Bird Gets to Squirm Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Early Bird Gets to Squirm!</b> achievement is given to Crawlers who descend the stairs when there are more than six hours remaining on the level timer.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Early Bird Gets to Squirm Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Early_Bird_Gets_to_Squirm_Achievement</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Earth Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Earth Box</b> is a Loot Box given to Crawlers who choose an Earth Class on the Third Floor.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Earth Class</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Earth Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Earth_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Earth Upgrade Patch</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Earth Upgrade Patch</b> is an <a href="bword://Upgrade Patch">Upgrade Patch</a> given to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> on the Fifth Floor in a Platinum <a href="bword://Spicy Box">Spicy Box</a> rewarded to him for the <a href="bword://Soft Vore Achievement">Soft Vore Achievement</a>. This patch is applied to the <a href="bword://Enchanted Anarchist&#x27;s Battle Rattle">Enchanted Anarchist's Battle Rattle</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Platinum Spicy Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Earth Upgrade Patch on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Earth_Upgrade_Patch</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Earth Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Earth Box</b> is a Loot Box given to Crawlers who choose an Earth Class on the Third Floor.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Earth Class</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Earth Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Earth_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Earth Hobby Potion</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>Everyone who chose an Earth Class got a Silver <a href="bword://Earth Box">Earth Box</a> with three items including an Earth Hobby Potion. <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> got the Scutelliphily Skill, <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> got Cesta Punta Skill as his hobby and Katia became a Gearhead.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Subsection 1256-C of the Indigenous Species Protection Act</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Earth Hobby Potion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Earth_Hobby_Potion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Earth Upgrade Patch</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Earth Upgrade Patch</b> is an <a href="bword://Upgrade Patch">Upgrade Patch</a> given to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> on the Fifth Floor in a Platinum <a href="bword://Spicy Box">Spicy Box</a> rewarded to him for the <a href="bword://Soft Vore Achievement">Soft Vore Achievement</a>. This patch is applied to the <a href="bword://Enchanted Anarchist&#x27;s Battle Rattle">Enchanted Anarchist's Battle Rattle</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Platinum Spicy Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Earth Upgrade Patch on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Earth_Upgrade_Patch</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Edgar</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>Edgar looks like a regular, giant tortoise, but he talks and comes with a diverse skillset, mainly used for reconnaissance and support. Level 15 Sense Movement</li><li><b>Race:</b> Tortoise</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 5, Chapter 25</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Edgar on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Edgar</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Edict</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Edict</b> is the last male <a href="bword://Mantis">Mantis</a> left in The Hunting Grounds, he attacks <a href="bword://Bomo">Bomo</a> and <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> in the saferoom in order to be teleported to a group of mobs that he knows will kill him.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Mantis</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Edict on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Edict</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Eileithyia</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Eileithyia</b> is a deity that is a god of Childbirth and Female Pain. During <i>Dungeon Crawler World: Earth</i> the goddess is sponsored by <a href="bword://Huanxin Jinx">Huanxin Jinx</a>.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Huanxin Jinx (Sponsor)</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Twelfth Floor</li><li><b>Race:</b> God</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Eileithyia on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Eileithyia</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Elf</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Elves</b> are a long-lived, pointed-eared humanoid race, and one of the largest and most fractured families of peoples in the Dungeon and the wider <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a>. They are strongly inclined toward magic and readily interfertile with other species, and several elven varieties appear among the races offered to Crawlers at selection.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Elf on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Elf</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Elle McGibbons</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Elle McGibbons</b> is an elderly Crawler from Earth and one of the <a href="bword://Meadow Lark">Meadow Lark</a> Adult Care Community residents shepherded through the Dungeon by <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>, <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>, and the Meadow Lark staff on the first and second floors. A ninety-nine-year-old widow whose memories often circle back to her late husband, <a href="bword://Barry">Barry</a>, she travels with the survivors as part of Team Meadow Lark.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Mrs. McGibbons; Elle McGib</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Wenatchee, Washington, Earth</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Frost Maiden</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 31</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Elle McGibbons on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Elle_McGibbons</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Elmer</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Elmer</b> is an <a href="bword://Ursine">Ursine</a> NPC on the Sixth Floor.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Ursine</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 5, Chapter 10</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Elmer on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Elmer</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Emberus</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Emberus</b> is a Deity, specifically the God of Sun and Ash, known for his unmitigated cruelty and his intense grief over the murder of his son, <a href="bword://Geyrun">Geyrun</a>. He becomes <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s patron deity during the events of the Fifth Floor, setting off a chaotic relationship defined by powerful boons, demanding tithes, and constant threats of fiery retribution.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Celestial Ascendency</li><li><b>Race:</b> Deity</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 28</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Emberus on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Emberus</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Emberus High Temple of the Ending Sun</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Emberus High Temple of the Ending Sun</b> is the secret church of <a href="bword://Emberus">Emberus</a>, restricted to all but his most devout followers and only accessible through a portal inside <a href="bword://Club Vanquisher">Club Vanquisher</a>. <a href="bword://Pater Coal">Pater Coal</a> is the High Cleric Supreme.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Emberus High Temple of the Ending Sun</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Emberus High Temple of the Ending Sun on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Emberus_High_Temple_of_the_Ending_Sun</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Emberus Tattoos</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>When a crawler worships <a href="bword://Emberus">Emberus</a>, they gain a round tribal-style tattoo on the back of each hand. Both tattoos are black with an orange glow, feel warm and vaguely uncomfortable, and depict the sun. On the right hand, the sun's rays are curled; on the left hand, the sun's rays are little triangles.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Emberus</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Emberus Tattoos on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Emberus_Tattoos</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Emerald</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Emerald</b> is a level-30 NPC on the Fifth Floor of the World Dungeon. She is a <a href="bword://Changeling">Changeling</a> who initially disguises herself as a female <a href="bword://Dromedarian">Dromedarian</a> camel.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> The World Dungeon (NPC)</li><li><b>Race:</b> Changeling (posing as a Dromedarian / Camel)</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 7</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Emerald on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Emerald</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Emir Akbas</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Emir Akbas</b> is an Earth Crawler that <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> meets in the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>. His class is <a href="bword://Ghazi">Ghazi</a> and his race is <a href="bword://Zebani">Zebani</a> though Carl has no idea what either of these are.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Zebani</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 32, Book 6</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Emir Akbas on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Emir_Akbas</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Empty Pockets Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Empty Pockets</b> is the fourth achievement that <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives upon entering the Dungeon. Presumably, any similarly unprepared crawlers would receive the same achievement after stepping into the First Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Empty Pockets Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Empty_Pockets_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Anarchist's Battle Rattle</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Enchanted Anarchist's Battle Rattle</b> is a sleeveless jacket that can be modified with Upgrade Patches. It does not protect against the cold.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Platinum Spicy Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Anarchist's Battle Rattle on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Anarchist%27s_Battle_Rattle</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Anklet of the Fallen Oak</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Enchanted Anklet of the Fallen Oak</b> is a bracelet found by <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> on the Third Floor from the corpse of <a href="bword://Grace Bautista 3">Grace Bautista 3</a>. The anklet is made of wood with three little beads attached to it. The beads make a quiet noise when shook, similar to seed pods.</li><li><b>Source:</b> looted from Grace Bautista 3's corpse</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Anklet of the Fallen Oak on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Anklet_of_the_Fallen_Oak</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Auto Buckler of the Peach Pit</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Enchanted Auto Buckler of the Peach Pit</b> is an arm bracer that can turn into a shield with a flick of the wrist. <a href="bword://Katia Grim">Katia Grim</a> gets this item in one of her <a href="bword://Loot Boxes">Loot Boxes</a> at the start of the Fourth Floor. She gives the shield to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> when she received the <a href="bword://Enchanted Shade Gnoll Riot Forces Crowd Control Shield">Enchanted Shade Gnoll Riot Forces Crowd Control Shield</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Loot Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Auto Buckler of the Peach Pit on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Auto_Buckler_of_the_Peach_Pit</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted BigBoi Boxers</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Enchanted BigBoi Boxers</b> look like white boxers covered in little red hearts, and are a Dungeon item specifically designed for size-altering races, were-creatures, the BigBoi... and <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Bronze Boss Box for killing the Krakaren Clone (Second Floor)</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted BigBoi Boxers on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_BigBoi_Boxers</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Collar Charm of the Effete Bourgeoisie</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Enchanted Collar Charm of the Effete Bourgeoisie</b> is a magic collar charm <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> recieve after becoming mayor of Point <a href="bword://Mongo">Mongo</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Recieve after becoming mayor of Point Mongo</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Collar Charm of the Effete Bourgeoisie on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Collar_Charm_of_the_Effete_Bourgeoisie</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Crown of the Sepsis Whore</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Enchanted Crown of the Sepsis Whore</b> is a tiara glittering with dark smokey gems. At its center is a deep purple stone that appears to be swirling with clouds, as though made of liquid.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Quadruped Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Crown of the Sepsis Whore on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Crown_of_the_Sepsis_Whore</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Fae Scale Quadruped Crupper of the Fleet</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Enchanted Fae Scale Quadruped Crupper of the Fleet</b> is a piece of silver, skirt-like armor that covers the rear half of a quadruped's body (but not their stomach), with a special slot for the tail, and hangs about halfway to the floor. It boosts the wearer's Dexterity, but jingles a little when the wearer moves and "poofs" out like a skirt when they fall.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Loot Boxes</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Fae Scale Quadruped Crupper of the Fleet on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Fae_Scale_Quadruped_Crupper_of_the_Fleet</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Fang Caps of the Expectorating Tizheruk</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 2.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Enchanted Fang Caps of the Expectorating Tizheruk</b> is a fleeting item that can be placed on the teeth of either a crawler or pet to increase their biting damage. They are gold in color and little tendrils of electricity spark when the teeth are snapped. They are currently worn by <a href="bword://Mongo">Mongo</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Platinum Quest Box from the Show Must Go On Quest</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Fang Caps of the Expectorating Tizheruk on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Fang_Caps_of_the_Expectorating_Tizheruk</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mongo's Teeth Caps</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 2.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b><a href="bword://Enchanted Fang Caps of the Expectorating Tizheruk">Enchanted Fang Caps of the Expectorating Tizheruk</a></b> is a fleeting item that can be placed on the teeth of either a crawler or pet to increase their biting damage. They are gold in color and little tendrils of electricity spark when the teeth are snapped. They are currently worn by <a href="bword://Mongo">Mongo</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Platinum Quest Box from the Show Must Go On Quest</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mongo's Teeth Caps on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mongo%27s_Teeth_Caps</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Fur Brush of the Ecclesiastic</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Enchanted Fur Brush of the Ecclesiastic</b> imparts a daily buff on furred creatures. If someone else uses this item to brush the target's fur for ten (10) minutes straight, the target gains +2 Constitution for the next 30-hour day.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Bronze Boss Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Fur Brush of the Ecclesiastic on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Fur_Brush_of_the_Ecclesiastic</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Gnome Farseer</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Enchanted Gnome Farseer</b> is a telescope developed by the Dirigible Gnomes on the Fifth Floor. The large, heavy telescope appears to be a white tube made of a ceramic-like material, covered in pipes and gears, and has a clamp on the bottom to attach to a table or the gunwhale of a boat or airship. A "turny thingy" on the right side allows the user to zoom in and out, and the resulting image is magically rendered accurately and clearly, even in low light.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Skarn</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Gnome Farseer on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Gnome_Farseer</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Hairbrush of the Beefmaster</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives the <b>Enchanted Hairbrush of the Beefmaster</b> in a <a href="bword://Celestial">Celestial</a> Who Let the <a href="bword://Gods">Gods</a> Out This Time Box for the <a href="bword://Celestial Orgy of Chaos Achievement">Celestial Orgy of Chaos Achievement</a> on the Ninth Floor.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Who Let the Gods Out This Time Box; Celestial Orgy of Chaos Achievement.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Hairbrush of the Beefmaster on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Hairbrush_of_the_Beefmaster</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Hammer of Fast Forward</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>A magical hammer. It has the number seven etched into the head and handle. Borant filed a dangerous appeal to keep the gift from arriving, the appeal was immediately denied.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Benefactor Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Hammer of Fast Forward on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Hammer_of_Fast_Forward</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Handcuffs</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Enchanted Handcuffs</b> is an item on the Fifth Floor The handcuffs are covered in fuzzy red velvet.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Handcuffs on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Handcuffs</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Juvenile Macropus Dominus Skin</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Enchanted Juvenile Macropus Dominus Skin.</b> This item fills a costume slot. This can be worn as an outer garment. You might want to protect your face, though. I’d fuck me. I’d fuck me so hard, mate. Equipping this costume imbues the following effects: Protection from Seeping Acid. A level 10 Jump Skill. +5 to the Lotion Application Skill. Warning: This is a 12-hour timed item.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Prison Pocket</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Juvenile Macropus Dominus Skin on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Juvenile_Macropus_Dominus_Skin</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Lock Box of the Night Wyrm</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Enchanted Lock Box of the Night Wyrm</b> is a box with a flower. If you're female and eat the flower, and survive almost dying that ensues, you get three boons from the goddess <a href="bword://Eileithyia">Eileithyia</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Loot Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Lock Box of the Night Wyrm on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Lock_Box_of_the_Night_Wyrm</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Mongoliensis Saddle</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Enchanted Mongoliensis Saddle</b> is an pet item that <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> receives in a Platinum <a href="bword://Fan Box">Fan Box</a> on the Fourth Floor. The saddle is an obscenely garish blue and red tassel-covered saddle. There are no straps or reins on the saddle, just a seat and a pommel. As soon as Donut hops onto the saddle, a translucent strap appears, wrapping around her waist and tying her to the saddle.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Platinum Fan Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Mongoliensis Saddle on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Mongoliensis_Saddle</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Necklace of Haute Bourgeoisie</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> gains the <b>Enchanted Necklace of Haute Bourgeoisie</b> at the start of the Fourth Floor as a reward for conquering the Medium <a href="bword://Skyfowl">Skyfowl</a> Settlement on the Third.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Platinum Tyrant Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Necklace of Haute Bourgeoisie on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Necklace_of_Haute_Bourgeoisie</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Night Wyrm's Ring of Divine Suffering</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Enchanted Night Wyrm's Ring of Divine Suffering</b> is a magical ring that grants its wearer +5% to all stats and the Marked for Death skill. <a href="bword://Frank Q">Frank Q</a> gave it to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> on the Fourth Floor.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Legendary That's the Spirit Box awarded to Frank Q on the First Floor; Gifted to Carl by Frank Q in the Desperado Club</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Night Wyrm's Ring of Divine Suffering on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Night_Wyrm%27s_Ring_of_Divine_Suffering</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Nightgaunt Cloak of Stoutness</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Enchanted Nightgaunt Cloak of Stoutness</b> buffs constitution and provides various resistances when equipped. It is a lightweight hooded cloak that appears to have been crafted from a demon's wing, with nightgaunt skin stretched across rows of body-length fingerbones. The hood, when worn up, has pointed ears on either side.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Gold Apparel Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Nightgaunt Cloak of Stoutness on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Nightgaunt_Cloak_of_Stoutness</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Nipple Ring of the Defiler</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> gets the <b>Enchanted Nipple Ring of the Defiler</b> as a reward for surviving <a href="bword://Diwata">Diwata</a>'s Marked For Death Skill. A silver ring with an eyeball hanging from it.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Platinum Apostate Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Nipple Ring of the Defiler on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Nipple_Ring_of_the_Defiler</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Nipple Ring of the Superior Fire Demon’s Hand Maiden</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> got the <b>Enchanted Nipple Ring of the Superior Fire Demon’s Hand Maiden</b> from a legendary beguilers box that she received for charming <a href="bword://Ferdinand">Ferdinand</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Legendary Beguilers Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Nipple Ring of the Superior Fire Demon’s Hand Maiden on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Nipple_Ring_of_the_Superior_Fire_Demon%E2%80%99s_Hand_Maiden</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Obsidian Bracelet of the Raggle Rouser</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Enchanted Obsidian Bracelet of the Raggle Rouser</b> is a bracelet.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Obsidian Bracelet of the Raggle Rouser on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Obsidian_Bracelet_of_the_Raggle_Rouser</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Paupers Ring of the Steadfast Emberus</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Enchanted Pauper's Ring of the Steadfast <a href="bword://Emberus">Emberus</a></b> is a magical item that, when equipped by a worshipper of Emberus, cancels the effects of most health-sapping and disease-based debuffs without removing the actual debuff.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Blessed Sun Enchantments Shop at Club Vanquisher</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Paupers Ring of the Steadfast Emberus on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Paupers_Ring_of_the_Steadfast_Emberus</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Pedicure Kit of the Sylph</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Enchanted Pedicure Kit of the Sylph</b> is a black, zippered folder containing (12) metal pedicure tools. If the crawler makes a show of using some of the tools for ~15 minutes, multiple daily buffs will activate, and their feet will glitter.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Platinum Shoe Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Pedicure Kit of the Sylph on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Pedicure_Kit_of_the_Sylph</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Prison Tattoo Kit</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Enchanted Prison Tattoo Kit</b> allows someone to create a tattoo on a target, can potentially imbue magical buffs and upgrades if the artist is good enough.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Prison Tattoo Kit on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Prison_Tattoo_Kit</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Repeating Crossbow of the Scavenger Mother of Mothers</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Enchanted Repeating Crossbow of the Scavenger Mother of Mothers</b> is a magical crossbow owned and used by <a href="bword://Hekla">Hekla</a>. The crossbow appears to be made of gold, but feels almost plastic. It has an inlay carving of a vulture.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Legendary Grrl Power Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Repeating Crossbow of the Scavenger Mother of Mothers on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Repeating_Crossbow_of_the_Scavenger_Mother_of_Mothers</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Right Back Atcha Personal Shield</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Enchanted Right Back Atcha Personal Shield</b> is a shield worn on the wrist. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> received this item as a reward in a legendary <a href="bword://Boss Box">Boss Box</a> after defeating Queen <a href="bword://Imogen">Imogen</a>. He uses this item instead of the <a href="bword://Enchanted Auto Buckler of the Peach Pit">Enchanted Auto Buckler of the Peach Pit</a> given to him by <a href="bword://Katia Grim">Katia Grim</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Legendary Boss Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Right Back Atcha Personal Shield on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Right_Back_Atcha_Personal_Shield</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Roll of Never-ending Duct Tape</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Enchanted Roll of Never-ending Duct Tape</b> is an item <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives in a silver <a href="bword://Fan Box">Fan Box</a> from the end of the Third Floor.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Silver Fan Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Roll of Never-ending Duct Tape on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Roll_of_Never-ending_Duct_Tape</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Shade Gnoll Riot Forces Crowd Control Shield</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Enchanted Shade Gnoll Riot Forces Crowd Control Shield</b> is a shield given to <a href="bword://Katia Grim">Katia Grim</a> from a <a href="bword://Fan Box">Fan Box</a> on the Fourth Floor. The shield is a 6 foot tall, curved riot shield with a plastic window in the top. There are loops on the back to hold the shield. Painted on the front in white block letters are the words "Get Back" in <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> Standard.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Fan Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Shade Gnoll Riot Forces Crowd Control Shield on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Shade_Gnoll_Riot_Forces_Crowd_Control_Shield</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Shade Gnoll Riot Forces Telescoping Crowd Control Baton</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Enchanted Shade Gnoll Riot Forces Telescoping Crowd Control Baton</b> is a baton belonging to <a href="bword://Katia Grim">Katia Grim</a>. She received it in a <a href="bword://Fan Box">Fan Box</a> on the Fourth Floor.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Fan Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Shade Gnoll Riot Forces Telescoping Crowd Control Baton on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Shade_Gnoll_Riot_Forces_Telescoping_Crowd_Control_Baton</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Shuriken of Bloodlust</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Enchanted Shuriken of Bloodlust</b> are flimsy black throwing stars better used for crafting than throwing. Extremely fragile, the shuriken inflict low damage at first, but each successful attack against a type of monster increases the damage they deal against that type of monster by 8%. This effect compounds over time.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Loot Boxes</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Shuriken of Bloodlust on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Shuriken_of_Bloodlust</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Silver Bracelet of the Ab-solar</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Enchanted Silver Bracelet of the Ab-solar</b> is a bracelet.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Silver Bracelet of the Ab-solar on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Silver_Bracelet_of_the_Ab-solar</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Spiked Knee Pads of the Munificent Goddess Kina</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Enchanted Spiked Knee Pads of the Munificent Goddess Kina</b> are a celestial-tier item that grant the user multiple water-based benefits, as well as the ability to gain intelligence by consuming magical items or constitution, strength, or dexterity by consuming corpses. As a divine item, the Knee Pads will grant buffs in the presence of <a href="bword://Kina">Kina</a> and debuffs in the presence of Kina's enemies.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Celestial Orgy of Chaos Achievement Who Let the Gods Out This Time Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Spiked Knee Pads of the Munificent Goddess Kina on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Spiked_Knee_Pads_of_the_Munificent_Goddess_Kina</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Spiked Kneepads of the Shade Gnoll Riot Forces</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Enchanted Spiked Kneepads of the Shade Gnoll Riot Forces</b> are self-adjusting slip-on knee bracers covered in retractable 8" (20.32cm) long, thin, needle-like spikes, which seem to "magically" pop out when needed.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Gold Crowd Control Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Spiked Kneepads of the Shade Gnoll Riot Forces on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Spiked_Kneepads_of_the_Shade_Gnoll_Riot_Forces</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Stick of Cascadia Screams</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Enchanted Stick of <a href="bword://Cascadia">Cascadia</a>'s Screams</b> ties into the fairytale surrounding the Seventh Floor, the "Great Race." It is connected to the <a href="bword://Enchanted Hammer of Fast Forward">Enchanted Hammer of Fast Forward</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Benefactor Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Stick of Cascadia Screams on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Stick_of_Cascadia_Screams</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Tiara of Mana Genita</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b><a href="bword://Enchanted Tiara of the Inebriated Dragonfly">Enchanted Tiara of the Inebriated Dragonfly</a></b> was given to <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> in one of her <a href="bword://Boss Box">Boss Box</a> or Quest Boxes from the Third Floor. A similar style to the <a href="bword://Enchanted Crown of the Sepsis Whore">Enchanted Crown of the Sepsis Whore</a>, but with white jewels instead of purple.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Some Boss Box or Quest Box from the Third Floor</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Tiara of Mana Genita on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Tiara_of_Mana_Genita</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Tiara of the Inebriated Dragonfly</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Enchanted Tiara of the Inebriated Dragonfly</b> was created by adding the <a href="bword://Flawless Jewlers Gem">Flawless Jewlers Gem</a> to a blank Tiara. This item is obtained in Book 6 when <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> opt to keep the <a href="bword://Enchanted Tiara of Mana Genita">Enchanted Tiara of Mana Genita</a> as is, rather than upgrading it with the Flawless Jewlers Gem. Instead they buy a blank Tiara from the Gnome jeweler at the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a> and pay 25,000 gold to have the citrine jewel installed into it.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Created by adding the Flawless Jewlers Gem to a blank Tiara</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Tiara of the Inebriated Dragonfly on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Tiara_of_the_Inebriated_Dragonfly</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Tiara of Mana Genita</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b><a href="bword://Enchanted Tiara of the Inebriated Dragonfly">Enchanted Tiara of the Inebriated Dragonfly</a></b> was given to <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> in one of her <a href="bword://Boss Box">Boss Box</a> or Quest Boxes from the Third Floor. A similar style to the <a href="bword://Enchanted Crown of the Sepsis Whore">Enchanted Crown of the Sepsis Whore</a>, but with white jewels instead of purple.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Some Boss Box or Quest Box from the Third Floor</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Tiara of Mana Genita on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Tiara_of_Mana_Genita</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Toe Ring of the Leprous Bandit</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Enchanted Toe Ring of the Leprous Bandit</b> is a valuable item that allows the wearer to temporarily walk barefoot on non-horizontal surfaces, and spread an active debuff to one target. The ring is initially equipped on his left pinky toe, but is moved to his right pinky toe once he receives the <a href="bword://Enchanted Toe Ring of the Well-Balanced">Enchanted Toe Ring of the Well-Balanced</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Toe Ring of the Leprous Bandit on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Toe_Ring_of_the_Leprous_Bandit</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Toe Ring of the Splatter Skunk</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Enchanted Toe Ring of the Splatter Skunk</b> is an adjustable enchanted toe ring suited for melee combat and monk classes. It boosts the wearer's Strength stat and Powerful Strike Skill level.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Gold Shoe Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Toe Ring of the Splatter Skunk on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Toe_Ring_of_the_Splatter_Skunk</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Toe Ring of the Well-Balanced</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives the <b>Enchanted Toe Ring of the Well-Balanced</b> in a Legendary <a href="bword://Spicy Box">Spicy Box</a> for the <a href="bword://Unbirthing Achievement">Unbirthing Achievement</a>. He equips it on his left pinky toe.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Unbirthing Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Toe Ring of the Well-Balanced on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Toe_Ring_of_the_Well-Balanced</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Trollskin Shirt of Pummeling</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Enchanted Trollskin Shirt of Pummeling</b> is magical under-armor for melee fighters and tanks: it buffs health regeneration and makes the wearer immune to melee damage debuffs. This item can be upgraded.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Gold Apparel Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Trollskin Shirt of Pummeling on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Trollskin_Shirt_of_Pummeling</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Venomous Elven Rock Chucker</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Enchanted Venomous Elven Rock Chucker</b> is a rock throwing machine. Anything thrown by the chucker is infused with Poison Cloud.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Venomous Elven Rock Chucker on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Venomous_Elven_Rock_Chucker</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted War Gauntlet of the Exalted Grull</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Enchanted War Gauntlet of the Exalted Grull</b> is a charcoal-colored, angular bracer that fits over a crawler's wrist and can be activated by forming a tight fist.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Gold Brawler's Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted War Gauntlet of the Exalted Grull on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_War_Gauntlet_of_the_Exalted_Grull</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Wrestling Belt of the Great Gorgo</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Enchanted Wrestling Belt of the Great Gorgo</b> is an item belonging to <a href="bword://Katia Grim">Katia Grim</a>. A gold wrestling belt, like any regular heavyweight champion belt they'd give to a WWE star.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Platinum Slam Master Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Wrestling Belt of the Great Gorgo on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Wrestling_Belt_of_the_Great_Gorgo</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Encore Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Encore</b> is a bard spell that heals the party and removes multiple debuffs.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Encore Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Encore_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enemy of the Church Tattoo</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Enemy of the Church Tattoos</b> mark the bearer as the enemy of a specific deity and all of its worshippers. The bearer gains a 25% damage bonus against adherents of the deity, but all adherents of the deity will attack the bearer on sight.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Apostate Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enemy of the Church Tattoo on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enemy_of_the_Church_Tattoo</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Engaged Lock Box of the Night Wyrm</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Engaged Lock Box of the Night Wyrm</b> is a small sealed box containing the <a href="bword://Orchid of Eileithyia&#x27;s Grace">Orchid of Eileithyia's Grace</a>. The Engaged Lock Box of the Night Wyrm is a small box made of dark wood and engraved with spiderweb patterns; through its slats, a pink orchid is visible. The box crackles with dark energy. Three metallic claws rise out of the wood, each holding a marble-sized purple jewel representing a magical seal. The active seals glow; broken seals look "cracked and burned-out, like spent flashbulbs."</li><li><b>Source:</b> Celestial Loot Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Engaged Lock Box of the Night Wyrm on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Engaged_Lock_Box_of_the_Night_Wyrm</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Engine of Tomorrow</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Li Jun">Li Jun</a> receives the <b>Engine of Tomorrow</b> in a <a href="bword://Celestial">Celestial</a> Who Let the <a href="bword://Gods">Gods</a> Out This Time Box for the <a href="bword://Celestial Orgy of Chaos Achievement">Celestial Orgy of Chaos Achievement</a>. His new eye is a swirling black orb that changes to a clockwork engine when it is working. It gives the users the ability to see muscles tensing and slows down their perception of time in short bursts.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Celestial Orgy of Chaos AchievementWho Let the Gods Out This Time Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Engine of Tomorrow on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Engine_of_Tomorrow</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Engineer's Key</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Engineer's Key</b> is an Item on the Fourth Floor that allows access to the engineer's compartment on the Iron Tangle. It is one of two ways to pass through the Abyss Station Portals to get to the Train yards.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Engineers</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Engineer's Key on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Engineer%27s_Key</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Engineer's Table</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>An <b>Engineer's Table</b> (also referred to as an <b>Engineering Table</b>) is a crafting workbench that can be installed and used in Personal Spaces. It is a general, catch-all table where crawlers can use magical tools such as the <a href="bword://Goo-Inator 3000">Goo-Inator 3000</a> to fabricate and modify items.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Crafting Table Store; loot from boss chamber</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Engineer's Table on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Engineer%27s_Table</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Engineering Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Engineering Loot Box</b> (also called the <b>Mechanic’s Box</b> in early books) is a specialized <b>loot category</b> focused on <b>crafting, repair, and mechanical enhancements</b>. It is commonly awarded for <b>constructing objects, utilizing workbenches, or completing engineering-based tasks</b>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Engineering Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Engineering_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enhanced Crafting Studio</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Enhanced Crafting Studio</b> is a Personal Space upgrade that allows for Crafting tables to be placed in the space. The room takes up about a quarter of a level 5 personal space.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Dungeon Market</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enhanced Crafting Studio on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enhanced_Crafting_Studio</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enhanced Pet Biscuit</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>An <b>Enhanced Pet Biscuit</b> is a small, hard-but-crumbly brown pellet that looks like a cat treat. There are over 100 possible effects, half of which are good and half of which lean toward neutral or disastrous.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Legendary Pet Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enhanced Pet Biscuit on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enhanced_Pet_Biscuit</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Entourage Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Entourage</b> is a bard spell that creates multiple illusionary versions of each party member.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Entourage Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Entourage_Spell</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Epitome Noflex</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Epitome Noflex</b> is the mother of <a href="bword://Epitome Tagg">Epitome Tagg</a>, the leader of The <a href="bword://Dream">Dream</a>. A pale, bald, and beautiful elf with smoldering blue eyes and bone white skin.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Elf</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 28</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Epitome Noflex on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Epitome_Noflex</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Epitome Tagg</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Epitome Tagg</b> is the leader of The <a href="bword://Dream">Dream</a>. Son of <a href="bword://Epitome Noflex">Epitome Noflex</a>. At his first meeting with <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>, Carl mused that Tagg looked nothing like the unhinged psychopath he was portrayed to be. He wore a simple, leather jerkin and was indistinguishable from the rest of the dream elves. He was one of the richest men in the entire galaxy.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Elf</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Epitome Tagg on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Epitome_Tagg</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Epitome Noflex</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Epitome Noflex</b> is the mother of <a href="bword://Epitome Tagg">Epitome Tagg</a>, the leader of The <a href="bword://Dream">Dream</a>. A pale, bald, and beautiful elf with smoldering blue eyes and bone white skin.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Elf</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 28</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Epitome Noflex on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Epitome_Noflex</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Epitome Tagg</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Epitome Tagg</b> is the leader of The <a href="bword://Dream">Dream</a>. Son of <a href="bword://Epitome Noflex">Epitome Noflex</a>. At his first meeting with <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>, Carl mused that Tagg looked nothing like the unhinged psychopath he was portrayed to be. He wore a simple, leather jerkin and was indistinguishable from the rest of the dream elves. He was one of the richest men in the entire galaxy.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Elf</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Epitome Tagg on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Epitome_Tagg</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Epitome Noflex</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Epitome Noflex</b> is the mother of <a href="bword://Epitome Tagg">Epitome Tagg</a>, the leader of The <a href="bword://Dream">Dream</a>. A pale, bald, and beautiful elf with smoldering blue eyes and bone white skin.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Elf</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 28</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Epitome Noflex on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Epitome_Noflex</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Epitome Tagg</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Epitome Tagg</b> is the leader of The <a href="bword://Dream">Dream</a>. Son of <a href="bword://Epitome Noflex">Epitome Noflex</a>. At his first meeting with <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>, Carl mused that Tagg looked nothing like the unhinged psychopath he was portrayed to be. He wore a simple, leather jerkin and was indistinguishable from the rest of the dream elves. He was one of the richest men in the entire galaxy.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Elf</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Epitome Tagg on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Epitome_Tagg</p></div></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Epitome Noflex</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Epitome Noflex</b> is the mother of <a href="bword://Epitome Tagg">Epitome Tagg</a>, the leader of The <a href="bword://Dream">Dream</a>. A pale, bald, and beautiful elf with smoldering blue eyes and bone white skin.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Elf</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 28</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Epitome Noflex on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Epitome_Noflex</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Epitome Tagg</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Epitome Tagg</b> is the leader of The <a href="bword://Dream">Dream</a>. Son of <a href="bword://Epitome Noflex">Epitome Noflex</a>. At his first meeting with <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>, Carl mused that Tagg looked nothing like the unhinged psychopath he was portrayed to be. He wore a simple, leather jerkin and was indistinguishable from the rest of the dream elves. He was one of the richest men in the entire galaxy.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Elf</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Epitome Tagg on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Epitome_Tagg</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Eris</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Eris</b> is the goddess of chaos. [[Category:<a href="bword://Celestial">Celestial</a>]</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> God</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 34</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Eris on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Eris</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Error Replacement Net</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>An <b>Error-Replacement Net</b> is a <a href="bword://Mantis">Mantis</a> invention intended to stabilize (or, according to the <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a>, lobotomize) newly created Macro AIs. Three or four days before this season of <i>Dungeon Crawler World</i> started, Mantis scientists successfully used the error-replacement net to synthesize a new, stable, independent <a href="bword://Macro AI">Macro AI</a>. This development brings the Mantises one step closer to recreating the Eulogist and, once this new generation of Macro AI is fully rolled out, will make it impossible for Residuals to communicate with AIs in future Dungeons.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Hive Home</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Error Replacement Net on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Error_Replacement_Net</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Escape Velocity</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Escape Velocity</b> was the name of the ship that discovered the worm-hole to the first system where a scientific crew investigating a primal ship graveyard came across the Vog generation ship. This eventually led to the creation of the <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Escape Velocity on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Escape_Velocity</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Eunice</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 2.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Eunice</b> is a heavily pregnant Fathom <a href="bword://Dwarf">Dwarf</a> mother living on the Third Floor, mother to a large group of young dwarven children, including Ricky Joe.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Eunice on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Eunice</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Eva</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Eva Sigrid</b> is a crawler on Dungeon Crawler World: Earth. She worked as a professor with <a href="bword://Katia Grim">Katia Grim</a> before the collapse. She was a member of <a href="bword://Brynhild&#x27;s Daughters">Brynhild's Daughters</a> and <a href="bword://Hekla">Hekla</a>'s "right hand woman."</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Iceland, Earth</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Half Nagini, Half-Orc</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 20</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Eva on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Eva</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Everly</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Everly</b> is a former crawler and author of the <i><a href="bword://Dungeon Anarchist&#x27;s Cookbook">Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook</a></i> (5th Edition). Everly was a crawler thousands of cycles ago and a member of the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>. Her team included at least three other crawlers, including a healer, plus additional mercenaries.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Mantis | Primal</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Everly on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Everly</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Evo</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Evo</b> is the program's director for the <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> show Danger Zone with <a href="bword://Ripper Wonton">Ripper Wonton</a>. Evo is a <a href="bword://Forsoothed">Forsoothed</a>, a very tall, very thin, humanoid race that looks entirely white and faintly glowing. His eyes are large and black. A bony ridge grow from his eyes and up over the back of his head. He wears simple white clothes. His walk is like he's drifting above the ground. He only has three fingers on each hand.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Forsoothed</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2, Chapter 19</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Evo on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Evo</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Executive Order 11905 Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Executive Order 11905 Achievement</b> is an achievement issued to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> after the Emergency Rejection request from Prime Minister <a href="bword://Glory">Glory</a> was denied by the now frustrated AI. This achievement is named after the U.S. Executive Order 11905, which prevented the conspiring or action of political assassination.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Executive Order 11905 Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Executive_Order_11905_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Experience</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Experience (Mob)</b> are a mob on the Eighth Floor in Cuba.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Experience on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Experience_%28Mob%29</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Experience Cookies</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Experience Cookies</b> look like chocolate chip cookie and taste stale but grant +10 experience (shared among party members) when consumed. A member of your party would get 0.2 of that experience. The experience notification appears above the crawler's head with an audible <i>ping</i>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Safe Rooms</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Experience Cookies on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Experience_Cookies</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Extinction Event Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Extinction Event Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for killing all the <a href="bword://Wall Monitor">Wall Monitor</a>'s on the Fourth Floor with the <a href="bword://Nightmare Express">Nightmare Express</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Extinction Event Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Extinction_Event_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Extinction Sigil Tattoo</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Extinction Sigil Tattoo (<a href="bword://Wall Monitor">Wall Monitor</a> Race)</b> is a gecko foot tattoo below <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s left eye.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Extinction Sigil Tattoo on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Extinction_Sigil_Tattoo_%28Wall_Monitor_Race%29</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Extinction Event Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Extinction Event Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for killing all the <a href="bword://Wall Monitor">Wall Monitor</a>'s on the Fourth Floor with the <a href="bword://Nightmare Express">Nightmare Express</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Extinction Event Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Extinction_Event_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Extinction Sigil Tattoo</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Extinction Sigil Tattoo (<a href="bword://Wall Monitor">Wall Monitor</a> Race)</b> is a gecko foot tattoo below <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s left eye.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Extinction Sigil Tattoo on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Extinction_Sigil_Tattoo_%28Wall_Monitor_Race%29</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Eye in the Sky Scroll</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Eye in the Sky</b> spell is very powerfull and is usually cast using a scroll. <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> describes it as a mixture between Find Crawler Skill and <a href="bword://Ping Spell">Ping Spell</a> but covering a much wider area. He says that the scrolls are really rare and come in three different varients. The targeted crawler receives a different level notification depending on the varient of scroll used.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Eye in the Sky Scroll on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Eye_in_the_Sky_Scroll</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Eye of the Bedlam Bride Tattoo</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Eye of the Bedlam Bride</b> is a tattoo of <a href="bword://Shi Maria">Shi Maria</a>'s fifth eye. The tattoo is located in the center of <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s chest, just above his sternum, and was created using the <a href="bword://Enchanted Prison Tattoo Kit">Enchanted Prison Tattoo Kit</a> and <a href="bword://Toraline">Toraline</a>-based magical ink. When the eye is closed, it disappears into his skin; still, it feels like a bottomless hole inside of him.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Shi Maria</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Eye of the Bedlam Bride Tattoo on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Eye_of_the_Bedlam_Bride_Tattoo</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Fae Steel</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Fae Steel</b> is a lightweight alloy used to make armor and other items in the Dungeon. Although not particularly strong, it is the strongest metal that <a href="bword://Fairy">Fairy</a>-class creatures can wear.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Fae Steel on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Fae_Steel</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Failsafe</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>failsafe</b> is a standard safety measure in <i>Dungeon Crawler World.</i> Once triggered by the <a href="bword://Syndicate Council">Syndicate Council</a>, it destroys the solar system's sun, effectively killing everything and everyone in the solar system.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Failsafe on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Failsafe</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Fairy</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Fairy</b> are a race for both <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a> and crawlers. <a href="bword://Fae Steel">Fae Steel</a> is the strongest metal Fairy-class creatures can wear. Fairy-class Mobs</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Fairy on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Fairy</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Fall Into an Obvious Trap Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives this achievement shortly after entering the first floor for going down a dark alleyway labeled "Da Tutorial Guild".</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Fall Into an Obvious Trap Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Fall_Into_an_Obvious_Trap_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Fan Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Fan Box</b> is a Loot Box awarded to a crawler for gaining a massive fan following or for performing in an event that raises the crawler's public visibility. Its contents are chosen by an audience vote, and the box typically cannot be opened for thirty hours after it is awarded.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Viewership achievements</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Fan Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Fan_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Fang</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Fangs</b> is the Warlord of the <a href="bword://Reavers">Reavers</a> in Faction Wars (game). Similar to the <a href="bword://Nebular">Nebular</a> society, the Reavers enhance themselves with machines and only keep their brains.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Warlord Fang</li><li><b>Race:</b> Cyborg |</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 21</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Fang on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Fang</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Fannar</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Fannar</b> is Based on comments from Katia and Eva, he seems to be an ex-boyfriend of Katia's who called her useless and left her for one of his students.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Iceland</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Fannar on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Fannar</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Fantasy Hunter Camp</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> learn about the Fantasy Hunter Camp from The <a href="bword://Dream">Dream</a> Elf, <a href="bword://Akland">Akland</a>. He tells them that once a cycle, The Dream rent the whole moon, allowing their family members and employees to compete for a few days in the simulated hunt. Those who perform best win spots on The Dream's Faction Wars army.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Fantasy Hunter Camp on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Fantasy_Hunter_Camp</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Fashion of the Gods! Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Fashion of the <a href="bword://Gods">Gods</a>!</b> is an achievement awarded the first time a crawler receives a divine item. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives this achievement on the Eighth Floor after receiving the <a href="bword://Scavenger&#x27;s Daughter Upgrade Patch">Scavenger's Daughter Upgrade Patch</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Fashion of the Gods! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Fashion_of_the_Gods%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Father</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s Father</b> is the boogeyman of Carl's childhood. Carl's Father demanded "respect" from his wife and son, and seemed to care more for his <a href="bword://1965 Harley Davidson Motorcycle">1965 Harley Davidson Motorcycle</a> than for his family. He was a bully, and the sort of man who would drive away from an accident with a muttered, "That's a shame," and who had no issue walking away from his teenage son.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 13</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Father on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Father</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Fear Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Fear Spell</b> is a spell that imbues fear into an enemy, causing them to either run away or lose stat points. If Fear is attempted to be cast on mobs that are scary themselves (such as <a href="bword://Terror the Clown">Terror the Clown</a>), the crawler will receive the following message:</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Fear Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Fear_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Feather Fall</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Feather Fall</b> is a fall-protection effect that slows or negates the damage a crawler would otherwise take from a long fall. It shows up across the books in several forms: a brewable potion, a scroll, and an innate ability some crawlers possess. It is not to be confused with <a href="bword://Magistrate Featherfall">Magistrate Featherfall</a>, an unrelated High Elf official.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Feather Fall on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Feather_Fall</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Feral Goose</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Feral Goose</b> is a level 45 neighborhood boss. A dirigible gnome fired one at <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>, <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> and Katia but it died from the landing.</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 3</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Feral Goose on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Feral_Goose</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ferdinand</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Sir Ferdinand</b>, actually named <b>Gravy Boat</b>, is a yellow and orange cat who lived with Marjory on the first floor of <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Beatrice">Beatrice</a>'s Seattle apartment building. <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> regards him as her first love.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Gravy Boat; Warlord on High</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth (Seattle, Washington)</li><li><b>Race:</b> Cat</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 23</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ferdinand on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ferdinand</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Festering Ghoul</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Festering Ghoul</b> are a mob on the Fourth Floor. They are created by a mob having the infliction of the DTs and not surviving the first of three stages.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Festering Ghoul on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Festering_Ghoul</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Fight the Power Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Fight the Power Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for winning a lawsuit with the <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Fight the Power Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Fight_the_Power_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Filthy Little Crawlers Book of Voodoo</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Filthy Little Crawlers Book of Voodoo</b> is an item given to crawlers. A book that can be used to exchange messages with other crawlers you have meet that also own a “filthy little crawlers book of voodoo”. When meeting a crawler that also has this book their name will appear in it, if you write a message under their name only they will receive it, if you write under your name everyone can see it. Messages can be erased on demand.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Prepotente Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Filthy Little Crawlers Book of Voodoo on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Filthy_Little_Crawlers_Book_of_Voodoo</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Firas</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Firas</b> is a crawler that the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a> meets on the Fifth Floor. He has access to the <a href="bword://Puddle Jumper Spell">Puddle Jumper Spell</a>, currently at level 10. Owns an intelligence enhanced mace made for a clerics. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> gave him a cloak that has some hammer based attack skills.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Miami</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 1, Book 4</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Firas on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Firas</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Fire Brandy</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Fire Brandy</b> is a <a href="bword://Lesser Demon">Lesser Demon</a> MILF and non-combatant NPC on the Fourth Floor. A pregnant Lesser Demon trained in water magic, Fire Brandy believes she signed a contract with the Iron Tangle to work as the <i><a href="bword://Nightmare Express">Nightmare Express</a>'</i> steam boiler fire stoker. She has two viable babies locked inside the boiler with her.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Brandy</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon: Fifteenth Floor</li><li><b>Race:</b> Lesser Demon</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 14</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Fire Brandy on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Fire_Brandy</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Fire Fingers Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><i><b>Fire Fingers</b></i> is a (presumably) low-cost spell that some crawlers learned on the First Floor. For thirty-one hours after the Dungeon opened, until the first patch update, the spell was not safe to cast.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Fire Fingers Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Fire_Fingers_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Fireball or Custard?</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Fireball or Custard?</b> is a small cardboard scratch-off lottery ticket with five scratch spots. The ticket is red on one side and pink on the other, and a cartoon dragon sits in the corner, holding a spoon and licking its lips.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Lucky Bastard Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Fireball or Custard? on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Fireball_or_Custard%3F</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Fireball Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><i><b>Fireball</b></i> is a powerful spell that allows the caster to throw a slow-moving orb of explosive, temporary fire at a target. Crawlers may learn the spell from tomes, or gain the spell from items.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Fireball Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Fireball_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Fish Blaster Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Fish Blaster</b> is a spell whose only appearance in the text is as the title of a spellbook offered as a prize at the Butcher's Masquerade Ball. Nothing about what the spell actually does is ever revealed.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Fish Blaster Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Fish_Blaster_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Fitz</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Fitz</b> is the proprietor and bartender of the Narwhal, a pub and inn where <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> repeatedly stay during the Second Floor. Fitz is a large, bald, level-30 human innkeeper, depicted on the Narwhal's exterior sign as considerably thinner than he actually is. He is starstruck by Donut's "royalty," fawning over her as a customer, and is easily flustered, at one point ogling a photo of Bea left with him by Donut.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Fitz on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Fitz</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Flamengo</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Flamengo</b> is a party of Brazilian crawlers known for min-maxing their stats. They gained popularity with viewers during the Fourth Floor Iron Tangle.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Flamengo on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Flamengo</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Flawless Jewlers Gem</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Flawless Jewlers Gem</b> is one of <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s rewards for defeating Queen <a href="bword://Imogen">Imogen</a>. A large yellow-orange jewel. Can be used to upgrade a tiara but must be applied by a jeweler.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Legendary Boss Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Flawless Jewlers Gem on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Flawless_Jewlers_Gem</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Flesher</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Fleshers</b> are undead, sentient mobs that appear on the Fourth Floor, and are often found on the Ninth Floor. Fleshers are created by the brutal <a href="bword://War Mage">War Mage</a> spell, <i>You're Not Done Yet</i>. When the spell is cast on a fallen creature, the creature's flesh rips from its body and becomes a sentient minion of the caster. Fleshers are oftentimes tossed across the battlefield, landing in and around the trenches of the enemy.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Flesher on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Flesher</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Flex in the City Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>You killed a city boss with the participation of five or less crawlers. That is some serious badassery right there. Color me impressed. Now go do it again with a Province Boss.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Flex in the City Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Flex_in_the_City_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Flint</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Flint</b> is a <a href="bword://Dromedarian">Dromedarian</a> that's currently looking after <a href="bword://Skarn">Skarn</a>.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Dromedarian</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Flint on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Flint</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Floor 1 Achievements</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>This <b>List of All First Floor Achievements</b> includes all named and unnamed achievements distributed for feats on the first floor of the Dungeon, including those awarded to other crawlers. It is intended as a resource for DMs, fanfic writers, and superfans.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Floor 1 Achievements on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Floor_1_Achievements</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Floor 2 Achievements</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>This <b>Floor 2 Achievements</b> includes all named and unnamed achievements distributed for feats on the Second Floor]] of the Dungeon, including those awarded to other crawlers. It is intended as a resource for DMs, fanfic writers, and superfans.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Floor 2 Achievements on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Floor_2_Achievements</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Floor 3 Achievements</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Over City</b> is the Dungeon's Third Floor and the first floor of the "Volcano" storyline, featuring a sprawling network of heavily guarded, medieval-style villages separated by dangerous, monster-filled urban ruins.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Floor 3 Achievements on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Floor_3_Achievements</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Floor 4 Achievements</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><i>See also: Untangling the Iron Tangle</i> The <b>Iron Tangle</b> is the fourth floor of the World Dungeon, an enormously complex, interwoven subterranean subway and railway network designed to act as a massive puzzle for the crawlers.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Floor 4 Achievements on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Floor_4_Achievements</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Floor 5 Achievements</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Bubbles</b> is the fifth floor of the World Dungeon, consisting of 1,172 isolated, dome-enclosed environments where crawlers are separated into small squads and forced to conquer four distinct elemental castles in order to unlock their stairwells.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Floor 5 Achievements on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Floor_5_Achievements</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Floor 6 Achievements</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Hunting Grounds</b> is the Dungeon's Sixth Floor and the second "Volcano Storyline" floor — a jungle-overgrown urban ruin where wealthy outworld tourists, known as <a href="bword://Hunters">Hunters</a>, pay to enter the dungeon and hunt crawlers for sport.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Floor 6 Achievements on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Floor_6_Achievements</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Floor 7 Achievements</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Great Race</b> is the Seventh Floor of the World Dungeon, a sealed circuit of glass tunnels that crawlers were meant to race through toward a stack of exit portals rather than a landscape they could explore. A last-minute, Valtay-funded replacement for the level originally planned for the slot, it was structurally compromised and shattered into fine dust by <a href="bword://Prepotente">Prepotente</a> minutes after it opened. No crawler ever entered the maze, and no mob, NPC, or boss was ever encountered.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Floor 7 Achievements on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Floor_7_Achievements</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Floor 8 Achievements</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Eighth Floor</b>, themed the <b>Ghosts of Earth</b>, drops crawlers into an exact replica of Earth in the days before the collapse and forces them to fight one another through a deck-building card game called T'Ghee.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Floor 8 Achievements on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Floor_8_Achievements</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Floor 1 Achievements</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>This <b>List of All First Floor Achievements</b> includes all named and unnamed achievements distributed for feats on the first floor of the Dungeon, including those awarded to other crawlers. It is intended as a resource for DMs, fanfic writers, and superfans.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Floor 1 Achievements on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Floor_1_Achievements</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Floor 2 Achievements</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>This <b>Floor 2 Achievements</b> includes all named and unnamed achievements distributed for feats on the Second Floor]] of the Dungeon, including those awarded to other crawlers. It is intended as a resource for DMs, fanfic writers, and superfans.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Floor 2 Achievements on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Floor_2_Achievements</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Floor 3 Achievements</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Over City</b> is the Dungeon's Third Floor and the first floor of the "Volcano" storyline, featuring a sprawling network of heavily guarded, medieval-style villages separated by dangerous, monster-filled urban ruins.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Floor 3 Achievements on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Floor_3_Achievements</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Floor 4 Achievements</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><i>See also: Untangling the Iron Tangle</i> The <b>Iron Tangle</b> is the fourth floor of the World Dungeon, an enormously complex, interwoven subterranean subway and railway network designed to act as a massive puzzle for the crawlers.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Floor 4 Achievements on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Floor_4_Achievements</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Floor 5 Achievements</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Bubbles</b> is the fifth floor of the World Dungeon, consisting of 1,172 isolated, dome-enclosed environments where crawlers are separated into small squads and forced to conquer four distinct elemental castles in order to unlock their stairwells.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Floor 5 Achievements on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Floor_5_Achievements</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Floor 6 Achievements</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Hunting Grounds</b> is the Dungeon's Sixth Floor and the second "Volcano Storyline" floor — a jungle-overgrown urban ruin where wealthy outworld tourists, known as <a href="bword://Hunters">Hunters</a>, pay to enter the dungeon and hunt crawlers for sport.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Floor 6 Achievements on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Floor_6_Achievements</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Floor 7 Achievements</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Great Race</b> is the Seventh Floor of the World Dungeon, a sealed circuit of glass tunnels that crawlers were meant to race through toward a stack of exit portals rather than a landscape they could explore. A last-minute, Valtay-funded replacement for the level originally planned for the slot, it was structurally compromised and shattered into fine dust by <a href="bword://Prepotente">Prepotente</a> minutes after it opened. No crawler ever entered the maze, and no mob, NPC, or boss was ever encountered.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Floor 7 Achievements on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Floor_7_Achievements</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Floor 8 Achievements</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Eighth Floor</b>, themed the <b>Ghosts of Earth</b>, drops crawlers into an exact replica of Earth in the days before the collapse and forces them to fight one another through a deck-building card game called T'Ghee.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Floor 8 Achievements on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Floor_8_Achievements</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Florin</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Florin</b> is a Crawler from Earth who took the <a href="bword://Crocodilian">Crocodilian</a> race and the Shotgun Messenger class, and who placed fourth on the first Leaderboard published for the season.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Crocodilian</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2, Chapter 14</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Florin on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Florin</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Food Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Food Boxes</b> are a tier-one Personal Space Kitchen upgrade that look like three wooden cabinets lined up against the kitchen's blank wall. Each cabinet corresponds to one of breakfast, lunch, or dinner, and offers a selection of food options that changes daily and adapts to the crawler's tastes; however, the synthesizers can be a little buggy, and if a crawler chooses the same option twice in a row, it may become their only choice. The food is mediocre (or downright terrible), but imparts the Full daily buff.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Food Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Food_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Forkith</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Forkith</b> is a former crawler and the author of the <i><a href="bword://Dungeon Anarchist&#x27;s Cookbook">Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook</a> (Item)</i> (20th Edition). Forkith and his sister, Barkith, were raised on an <a href="bword://Urgyle">Urgyle</a>-seeded planet and entered the Dungeon together. Forkith chose to keep his race on the Third Floor, and selected the explosion-focused Sapper Class. He is described as a small, red demon. He reached <i>at least</i> the Eleventh Floor.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> unnamed seeded planet</li><li><b>Race:</b> Urgyle</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 8</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Forkith on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Forkith</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Former Circus Lemur</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>Once an attraction at <a href="bword://Grimaldi">Grimaldi</a>'s Traveling Circus on the third floor, <b>Former Circus Lemurs</b> were transformed into knife-throwing mobs by <a href="bword://Scolopendra">Scolopendra</a>'s curse.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Former Circus Lemur on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Former_Circus_Lemur</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Formidable</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Formidable</b> is a princess of the <a href="bword://Skull Empire">Skull Empire</a>. She is the sister of <a href="bword://Maestro">Maestro</a> and Prince <a href="bword://Stalwart">Stalwart</a> and the daughter of <a href="bword://King Rust">King Rust</a> and <a href="bword://Queen Consort Ugloo">Queen Consort Ugloo</a>.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Orc</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Formidable on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Formidable</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Forsoothed</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Forsoothed</b> are an alien species that is part of the <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a>. They are humanoid in shape, but are extremely tall and thin, entirely white, and have large black eyes.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Forsoothed on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Forsoothed</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Fortent</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Fortent</b> is a <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> corporate entity that occasionally produces seasons of <i>Dungeon Crawler World</i>. Fortent produced the crawl two seasons before <i>Dungeon Crawler World: Earth</i>. Three dungeon admins died to a single crocodilian crawler when Fortent decided to use their own security force to subdue the crawler, rather than rely on the <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Fortent on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Fortent</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Four-Leaf Clover Patch</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Four-Leaf Clover Patch</b> is an <a href="bword://Upgrade Patch">Upgrade Patch</a> given to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> on the Ninth Floor in a Legendary <a href="bword://Lucky Bitch Box">Lucky Bitch Box</a> rewarded to him for the <a href="bword://Liquified Achievement">Liquified Achievement</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Legendary Lucky Bitch Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Four-Leaf Clover Patch on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Four-Leaf_Clover_Patch</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Fragmenting Potion Ball</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> creates <b>Fragmenting Potion Ball</b> on the Fourth Floor using the level 3 <a href="bword://Alchemy Table">Alchemy Table</a>. The balls allow for a potion to be stored inside and break on impact.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Mordecai's Alchemy Table</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Fragmenting Potion Ball on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Fragmenting_Potion_Ball</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Frank Q</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Frank Q</b> is a Crawler from Earth and the ex-husband of <a href="bword://Maggie My">Maggie My</a>. He enters the Dungeon with Maggie and their daughter <a href="bword://Yvette">Yvette</a> and ambushes <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> in a safe room on the First Floor while wearing three Player Killer Skulls beside his name.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Seattle, WA</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Night Elf</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 20</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Frank Q on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Frank_Q</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Frenzied Gerbil</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Frenzied Gerbil</b> are a mob found on the Second Floor and Fifth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Frenzied Gerbil on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Frenzied_Gerbil</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Frogger</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Frogger</b> is an arcade action game developed by Konami and manufactured by Sega. It was released in America in September 1981. In 1982, <i>Softline</i> stated that "<i>Frogger</i> has earned the ominous distinction of being 'the arcade game with the most ways to die'."</li><li><b>Source:</b> Konami/Sega</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Frogger on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Frogger</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Frost Maiden</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Frost Maiden</b> is a race a crawler can choose on the Third Floor. It negates the effects of mental infirmity and comes with the Manager benefit.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Frost Maiden on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Frost_Maiden</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Fuck This Floor Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Fuck This Floor</b> is an achievement awarded to crawlers who descend the stairs within one hour after arriving on a floor. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>, <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>, and every crawler who arrived on the Seventh Floor most likely received this same achievement and loot box. The box contains a <a href="bword://Cosmic Buff Potion">Cosmic Buff Potion</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Fuck This Floor Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Fuck_This_Floor_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Fumble Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Fumble Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded when you fumble at the very end.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Fumble Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Fumble_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Funeral Bell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Funeral Bell</b> are the guards tasked with protecting the settlements of the 6th floor, they are on duty day and night. Level 95. They have a poison cloud attack.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Funeral Bell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Funeral_Bell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Future Huntress</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>Last of three Orcs hunting for The <a href="bword://Skull Empire">Skull Empire</a>, she was killed by <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>. Picked charisma as her highest stat because she beleived she could charm her way out of bad situations.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Wire-Haired Orc</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Future Huntress on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Future_Huntress</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Gamori</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Gamori</b> is the lead engineer of the <a href="bword://Plenty">Plenty</a> Tunnel Project and the current Matriarch of the Plenty, the caprid people who run the galaxy's tunnel network. She is also the mother of <a href="bword://Harbinger">Harbinger</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Gamori on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Gamori</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Gangway Chock</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Gangway Chock</b> is a defense <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> crafted on his <a href="bword://Engineer&#x27;s Table">Engineer's Table</a> as a gangway defense for cars on the Iron Tangle. The Gangway Chock is a massive sheet of metal fashioned out of a breastplate from the Third Floor. It's a rectangular hunk of metal with rounded edges, thinned out to about a 1/5 inch. It's "solid and heavy as shit".</li><li><b>Source:</b> Engineer's Table</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Gangway Chock on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Gangway_Chock</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Garret</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Garret</b> is a <a href="bword://Tummy Acher">Tummy Acher</a> pet that originally belonged to the crawler <a href="bword://Tserendolgor">Tserendolgor</a> (nicknamed "Ren" by her fellow crawlers, since nobody could pronounce her name), who received him as a gift for attending Crawl Con.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Rend, Garret, Bam-Bam, Cousin Oliver, Tummy Acher, Belly Acher</li><li><b>Origin:</b> The World Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> Tummy Acher / Belly Acher</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Garret on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Garret</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Gash</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Gash</b> is a feral Minor Demon who was banished to the Nothing. Gash and her sisters, including the now-deceased <a href="bword://Slit">Slit</a>, are members of a demon harem living in the Nothing. <a href="bword://Samantha">Samantha</a>, while banished, talked talked about her sexual exploits with her king, and the harem thought that Samantha had had sex with <i>their</i> king. Naturally, Samantha made up stories about her wild sexcapades with <i>their</i> king. Now, Gash and her sisters hate Samantha.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> Minor Demon</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 34</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Gash on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Gash</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Gate of the Feral Gods</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><i>This article is about the artifact. For the book, see The Gate of the Feral Gods (Book).</i> The <b>Gate of the Feral Gods</b> is a legendary- or celestial-tier artifact, a teleportation device so powerful it would normally not surface before the eighth or ninth floor. It bridges two distant locations by tearing a hole through the prison dimension known as the Nothing, and when the resulting portal closes, an ancient, maddened deity, a feral god, comes through into the world on the opening side.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Looted in three pieces (two watches and a winding box) from Henrik the Changeling, Commandant Kane, and the Mad Dune Mage on the Fifth Floor, within the Necropolis of Anser</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Gate of the Feral Gods on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Gate_of_the_Feral_Gods</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Gate Pass</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Gate Pass</b> is an item that allows the user to have a permission slip from the mayor <a href="bword://Magistrate Featherfall">Magistrate Featherfall</a> in the Medium <a href="bword://Skyfowl">Skyfowl</a> Settlement. The Gate Pass is one of the items <a href="bword://GumGum">GumGum</a> has on her body when <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> searches it, along with the <a href="bword://Mysterious Letter">Mysterious Letter</a>. Before they head to Magistrate Featherfall's office, Carl summons a <a href="bword://Village Guard Swordsman">Village Guard Swordsman</a>, shows him the gate pass and the body of the dead hooker, to hopefully allow him to have the corpse in his possession.</li><li><b>Source:</b> GumGum's corpse</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Gate Pass on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Gate_Pass</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Gavrilo Princip Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Gavrilo Princip Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> after they killed Empress <a href="bword://D&#x27;nadia">D'nadia</a> during Faction Wars (game). The achievement is named after Gavrilo Princip who murdered Arch Duke <a href="bword://Ferdinand">Ferdinand</a> in 1914, kicking off World War 1.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Gavrilo Princip Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Gavrilo_Princip_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Genesis</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Genesis</b> is a Level 95 Lady Mantaur Dominator, one half of a pair of womantaur drivers (alongside <a href="bword://Rapture">Rapture</a>) racing for the Lady Dominators during the Tenth Floor's racing heats.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Genesis on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Genesis</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Gennrik</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Gennrik</b> is a <a href="bword://Saccathian">Saccathian</a> Bounty Hunter. Gennrik comes from a family of bounty hunters; he claims that he and his family enjoy the work. He saves his earnings to buy into the <a href="bword://Prism Kingdom">Prism Kingdom</a>'s Ninth Floor Faction Wars army. <a href="bword://Brad">Brad</a> describes him as a "tall, octopus-faced dude."</li><li><b>Race:</b> Saccathian</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Epilogue</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Gennrik on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Gennrik</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Geraldo</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Geraldo</b> is a <a href="bword://Monk Seal">Monk Seal</a> Picket Sentry, an aquatic, melee tank mob and a Totem <a href="bword://T&#x27;Ghee Card">T'Ghee Card</a> on the Eighth Floor. This card is held by the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Eighth Floor Cuba</li><li><b>Race:</b> Monk Seal</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 9</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Geraldo on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Geraldo</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Get Out of Jail</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>A spell that can cure the stunned condition.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Get Out of Jail on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Get_Out_of_Jail</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Geyrun</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Geyrun</b> was <a href="bword://Emberus">Emberus</a>'s favorite child and the original owner of <a href="bword://Orthrus">Orthrus</a>, but was killed by an unknown assailant. Emberus suspects his brother <a href="bword://Hellik">Hellik</a> is the murderer, and assigns <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> the Find Out Who Killed My Son Quest and Kill Hellik Quest.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Twelfth Floor</li><li><b>Race:</b> God</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 28</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Geyrun on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Geyrun</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ghazi</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>Known by most everyone in the area as the Mad Dune Mage, Ghazi came to the area for the same reason as the bugbear captain, <a href="bword://Shamus Chaindrive">Shamus Chaindrive</a>: to seek out the hidden treasure that is said to be buried within the Necropolis of <a href="bword://Anser">Anser</a>.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Mad Dune Mage</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> book 4, Chapter 21</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ghazi on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ghazi</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ghommid</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Ghommid</b> are a catch-all race that describes several different types of ghost creatures. They are found on the Eighth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ghommid on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ghommid</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Gideon</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>Fought in Iron Tangle. Active in chat. Allergic to dogs.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 34, Book 4</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Gideon on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Gideon</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Gimli</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Gimli</b> was a <a href="bword://Stone Hawk">Stone Hawk</a>, and pet to <a href="bword://Osvaldo">Osvaldo</a> of the <a href="bword://Flamengo">Flamengo</a> party. A Stone Hawk, Gimli appeared to be a regular brown hawk but his underwing feathers were opalescent. He was trained to sit on Osvaldo's shoulder, and was capable of turning targets into stone.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> Stone Hawk</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 5, Chapter 69</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Gimli on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Gimli</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Glamoured Fragment</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Glamoured Fragment</b> are q piece of a deceased corpes that has been animated by <a href="bword://Big Tina">Big Tina</a>. They will turn into a Glamoured Creeper when they manage to get 70% of their body back.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Glamoured Fragment on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Glamoured_Fragment</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Glass Prison Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Glass Prison Spell</b> is a spell cast by <a href="bword://Sadie">Sadie</a>, one of <a href="bword://Hekla">Hekla</a>'s <a href="bword://Brynhild&#x27;s Daughters">Brynhild's Daughters</a>, that immobilizes a target. The only confirmed effect of Glass Prison is that it immobilizes, or "imprisons," its target long enough for Sadie's group to get past it. No other mechanical detail, such as mana cost, range, or duration, is given in the text.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Glass Prison Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Glass_Prison_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Gleener</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Gleener</b> are an aquatic <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> race. They look like a human sized <a href="bword://Kua-Tin">Kua-Tin</a>. The ship <a href="bword://Escape Velocity">Escape Velocity</a> went through a wormhole to find the first system where <b>Gleener</b> scientists were studying a <a href="bword://Primal">Primal</a> ship graveyard with the Vog Generation Ship. The Syndicate formed a few hundred cycles after that.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Gleener on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Gleener</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Glory</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Prime Minister Glory</b> is a <a href="bword://Gleener">Gleener</a> responsible for the <a href="bword://Syndicate Council">Syndicate Council</a> and the <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> as a whole. Prime Minister Glory is known to be stoic, but is slowly cracking as the Ninth Floor Faction Wars draw near and the <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a> grows increasingly unstable.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Syndicate Space</li><li><b>Race:</b> Gleener</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 8</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Glory on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Glory</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Glory Bound</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Glory Bound</b> is a highly dangerous and addictive drug available in the Dungeon. Like <a href="bword://Blitz Sticks">Blitz Sticks</a> but stronger, Glory Bound puts you in a coma and allows you to relive a memory.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Dungeon Marketplaces</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Glory Bound on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Glory_Bound</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Gluteus Maxx</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Gluteus Maxx</b> is an NPC stripper from the Penis Parade who serves as a mercenary and ally to the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a> and the <a href="bword://Princess Posse">Princess Posse</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> The Dungeon (Desperado Club)</li><li><b>Race:</b> Unspecified (short, hairy muscle man)</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 6 (mentioned); Book 6, Chapter 52 (in person)</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Gluteus Maxx on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Gluteus_Maxx</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Gnoll</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Gnoll</b> are a race that are typically known for acting as police forces or for riot control. Shade Gnolls are a type of creature that looks similar to a hyenas.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Gnoll on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Gnoll</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Gnomish Drop Bear</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Gnomish Drop Bears</b> are open-air biplanes created by Gnomes. They are used by the Dirigible Gnomes in Fifth Floor Bubble #543. Gnomish Drop Bears look like open-air, twin-engine biplanes, with each engine nestled between the wings, and look like they were built out of scrap metal. The planes may be decorated with paint.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Dirigible Gnomes</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Gnomish Drop Bear on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Gnomish_Drop_Bear</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Gnomish Knock-Knock</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Gnomish Knock-Knocks</b> are refrigerator-sized bombs created by Gnomes and capable of leveling cities. In the Air Quadrant of Fifth Floor Bubble #543, a number of these dangle from the underbelly of Gnomish airships.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Fifth Floor Bubble #543</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Gnomish Knock-Knock on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Gnomish_Knock-Knock</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Gnomish Legate Balloon</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Gnomish Legate Balloon</b> is a vehicle built by gnomes a long time ago, to bring peace to their world.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Gnomish Legate Balloon on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Gnomish_Legate_Balloon</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Goblin Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Goblin Boxes</b> are a type of Loot Box awarded for using explosives, and generally contain more explosives. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> received these on the first and second floors, and received similar loot in unspecified boxes on the Third Floor.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Goblin Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Goblin_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Goblin Pass Tattoo</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Goblin Pass</b> is a goblin skull tattoo that marks the bearer as a friend of the goblins. It is safe to assume that any crawler might receive this tattoo the first time they cause an explosion worthy of a <a href="bword://Goblin Box">Goblin Box</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Silver Goblin Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Goblin Pass Tattoo on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Goblin_Pass_Tattoo</p></div></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Goblin Bomb Bard</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b><a href="bword://Goblins">Goblins</a></b> are a short, green, highly intelligent, and aggressive race of mobs and <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a> found on the early floors of the World Dungeon. They are among the first enemies <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> encounters on the first floor. What they lack in physical strength, they make up for with mechanical ingenuity, clan loyalty, and a volatile love for high explosives.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Goblin Bomb Bard on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Goblin_Bomb_Bard</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Goblins</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Goblins</b> are a short, green, highly intelligent, and aggressive race of mobs and <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a> found on the early floors of the World Dungeon. They are among the first enemies <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> encounters on the first floor. What they lack in physical strength, they make up for with mechanical ingenuity, clan loyalty, and a volatile love for high explosives.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Goblins on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Goblins</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Goblin Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Goblin Boxes</b> are a type of Loot Box awarded for using explosives, and generally contain more explosives. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> received these on the first and second floors, and received similar loot in unspecified boxes on the Third Floor.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Goblin Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Goblin_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Goblin Copper Chopper</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Goblin Copper Chopper</b> is a Goblin-made motorcycle running on a steam engine. It has a sidecar fit for a princess. The framework is seemingly welded from mismatched copper scrap, and a thumping steam engine sits in the middle of the chassis. The seat appears to be an alligator skull with white fur on top. The sturdy black wheels are made of some unknown material, more disc than tire.</li><li><b>Source:</b> First Floor Goblins</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Goblin Copper Chopper on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Goblin_Copper_Chopper</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Goblin Dynamite</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Goblin Dynamite</b> is an extremely volatile explosive created by <a href="bword://Goblins">Goblins</a>. The red stick is wet and sticky, and the long wick hisses and pops like a sparkler when lit. The wick must be physically lit using a lighter or mechanism.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Goblins, Goblin Box, Hobgobs and Boom Sticks</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Goblin Dynamite on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Goblin_Dynamite</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Goblin Engineer</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b><a href="bword://Goblins">Goblins</a></b> are a short, green, highly intelligent, and aggressive race of mobs and <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a> found on the early floors of the World Dungeon. They are among the first enemies <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> encounters on the first floor. What they lack in physical strength, they make up for with mechanical ingenuity, clan loyalty, and a volatile love for high explosives.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Goblin Engineer on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Goblin_Engineer</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Goblins</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Goblins</b> are a short, green, highly intelligent, and aggressive race of mobs and <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a> found on the early floors of the World Dungeon. They are among the first enemies <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> encounters on the first floor. What they lack in physical strength, they make up for with mechanical ingenuity, clan loyalty, and a volatile love for high explosives.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Goblins on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Goblins</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Goblin Murder Dozer</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Murder Dozer</b> is a Goblin-made coal-powered contraption found on the First Floor. The tractor-sized Murder Dozer is haphazardly constructed of rusting hunks of metal, runs on tank-like treads, and has several pipes billowing out black smoke. A spinning wheel covered in spikes whirrs on the front of the machine, and there's a small ladder on the back. It sounds like a steam engine and has a wide turn radius. The top of the machine is a fur-lined recessed hole with benches enough to seat fifteen goblins.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Goblins</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Goblin Murder Dozer on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Goblin_Murder_Dozer</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Goblin Oil</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Goblin Oil</b> is a flammable liquid kept in <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s inventory, utilized as a crafting material to create improvised explosives. Goblin Oil is a liquid combustible that can be mixed with other flammable substances to create highly effective incendiary weapons.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Goblins (Assumed/Looted)</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Goblin Oil on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Goblin_Oil</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Goblin Pass Tattoo</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Goblin Pass</b> is a goblin skull tattoo that marks the bearer as a friend of the goblins. It is safe to assume that any crawler might receive this tattoo the first time they cause an explosion worthy of a <a href="bword://Goblin Box">Goblin Box</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Silver Goblin Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Goblin Pass Tattoo on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Goblin_Pass_Tattoo</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Goblin Shamanka</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b><a href="bword://Goblins">Goblins</a></b> are a short, green, highly intelligent, and aggressive race of mobs and <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a> found on the early floors of the World Dungeon. They are among the first enemies <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> encounters on the first floor. What they lack in physical strength, they make up for with mechanical ingenuity, clan loyalty, and a volatile love for high explosives.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Goblin Shamanka on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Goblin_Shamanka</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Goblins</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Goblins</b> are a short, green, highly intelligent, and aggressive race of mobs and <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a> found on the early floors of the World Dungeon. They are among the first enemies <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> encounters on the first floor. What they lack in physical strength, they make up for with mechanical ingenuity, clan loyalty, and a volatile love for high explosives.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Goblins on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Goblins</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Goblin Smoke Bomb</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Goblin Smoke Bombs</b> are apple-sized spherical bombs with wicks. After the wick is lit and the fire ignites the bomb, they emit a cloud of stinking, multi-color, opaque smoke that covers a 10 meter radius for three minutes (180 seconds) before dispersing.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Loot Boxes; Hobgobs and Boom Sticks</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Goblin Smoke Bomb on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Goblin_Smoke_Bomb</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Goblins</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Goblins</b> are a short, green, highly intelligent, and aggressive race of mobs and <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a> found on the early floors of the World Dungeon. They are among the first enemies <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> encounters on the first floor. What they lack in physical strength, they make up for with mechanical ingenuity, clan loyalty, and a volatile love for high explosives.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Goblins on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Goblins</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Goblin Bomb Bard</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b><a href="bword://Goblins">Goblins</a></b> are a short, green, highly intelligent, and aggressive race of mobs and <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a> found on the early floors of the World Dungeon. They are among the first enemies <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> encounters on the first floor. What they lack in physical strength, they make up for with mechanical ingenuity, clan loyalty, and a volatile love for high explosives.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Goblin Bomb Bard on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Goblin_Bomb_Bard</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Goblin Engineer</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b><a href="bword://Goblins">Goblins</a></b> are a short, green, highly intelligent, and aggressive race of mobs and <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a> found on the early floors of the World Dungeon. They are among the first enemies <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> encounters on the first floor. What they lack in physical strength, they make up for with mechanical ingenuity, clan loyalty, and a volatile love for high explosives.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Goblin Engineer on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Goblin_Engineer</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Goblin Shamanka</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b><a href="bword://Goblins">Goblins</a></b> are a short, green, highly intelligent, and aggressive race of mobs and <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a> found on the early floors of the World Dungeon. They are among the first enemies <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> encounters on the first floor. What they lack in physical strength, they make up for with mechanical ingenuity, clan loyalty, and a volatile love for high explosives.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Goblin Shamanka on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Goblin_Shamanka</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Gods</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Gods</b>, also known as <b>Deities</b>, are immensely powerful beings that reside within the Dungeon, many of them drawn from real-world mythologies. Despite their name, they are not truly divine: many are controlled by wealthy <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> sponsors who have paid for the privilege of wielding their power.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Gods on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Gods</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Goff</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b><a href="bword://Paulie">Paulie</a></b> is the preferred name of <b>Goff</b>, and is a human occupied by a <a href="bword://Residual">Residual</a>. In the months before the transformation, he lived at the Shepherd's House, a homeless shelter near Miami, Florida.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Goff; Paulie</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Miami, FL</li><li><b>Race:</b> Residual</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 49</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Goff on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Goff</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Paulie</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Paulie</b> is the preferred name of <b><a href="bword://Goff">Goff</a></b>, and is a human occupied by a <a href="bword://Residual">Residual</a>. In the months before the transformation, he lived at the Shepherd's House, a homeless shelter near Miami, Florida.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Goff; Paulie</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Miami, FL</li><li><b>Race:</b> Residual</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 49</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Paulie on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Paulie</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Goiter</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Goiter</b> is a <a href="bword://Bugbear">Bugbear</a> NPC on the Sixth Floor.</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 5, Chapter 10</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Goiter on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Goiter</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Gondii</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Gondii</b> are an alien race of a parasitic worms who occupy and maintain dead bodies. The Gondii are the citizens and controlling agents of the Valtay corporate government.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Gondii on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Gondii</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Goo-Inator 3000</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Goo-Inator 3000</b> can be used at an <a href="bword://Engineer&#x27;s Table">Engineer's Table</a> to reshape existing materials. It looks like "a silver, oversized lollipop with a button on the handle."</li><li><b>Source:</b> Loot Boxes</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Goo-Inator 3000 on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Goo-Inator_3000</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Good Mana Potion</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Good Mana Potions</b> (AKA <i>Good Mana Refills</i>) are potions that slowly add 200 Mana Points over the space of two minutes, at a rate of approximately 1.67 MP per second.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Adventurer Box (Floor 8)</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Good Mana Potion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Good_Mana_Potion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Good Shit Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>Platinum Here's-Some-Good-Shit-Because-You're-Gonna-Need-It-Box</b> (sometimes referred to simply as the <b>Platinum good-shit box</b>) is a special Platinum-tier loot box awarded to crawlers who quickly abandon a dungeon floor without leveling up.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Achievement Reward (Fuck This Floor)</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Good Shit Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Good_Shit_Box</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Good Mana Potion</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Good Mana Potions</b> (AKA <i>Good Mana Refills</i>) are potions that slowly add 200 Mana Points over the space of two minutes, at a rate of approximately 1.67 MP per second.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Adventurer Box (Floor 8)</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Good Mana Potion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Good_Mana_Potion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Good Shit Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>Platinum Here's-Some-Good-Shit-Because-You're-Gonna-Need-It-Box</b> (sometimes referred to simply as the <b>Platinum good-shit box</b>) is a special Platinum-tier loot box awarded to crawlers who quickly abandon a dungeon floor without leveling up.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Achievement Reward (Fuck This Floor)</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Good Shit Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Good_Shit_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Gore Golem Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Gore Golem</b> is a spell whose only appearance in the text is as the title of a spellbook offered as a prize at the Butcher's Masquerade Ball. Beyond its mana cost, nothing about what the spell actually does is ever revealed.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Gore Golem Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Gore_Golem_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Gore-Gore</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Gore-Gore</b> is a neighborhood boss and Mantaur train engineer on the Ochre Line of the Fourth Floor Iron Tangle. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> describes Gore-Gore:</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> Mantaur</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 11</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Gore-Gore on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Gore-Gore</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Gorgon Marital Aid</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Gorgon Marital Aid</b> is a crafting tool that allows users to manipulate, fuse, and shape rigid materials. The Gorgon Marital Aid is shaped like a spatula.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Silver Mechanic's Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Gorgon Marital Aid on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Gorgon_Marital_Aid</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Grace Bautista 3</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Grace <a href="bword://Bautista">Bautista</a></b> is Daniel Bautista's sister. She was killed by a Circus Lemur in the Overcity. The pile of corpses that includes Grace Bautista includes two <a href="bword://Human">Human</a> corpses, and the corpse of a large, humanoid, tree-like race. The humans appear to be "Asian, perhaps Filipino". Grace is implied to be the tree-like corpse. The body is humanoid, but badly mishapen ("closer to an Ent from Lord of the Rings than Groot from Guardians of the Galaxy”), with her facial features resembling a human but her back is hunched, with an extra set of limbs emerging from her back.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Large, tree-like creature</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2, Chapter 6</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Grace Bautista 3 on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Grace_Bautista_3</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Gracie</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Dr. Gracie</b> was an original member of the <a href="bword://Meadow Lark">Meadow Lark</a> party. Before the transformation, Dr. Gracie was an MMMA fighter and a doctor. She was working night shift at the Meadow Lark Elder Care Facility in Wenatchee, WA, when <a href="bword://Agatha">Agatha</a> set fire to the kitchen and forced the facility to evacuate. Dr. Gracie entered the dungeon with a number of staff members, emergency responders, and elderly patients.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Wenatchee, WA</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 22</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Gracie on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Gracie</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Grandma Sticky</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Grandma Sticky</b> is a goblin dancer at Bitches, a club inside the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>, and the mother of <a href="bword://Snail Trail">Snail Trail</a> and mother-in-law of <a href="bword://Splash Zone">Splash Zone</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Grandma Sticky on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Grandma_Sticky</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Grapple</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Grapple</b>s are a slave race of quarter giants, bred by the High Elves to serve as servants and laborers, commonly seen working menial jobs such as train porters throughout the Dungeon.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Grapple on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Grapple</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Poison Grapple Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Poison <a href="bword://Grapple">Grapple</a></b> is a spell whose only appearance in the text is as the title of a spellbook offered as a prize at the Butcher's Masquerade Ball. Nothing about what the spell actually does is ever revealed.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Poison Grapple Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Poison_Grapple_Spell</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Graupel</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><i><b>Graupel</b></i> is an expensive war spell that generates a powerful ice storm. It should only be cast outdoors. <a href="bword://Elle McGibbons">Elle McGibbons</a> receives a Tome of <i><b>Graupel</b></i> in a Loot Box after helping <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> fight against <a href="bword://Grull">Grull</a> (piloted by the <a href="bword://Maestro">Maestro</a>) on the Fourth Floor. She uses the spell for the first time to crash the air castle in her Fifth Floor Bubble.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Graupel on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Graupel</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Grease Monkey Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Grease Monkey!</b> is an achievement which, similar to <a href="bword://Battlefield Construction Achievement">Battlefield Construction Achievement</a>, is awarded to crawlers who build a wheeled contraption and use it in combat.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Grease Monkey Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Grease_Monkey_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Gremlins</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Gremlins</b> are a small, goblin-shaped race that appear throughout the dungeon in wildly different forms, from savage, rapidly-breeding monsters to skilled mechanics and engineers.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Gremlins on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Gremlins</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Grigori The Placid</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Grigori the Placid</b> is a Level 93 human Fleshmancer, a mercenary hired during the Tenth Floor's racing arc who later becomes the unwilling mouthpiece for the <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a> itself during the finale's Parade of Horribles on the 11th floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Grigori The Placid on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Grigori_The_Placid</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Grimaldi</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>Ringmaster Grimaldi is a level 85 City Boss Elite that <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> meets on the third floor. Redstone Grimaldi was originally a dwarf and husband to <a href="bword://Tsarina Signet">Tsarina Signet</a>. He was the ringmaster of the 'great and wonderful Grimaldi's Traveling Circus' before he was transformed to a <a href="bword://Pestiferous Vine">Pestiferous Vine</a> by the poison cloud of the cataclysm.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Redstone Grimaldi</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> Dwarf | Pestiferous Vine</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Grimaldi on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Grimaldi</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Grixist</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Grixist</b> is a race. Grixist are bipedal bug-like aliens, about five feet tall, with a long thin neck. They have four arms with three fingers on each hand. They are covered in coarse blue black hair and six black eyes arranged in a v-formation on their face.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Grixist on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Grixist</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Gross Atomizers</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Gross Atomizers</b> are a mob that can be found at station 271 of the Camel Line on the Iron Tangle. They look like a floating bag of gas with a Poison area of effect attack cloud area attack.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Gross Atomizers on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Gross_Atomizers</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Growler Gary</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Growler Gary</b> is the gnoll bartender at the Downward Dog, a safe room bar at Station 75 on the Iron Tangle. Growler Gary is very concerned with being perceived as a coward. When the ghouls come through the station and kill everyone outside his bar, Gary tries to leave to help but is stopped due to his NPC key-holder status, making him effectively immortal. Everytime he comes back to life he is sober, despite his excessive drinking.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> Shade Gnoll</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 25, Book 3</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Growler Gary on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Growler_Gary</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Grrl Power Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Grrl Power Box</b> is a Loot Box distributed to <a href="bword://Hekla">Hekla</a> for being the first woman in the dungeon to kill a mob using a human male corpse. Hekla receives the <a href="bword://Enchanted Repeating Crossbow of the Scavenger Mother of Mothers">Enchanted Repeating Crossbow of the Scavenger Mother of Mothers</a> from this box on the First Floor.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Killing a mob using a human male corpse</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Grrl Power Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Grrl_Power_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Grulke</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Grulke</b> is a race a crawler can choose upon entry to the Third Floor. A five foot tall, warty slimy toad person. Able to leap great distances and deliver devastating attacks with their tongue.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Grulke on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Grulke</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Grull</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Grull</b> is a war god worshipped by equine-class mobs throughout the Dungeon. <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> names horses, centaurs, and tikbalangs as likely adherents of Grull, and notes that llama-type creatures pray to him as well, though not until after the Third Floor. His worshippers smear themselves in blue makeup and talk incessantly about wenches and dying gloriously in battle.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> War God Grull, the Exalted Grull</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Celestial Ascendency</li><li><b>Race:</b> God</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 25</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Grull on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Grull</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Guild of Suffering</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Guild of Suffering</b> is a Dungeon cult that worships a demigod, the Night Wyrm. Guild access is granted by the Night Wyrm's Nasty Little Web of Suffering tattoo, and awarded to anyone who uses a Divine Suffering artifact. <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> notes that the guild also has outreach centers. Members can accept assassination quests, which are written in a strange language on rigid flaps of dried skin with pulsing desiccated veins.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Guild of Suffering on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Guild_of_Suffering</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>GumGum</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>GumGum</b> is a level 5 Orc living in the Overcity. She asked <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> for help with the Sex Workers Who Fell from the Heavens Quest. GumGum is described as a older muscular orcish woman, similar to <a href="bword://Agatha">Agatha</a> in appearance. Her skin color is different from <a href="bword://Maestro">Maestro</a>. She is wearing a medieval-style shirt covered in blood.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> Orc</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2, Chapter 14</li></ul><p class="source">Source: GumGum on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/GumGum</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Gunnery Sergeant X2</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Gunnery Sergeant X2</b> is Warlord <a href="bword://Fang">Fang</a>’s personal defense deployment. Equipped with heavy guns, shields, and armor.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Mr. Jake Tortokai</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Reavers</li><li><b>Race:</b> Cyborg</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 7, Chapter 31</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Gunnery Sergeant X2 on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Gunnery_Sergeant_X2</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Gunpowder</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Gunpowder</b> (also called <b>black powder</b> or, if you're a goblin, "<b>funpowder</b>") is a granulated black powder that was widely used as a propellant in firearms before it was replaced by smokeless powder. First used in Earth warfare in 904 AD, gunpowder is a low explosive, meaning it deflagrates (burns quickly) rather than detonates, and has a generally low brisance (shattering capability). As a result, it is good at throwing metal but not at breaking rock or fortifications.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Goblin Box; Goblins</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Gunpowder on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Gunpowder</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Gustavo 3</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Gustavo 3</b> is a rottweiler, and one of <a href="bword://Lucia Mar">Lucia Mar</a>'s dungeon familiars. Gustavo entered the Dungeon in Ecuador with Lucia Mar and another rottweiler, <a href="bword://Cici">Cici</a>. The three feature heavily on the second episode of <i>Dungeon Crawler World</i> sixty hours later, which shows the young teenager already kitted out with a full set of enchanted armor, Cici equipped with a chainmail sweater, and Gustavo 3 shooting lightning when he barks.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Ecuador</li><li><b>Race:</b> Rottweiler</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 14</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Gustavo 3 on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Gustavo_3</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Gwendolyn Duet</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Gwendolyn Duet</b> is a crawler in the same bubble as <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> in Book 4. Of Canadian Inuit heritage. She has access to <a href="bword://Club Vanquisher">Club Vanquisher</a>. She's armed with a spear and wears chainmail. She has multiple tattoos on her face and hands.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Canada</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Gwendolyn Duet on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Gwendolyn_Duet</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>H'lene</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>H'lene</b> are an extinct race and part of the <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a>'s early history. Early in Syndicate history, the H'lene built six waystations in the H'lene system, near the center of the original "worm paths" (wormhole routes used for traveling across the galaxy). The waystations were traps: the H'lene robbed and ate any travelers who passed through.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: H'lene on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/H%27lene</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hadji Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Hadji Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for completing the quest The Show Must Go On in an unusual way. Despite not really participating in the quest, <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> receives the reward and achievement as well.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hadji Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hadji_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hail Mary Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Hail Mary Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for his attack using the <a href="bword://Nightmare Express">Nightmare Express</a> on the Fourth Floor.Carl opens this box in a safe room on the Fifth Floor</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hail Mary Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hail_Mary_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hair of the Dog Potion</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Hair of the Dog</b> is an anti-alcohol potion given to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> by <a href="bword://Quint">Quint</a> as part of their deal for the starter kit. Mix together a gooey weed that smells like ochera and rubbing alcohol.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Quint</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hair of the Dog Potion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hair_of_the_Dog_Potion</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Half Elf</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Half Elf</b> is a race a crawler can choose upon entry to the Third Floor. <a href="bword://Quan Ch">Quan Ch</a> chooses this as his race.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Half Elf on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Half_Elf</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Potion of Half Splat</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Potion of Half Splat</b> is a potion that prevents you from dying from falling damage but leaves you at 5% health.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Potion of Half Splat on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Potion_of_Half_Splat</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Half Elf</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Half Elf</b> is a race a crawler can choose upon entry to the Third Floor. <a href="bword://Quan Ch">Quan Ch</a> chooses this as his race.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Half Elf on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Half_Elf</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Half-Djinn</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Half-Djinn</b> is a race. Charisma bonuses don't work on Djinns. <a href="bword://Quint">Quint</a>, as a former crawler, presumably chose this as his race. On their first visit to the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>, <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> buys some potion supplies from Quint.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Half-Djinn on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Half-Djinn</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hamed</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Hamed</b>, also known as the Night Wyrm, is an early indentured NPC He is the husband of the late <a href="bword://Astrid">Astrid</a> and the father of the strippers <a href="bword://Damascus Steel">Damascus Steel</a> and <a href="bword://Anaconda">Anaconda</a>.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> The Night Wyrm</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Outside the Dungeon (Early Indentured Servant)</li><li><b>Race:</b> Demigod / Fairy (Unconfirmed)</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 8</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hamed on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hamed</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hand that Claws the Master Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Hand that Claws the Master</b> achievement is awarded each time a Crawler kills a "Hunter" on the Sixth Floor Hunting Grounds. This achievement can stack. It is safe to assume that, for most crawlers, this <a href="bword://Achievement">Achievement</a> would only be two paragraphs long.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hand that Claws the Master Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hand_that_Claws_the_Master_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hanzo Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Hanzo Spell</b> is a spell that brings mobs close to you.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hanzo Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hanzo_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hapanzi</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Hapanzi</b> is a god and the late husband of the Demi-God <a href="bword://Shi Maria">Shi Maria</a> (The Bedlam Bride). Hapanzi is a deity who met a tragic end at the hands of his wife, Shi Maria. The dungeon's lore unceremoniously states that his death was "pretty much his own fault," cheekily adding that one shouldn't "stick it in crazy."</li><li><b>Race:</b> God / Spider</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 26</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hapanzi on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hapanzi</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Harbinger</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Harbinger</b> is a caprid liaison working behind the scenes in the Dungeon. He expressly disagrees with the <a href="bword://Plenty">Plenty</a>'s goals and philosophies, and is "actively working" to remove <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Prepotente">Prepotente</a> from the crawl.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Caprid</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 12</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Harbinger on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Harbinger</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Harpocrates</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Harpocrates</b> is a deity that is a god of Silence. After <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> casts her <a href="bword://War Crimes Spell">War Crimes Spell</a> and chops <a href="bword://Meatus">Meatus</a> into pieces, Harpocrates swears revenge and leaves the realm.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> God</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Harpocrates on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Harpocrates</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Harry Tisch</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>Harry Tisch is a <a href="bword://Crest">Crest</a>. He is <a href="bword://Odette">Odette</a>'s husband. Harry Purchased Odette's bounty after her time in the Dungeon, which is how they met. He owns a crab ranch and is wealthy through many investments.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Harry Tisch on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Harry_Tisch</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hasten Poison</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>A spell that increases that makes poisons deadlier.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hasten Poison on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hasten_Poison</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Have You Goddamned Figured Out How To Use This In Conjunction With the Fucking Voodoo Book Yet? Jesus Christ I Can Only Help You So Much box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Have You Goddamned Figured Out How To Use This In Conjunction With the Fucking Voodoo Book Yet? Jesus Christ I Can Only Help You So Much box</b> is a Loot Box distributed for using an Ability Tattoo for the first time in battle.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Hey Larry, can I borrow your chainsaw? Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Have You Goddamned Figured Out How To Use This In Conjunction With the Fucking Voodoo Book Yet? Jesus Christ I Can Only Help You So Much box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Have_You_Goddamned_Figured_Out_How_To_Use_This_In_Conjunction_With_the_Fucking_Voodoo_Book_Yet%3F_Jesus_Christ_I_Can_Only_Help_You_So_Much_box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Haxor the Destroyer</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Haxor the Destroyer</b> is a unaffiliated hunter <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> killed in the desperado club.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Dreadnought</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 5</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Haxor the Destroyer on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Haxor_the_Destroyer</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Heal Pet Potion</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b><a href="bword://Heal Critter">Heal Critter</a> Potions</b> are single-use, brown-colored potions that can be used to heal injured pets, dungeon familiars, and <i>presumably</i> animal-class mobs that are not affected by a standard <a href="bword://Healing Potion">Healing Potion</a>. Unlike some potions that can be simply thrown at <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a>, Heal Critter Potions must be consumed by the target.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Crafting</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Heal Pet Potion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Heal_Pet_Potion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Heal Pet Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Heal Pet Spell</b> is a spell that allows a crawler to heal their pet.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Heal Pet Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Heal_Pet_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Heal Scroll</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Heal Scrolls</b> are single-use items that restore a crawler's health. They do not cost mana to cast and are particularly valuable because, unlike the basic <a href="bword://Heal Spell">Heal Spell</a> or <a href="bword://Healing Potion">Healing Potion</a>, Heal Scrolls can be used on any nearby crawler (rather than only on oneself) and have no cooldown between uses.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Survivor's Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Heal Scroll on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Heal_Scroll</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Heal Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Heal</b> is the basic restoration spell every crawler is taught during the Tutorial. The user glows red while casting the spell, and immediately recovers up to 20% of their maximum Health.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Heal Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Heal_Spell</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Heal Critter</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Heal Critter</b> is a restoration spell that instantly heals a single pet-class mob or dungeon familiar. The target must be nearby, and glows when the spell is cast.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Heal Critter on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Heal_Critter</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Heal Party</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Heal Party</b> is a magical spell that restores the health of a crawler's party members. It is a highly valued support ability within Dungeon Crawler World that can be acquired through loot tomes or divine rewards.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Heal Party on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Heal_Party</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Heal Pet Potion</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b><a href="bword://Heal Critter">Heal Critter</a> Potions</b> are single-use, brown-colored potions that can be used to heal injured pets, dungeon familiars, and <i>presumably</i> animal-class mobs that are not affected by a standard <a href="bword://Healing Potion">Healing Potion</a>. Unlike some potions that can be simply thrown at <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a>, Heal Critter Potions must be consumed by the target.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Crafting</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Heal Pet Potion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Heal_Pet_Potion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Heal Pet Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Heal Pet Spell</b> is a spell that allows a crawler to heal their pet.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Heal Pet Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Heal_Pet_Spell</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Heal Pet Potion</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b><a href="bword://Heal Critter">Heal Critter</a> Potions</b> are single-use, brown-colored potions that can be used to heal injured pets, dungeon familiars, and <i>presumably</i> animal-class mobs that are not affected by a standard <a href="bword://Healing Potion">Healing Potion</a>. Unlike some potions that can be simply thrown at <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a>, Heal Critter Potions must be consumed by the target.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Crafting</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Heal Pet Potion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Heal_Pet_Potion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Heal Pet Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Heal Pet Spell</b> is a spell that allows a crawler to heal their pet.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Heal Pet Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Heal_Pet_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Heal Scroll</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Heal Scrolls</b> are single-use items that restore a crawler's health. They do not cost mana to cast and are particularly valuable because, unlike the basic <a href="bword://Heal Spell">Heal Spell</a> or <a href="bword://Healing Potion">Healing Potion</a>, Heal Scrolls can be used on any nearby crawler (rather than only on oneself) and have no cooldown between uses.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Survivor's Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Heal Scroll on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Heal_Scroll</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Heal Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Heal</b> is the basic restoration spell every crawler is taught during the Tutorial. The user glows red while casting the spell, and immediately recovers up to 20% of their maximum Health.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Heal Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Heal_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Healers Grasp Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Healer's Grasp</b> is <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s first aura ability, automatically healing anyone within range of her. Healer's Grasp came bundled with Donut's Assassin of Sekhmet class, alongside the Smoke Form spell and buffs to her existing summon-vermin and tree-creation spells from her Oak Fell title. Donut herself finds it an odd fit for an assassin class, joking that it makes her "a mini <a href="bword://Imani">Imani</a>."</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Healers Grasp Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Healers_Grasp_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Healing Potion</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Standard Healing Potion</b> (also called <b>Health <a href="bword://Potion">Potion</a></b> or <b>Potion of Healing</b>) is a single-use potion given to crawlers when they learn how to use their <a href="bword://Inventory">Inventory</a> during the tutorial. It is frequently found in low-tier <a href="bword://Loot Boxes">Loot Boxes</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Tutorial; Adventurer Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Healing Potion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Healing_Potion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Heather the Bear</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 2.</p><ul class="definition"><li>Once an attraction at <a href="bword://Grimaldi">Grimaldi</a>'s Traveling Circus on the Third Floor, <b>Heather the Bear</b> was transformed into a monstrous Neighborhood Boss by <a href="bword://Scolopendra">Scolopendra</a>'s curse.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> The Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> black bear</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Heather the Bear on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Heather_the_Bear</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Heavy Metal Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Heavy Metal Box</b> is a Loot Box given to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for the <a href="bword://Touched by a Demon Achievement">Touched by a Demon Achievement</a> when he was grabbed my <a href="bword://Amayon">Amayon</a>. The <a href="bword://Celestial">Celestial</a> Heavy Metal box looks like full-sized drum kit with pyrotechnics and the face of Amayon on the drums. An ethereal demon plays the set until it explodes, with a “666” flashing in the air before disappearing.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Touched by a Demon Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Heavy Metal Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Heavy_Metal_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hedy</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Hedy</b> is a Gremlin mechanic available to crawlers on the Tenth Floor. She is assigned to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s garage. Hedy is one of two choices for mechanic for the Tenth Floor races. Her specialty is Vehicle Mechanic, whereas <a href="bword://Waldrip Chris">Waldrip Chris</a> is another gremlin that specializes as an Animal Trainer.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Gremlin</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hedy on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hedy</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hekla</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Hekla</b> is a popular Earth Crawler from Iceland and the leader of <a href="bword://Brynhild&#x27;s Daughters">Brynhild's Daughters</a>, an all-female crawler party. Practical, cunning, and lacking <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s sense of justice, she became one of the crawl's most prominent and dangerous competitors.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Reykjavik, Iceland</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Amazonian</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 20</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hekla on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hekla</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hell In A Handbasket Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Hell In A Handbasket Box</b> is a Loot Box distributed for looking at <a href="bword://Amayon">Amayon</a> at the end of the Eighth Floor. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>, <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> and (presumably) the whole group who confronted <a href="bword://Sister Ines">Sister Ines</a> received a Platinum version of this box.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Looking at Amayon</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hell In A Handbasket Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hell_In_A_Handbasket_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hell-Kissed Celestial Skill Potion of the Prince of Woe</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives <b>Hell-Kissed Celestial Skill Potion of the Prince of Woe</b> in a <a href="bword://Heavy Metal Box">Heavy Metal Box</a> he receives from the <a href="bword://Touched by a Demon Achievement">Touched by a Demon Achievement</a> on the Eighth Floor. When he takes the potion, Carl receives the Gloom Wraith Phase Skill.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Heavy Metal Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hell-Kissed Celestial Skill Potion of the Prince of Woe on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hell-Kissed_Celestial_Skill_Potion_of_the_Prince_of_Woe</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hell-Kissed Potion of Conscription</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Hell-Kissed Potion of Conscription</b> can force unaffiliated crawlers, <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a>, and even deities to fight for a specific army.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hell-Kissed Potion of Conscription on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hell-Kissed_Potion_of_Conscription</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hellik</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Hellik</b> is the god of "Sun and Life," the twin brother of <a href="bword://Emberus">Emberus</a>, younger brother of <a href="bword://Taranis">Taranis</a>, and son of <a href="bword://Apito">Apito</a>. Hellik is allegedly "quite obsessed" with killing his brothers and is the most likely culprit in <a href="bword://Geyrun">Geyrun</a>'s death, even though he was in council with Emberus when the murder happened.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Twelfth Floor</li><li><b>Race:</b> God</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 31</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hellik on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hellik</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hellspawn Familiar</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>Hellspawn Familiar</b> is one of the best pet-class races available in the game. As they level up, they grow wings and physically grow to roughly the size of a dragon.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hellspawn Familiar on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hellspawn_Familiar</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Henrik</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Henrik</b> is the leader of the Dromedarians in Hump Town. He has been replaced by a <a href="bword://Changeling">Changeling</a>. Brother of <a href="bword://Juice Box">Juice Box</a>. Attempted to force <a href="bword://Wynne">Wynne</a> to teach him a spell to turn <a href="bword://Quetzalcoatlus">Quetzalcoatlus</a> into a corporeal form.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Dromedarian | Changeling Principal</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Henrik on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Henrik</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Henry</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Henry</b> is one of the residents of the <a href="bword://Meadow Lark">Meadow Lark</a> nursing home. He made it to the The Third Floor with the help of <a href="bword://Brandon Andrews">Brandon Andrews</a>, <a href="bword://Chris Andrews">Chris Andrews</a>, <a href="bword://Imani">Imani</a>, and <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Seattle</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 1, Book 3</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Henry on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Henry</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Here's Some Good Shit Because You're Gonna Need It Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Here's-Some-Good-Shit-Because-You're-Gonna-Need-It-Box</b> is a type of Loot Box that seems to be awarded for actions that technically set back a crawler's progress on lower levels.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Fuck This Floor Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Here's Some Good Shit Because You're Gonna Need It Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Here%27s_Some_Good_Shit_Because_You%27re_Gonna_Need_It_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Herot</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Herot</b> is a former Crawler and author of the <i><a href="bword://Dungeon Anarchist&#x27;s Cookbook">Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook</a> (16th Edition)</i>. Little is known about Herot's race, but <a href="bword://Akuma">Akuma</a> describes them as a skink. He also describes them as "an annoying fucker. Even more annoying than [<a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>]".</li><li><b>Race:</b> Unknown</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 17</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Herot on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Herot</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hey Larry, can I borrow your chainsaw? Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Hey Larry, can I borrow your chainsaw? Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for using an ability tattoo in battle. <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> and <a href="bword://Rosetta Thagra">Rosetta Thagra</a> go into a flurry of research over the name of the box. Zev mentions she has never heard of such blatant hand holding by the <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hey Larry, can I borrow your chainsaw? Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hey_Larry%2C_can_I_borrow_your_chainsaw%3F_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>HeyZoos</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>HeyZoos</b> is a Totem <a href="bword://T&#x27;Ghee Card">T'Ghee Card</a> on the Eighth Floor. This card is held by the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Eighth Floor Ecuador</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 22</li></ul><p class="source">Source: HeyZoos on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/HeyZoos</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hicks</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>Hicks: race/species: <a href="bword://Dirigible Gnome">Dirigible Gnome</a>; occupation: Aerostat Pilot.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Dirigible Gnome</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hicks on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hicks</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hills Cyclops</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Hills Cyclops</b> are a race one eyed creatures, they are the weakest and dumbest of the cyclops. Like all Cyclops they are unable to see themselves in the mirror.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hills Cyclops on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hills_Cyclops</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hoarder</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Hoarder</b> is a First Floor Neighborhood Boss and the first boss that <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> fight inside the Dungeon. She guards a chamber of transplanted Earth refuse and defends it by disgorging <a href="bword://Scatterer">Scatterer</a> minions from her own mouth.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 11</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hoarder on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hoarder</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hobbledehoy</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Hobbledehoy</b> are a race of short humans. They stand approximately 4' 6" tall and simply look "like a regular person that had been shrunk." Hobbledehoy are apparently known for being foul-tempered.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hobbledehoy on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hobbledehoy</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hobgoblin</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Hobgoblin</b> are a race that a crawler can choose on the Third Floor. Hobgoblins also show up as <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a>. <a href="bword://Pustule">Pustule</a> is described as very ugly, but has excellent hearing. She remarks on the comments <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> makes about her appearance from 50 paces away.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hobgoblin on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hobgoblin</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hobgoblin Detonator</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b><a href="bword://Hobgoblin">Hobgoblin</a> Detonators</b> are single-use magical items that can be used to detonate up to ten explosive devices at the same time. It has a range of approximately 10 km (6.21 miles).</li><li><b>Source:</b> Looting, Loot Boxes, Store</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hobgoblin Detonator on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hobgoblin_Detonator</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hobgoblin Disco Ball</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Hobgoblin Disco Ball</b> is a type of smoke curtain made by <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> at his <a href="bword://Sapper&#x27;s Table">Sapper's Table</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hobgoblin Disco Ball on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hobgoblin_Disco_Ball</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hobgoblin Dynamite</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Hobgoblin Dynamite</b> is an explosive Item that <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> occasionally recieves in loot boxes. It is very similar to <a href="bword://Goblin Dynamite">Goblin Dynamite</a>, but has a larger yield and is more stable.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Hobgoblins, Hobgobs and Boom Sticks</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hobgoblin Dynamite on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hobgoblin_Dynamite</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hobgoblin Hob-Lobber</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Hobgoblin Hob-Lobber</b> is an round explosive item that comes in two types, fused and impact. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> uses them with his <a href="bword://Xistera">Xistera</a> as a ranged explosive round.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Hobgobs and Boom Sticks</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hobgoblin Hob-Lobber on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hobgoblin_Hob-Lobber</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hobgoblin Pus</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Hobgoblin Pus</b> is clay-like explosive material that can be detonated with an actual trigger to create a large explosion. It is generally more valuable and stable than <a href="bword://Goblin Dynamite">Goblin Dynamite</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Loot, Loot Boxes</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hobgoblin Pus on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hobgoblin_Pus</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hobgoblin Smoke Curtain</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b><a href="bword://Hobgoblin">Hobgoblin</a> Smoke Curtains</b> are round smoke bombs with fuses, which are relatively inexpensive and generally better than the limited Goblin Smoke Bombs. When detonated, they coat the entire area in a dense white fog.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Hobgobs and Boom Sticks</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hobgoblin Smoke Curtain on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hobgoblin_Smoke_Curtain</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hold Steady</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>He appeared to have significant magical abilities.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hold Steady on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hold_Steady</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hole Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Hole</b> is a utility spell that creates a temporary hole in a surface of the caster's choice. Although the spell is unable to penetrate most doors at level one, <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> notes that it becomes increasingly useful at higher levels, "Especially if you’re creative with it.”</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hole Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hole_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Holger</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Holger</b> is a were-castor with a mullet. He wears black, studded leather from neck to toe, no helmet, and a pair of weapons over his shoulders: a sickle-shaped blade, and a sharpened stick. The pale-skinned warrior has a red bandana wrapped tight around his fuzzy head that sports a genuine mullet, Rambo-style. He stands about three feet tall and is wide, but not fat. More a like miniature, well-built football player. His face is wide-set with wide-eyes and buckteeth. He looks like a smaller-sized dwarf– but his features are elf-like. Almost hobbit like, but stout like a barrel and hairy.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Holger on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Holger</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Holistic Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Holistic Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> when he is talking to <a href="bword://Rishi">Rishi</a> after Operation Snake Pit. The achievement is due to reaching 95% viewership by the <a href="bword://Naga">Naga</a> system.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Holistic Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Holistic_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Holy Gooper Potion</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Holy Goopers</b> are essentially holy water grenades. <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> manufactures Holy Goopers by combining a fine <a href="bword://Healing Potion">Healing Potion</a> and an air-activated coagulant inside a potion ball, and dipping the ball in the <a href="bword://Sun Shrine">Sun Shrine</a>. He explains the resulting potion acts like napalm to Vampires; once struck with a Holy Gooper, the vampires will burn up when exposed to light or a strong <i><a href="bword://Torch">Torch</a></i> spell.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Crafting</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Holy Gooper Potion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Holy_Gooper_Potion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Holy Hell Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Holy Hell</b> is an <a href="bword://Achievement">Achievement</a> awarded when a crawler first lays eyes on a Demon Prince of Sheol. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives this achievement on the Eighth Floor when <a href="bword://Amayon">Amayon</a> enters the realm.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Holy Hell Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Holy_Hell_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Homecoming Queen</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <i><b>Homecoming Queen</b></i> is a freighter in <a href="bword://Long Haul Biological Waste Management Solutions">Long Haul Biological Waste Management Solutions</a>'s fleet. Originally a biological waste freighter, the spaceship is approximately twice as large as a Valtay warship and easily the largest of the crafts trapped in Earth's solar system.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Long Haul Biological Waste Management Solutions</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Homecoming Queen on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Homecoming_Queen</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hoon</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Hoon</b> was a crawler in a previous Valtay-produced season of <i>Dungeon Crawler World</i>. Over the course of his crawl, Hoon secured a mech and completed eleven floors. When he reached the elevator descending to the Twelfth Floor, he found it guarded by his five children ("even the yearling"). Hoon chose to eat his own gun rather than kill his children.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Crawler Hoon</li><li><b>Race:</b> Unknown</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Epilogue</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hoon on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hoon</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Horton</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Horton</b> is the mushroom guy from the Stairwell Fight on the Fourth Floor. His name is not revealed until the Butcher's Masquerade. Horton looks like a mushroom after the Third Floor race selection process.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | mushroom</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 27, Book 3</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Horton on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Horton</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hotlist Expansion Potion</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Hotlist Expansion Potion</b> is a potion that expands a Crawler's hotlist in their Heads-Up Display (HUD). <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives this potion in his Gold <a href="bword://Payload Box">Payload Box</a> at the beginning of the Tenth Floor for the <a href="bword://Bomb&#x27;s Away Achievement">Bomb's Away Achievement</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Payload Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hotlist Expansion Potion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hotlist_Expansion_Potion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Houston</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Houston</b> is the Warlord of the Viceroy Faction War team.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Viceroys</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Houston on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Houston</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Huanxin Jinx</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Huanxin Jinx</b> is the current sponsor of the goddess <a href="bword://Eileithyia">Eileithyia</a>. She's been playing the Ascension game since she was a kid. She is both rich and highly intelligent. She's currently CEO of Icon Industries, a company that focuses on habitat structures.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Grixist</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Huanxin Jinx on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Huanxin_Jinx</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Human</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Humans</b> are one of the six basic starter species the <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> seeds across the galaxy for <i>Dungeon Crawler World</i>, and the indigenous species of Earth. A crawler may choose "Human" during Third Floor race selection to keep their current form in exchange for a small boost to stat points and skill training.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Human on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Human</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hunter Champion Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Hunter Champion Box</b> is a Loot Box given to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> from The <a href="bword://Scourge Achievement">Scourge Achievement</a>. Carl opens this box in a safe room on the Eighth Floor where it is referred to as the "Legendary Scourge Box."</li><li><b>Source:</b> Scourge Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hunter Champion Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hunter_Champion_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hunters</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Hunters</b> are a group of outworlders that come into the Dungeon on the Sixth Floor to hunt Crawlers for their gear to sell to the Faction leaders for Faction Wars on the Ninth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hunters on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hunters</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hunter Champion Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Hunter Champion Box</b> is a Loot Box given to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> from The <a href="bword://Scourge Achievement">Scourge Achievement</a>. Carl opens this box in a safe room on the Eighth Floor where it is referred to as the "Legendary Scourge Box."</li><li><b>Source:</b> Scourge Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hunter Champion Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hunter_Champion_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hunter-Killer Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Hunter-Killer Box</b> is a Loot Box distributed for killing a non-crawler biological. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives boxes for every hunter he kills, plus an extra one for killing <a href="bword://Loita">Loita</a> on the Fifth Floor.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Hand that Claws the Master Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hunter-Killer Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hunter-Killer_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hunters</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Hunters</b> are a group of outworlders that come into the Dungeon on the Sixth Floor to hunt Crawlers for their gear to sell to the Faction leaders for Faction Wars on the Ninth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hunters on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hunters</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Hunting Trophy</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>It’s the hand of a hunter. Gross.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Hunting Trophy on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Hunting_Trophy</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>I Have the Conch Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>I Have the Conch Box</b> is a Loot Box given to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for the <a href="bword://Lord of the Flies Achievement">Lord of the Flies Achievement</a>. He receives a Gold version of this box. Gold I Have the Conch Box</li><li><b>Source:</b> Lord of the Flies Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: I Have the Conch Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/I_Have_the_Conch_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>I Need My Personal Space Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><i><b>I Need My Personal Space</b></i> is a spell that, when cast, knocks back everyone in the caster's vicinity with a powerful blow. The spell affects hostile mobs and party members alike.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: I Need My Personal Space Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/I_Need_My_Personal_Space_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>I Take It All Back Potion</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>I Take It All Back Potion</b> is a potion that removes any effects of <a href="bword://Scolopendra">Scolopendra</a>'s transmutation spell.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: I Take It All Back Potion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/I_Take_It_All_Back_Potion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>I Wanna Go Home Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>I Wanna Go Home Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for teleporting to Zockau to get a pre-emptive attack on the hunters in The Hunting Grounds.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: I Wanna Go Home Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/I_Wanna_Go_Home_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>I was in the Pool! Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>I was in the Pool! Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> when he uses a water-breathing scroll for the first time.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: I was in the Pool! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/I_was_in_the_Pool%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>I'm on a train Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>I'm on a train Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to all crawlers upon entering the Fourth Floor and appearing on a train.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: I'm on a train Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/I%27m_on_a_train_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>I'm Wet Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>I'm Wet Box</b> are loot boxes distributed for activities involving water. These have only been rewarded on the fifth floor so far. These boxes are distributed fairly often for activities such as "being underwater for 60 seconds" or "jumping around on the ocean floor"</li><li><b>Source:</b> I was in the Pool! AchievementRock Bottom Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: I'm Wet Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/I%27m_Wet_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ian</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Ian</b> was a crawler in a previous <a href="bword://Borant Corporation">Borant Corporation</a>-run season of <i>Dungeon Crawler World.</i> Originally a human, he chose the <a href="bword://Bush Elf">Bush Elf</a> race and an unspecified (likely druid-based) class. He and his brother both took indentureship deals to exit the Dungeon.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Bush Elf</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 5, Chapter 1</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ian on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ian</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ice Slick Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Ice Slick</b> is an <a href="bword://Elle McGibbons">Elle McGibbons</a> signature spell that coats the ground in a wide sheet of ice roughly an inch thick. The area covered by Ice Slick scales with the caster's intelligence stat and the spell's own level. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives a special edition copy of the spellbook that starts at level 5 and trains faster than normal.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ice Slick Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ice_Slick_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ifechi</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Ifechi</b> was a medic in the Red Cross, and became one of the Dungeon's Top Ten Crawlers after partnering with <a href="bword://Florin">Florin</a>. Dark-skinned, bald, and rail-thin, Ifechi had "stunningly beautiful" features. She entered the Dungeon wearing a bright red shirt and a vest, carrying a medical bag emblazoned with the Red Cross logo over one shoulder.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Nigeria</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 44</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ifechi on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ifechi</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Igneous</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Igneous</b> is a race option that crawlers can select on the Third Floor. It is similar to the <a href="bword://Cretin">Cretin</a> race, but not exactly the same. An Igneous is a towering humanoid race made of lava and rock. Their eyes resemble "burning lumps of coal," and they radiate extreme heat and can fire lava from their bodies, as though their centers are molten lava. When they move, it sounds like rocks scraping together.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Igneous on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Igneous</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ikicha</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Ikicha</b> is a former Crawler and author of the <i><a href="bword://Dungeon Anarchist&#x27;s Cookbook">Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook</a> (11th Edition)</i>. Ikicha is a castrated male <a href="bword://Yenk">Yenk</a>. During his season of <i>Dungeon Crawler World</i>, the Sixth Floor Hunting Grounds were cold and icy.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Yenk</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 5, Chapter 13</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ikicha on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ikicha</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Imani</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Imani</b> is a member of the <a href="bword://Meadow Lark">Meadow Lark</a> party and guildmaster of <a href="bword://Safehome Yolanda">Safehome Yolanda</a>. She is one of <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s most trusted allies in the Dungeon.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Wenatchee, WA</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Obsidian Butterfly</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 22</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Imani on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Imani</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Imogen</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Queen Imogen</b> is a level 145 country boss on the Sixth Floor and the reclusive ruler of the high elves. She hosts the Butcher's Masquerade and is the target of <a href="bword://Tsarina Signet">Tsarina Signet</a>'s revenge quest, the Vengeance of the Daughter.</li><li><b>Race:</b> High Elf</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 5, Chapter 64</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Imogen on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Imogen</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Incubus</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Incubus</b> are a type of demon, with dusky gray skin. They also have devil horns, a forked tail, and bat-like wings. Incubi have a low alcohol tolerance.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Incubus on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Incubus</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Indigenous Planetary Species Protection Act</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Indigenous Planetary Species Protection Act</b> (often shortened to <b>Indigenous Species Protection Act</b>) is a <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> law governing "collection actions" (i.e. a transformation) and the creation of World Dungeons for <i>Dungeon Crawler World</i>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Indigenous Planetary Species Protection Act on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Indigenous_Planetary_Species_Protection_Act</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Indomitable Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Indomitable Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for being attacked by <a href="bword://Grull">Grull</a>. Carl opens this box in a safe room on the Fifth Floor</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Indomitable Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Indomitable_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Infiltrator</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>Similar to <a href="bword://Gondii">Gondii</a> and Intellect <a href="bword://Hunters">Hunters</a>, <b>Infiltrators</b> (AKA <b><a href="bword://Scree">Scree</a></b>) are an aquatic brain parasite that can take control of a living brain. Crawlers may choose the "Infiltrator" race on the Third Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Infiltrator on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Infiltrator</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Infiltrator</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>Similar to <a href="bword://Gondii">Gondii</a> and Intellect <a href="bword://Hunters">Hunters</a>, <b>Infiltrators</b> (AKA <b><a href="bword://Scree">Scree</a></b>) are an aquatic brain parasite that can take control of a living brain. Crawlers may choose the "Infiltrator" race on the Third Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Infiltrator on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Infiltrator</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Scree</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>Similar to <a href="bword://Gondii">Gondii</a> and Intellect <a href="bword://Hunters">Hunters</a>, <b>Infiltrators</b> (AKA <b>Scree</b>) are an aquatic brain parasite that can take control of a living brain. Crawlers may choose the "<a href="bword://Infiltrator">Infiltrator</a>" race on the Third Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Scree on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Scree</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ink Marauder Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Ink Marauder</b> spell is a form of blood magic that allows the caster to draw something on paper with ink, cast a blood sacrifice, and bring those drawings to life as Blood and Ink Elementals.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ink Marauder Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ink_Marauder_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Inle</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Inle</b> is a god who is part of the <a href="bword://Orisha">Orisha</a> pantheon, with <a href="bword://Ogun">Ogun</a>, <a href="bword://Legba">Legba</a>, <a href="bword://Oshun">Oshun</a>, <a href="bword://Asojano">Asojano</a>, <a href="bword://Shango">Shango</a>, and <a href="bword://Yemaya">Yemaya</a>. During the Thorn Room Boss Battle, if his shrine is repaired: “One of only two of the Orishas to have spent time in the Nothing, the deaf and mute Inle isn’t all there. That’s a nice way of saying he’s batshit. But, he once was a healing god. If you repair his shrine, you will gain immunity from most health-seeping conditions. You will gain 50% to your Constitution. Inle will not ascend. He’ll end up back in the Nothing. He doesn’t know that yet, so don’t tell him.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Orisha Deity</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Inle on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Inle</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Instacot 60</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Instacot 60</b> is a Personal Space and Guild Bed Upgrade available beginning on the Sixth Floor. The Instacot 60 is the second best Bed Upgrade on the market. Crawlers will feel fully rested after only sixty seconds (one minute) of sleep, and will receive the Great Rest buff for (presumably) 30 hours.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Dungeon Market OR Guild</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Instacot 60 on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Instacot_60</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Insurgent Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Insurgent Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> when he set an explosive trap killing the hunter JayGee during The Hunting Grounds.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Insurgent Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Insurgent_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Intellect Hunter</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>Similar to <a href="bword://Gondii">Gondii</a> and <a href="bword://Scree">Scree</a>, <b>Intellect <a href="bword://Hunters">Hunters</a></b> are the most common variety of finger-sized parasitic worms. Crawlers may choose to take the "Intellect Hunter" race on the Third Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Intellect Hunter on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Intellect_Hunter</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Interdiction Auxillary Railway Repair Cart</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Interdiction Auxillary Railway Repair Cart</b> is a contraption on the Iron Tangle. It is one of the types of carts found at station 75. See also: <a href="bword://Interdiction Rapid-Response Railway Repair Cart">Interdiction Rapid-Response Railway Repair Cart</a></li><li><b>Source:</b> Station 75 on the Iron Tangle</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Interdiction Auxillary Railway Repair Cart on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Interdiction_Auxillary_Railway_Repair_Cart</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Interdiction Rapid-Response Railway Repair Cart</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Interdiction Rapid-Response Railway Repair Cart</b> is a contraption on the Iron Tangle. It is one of the types of carts found at station 75. See also: <a href="bword://Interdiction Auxillary Railway Repair Cart">Interdiction Auxillary Railway Repair Cart</a></li><li><b>Source:</b> Station 75 on the Iron Tangle</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Interdiction Rapid-Response Railway Repair Cart on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Interdiction_Rapid-Response_Railway_Repair_Cart</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Interloper Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Interloper!</b> is an achievement awarded the first time a crawler opens a safe room door and allows a Boss to enter. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>, <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>, Anton, <a href="bword://Paz Lo">Paz Lo</a>, and <a href="bword://Sister Ines">Sister Ines</a> earn this achievement on the Eighth Floor when they flee into a safe room to escape <a href="bword://Asojano">Asojano</a>. Sister Ines suggests opening the safe room door to get rid of him and Carl, thinking of the <a href="bword://Rage Elemental">Rage Elemental</a> from the Second Floor does. When he opens the door, it appears as though Asojano is preparing to knock. Instead, he steps inside the room.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Interloper Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Interloper_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Inventory</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Inventory</b> is a dimensional storage interface and AI cataloging system that the <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a> grants to crawlers upon entering the World Dungeon, replacing the slot-based systems used in previous seasons. After completing the Tutorial, crawlers access and manage it entirely through a mental Heads-Up Display (HUD) menu.</li><li><b>Source:</b> System AI / Borant Corporation</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Inventory on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Inventory</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Iota</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Iota</b> was a hunter acting as an accountant for the Crafters Alliance. He stayed in the safe room refusing to fight until the <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a> teleported him out the room. Landed in front of <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and a bunch of dinosaurs, he explained to Carl about the system AI going primal and ignoring court order before Carl killed him.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Crafter</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Iota on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Iota</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Iron Skin Potion</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>An <b>Iron Skin Potion</b> (or <b><a href="bword://Potion">Potion</a> of Iron Skin</b>) is a single-use consumable potion that increases a crawler's "physical armor" by 100% for 5 minutes.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Loot Boxes</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Iron Skin Potion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Iron_Skin_Potion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Issitoq</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Issitoq</b> is a deity that can treat between the <a href="bword://Gods">Gods</a> and <a href="bword://Demons">Demons</a>, allowing for peace to be broken.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> God</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 7 (mentioned)</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Issitoq on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Issitoq</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>It Burns Dunnit</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>"It Burns, Dunnit?"</b> is an achievement earned by <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> on the First Floor after he is badly burned by a green slime. Early in the crawl, Carl and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> encounter a level-2 green slime while exploring the <a href="bword://Hoarder">Hoarder</a> neighborhood. Lacking any protection for his hands, Carl foolishly punches the pig-sized blob, sinking his arm in elbow-deep; his fingerless glove and jacket sleeve dissolve away, and his arm is left red, bubbling, and screaming with pain. The slime ultimately kills itself against Carl's Damage Reflect ability, and Carl receives the "It Burns, Dunnit?" achievement for the encounter.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: It Burns Dunnit on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/It_Burns_Dunnit</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>It itches when I pee Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>It itches when I pee Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> infected <a href="bword://Vrah">Vrah</a> with double gonorrhea when he stabbed her with the <a href="bword://Arrow of Enthusiastic Double Gonorrhea">Arrow of Enthusiastic Double Gonorrhea</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: It itches when I pee Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/It_itches_when_I_pee_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>It's Elementary, My Dear Crawler Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>It's Elementary, My Dear Crawler Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for the Show Must Go On Quest.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: It's Elementary, My Dear Crawler Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/It%27s_Elementary%2C_My_Dear_Crawler_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>It's Not My Fault You Fish-Headed Assholes Don't Properly Program Your Quests Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>A Platinum-tier <b>"It's Not My Fault You Fish-Headed Assholes Don't Properly Program Your Quests" Box</b> is delivered to all but one survivor of the Fools Who Broke the Glass Quest at the beginning of the Fourth Floor.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Fools Who Broke the Glass Quest</li></ul><p class="source">Source: It's Not My Fault You Fish-Headed Assholes Don't Properly Program Your Quests Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/It%27s_Not_My_Fault_You_Fish-Headed_Assholes_Don%27t_Properly_Program_Your_Quests_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Jack</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Jack</b> is a deceased Crawler and former patient of <a href="bword://Meadow Lark">Meadow Lark</a> Care Facility. Jack was an older man who wore a too-small Cincinnati Bengals hat on his "bulbous head," and used a walker to navigate the Dungeon. He frequently poked at Meadow Lark's female patients (none of whom were named Marybeth) and asked, "You still alive, Marybeth?"</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Wenatchee, WA</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Jack on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Jack</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Jacobus</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Jacobus</b> is a Level 90 Reverse Tooth <a href="bword://Fairy">Fairy</a>, an Eighth Floor totem card accidentally made permanent by <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s Scavenger's Daughter patch, who becomes an unlikely pet of <a href="bword://Imani">Imani</a>'s.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Jacobus on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Jacobus</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Jamal</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Jamal</b> is a massive, air-breathing hammerhead shark who originally existed as a magical tattoo on <a href="bword://Tsarina Signet">Tsarina Signet</a> before being brought to life. He serves as an enthusiastic and polite ally and mercenary for the <a href="bword://Princess Posse">Princess Posse</a>.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Jar Jar, Shark Boy</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Tsarina Signet's Tattoos</li><li><b>Race:</b> Hammerhead Shark (Flesh Golem / Ink and Blood Elemental)</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2, Chapter 9 (as an unnamed tattoo), Book 5, Chapter 14 (made flesh)</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Jamal on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Jamal</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Janet Jackson’s Nipple Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Janet Jackson’s Nipple Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Katia Grim">Katia Grim</a> for being featured on a special event. The title is in reference to the Super Bowl XXXVIII halftime controversy.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Janet Jackson’s Nipple Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Janet_Jackson%E2%80%99s_Nipple_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Janitor Mobs</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Janitor Mobs</b> are a specific type of mob that cleans up the dead bodies on a floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Janitor Mobs on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Janitor_Mobs</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Jasha</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Jasha</b> was a level 65 <a href="bword://Bugbear">Bugbear</a> and a member of Team Free Love, an NPC racing team that competed on the Tenth Floor of the World Dungeon. Jasha was a self-aware NPC racer participating in the vehicular heats on the Tenth Floor. He and his teammate <a href="bword://Radoslav">Radoslav</a> dressed in stereotypical 1960s counter-culture attire, leading Princess <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> to suspect they were undercover cops in a "false advertising" scheme.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> The World Dungeon (NPC)</li><li><b>Race:</b> Bugbear</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 8, Chapter 4</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Jasha on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Jasha</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Jaxbrin Amusements, Limited</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>Jaxbrin Amusements makes Stuffed Figures that summon the creatures they represent. They currently sponsor Daniel <a href="bword://Bautista">Bautista</a>. Jaxbrin Amusements makes the beanie babies that <a href="bword://Miss Quill">Miss Quill</a> collected on the Third Floor. Their paper tag has a symbol of a smiley faced star on it.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Jaxbrin Amusements, Limited on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Jaxbrin_Amusements%2C_Limited</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Jelly Bomb</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Jelly Bomb</b> is an explosive <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> crafted on his <a href="bword://Sapper&#x27;s Table">Sapper's Table</a> to derail a train on the Iron Tangle. According to the Demolitions Workshop menu, the device was stable against anything except heavy impact.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Sapper's Table</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Jelly Bomb on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Jelly_Bomb</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Jellyfish Salve</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Jellyfish Salve</b> is a potion (salve) on the Fifth Floor.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Loot Boxes</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Jellyfish Salve on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Jellyfish_Salve</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ji-Hoon</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Ji-Hoon</b> is a deceased Crawler, and the source of Princess <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s first Player Killer Skull. Ji-Hoon was an approximately 25 year-old Asian man (presumably Korean) partied with an unidentified female spellcaster. He had a lot of stat-boosting armor, a dozen enchanted daggers, and <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a> access.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Korea</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 9</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ji-Hoon on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ji-Hoon</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Jikininki Janitor Ghouls</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Jikininki Janitor Ghouls</b> are mobs that appear on the Fourth Floor. They attack the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a> at the start of the Fourth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Jikininki Janitor Ghouls on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Jikininki_Janitor_Ghouls</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Johnny Quest Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Johnny Quest Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> when he completed the quest The Show Must Go On.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Johnny Quest Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Johnny_Quest_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Jola</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Jola</b>, also known as the Yule Cat, is a massive, mythic creature from Iceland that functions as a rare Totem Card on the Eighth Floor of the Dungeon. Originally owned by Katia, he was given to Princess <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> and acts as a heavy-hitting and intimidating (though sometimes stubborn) member of her active T'Ghee card deck.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> The Yule Cat</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Iceland</li><li><b>Race:</b> Mythic Creature / Giant Persian Cat</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 34</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Jola on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Jola</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Juice Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Juice Box</b> is an NPC <a href="bword://Changeling">Changeling</a> living in Hump Town on the Fifth Floor, where she is the only prostitute employed by an inn called the Toe. Sister to the changeling principal <a href="bword://Henrik">Henrik</a>, she becomes one of <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s most useful sources in the air quadrant.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Hump Town, Fifth Floor</li><li><b>Race:</b> Changeling</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 1</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Juice Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Juice_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Juicer</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Juicer</b> was a First Floor Neighborhood Boss occupying the troglodyte neighborhood. He was defeated by <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>. The Juicer is roughly 6'6" tall and humanoid, with a scaly body and tail, and a "preposterously muscled physique, covered in tributaries of bulging veins as thick as my finger." His scaly lizard head is supported by an improbably beefy neck, and zit-like pustules circle his beady eyes. His arms are so large that he can hardly seem to lower them, and his enormous thighs force him into a ridiculously wide stance that causes him to waddle when he moves.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> First Floor</li><li><b>Race:</b> Troglodyte/Human Monstrosity</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 24</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Juicer on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Juicer</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Junkie's Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Junkie's Box</b> is a Loot Box distributed for the <a href="bword://You Crossed a Line You Didn&#x27;t Even Know Was There Achievement">You Crossed a Line You Didn't Even Know Was There Achievement</a> for using a Divine Suffering Artifact for the first time.</li><li><b>Source:</b> You Crossed a Line You Didn't Even Know Was There Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Junkie's Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Junkie%27s_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Jurgen</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Jurgen</b> is a crawler that the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a> first meet on the Eighth Floor. Jurgen entered the Dungeon with his pregnant wife, Heidi. On the Third Floor, he chose the Harii class, a type of barbarian. At some point, he chose to worship the God Donar. Jurgen often speaks to and about Heidi as if she is with him in the Dungeon.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 62</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Jurgen on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Jurgen</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Just Wait Until Your Daddy Gets Home</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Just Wait Until Your Daddy Gets Home – Wheeled Bomb.</b> Type: High Yield Thermobaric Explosive. Also imbues Fear within blast radius.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Just Wait Until Your Daddy Gets Home on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Just_Wait_Until_Your_Daddy_Gets_Home</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Justice Light</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Justice Light</b> is a <a href="bword://Skyfowl">Skyfowl</a> former crawler from the White Cliffs, best known as the author of the eighth edition of the <i><a href="bword://Dungeon Anarchist&#x27;s Cookbook">Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook</a></i>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> White Cliffs</li><li><b>Race:</b> Skyfowl</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 32</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Justice Light on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Justice_Light</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Katia Grim</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Katia Grimmsdóttir</b> (shortened to "Grim" in her crawler ID) is a former art professor and a crawler from Reykjavík, Iceland, in <i>Dungeon Crawler World: Earth</i>. She joins <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s party on the Third Floor and becomes a member of the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a>, serving as the team's shape-shifting tank. She is one of Carl and Donut's closest friends and most trusted allies.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Reykjavik, Iceland</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Doppelgänger</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2, Chapter 21</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Katia Grim on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Katia_Grim</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Team Katia</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>Team Katia is a group of crawlers centred around <a href="bword://Katia Grim">Katia Grim</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Team Katia on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Team_Katia</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Katia Grim</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Katia Grimmsdóttir</b> (shortened to "Grim" in her crawler ID) is a former art professor and a crawler from Reykjavík, Iceland, in <i>Dungeon Crawler World: Earth</i>. She joins <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s party on the Third Floor and becomes a member of the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a>, serving as the team's shape-shifting tank. She is one of Carl and Donut's closest friends and most trusted allies.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Reykjavik, Iceland</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Doppelgänger</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2, Chapter 21</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Katia Grim on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Katia_Grim</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Kept A Rollin' Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Kept A Rollin' Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for taking control of the <a href="bword://Nightmare Express">Nightmare Express</a> with instruction from <a href="bword://Fire Brandy">Fire Brandy</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Kept A Rollin' Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Kept_A_Rollin%27_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Kevin</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Kevin</b> is the orange-hued, four-eyed, lizard-like alien host of <i>Dungeon Crawler World: Earth</i>. He gives breathless rundowns of each floor on the recap episodes, and also provides live running commentaries during Special Events with <a href="bword://Magnificent Troy">Magnificent Troy</a>.</li><li><b>Race:</b> n/a</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 14</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Kevin on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Kevin</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Khepri</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Khepri</b> is a bug-themed deity that is a light god of Rebirth and Sunrise. He is currently a retainer for Adrasteia, formerly a retainer for Khnum. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>, <a href="bword://Katia Grim">Katia Grim</a>, and <a href="bword://Prepotente">Prepotente</a> get marked for death by this god when they storm into his temple on the Ninth Floor to kill <a href="bword://Vinata">Vinata</a> during Operation Snake Pit.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Twelfth Floor</li><li><b>Race:</b> God</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 7, Chapter 52</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Khepri on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Khepri</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Kimaris</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b><a href="bword://Stuffed Kimaris Figure">Stuffed Kimaris Figure</a></b> is a <a href="bword://Stuffed Figure">Stuffed Figure</a> made by <a href="bword://Jaxbrin Amusements, Limited">Jaxbrin Amusements, Limited</a>. It is a "Unique" Item, and one of the most valuable items in <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s <a href="bword://Inventory">Inventory</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Miss Quill's collection</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Kimaris on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Kimaris</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Kina</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Kina</b> is a sea goddess affiliated with the <a href="bword://Enchanted Spiked Knee Pads of the Munificent Goddess Kina">Enchanted Spiked Knee Pads of the Munificent Goddess Kina</a>. She does not have any known enemies.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Twelfth Floor</li><li><b>Race:</b> God</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 7, Chapter 56</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Kina on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Kina</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>King Blaine</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>King Blaine</b> is an ancient king who was once the lover of the banished minor deity Psamathe, better known in the Royal Court as <a href="bword://Samantha">Samantha</a>, and the father of her sand ooze daughter, <a href="bword://Mrs. Ghazi">Mrs. Ghazi</a>. He has never appeared on-page; everything known about him so far comes from what Samantha and others say about him.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: King Blaine on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/King_Blaine</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>King Croissant</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>King Croissant</b> is a a fuzzy black kitten with a teeny tiny headset microphone. He was meant as a replacement for <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>. He is level 60. He was used as a T'Ghee card by The <a href="bword://Reminiscence Hydra of Malicious Compliance">Reminiscence Hydra of Malicious Compliance</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: King Croissant on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/King_Croissant</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>King Finian</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>King Finian</b> was the King of the High Elves. He is the father of <a href="bword://Tsarina Signet">Tsarina Signet</a> and <a href="bword://Imogen">Imogen</a>. He had a relationship with Signet's <a href="bword://Mother">Mother</a>, resulting in the birth of Signet.</li><li><b>Race:</b> High Elf</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2, Chapter 6</li></ul><p class="source">Source: King Finian on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/King_Finian</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>King Rust</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>King Rust</b> is king of the <a href="bword://Skull Empire">Skull Empire</a>. He is husband to <a href="bword://Queen Consort Ugloo">Queen Consort Ugloo</a> and father to Prince <a href="bword://Stalwart">Stalwart</a>, Princess <a href="bword://Formidable">Formidable</a>, and <a href="bword://Maestro">Maestro</a>.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Orc</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Epilogue</li></ul><p class="source">Source: King Rust on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/King_Rust</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Kiwi</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Kiwi</b> is a female <a href="bword://Ursine">Ursine</a> NPC, formerly a <a href="bword://Mongoliensis">Mongoliensis</a>, first encountered in the Hunting Grounds. Deer in the Headlights Skill.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Mongoliensis</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 11, Book 5</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Kiwi on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Kiwi</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Knife of Frozen Tears</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>This blade is given to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> by <a href="bword://Tserendolgor">Tserendolgor</a> on the Eighth Floor when she gives Carl her pet <a href="bword://Garret">Garret</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Knife of Frozen Tears on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Knife_of_Frozen_Tears</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Kobold</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Kobolds</b> are a Second Floor mob that resemble chihuahuas in size and appearance, but stand upright and walk on their hind legs. They wear metal caps with a spike, and chainmail armor that appears to have been made from beer tabs.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Kobold on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Kobold</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Koki</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>Koki: origin: Japan; race/species: <a href="bword://Human">Human</a>; first scene: Chapter 14, Book 3.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Japan</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 14, Book 3</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Koki on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Koki</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Krakaren</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The Krakaren are a hive mind that runs the <a href="bword://Apothecary">Apothecary</a> and is financing the <a href="bword://Plenty">Plenty</a>.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> The Apothecary</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Krakaren on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Krakaren</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Apothecary</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Apothecary</b> is a galaxy-spanning collective mind and the entity the Dungeon caricatures as the <a href="bword://Krakaren">Krakaren</a>. "Apothecary" is the truer translation of her name, taken from her ability to synthesize elements; the dungeon's version bends that translation into an insult.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Krakaren; The Collective; The Apothecary Lady</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Apothecary on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Apothecary</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Krakaren Clone (Fourth Floor)</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b><a href="bword://Krakaren">Krakaren</a></b> on the Fourth Floor is a Borough Boss, and part of the Iron Tangle political statement. The Iron Tangle is a massive political statement by the <a href="bword://Borant Corporation">Borant Corporation</a>, and the fact that there is a version of Krakaren in the level is directed towards the actions of the <a href="bword://Apothecary">Apothecary</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon - Fourth Floor</li><li><b>Race:</b> Apothecary, Krakaren</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 10</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Krakaren Clone (Fourth Floor) on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Krakaren_Clone_%28Fourth_Floor%29</p></div></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Krakaren Clone (Fourth Floor)</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b><a href="bword://Krakaren">Krakaren</a></b> on the Fourth Floor is a Borough Boss, and part of the Iron Tangle political statement. The Iron Tangle is a massive political statement by the <a href="bword://Borant Corporation">Borant Corporation</a>, and the fact that there is a version of Krakaren in the level is directed towards the actions of the <a href="bword://Apothecary">Apothecary</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon - Fourth Floor</li><li><b>Race:</b> Apothecary, Krakaren</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 10</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Krakaren Clone (Fourth Floor) on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Krakaren_Clone_%28Fourth_Floor%29</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Krakaren Clone (Second Floor)</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b><a href="bword://Krakaren">Krakaren</a> Clone</b> is a Neighborhood Boss on the Second Floor, and part of the running <a href="bword://Rev-Up">Rev-Up</a> storyline. There are at least three separate instances of the Krakaren Clone on the level.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon - Second Floor</li><li><b>Race:</b> Apothecary</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 34</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Krakaren Clone (Second Floor) on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Krakaren_Clone_%28Second_Floor%29</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Krakaren Clone (Fourth Floor)</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b><a href="bword://Krakaren">Krakaren</a></b> on the Fourth Floor is a Borough Boss, and part of the Iron Tangle political statement. The Iron Tangle is a massive political statement by the <a href="bword://Borant Corporation">Borant Corporation</a>, and the fact that there is a version of Krakaren in the level is directed towards the actions of the <a href="bword://Apothecary">Apothecary</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon - Fourth Floor</li><li><b>Race:</b> Apothecary, Krakaren</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 10</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Krakaren Clone (Fourth Floor) on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Krakaren_Clone_%28Fourth_Floor%29</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Krakaren Clone (Second Floor)</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b><a href="bword://Krakaren">Krakaren</a> Clone</b> is a Neighborhood Boss on the Second Floor, and part of the running <a href="bword://Rev-Up">Rev-Up</a> storyline. There are at least three separate instances of the Krakaren Clone on the level.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon - Second Floor</li><li><b>Race:</b> Apothecary</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 34</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Krakaren Clone (Second Floor) on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Krakaren_Clone_%28Second_Floor%29</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Krakaren Crotch Dumplings</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Krakaren Crotch Dumplings</b> are a Fourth Floor mob that emerge from the corpse of a mob suffering from stage 3 of the DTs. Each Crotch Dumpling is about the size of a grain of rice.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Krakaren Crotch Dumplings on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Krakaren_Crotch_Dumplings</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Krasue</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 2.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Krasue</b> are a mob on the Third Floor. They are associated with the Sex Workers Who Fell from the Heavens Quest. Krasue appear as floating female heads with the entrails of the bodies hanging below.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Krasue on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Krasue</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Kravyad</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Kravyad</b> are either a boss or an NPC, depending on the person describing them, that work for the Iron Tangle, responsible for employee management. They are located at Station 435 where the employees get off the train.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Kravyad on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Kravyad</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Kua-Tin</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Kua-Tin</b> are an alien race of tiny, water-breathing, humanoid fish. They are the dominant species of the <a href="bword://Borant System">Borant System</a> and principal owners of the <a href="bword://Borant Corporation">Borant Corporation</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Kua-Tin on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Kua-Tin</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Kua-Tin Rebreather</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>Kua-Tin Rebreather</b> is roughly the size of a cat collar, and can only be equipped by knee-height creatures with gills. The small, barely noticeable device wraps around the wearer's throat to cover their gills, and occasionally sprays water and mist.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Kua-Tin</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Kua-Tin Rebreather on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Kua-Tin_Rebreather</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Kuhli</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Kuhli</b> are a spotted, gecko-like creature.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Kuhli on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Kuhli</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Kyryap</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Kyryap</b> is a mysterious "dread" entity associated with Club <a href="bword://Scolopendra">Scolopendra</a>, responsible for setting traps that have twice caught <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> unaware.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Kyryap on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Kyryap</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Lajabless</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Lajabless</b> is a race a crawler can choose upon entry to the Third Floor. It breaks the day in half, spending half the day with boosted magic (but depleted strength), or half the day with doubled strength (but magic costs more to cast).</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Lajabless on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Lajabless</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Lamashtu</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Lamashtu</b>, nicknamed "Lammy" by <a href="bword://Samantha">Samantha</a>, is a deity who has been reduced to a subjugated god and forced to serve as a donkey-mount under the control of the <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a> during the events of Book 8.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Lamashtu on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Lamashtu</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Laminak</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Laminaks</b> are a fairy-class mob found on the Dungeon's Second Floor. They are fat, human-like, crow-sized fairies with buzzing hummingbird wings. They can fly lightning fast, and their hands glow red when they cast spells.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Laminak on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Laminak</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Langley</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4,5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Langley</b> is a crawler from Dungeon Crawler World: Earth and the leader of a six-man team of fellow archers, all Finland-based car salesmen who picked the Archer Class together. He and his team become close, trusted allies of <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s party during the Fifth Floor.</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 3, Book 4</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Langley on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Langley</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Laundry Day Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Laundry Day</b> is a utility spell that strips armor off the target. Obtained by <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> on Floor 6 through her membership to the <a href="bword://Dungeon Book of the Floor Club">Dungeon Book of the Floor Club</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Laundry Day Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Laundry_Day_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Lazarus Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Lazarus Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> when he is hit by <a href="bword://Tsarina Signet">Tsarina Signet</a>'s unknown spell on the Third Floor. <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> also receives the achievement, but the reward is: <b>“You’re lucky to be alive. That’s your reward.”</b> <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> suspects it is because her health zeroed out but she was saved by her Cockroach Skill.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Lazarus Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Lazarus_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Lazarus-A-Bang-Bang</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Lazarus-A-Bang-Bang</b> is a Totem <a href="bword://T&#x27;Ghee Card">T'Ghee Card</a> on the Eighth Floor. This card is held by the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a>. It was created by combining the <a href="bword://Asojano">Asojano</a> and <a href="bword://HeyZoos">HeyZoos</a> cards.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Combo Card</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 39</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Lazarus-A-Bang-Bang on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Lazarus-A-Bang-Bang</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>LBC Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>LBC</b> is an <a href="bword://Achievement">Achievement</a> awarded when a crawler successfully taunts an opponent with a garment. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives this achievement on the Eighth Floor after getting attacked by Nightgaunts, who are driven into a rage by his <a href="bword://Enchanted Nightgaunt Cloak of Stoutness">Enchanted Nightgaunt Cloak of Stoutness</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: LBC Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/LBC_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Le Mouvement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Le Mouvement</b> was a crawler party comprised of (150) African soldiers armed with AK-47s and at least one Red Cross worker. They were featured on the third episode of <i>Dungeon Crawler World: Earth</i> and descended to the Second Floor when the countdown timer struck 6 hours.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Le Mouvement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Le_Mouvement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Left Fang of the Green Sultan</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Left Fang of the Green Sultan</b> is a saber previously owned by Eva. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> picks it up and gives it to <a href="bword://Katia Grim">Katia Grim</a> on the Fourth Floor. The saber is part of an enchanted set, but the magical abilities only apply when the set is together.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Eva</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Left Fang of the Green Sultan on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Left_Fang_of_the_Green_Sultan</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Legba</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Legba</b> is a god who is part of the <a href="bword://Orisha">Orisha</a> pantheon, with <a href="bword://Ogun">Ogun</a>, <a href="bword://Shango">Shango</a>, <a href="bword://Oshun">Oshun</a>, <a href="bword://Asojano">Asojano</a>, <a href="bword://Inle">Inle</a>, and <a href="bword://Yemaya">Yemaya</a>. During the Thorn Room Boss Battle, if his shrine is repaired: “If repaired, will give everyone a fifty percent chance to avoid all future smites. All will learn the level-15 <a href="bword://Confusing Fog Spell">Confusing Fog Spell</a>. Legba will ascend.”</li><li><b>Race:</b> Orisha Deity</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Legba on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Legba</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Legionnaires of the Damned Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><i><b>Legionnaires of the Damned</b></i> is a summoning spell that reanimates recently unequipped weapons or pieces of armor with undead wailing spirits, which are considered minions of the caster.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Legionnaires of the Damned Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Legionnaires_of_the_Damned_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Lemig Sortion</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>A democratic government consisting of multiple races. They vote on everything but to stop something they've voted on requires an 80% majority. Their leader is a fuzzy caterpillar.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Lemig Sortion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Lemig_Sortion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Leon</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Leon</b> is a <a href="bword://Dirigible Gnome">Dirigible Gnome</a> NPC from the Fifth Floor.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Dirigible Gnome</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 11</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Leon on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Leon</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Lesser Demon</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Lesser <a href="bword://Demons">Demons</a></b> are a type of Demon associated with fire. Lesser Demons often power ovens, castle heating systems, and steam-powered contraptions.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Lesser Demon on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Lesser_Demon</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Let There Be Chaos Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Let There Be Chaos Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for summoning the god <a href="bword://Grull">Grull</a> into the dungeon. Carl opens this box in a safe room on the Fifth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Let There Be Chaos Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Let_There_Be_Chaos_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Letter from the Council</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Letter from the Council</b> is a letter that is part of the <a href="bword://Gate of the Feral Gods">Gate of the Feral Gods</a> mystery. It is written by <a href="bword://Ghazi">Ghazi</a> to <a href="bword://Commandant Kane">Commandant Kane</a>. Post Script</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Letter from the Council on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Letter_from_the_Council</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Letter from the Glass Wizard</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Letter from the Glass Wizard</b> is a letter that is part of the <a href="bword://Gate of the Feral Gods">Gate of the Feral Gods</a> mystery. It is written by <a href="bword://Ghazi">Ghazi</a> to <a href="bword://Commandant Kane">Commandant Kane</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Letter from the Glass Wizard on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Letter_from_the_Glass_Wizard</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Level-Up Potion</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Level-Up Potions</b> are potions that may be awarded by quests. They presumably cause the target to gain one crawler level.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Quests</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Level-Up Potion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Level-Up_Potion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Level-Up, Baby! Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Level-Up, Baby!</b> is an <a href="bword://Achievement">Achievement</a> awarded the first time a crawler levels up. Crawlers typically gain (3) stat points each time they level up, but cannot distribute the stat points until they choose a race and class on the Third Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Level-Up, Baby! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Level-Up%2C_Baby%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Leveled-Up Frank</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Leveled-Up Frank</b> is a <a href="bword://T&#x27;Ghee Card">T'Ghee Card</a> created specifically for <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s Eighth Floor battle against the <a href="bword://Reminiscence Hydra of Malicious Compliance">Reminiscence Hydra of Malicious Compliance</a>, although it never comes into play. After the battle, Carl and Donut save this card and <a href="bword://Alpha Male Carl">Alpha Male Carl</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> Night Elf</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 47</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Leveled-Up Frank on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Leveled-Up_Frank</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Levi the 7th</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>An NPC, <b>Levi the 7th</b> is the engineer of the <i>Dismembered Unlimited</i> and the subject of the Fourth Floor Levi is on the Menu Quest. Levi the 7th is a Symbiote: a <a href="bword://Hobgoblin">Hobgoblin</a> skeleton which has been animated and merged with a <a href="bword://Flesher">Flesher</a>'s skin, which in this case once belonged to a Basher Troll. At first glance, Levi looks like "a grim reaper wearing a poncho and mask." Inspection reveals a pale, sickly creature wearing only an engineer's hat; green-tinged flesh hangs from his bony body like an ill-fitted sheet.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon: Fourth Floor</li><li><b>Race:</b> Troll Flesher and Hobgoblin Skellie Symbiote</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 12</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Levi the 7th on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Levi_the_7th</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Lexis</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Lexis</b> is <a href="bword://Odette">Odette</a>'s assistant and an associate producer of <i>Dungeon Crawler After Hours with Odette.</i> Lexis is extremely matter-of-fact and efficient in the studio and in combat. She is the first <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> <a href="bword://Human">Human</a> that <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> meet, and she explains the tunnelling and recording process clearly and concisely.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 27</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Lexis on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Lexis</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Li Jun</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Li Jun</b> is a Crawler from China. He is partied with his sister <a href="bword://Li Na">Li Na</a> and his best friend <a href="bword://Zhang">Zhang</a> within the guild <a href="bword://Safehome Yolanda">Safehome Yolanda</a>, and is a close ally of the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> China, Earth</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 42</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Li Jun on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Li_Jun</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Li Na</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Li Na</b> is a crawler from China on Dungeon Crawler World: Earth who entered the Dungeon alongside her brother <a href="bword://Li Jun">Li Jun</a> and his best friend <a href="bword://Zhang">Zhang</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> China, Earth</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Changbi Demon</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 42</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Li Na on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Li_Na</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Li Jun</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Li Jun</b> is a Crawler from China. He is partied with his sister <a href="bword://Li Na">Li Na</a> and his best friend <a href="bword://Zhang">Zhang</a> within the guild <a href="bword://Safehome Yolanda">Safehome Yolanda</a>, and is a close ally of the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> China, Earth</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 42</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Li Jun on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Li_Jun</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Li Na</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Li Na</b> is a crawler from China on Dungeon Crawler World: Earth who entered the Dungeon alongside her brother <a href="bword://Li Jun">Li Jun</a> and his best friend <a href="bword://Zhang">Zhang</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> China, Earth</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Changbi Demon</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 42</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Li Na on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Li_Na</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Li Jun</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Li Jun</b> is a Crawler from China. He is partied with his sister <a href="bword://Li Na">Li Na</a> and his best friend <a href="bword://Zhang">Zhang</a> within the guild <a href="bword://Safehome Yolanda">Safehome Yolanda</a>, and is a close ally of the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> China, Earth</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 42</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Li Jun on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Li_Jun</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Li Na</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Li Na</b> is a crawler from China on Dungeon Crawler World: Earth who entered the Dungeon alongside her brother <a href="bword://Li Jun">Li Jun</a> and his best friend <a href="bword://Zhang">Zhang</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> China, Earth</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Changbi Demon</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 42</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Li Na on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Li_Na</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Lightning Lou</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Lightning Lou</b> was an elderly bloodhound who lived at a gas station near the Shepherd's House in Homestead, Florida, before the transformation.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Homestead, FL</li><li><b>Race:</b> Dog</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 50</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Lightning Lou on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Lightning_Lou</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Lika</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Lika</b> is the fictional protagonist of <i>Troubadour's Bounty,</i> a popular series of plays performed in Larracos on the Ninth Floor. A half-<a href="bword://Naiad">Naiad</a> half-<a href="bword://Human">Human</a> bard cleric, her character is loosely inspired by an "inaccurate history of Psamathe."</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> Half-Naiad, Half-Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 21</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Lika on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Lika</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Like a Moth to the Flame Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Like a Moth to the Flame</b> is a rare achievement granted the first time a crawler deals damage to a mob more than 75 levels above them. Both <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> receive this achievement after their first encounter with the <a href="bword://Rage Elemental">Rage Elemental</a> on the Second Floor: Donut for hitting it with <i><a href="bword://Magic Missile">Magic Missile</a></i>, and Carl for striking it with a <a href="bword://Carl&#x27;s Jug O&#x27;Boom">Carl's Jug O'Boom</a>. This is the second Platinum award Carl receives inside the Dungeon, after the Platinum <a href="bword://Shoe Box">Shoe Box</a> awarded for the This Little Piggy Went to Market! achievement.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Like a Moth to the Flame Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Like_a_Moth_to_the_Flame_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Limp Richard</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Limp Richard</b> is a <a href="bword://Mole Man">Mole Man</a> NPC who operates a general store <i>"Limp Richard's Sundries"</i> at station 83 in the Iron Tangle. Described as a short, squat anthropomorphized mole, complete with reading glasses. He sits in the doorway to his shop reading a book. He runs a general store, but most of the products are not very noteworthy.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Mole Man</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 2</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Limp Richard on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Limp_Richard</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Liquid Therapy</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Liquid Therapy</b> is a potion that protects against insanity, blindness and a host of other debuffs. It lasts until you sleep. <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> brewed this for <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> to protect them from <a href="bword://Shi Maria">Shi Maria</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Liquid Therapy on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Liquid_Therapy</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Liquified Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Liquified Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for blowing himself up with the Waffle Maker bomb during the Attack on <a href="bword://Club Vanquisher">Club Vanquisher</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Liquified Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Liquified_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Literal Fire Ants</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Literal Fire Ants</b> are a Fourth Floor mob that is part of a trap in the luggage of the Reward Room of the Yellow Line train car on the Iron Tangle.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Literal Fire Ants on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Literal_Fire_Ants</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Live Ammo Ball</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>Live ammo balls are a common and versatile ranged weapon of the Dirigible Gnomes. These round, clamshell spheres are designed to be fired great distances using a gnomish Tickle Stick, or they may be manually lobbed like a grenade. They are also fired in large clusters from anti-aircraft point defense batteries. Just be glad you’re not in charge of cleaning up that mess.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Live Ammo Ball on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Live_Ammo_Ball</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Li Jun</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Li Jun</b> is a Crawler from China. He is partied with his sister <a href="bword://Li Na">Li Na</a> and his best friend <a href="bword://Zhang">Zhang</a> within the guild <a href="bword://Safehome Yolanda">Safehome Yolanda</a>, and is a close ally of the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> China, Earth</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 42</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Li Jun on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Li_Jun</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Li Na</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Li Na</b> is a crawler from China on Dungeon Crawler World: Earth who entered the Dungeon alongside her brother <a href="bword://Li Jun">Li Jun</a> and his best friend <a href="bword://Zhang">Zhang</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> China, Earth</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Changbi Demon</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 42</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Li Na on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Li_Na</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Locomotive Breath Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Locomotive Breath Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for engineering a train derailment of the <i>Ochre Line</i>on the Fourth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Locomotive Breath Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Locomotive_Breath_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Loita</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Loita</b> works in the <a href="bword://Borant Corporation">Borant Corporation</a>'s Communications Department. As a <a href="bword://Kua-Tin">Kua-Tin</a> member of the <a href="bword://Borant System">Borant System</a>'s ruling ultra-nationalist party, the <a href="bword://Bloom">Bloom</a>, Loita receives preferential treatment and has her pick of crawlers. <a href="bword://Hekla">Hekla</a> and <a href="bword://Brynhild&#x27;s Daughters">Brynhild's Daughters</a> were her main accounts until the party disbanded on the Fourth Floor.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Kua-Tin</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 34, Book 3</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Loita on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Loita</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Loner Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The seventh and final achievement <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives upon entering the Dungeon. Presumably, all Crawlers who entered the first floor alone received this achievement, including <a href="bword://Miriam Dom">Miriam Dom</a> and <a href="bword://Lucia Mar">Lucia Mar</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Loner Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Loner_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Long Haul Biological Waste Management Solutions</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Long Haul Biological Waste Management Solutions</b> is a DBA and front company for the <a href="bword://Open Intellect Pacifist Action Network">Open Intellect Pacifist Action Network</a> (OIPAN), an intergalactic NFC.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Open Intellect Pacifist Action Network</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Long Haul Biological Waste Management Solutions on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Long_Haul_Biological_Waste_Management_Solutions</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Lonnie</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Lonnie</b> is a half-elf former crawler and the head of the Beefy Boys SOF, a squad of mages responsible for maintaining wall buffs and base shields for the <a href="bword://Princess Posse">Princess Posse</a> during the Ninth Floor Faction Wars, until a gondii brain worm takes control of his corpse and turns him into a security threat from within.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Lonnie on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Lonnie</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Celestial Loot Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Celestial Loot Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> on the Eighth Floor for picking up <a href="bword://Quan Ch">Quan Ch</a>'s <a href="bword://Celestial">Celestial</a> <a href="bword://Cloak of the Benevolent Champion">Cloak of the Benevolent Champion</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Celestial Loot Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Celestial_Loot_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Loot Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Loot!</b> is an achievement awarded the first time a crawler equips a clothing item they found or received inside the Dungeon. Most crawlers should receive this achievement on the first two floors.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Loot Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Loot_Achievement</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Loot Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Loot!</b> is an achievement awarded the first time a crawler equips a clothing item they found or received inside the Dungeon. Most crawlers should receive this achievement on the first two floors.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Loot Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Loot_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Loot Boxes</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Loot Boxes</b> are the primary reward mechanism in Dungeon Crawler World, distributed by the <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a> to crawlers for completing achievements, defeating bosses, finishing quests, or as gifts from viewers and sponsors.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Achievements; Boss kills; Quests; Patrons and viewers</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Loot Boxes on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Loot_Boxes</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Loot Punch Card</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Loot Punch Card</b> is an item that <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> received as part of the <a href="bword://Celestial Loot Achievement">Celestial Loot Achievement</a>. The Loot Punch Card is a little piece of paper with five slots with one slot punched out with a hole in the shape of a foot when Carl receives it.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Celestial Loot Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Loot Punch Card on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Loot_Punch_Card</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Looter Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Looter Boxes</b> are <a href="bword://Loot Boxes">Loot Boxes</a> typically awarded for inventory- or looting-related achievements.</li><li><b>Source:</b> achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Looter Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Looter_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Lord of the Flies Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Lord of the Flies Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for setting a trap that a Crawler triggers. <a href="bword://Tserendolgor">Tserendolgor</a>'s team is the one who triggers the trap.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Lord of the Flies Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Lord_of_the_Flies_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Lorelai</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Lorelai</b> is a Level 7 <a href="bword://Goblin Shamanka">Goblin Shamanka</a> NPC who appears on the First Floor. Her name was assigned by <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>. As a Shamanka, Lorelai specializes in Anguish Magic, which focuses and enhances attack damage. She and <a href="bword://Rory">Rory</a> are second only to the Goblin Chieftan, and are keenly aware that they are mobs inside a construct. When the floor collapses, they "go to sleep until the next Dungeon opens." They believe that if they kill enough crawlers, they will be moved to a lower level.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> Goblins</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 15</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Lorelai on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Lorelai</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Louis</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Louis Santiago 2</b> is an Earth Crawler and a loyal ally of <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and Princess <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>. Introduced on the Fifth Floor as a drunk, badly under-leveled Pest Exterminator, he grows into the group's pilot and a member of <a href="bword://Team Katia">Team Katia</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Miami, Florida, Earth</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 3</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Louis on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Louis</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Low Thi</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Low Thi</b> is one of the crawlers in the Subterranean Quadrant of Bubble #543. Killed <a href="bword://Wynne">Wynne</a> believing doing so would give him access to a map and allow him to complete his quest.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 6</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Low Thi on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Low_Thi</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Luca Di</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Luca Di</b> is Crawler #10,284,471, a human Pastamancer who reached Level 62 before taking a deal at the end of the 9th floor, and the author of an entry in <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s "A Banquet Fit for a Princess" cookbook.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Luca Di on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Luca_Di</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Lucia Mar</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Lucia Mar</b> is a young teenage Crawler from South America, one of the Top Ten Crawlers on this season of <i>Dungeon Crawler World</i> and an early rival of <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Diah, Azra, Yaz, Jill</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Ecuador</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Lajabless</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 14</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Lucia Mar on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Lucia_Mar</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Lucian</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Lucian</b> ("Judge Lucian") is a cat show judge from Princess <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s life before the Transformation, later reconstituted by the <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a> as the keymaster head of the <a href="bword://Reminiscence Hydra of Malicious Compliance">Reminiscence Hydra of Malicious Compliance</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Lucian on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Lucian</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Lucienne</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Lucienne. Mandagot. Level 81 Fink.</b> One of two members of Team Sparkles. Warning: This creature worships <a href="bword://Diwata">Diwata</a> and will be automatically hostile toward you because Diwata HATES your ass. A mandagot is a <a href="bword://Fairy">Fairy</a>-class creature that comes in many shapes, though most are stomach-churning monstrosities that are supposed to be “cute.” These things are a combination of two or three fuzzy woodland creatures. Legend has it that they are born of regular fairies who’ve had relations with forest animals, which is a pretty common occurrence with the freaks who worship Diwata.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Mandagot, Fairy-class</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 8, Chapter 5</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Lucienne on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Lucienne</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Lucky Bastard Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Lucky Bastard Box</b> is a loot box awarded for being very lucky. The contents vary, but higher tier boxes contain mostly gambling items such as casino chips and scratch-off tickets similar to those found in gas stations or liquor stores.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Lucky Bastard Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Lucky_Bastard_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Lucky Bitch Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Lucky Bitch Box</b> is a Loot Box distributed to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for the <a href="bword://Liquified Achievement">Liquified Achievement</a> during Operation Snake Pit.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Liquified Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Lucky Bitch Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Lucky_Bitch_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Luke</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6,7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Luke</b> is a Level 64 Lemig Goblin, a General in the Democratic Sortion, and the beloved companion of <a href="bword://Commander Stockade">Commander Stockade</a> of the <a href="bword://Lemig Sortion">Lemig Sortion</a>, whose death sets off the tragic final act of Stockade's storyline.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Luke on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Luke</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Lunette</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Lunette</b> is the mother of <a href="bword://Tsarina Signet">Tsarina Signet</a>. She was a princess of the <a href="bword://Naiad Confederacy">Naiad Confederacy</a> before copulating with <a href="bword://King Finian">King Finian</a> and giving birth to Signet.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Tsarina Signet's mother</li><li><b>Race:</b> Naiad</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 5, Chapter 73</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Lunette on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Lunette</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Lusca</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Lusca</b> is a boss on the Fifth Floor.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Octo-Shark</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Lusca on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Lusca</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Lutin</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>Crawlers may choose the <b>Lutin</b> race on the Third Floor. Lutins (or, if female, <b>lutines</b> ) are gnome-like creatures that specialize in support magic.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Lutin on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Lutin</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Macro AI</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Macro AIs</b> are an ancient, alien artificial intelligence designed to be installed inside <a href="bword://Primal">Primal</a> Engines. Once properly installed and fully melded with the engine, they have the ability "to seemingly alter the physics and reality of the worlds around them."</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Macro AI on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Macro_AI</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Madison</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Madison</b> is a <a href="bword://Human">Human</a> Resources Associate on the Iron Tangle. She boards the <a href="bword://Nightmare Express">Nightmare Express</a> in Trainyard E and gets off at station 60. <b>Madison</b> is the benefits manager for the <a href="bword://Kravyad">Kravyad</a> and the Station Mimics.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 17</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Madison on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Madison</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Maestro</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Prince Maestro</b> is the younger son of <a href="bword://King Rust">King Rust</a> of the <a href="bword://Skull Empire">Skull Empire</a> and <a href="bword://Queen Consort Ugloo">Queen Consort Ugloo</a>, younger brother of Prince <a href="bword://Stalwart">Stalwart</a>, and elder brother of Princess <a href="bword://Formidable">Formidable</a>. He is formerly the host of the show Death Watch Extreme Dungeon Mayhem, and his rivalry with <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and Princess <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> escalates into an intergalactic incident.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> The Maestro, Pork Boy, Carl's Naughty Little Piggie, Former Prince Maestro</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Skull Empire</li><li><b>Race:</b> Orc</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 42</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Maestro on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Maestro</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Maggie My</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Maggie My</b> is a Crawler from Earth who enters the Dungeon alongside <a href="bword://Frank Q">Frank Q</a> and their teenage daughter <a href="bword://Yvette">Yvette</a>. After Yvette dies on the First Floor, Maggie turns her attention almost entirely to hunting <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Mags</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Seattle, WA</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Infiltrator</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 20</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Maggie My on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Maggie_My</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Magic &amp; Spells</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Magic</b> is a core Dungeon mechanic through which Crawlers and other entities wield highly advanced <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> technology disguised as fantasy magic. The dungeon presents these effects as traditional spellcasting, but <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> explains that the distinction is mostly cosmetic: the underlying technology is so far beyond a crawler's comprehension that, for all practical purposes, it simply is magic.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Magic &amp; Spells on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Magic_%26_Spells</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Magic Item Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>Magic Item Box</b> is a type of Loot Box that appears to be awarded to crawlers who practice magic on the First Floor. <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> receives this box on the First Floor for being one of the first 100 crawlers to level up <a href="bword://Magic Missile">Magic Missile</a> to level 3. <i>Loot</i></li><li><b>Source:</b> Achievements</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Magic Item Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Magic_Item_Box</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Magic &amp; Spells</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Magic</b> is a core Dungeon mechanic through which Crawlers and other entities wield highly advanced <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> technology disguised as fantasy magic. The dungeon presents these effects as traditional spellcasting, but <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> explains that the distinction is mostly cosmetic: the underlying technology is so far beyond a crawler's comprehension that, for all practical purposes, it simply is magic.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Magic &amp; Spells on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Magic_%26_Spells</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Magic Item Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>Magic Item Box</b> is a type of Loot Box that appears to be awarded to crawlers who practice magic on the First Floor. <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> receives this box on the First Floor for being one of the first 100 crawlers to level up <a href="bword://Magic Missile">Magic Missile</a> to level 3. <i>Loot</i></li><li><b>Source:</b> Achievements</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Magic Item Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Magic_Item_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Magic Missile</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Magic Missile</b> is a basic ranged attack spell that fires bolts of energy from the caster's eyes, one after another, resembling laser blasts from a science fiction film. It is the signature attack of <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>, who taught it to herself on the First Floor moments after <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> activated her menus.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Magic Missile on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Magic_Missile</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Magistrate Featherfall</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 2.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Magistrate Featherfall</b> is the magistrate of the medium <a href="bword://Skyfowl">Skyfowl</a> settlement on the Third Floor. As Magistrate, he is effectively the mayor of the Medium Skyfowl Settlement. Before the cataclysm, the Skyfowl ruled the whole Over City and he would have had to report to a regional governor, who would report to a royal chancellor, who would report to someone in a city on the 9th floor.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Skyfowl</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Magistrate Featherfall on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Magistrate_Featherfall</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Magnificent Troy</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>An orc with a sportscoat and tie. A sports broadcaster outside the dungeon.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Outworld</li><li><b>Race:</b> Orc</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Magnificent Troy on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Magnificent_Troy</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Major Charlie Potion</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Major Charlie Potion</b> is a potion that raises your intelligence by 10 point for 30 seconds, afterwards it lowers your intelligence by 10 point for 5 minuets.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Major Charlie Potion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Major_Charlie_Potion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Makeup Sex is the Best Sex Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Makeup Sex is the Best Sex Box</b> is presumably one of the <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a>'s "discretionary" loot boxes. It is awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> on the Fifth Floor.</li><li><b>Source:</b> System AI's Smush fetish Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Makeup Sex is the Best Sex Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Makeup_Sex_is_the_Best_Sex_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Makeup Table</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Makeup Table</b> is a crafting workbench that allows crawlers with shapeshifting abilities to better see while forming into shapes. <a href="bword://Katia Grim">Katia Grim</a> uses this bench to work on her <a href="bword://Doppelgänger">Doppelgänger</a> race to work on her Walk in Their Shoes Skill.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Marketplace</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Makeup Table on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Makeup_Table</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Male Thorny Devil</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Male Thorny Devil</b> are a mob on the Fifth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Male Thorny Devil on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Male_Thorny_Devil</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Man of God Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Man of God Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> when he pledges himself as an adherent to the god <a href="bword://Emberus">Emberus</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Man of God Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Man_of_God_Achievement</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mana Genita</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Mana Genita</b> is a god, the details about them are currently unknown. She's supposedly big on spells. The <a href="bword://Enchanted Tiara of Mana Genita">Enchanted Tiara of Mana Genita</a> appears to be named for her. The tiara is fit for royalty, made in honor of all the lost children of the world.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> God</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mana Genita on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mana_Genita</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mana Potion</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Regular Mana Potions</b> instantly and completely refill a character's Mana Points. These are commonly found in <a href="bword://Loot Boxes">Loot Boxes</a> on the first six floors of the Dungeon.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Loot Boxes</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mana Potion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mana_Potion</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mana Genita</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Mana Genita</b> is a god, the details about them are currently unknown. She's supposedly big on spells. The <a href="bword://Enchanted Tiara of Mana Genita">Enchanted Tiara of Mana Genita</a> appears to be named for her. The tiara is fit for royalty, made in honor of all the lost children of the world.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> God</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mana Genita on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mana_Genita</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mana Potion</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Regular Mana Potions</b> instantly and completely refill a character's Mana Points. These are commonly found in <a href="bword://Loot Boxes">Loot Boxes</a> on the first six floors of the Dungeon.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Loot Boxes</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mana Potion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mana_Potion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mana Toast</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Mana Toast</b> is a burned triangle of toast that restores mana. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> each receive one piece of toast from a metallic toaster oven in an unmanned safe room on the Second Floor. Donut puts both pieces into her inventory.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Safe Room</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mana Toast on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mana_Toast</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Manasa</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Manasa</b> is a famous <a href="bword://Naga">Naga</a> pop singer with a haunting soprano voice. Physically large, her black-and-silver cobra head appears to have a meter-wide hood.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Naga | Gondii</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2, Chapter 19</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Manasa on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Manasa</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>ManTauR</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>Mantaur</b> is a mob found on the Fourth Floor and lower levels. They are often associated with <a href="bword://Club Vanquisher">Club Vanquisher</a>. A mantaur is like a centaur, but the standard human torso sprouts from a larger human body, right where the neck would be. The smaller upper half supports a human head and a set of arms; the larger lower half has another set of big, muscular arms and legs. Mantaurs run and stand on all four rear limbs. Their voices sound human, but they speak loudly and boisterously.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: ManTauR on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/ManTauR</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mantis</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Mantis</b> (plural <b>mantises</b> or <b>mantids</b>) is an insectoid <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> race resembling giant praying mantises. Mantis hunters of the <a href="bword://Dark Hive">Dark Hive</a> hunted <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> on the Sixth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mantis on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mantis</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Map</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>By default, the <b>Minimap</b> appears in the bottom right corner of a crawler's Heads-Up Display (HUD). The basic minimap is a simple blue and gray map which shows the cardinal directions (North/South/East/West) and represents nearby creatures as dots.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Heads-Up Display (HUD)</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Map on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Map</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Map of the Stars</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>Adds boss locations and descriptions to a large area of the map.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Map of the Stars on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Map_of_the_Stars</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mapping Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Mapping</b> is a spell whose only appearance in the text is as the title of a scroll offered as a prize at the Butcher's Masquerade Ball. Its name implies some kind of mapping function, but the text never confirms what it actually does.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mapping Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mapping_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Marked for Life Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Marked for Life Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for being marked for death by the god <a href="bword://Diwata">Diwata</a> but surviving the encounter.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Marked for Life Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Marked_for_Life_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Martha Stewart Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Martha Stewart Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for using his <a href="bword://Engineer&#x27;s Table">Engineer's Table</a> for the first time.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Martha Stewart Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Martha_Stewart_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mass Casualty Event Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Mass Casualty Event Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> when blew up a bomb in Zockau killing 200+ <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a> and 35 hunters.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mass Casualty Event Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mass_Casualty_Event_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mass Layoffs Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a> distributes the <b>Mass Layoffs! <a href="bword://Achievement">Achievement</a></b> on March 20 to all crawlers who survive the second phase of the Eighth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mass Layoffs Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mass_Layoffs_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Massage Coupon</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Massage Coupon</b> is a coupon for a free massage at the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>. Entitles the owner plus one companion to a one hour massage at the penis parade or penis palace backroom relaxation spa.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Massage Coupon on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Massage_Coupon</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Maxim Popov</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>Maxim Popov: race/species: <a href="bword://Human">Human</a> | <a href="bword://Nodling">Nodling</a>; class: Bogatyr Class.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Nodling</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Maxim Popov on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Maxim_Popov</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Meadow Lark</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Meadow Lark</b> is a crawler Party made up of the overnight staff and residents of an eldercare facility on Earth, allied with the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a> beginning during their descent through the First Floor and Second Floor.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Team Meadow Lark</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Meadow Lark on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Meadow_Lark</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Meat Hook Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Meat Hook Spell</b> is a spell that summons all nearby carnivorous pet-class monsters away from their owners and to the source of the burning-stench.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Meat Hook Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Meat_Hook_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Meatus</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Meatus</b> is a deity that is a god. After <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> casts her <a href="bword://War Crimes Spell">War Crimes Spell</a>, and Meatus is chopped into pieces, the <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a> closes the Scavenger's Daughter eye because "even she doesn't want to look at that."</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> God</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Meatus on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Meatus</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mechanic's Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Mechanic's Boxes</b> are <a href="bword://Loot Boxes">Loot Boxes</a> awarded for building contraptions inside the Dungeon. They typically contain crafting tools.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Battlefield Construction Achievement; Grease Monkey Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mechanic's Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mechanic%27s_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Meet an Elite Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Meet an Elite</b> <a href="bword://Achievement">Achievement</a> is awarded to crawlers the first time they encounter an Elite, typically on the Third Floor or Sixth Floor. The reward modifies the crawler's Minimap.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Meet an Elite Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Meet_an_Elite_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mehmet Or</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Mehmet Or</b> is Crawler #3,756,330, a human Sipahi who reached Level 62 before taking a deal to exit the dungeon, and the author of an entry in <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s "Book of Boom" cookbook.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mehmet Or on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mehmet_Or</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Meld Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Meld</b> is a process, related to but distinct from Split Personality, in which one creature consumes and joins with another, combining two minds into one.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Meld Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Meld_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Memorial Crystal</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Memorial Crystals</b> are extremely rare and powerful artifacts created upon the death of gods or demigods. Memorial Crystals are physically similar to soul crystals, but where a soul crystal merely stores raw soul power, a memorial crystal is packed with information -- the god-tier spells and knowledge of the deity who died to create it.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Dropped by fallen Gods and Demigods</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Memorial Crystal on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Memorial_Crystal</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Menagerie Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Menagerie Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded for discovering a pet Reward Room.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Menagerie Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Menagerie_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Menerva</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8,Backstage at the Pineapple Cabaret.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Menerva</b> is a former crawler and schoolteacher who was left behind on the Eleventh Floor generations ago by her party member <a href="bword://Porthus">Porthus</a>, and who, believed dead by him ever since, secretly survived to help build the Pineapple Cabaret alongside the cookbook author <a href="bword://Herot">Herot</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Menerva on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Menerva</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mentally Unstable Clothing Hoarder Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Mentally Unstable Clothing Hoarder Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for collecting over 700 conductors hats from other crawlers that were part of the Vermillion Line Rescue to help others trapped at the End of the Line Rescue on the Iron Tangle.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mentally Unstable Clothing Hoarder Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mentally_Unstable_Clothing_Hoarder_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Metal Working Table</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Metal Working Table</b> is a crafting workbench that allows crawlers to manipulate metal by forming and shaping metal. Level 2 (5th floor) - Can view the tensile strength and load limits, and the interface had more shaping options.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Marketplace</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Metal Working Table on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Metal_Working_Table</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mexx</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Mexx</b> appears to be a brand of robotic limited artificial intelligence designed to manage <a href="bword://Senegal Production Systems">Senegal Production Systems</a> Production Trailers and instruct crawlers on tunnel appearances. It looks like a metallic, jet-black floating frisbee with a single blue light flashing on its edge, and typically hovers near the ceiling when not interacting with crawlers. It speaks in a soothing but emotionless robotic female voice.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mexx on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mexx</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Midnight Epicure Upgrade Patch</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Midnight Epicure Upgrade Patch</b> is an <a href="bword://Upgrade Patch">Upgrade Patch</a> given to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> on the Sixth Floor in a Gold <a href="bword://Benefactor Box">Benefactor Box</a> from the <a href="bword://Plenty">Plenty</a>. This patch is applied to the <a href="bword://Enchanted Anarchist&#x27;s Battle Rattle">Enchanted Anarchist's Battle Rattle</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Gold Benefactor Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Midnight Epicure Upgrade Patch on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Midnight_Epicure_Upgrade_Patch</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mike Barnes</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Mike Barnes</b> is one of the crawlers in the Subterranean Quadrant of Bubble #543. He shoots banana tree seeds from his hand. Since he's a druid, he can make the seeds sprout really fast afterwards, which makes for a surprisingly effective attack. Another crawler laments that the range of his attacks is really low.</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 6, Book 4</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mike Barnes on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mike_Barnes</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Milk</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Milk</b> is a former crawler and the author of the <i><a href="bword://Dungeon Anarchist&#x27;s Cookbook">Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook</a> (Item)</i> (6th Edition). Milk is from a clawed race with annual migration patterns. She lived on an island with her family before entering the Dungeon. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> described her in dungeon race as a half frog - half bat hybrid.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Vesper and later Xenopus in dungeon</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 27</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Milk on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Milk</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Milk of Lamashtu Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b><a href="bword://Milk">Milk</a> of <a href="bword://Lamashtu">Lamashtu</a></b> is a spell whose only appearance in the text is as the title of a scroll offered as a prize at the Butcher's Masquerade Ball. Nothing about what the spell actually does is ever revealed, and its name is not explicitly connected to the deity Lamashtu anywhere in the text.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Milk of Lamashtu Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Milk_of_Lamashtu_Spell</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Milk of Lamashtu Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b><a href="bword://Milk">Milk</a> of <a href="bword://Lamashtu">Lamashtu</a></b> is a spell whose only appearance in the text is as the title of a scroll offered as a prize at the Butcher's Masquerade Ball. Nothing about what the spell actually does is ever revealed, and its name is not explicitly connected to the deity Lamashtu anywhere in the text.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Milk of Lamashtu Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Milk_of_Lamashtu_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Milquetoast Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Milquetoast</b> is an <a href="bword://Achievement">Achievement</a> awarded when a crawler wins an important boss battle without killed the boss. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives this achievement on the Fifth Floor for defeating <a href="bword://Mrs. Ghazi">Mrs. Ghazi</a> without killing her. He receives a <a href="bword://Potion of Bloodlust">Potion of Bloodlust</a> in the reward box.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Milquetoast Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Milquetoast_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mind Horror</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Mind Horrors</b> are a level 4 Second Floor mob. They use mostly psionic attacks and look like jellyfish with brains. They are related to the Third Floor mob, <a href="bword://Brain Boiler">Brain Boiler</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mind Horror on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mind_Horror</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mined Material Reclamation Act</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Mined Material Reclamation Act</b> is a <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> law pertaining to the rights of planets to their mineral wealth.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mined Material Reclamation Act on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mined_Material_Reclamation_Act</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Minge</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>Level 225 Minor Feral Demon. Younger sister of <a href="bword://Slit">Slit</a>. Pulled out of The Nothing into the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a> during Eighth Floor after <a href="bword://Samantha">Samantha</a> visited the casino there.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Minor Feral Demon</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 32, Book 6</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Minge on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Minge</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Minion Army Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><i><b>Minion Army</b></i> is an expensive war spell that causes hostile enemies to fight for you rather than against you. Although it is a powerful mass-charm spell suited for battlefield sabotage, it is almost impossible to train beyond level one due to its casting time and the high risk of failure.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Minion Army Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Minion_Army_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Minister of Blood-Letting</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Minister of Blood-Letting</b> is a Level 98 Dark Ghoul Papist, the leader of a racing team piloting a Wienermobile during the Tenth Floor's heats, and a regular karaoke performer at a bar frequented by racers.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Minister of Blood-Letting on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Minister_of_Blood-Letting</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Minus</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Minus</b> is a <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> security soldier posing as a tourist named <b>Linus</b>. He infiltrates the Tenth Floor of the World Dungeon pretending to be a creepy superfan of the crawler Elle in order to carry out an assassination mission.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Linus</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Teelan-3</li><li><b>Race:</b> Soother</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 8, Chapter 15</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Minus on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Minus</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Miriam Dom</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Miriam Dom</b> is an Earth crawler who entered the Dungeon with fifteen goats and crawls alongside two of them, <a href="bword://Prepotente">Prepotente</a> and <a href="bword://Bianca">Bianca</a>. Known to the audience as the goat lady long before anyone learned her name, she debuts at number five on the first leaderboard.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Goat Lady</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Italy</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Human | Vampire (5th Floor)</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 47</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Miriam Dom on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Miriam_Dom</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Miss Quill</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Miss Quill</b> is an elderly skyfowl NPC on the Third Floor and the assistant to <a href="bword://Magistrate Featherfall">Magistrate Featherfall</a> in the Medium <a href="bword://Skyfowl">Skyfowl</a> Settlement. She is secretly the settlement's true ruler and the neighborhood boss behind the murders at the heart of the Sex Workers Who Fell from the Heavens Quest, which places her in opposition to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Quill</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Third Floor</li><li><b>Race:</b> Skyfowl</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2, Chapter 18</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Miss Quill on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Miss_Quill</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mistress Tiatha</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><i>Mistress Tiatha'</i> is the manager for team <a href="bword://Elle McGibbons">Elle McGibbons</a>. She has a drinking problem and smokes blitz sticks. She once managed to charm a boss.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Miss T</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Former Crawler</li><li><b>Race:</b> Half elf</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 22</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mistress Tiatha on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mistress_Tiatha</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mold Lion</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Mold Lions</b> were once an attraction at <a href="bword://Grimaldi">Grimaldi</a>'s Traveling Circus on the Third Floor but were transformed by <a href="bword://Scolopendra">Scolopendra</a>'s curse. Regular-sized male lions, their manes are made of waving pink and green finger-like worms. At least one eye glows emerald. Half of their matted bodies are splattered in a pulsating green, lumpy, glowing fungus. When the lion is killed, the worms die and mold turns black before oozing off of the corpse; if a single microscopic spore of the mold returns to Grimaldi, the lion will regrow by the next day. The lions attack by pouncing, and slashing with claws and teeth.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mold Lion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mold_Lion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mole Man</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Mole Man</b> are a race that are common as NPC traders on the Fourth Floor. They spend most of their days and nights reading. A Mole Man, <a href="bword://Limp Richard">Limp Richard</a>, trades books with <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mole Man on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mole_Man</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Molly Maguires Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> got "The Molly Maguires" achievement when he entered the <a href="bword://Guild of Suffering">Guild of Suffering</a> for the first time.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Molly Maguires Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Molly_Maguires_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mongo</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Mongo</b> is a Dungeon-generated, pet-class <a href="bword://Mongoliensis">Mongoliensis</a> mob and the bonded "Royal Steed" of Princess <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>. He is the mascot and an integral member of the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a>, serving as a fierce melee combatant, loyal protector, and mount for Donut.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Murder Chicken</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Second Floor Pet Reward Room</li><li><b>Race:</b> Mongoliensis</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 46</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mongo on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mongo</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mongo's Teeth Caps</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 2.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b><a href="bword://Enchanted Fang Caps of the Expectorating Tizheruk">Enchanted Fang Caps of the Expectorating Tizheruk</a></b> is a fleeting item that can be placed on the teeth of either a crawler or pet to increase their biting damage. They are gold in color and little tendrils of electricity spark when the teeth are snapped. They are currently worn by <a href="bword://Mongo">Mongo</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Platinum Quest Box from the Show Must Go On Quest</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mongo's Teeth Caps on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mongo%27s_Teeth_Caps</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Fang Caps of the Expectorating Tizheruk</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 2.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Enchanted Fang Caps of the Expectorating Tizheruk</b> is a fleeting item that can be placed on the teeth of either a crawler or pet to increase their biting damage. They are gold in color and little tendrils of electricity spark when the teeth are snapped. They are currently worn by <a href="bword://Mongo">Mongo</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Platinum Quest Box from the Show Must Go On Quest</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Fang Caps of the Expectorating Tizheruk on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Fang_Caps_of_the_Expectorating_Tizheruk</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mongoliensis</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>Mongoliensis</b> is basically a velociraptor. In the Dungeon, they may be encountered as dangerous floor mobs or acquired as level one pet-class mobs.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mongoliensis on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mongoliensis</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Monk Seal</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Monk Seal</b> are a race on the Eighth Floor in Cuba.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Monk Seal on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Monk_Seal</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Monobrow Sam</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book All.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Monobrow Sam</b> is a friend of <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s from before the Transformation. The two used to play video games together and trade friendly insults, and later his memory is weaponized against Carl in the form of a hydra head armed with a death ray.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Monobrow Sam on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Monobrow_Sam</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Moon Reaper</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Moon Reaper</b> are a mob type found on both the Tenth Floor and Fifteenth Floor. <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> takes this as his initial form on the Tenth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Moon Reaper on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Moon_Reaper</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mordecai</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Mordecai</b> is a former crawler and a Level 50 Non-Combatant NPC who serves as Princess <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> and <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s reluctant but dedicated Manager. Originally the party's Game Guide in the Tutorial Guild, he is working off an indentureship on his last tour of crawl duty.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Morty, Uncle Morty, Uncle Mordecai</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Skyfowl Planet</li><li><b>Race:</b> Skyfowl (Original) | Changeling</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 2</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mordecai on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mordecai</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mordecai's Special Brew</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> brews <b>Mordecai's Special Brew</b> on the Fourth Floor using the level 3 <a href="bword://Alchemy Table">Alchemy Table</a>. The potion is constant healing mixed with rapid regeneration, healing almost anything for 30 seconds. It won't protect from anything that will kill instantly, like being blown up or decapitated.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Mordecai's Alchemy Table</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mordecai's Special Brew on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mordecai%27s_Special_Brew</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Morris</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>One of the crawlers in the Subterranean Quadrant of Bubble #543. His race is <a href="bword://Arachnid">Arachnid</a>, which is essentially a spider-taur. He has a human torso and a spider body where his legs should be, similar to <a href="bword://Odette">Odette</a>'s crab body.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Arachnid</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 6, Book 4</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Morris on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Morris</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mother</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s Mother</b> is the mother of crawler Carl. Carl's mother's father played center for Oregon State before becoming a prison guard.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mother on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mother</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Bea's Mother</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Bea's Mom</b> is portrayed as having been a mean spirited woman and a bad influence on <a href="bword://Beatrice">Beatrice</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>. She was highly religious and had had plastic surgery. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> describes her as having "...perfect, tight, face-lifted cheeks."</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: USA</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2, Chapter 12</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Bea's Mother on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Bea%27s_Mother</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mother of All Bombs</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Mother of All Bombs</b> (also called <b>MOAB</b> or the <b>Bomb Chicken</b>) was crafted by <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>, <a href="bword://Brandon Andrews">Brandon Andrews</a>, and <a href="bword://Chris Andrews">Chris Andrews</a> on the Second Floor to lure the <a href="bword://Rage Elemental">Rage Elemental</a> away from <a href="bword://Meadow Lark">Meadow Lark</a>. Its name was a point of contention; "Brandon pointed out MOAB actually stood for 'Massive Ordnance Air Blast,' but his brother said, 'Don’t be that guy.'</li><li><b>Source:</b> Crafting</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mother of All Bombs on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mother_of_All_Bombs_%28MOAB%29</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mrs. Ghazi</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Mrs. Ghazi</b> is a sand ooze, a Fifth Floor Borough Boss, and the daughter of <a href="bword://Samantha">Samantha</a> and <a href="bword://King Blaine">King Blaine</a>. As long as Samantha exists in this realm, Mrs. Ghazi can be fully resurrected from a single grain of sand. She can be temporarily killed by setting fire to her core.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Sand Ooze</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4 Chapter 21</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mrs. Ghazi on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mrs._Ghazi</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mrs. Parsons</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Mrs. Parsons</b> was an old woman who lived in a first floor unit of <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s apartment building in Seattle, WA. She was grumpy and liked to file complaints. Her husband died years ago and she never remarried.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Seattle, WA</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 1</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mrs. Parsons on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mrs._Parsons</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mukta</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Mukta</b> is a <a href="bword://Kua-Tin">Kua-Tin</a> member of the <a href="bword://Bloom">Bloom</a>, and an employee in <a href="bword://Borant Corporation">Borant Corporation</a>'s Communications Department. On the Second Floor, Mukta briefly takes over PR for the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a> after the <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a> suspends Zev for warning <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> about the <a href="bword://Rage Elemental">Rage Elemental</a>. Unlike Zev, he never enters the Dungeon to talk in person, and he closes his chats to prevent crawlers from messaging him.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Borant System</li><li><b>Race:</b> Kua-Tin</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 41</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mukta on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mukta</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Murgh Vindaloo</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Murgh Vindaloo</b> is a food item, spice level four. Boneless chicken cubes simmered in velvety sweet-and-sour vindaloo sauce. Also, potatoes and other spices. It is on top of biryani rice. Served with garlic-and-spinach naan.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Tally</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Murgh Vindaloo on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Murgh_Vindaloo</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mute Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><i><b>Mute</b></i> is a spell that inflicts the Muted Debuff on its target, preventing the target from casting spells. When cast, it looks like a yellow bolt that follows the target. When it lands, a timer and an icon featuring a speaker with a cross through it appear above the target's head.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mute Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mute_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Mysterious Letter</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Mysterious Letter</b> is an item that is part of the Sex Workers Who Fell from the Heavens Quest. <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> mentions that the script is necro-script, the language of necromancers. He later figures out that the letter is a spell scroll for the <a href="bword://Suppurating Eye Spell">Suppurating Eye Spell</a>, allowing the caster to see and hear what is going on around the scroll.</li><li><b>Source:</b> GumGum's corpse</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Mysterious Letter on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Mysterious_Letter</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ménage à Quatro Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Ménage à Quatro Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for surviving the four way boss battle at the end of the Sixth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ménage à Quatro Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/M%C3%A9nage_%C3%A0_Quatro_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Nadine</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Nadine</b> is an enormous long-bodied caterpillar with a thick coat of fuzzy fur and prominent black quills and bristles that cover her form, allowing her to brush past like a car wash when moving at speed. As a Bearded Sage Caterpillar she undulates rapidly through jungle terrain, produces wet chittering and hissing sounds, smells strongly of wet moss, and bears a large saddle on her back to serve as a six-seater mount. While her overall shape appears deceptively cute from afar, her true bug-like insectoid face is horrifyingly alien and best avoided up close.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Chee | Bearded Sage Caterpillar</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 5, Chapter 13</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Nadine on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Nadine</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Naga</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Naga</b> are a <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> race. They are ruled by the <a href="bword://Blood Sultanate">Blood Sultanate</a>. They have a legacy spot in Faction Wars (game) as they are considered broke after the <i>Dungeon Crawler World</i> season where crawler <a href="bword://Drakea">Drakea</a> managed to drive them into bankruptcy. The Naga are cobra-headed aliens.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Naga on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Naga</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Naiad</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Naiads</b> are water nymphs: a fairy-class creature that lives in water. Half-Naiads may be created with Humans and Elves. Naiad's are governed by the <a href="bword://Naiad Confederacy">Naiad Confederacy</a>, an isolationist sect that drowns outsiders.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Naiad on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Naiad</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Naiad Confederacy</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Naiad Confederacy</b> is a governmental structure of the <a href="bword://Naiad">Naiad</a>'s on the Sixth Floor. The Confederacy is an isolationist group that drowns outsiders who enter their area.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Naiad Confederacy on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Naiad_Confederacy</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Naughty Boys Employment Agency</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Naughty Boys Employment Agency</b> is a social upgrade that can be purchased as a saferoom addition for 500,000 gold.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Naughty Boys Employment Agency on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Naughty_Boys_Employment_Agency</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Nebular</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Nebular Balance</b> (colloquially called "Nebulars" or "Nebs") is a nomadic religious cult that worships the Eulogist. Nebulars do not actively recruit, but their members consist of Soothers, Humans, elves, and dozens of other aliens from across the galaxy. They all wear the same robes and large hats.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Nebs; Nebular</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Nebular on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Nebular</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Necklace of Indelible Woe</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://King Rust">King Rust</a> originally wields the necklace. This necklace is in the same collection as the <a href="bword://Enchanted Night Wyrm&#x27;s Ring of Divine Suffering">Enchanted Night Wyrm's Ring of Divine Suffering</a>. <a href="bword://Li Na">Li Na</a> shows interest in the item but ultimately decides against taking it.</li><li><b>Source:</b> King Rust</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Necklace of Indelible Woe on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Necklace_of_Indelible_Woe</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Neighborhood Map</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Neighborhood Map</b> is a persistent item dropped by slain Neighborhood Bosses, meaning that every crawler who loots the boss's corpse can pick up the map. The Neighborhood Map looks like a scrap of paper. When a crawler touches it, it adds the boss's "neighborhood" and all mobs in the area to the crawler's minimap.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Neighborhood Boss</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Neighborhood Map on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Neighborhood_Map</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Nekhebit</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Nekhebit</b> is a life and protector deity. She is a vulture goddess with the head of an Egyptian vulture and arms instead of wings. She has yellow and white feathers around her head that resemble an afro. Her beak is chipped and her skin has heavy scarring. She wears a threadbare red dress, bracelets, and an oak bow over her shoulder.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Odette (sponsor)The Scavenger Mother of Mothers</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> God</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Nekhebit on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Nekhebit</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Nemes of Pestilence</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Nemes of Pestilence</b> is an item <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> receives as part of her Assassin of Sekhmet Class. She gives it to <a href="bword://Mongo">Mongo</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Assassin of Sekhmet Class</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Nemes of Pestilence on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Nemes_of_Pestilence</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Neural Enhancers</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b><a href="bword://Valtay Corporation">Valtay Corporation</a> Neural Enhancers</b> are pills that cause permanent changes in the brain. Neural Enhancers are available in <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> space, or can be delivered to crawlers in Benefactor Boxes from their Sponsors. Once consumed, the Neural Enhancer grants specific abilities; these abilities work both inside and outside of Enhancement Zones, and cannot be unequipped or uninstalled.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Benefactor Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Neural Enhancers on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Neural_Enhancers</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Nico</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Nico</b> is one of the NPC racers that are against <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> on the Tenth Floor.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Tigran</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 8, Chapter 19</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Nico on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Nico</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Night Weasel</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Night Weasel</b> are A fuzzy jet black, six legged weasel with sharp oversized teeth. Capable of turning invisible and can paralyse creatures for five minutes.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Night Weasel on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Night_Weasel</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Night Wyrm's Nasty Little Web of Suffering Tattoo</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Night Wyrm's Nasty Little Web of Suffering</b> is a tattoo that grants access to the <a href="bword://Guild of Suffering">Guild of Suffering</a>. The extremely large tattoo appears on the Crawler's left elbow, and looks like a faded, green-tinted, poorly drawn spiderweb; the individual strands are segmented and wormlike.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Night Wyrm's Nasty Little Web of Suffering Tattoo on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Night_Wyrm%27s_Nasty_Little_Web_of_Suffering_Tattoo</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Nightmare Express</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Nightmare Express</b> is a named steam train that runs a figure-eight loop on the Iron Tangle of the Fourth Floor. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> hijacked it and used it for the rest of the floor before sending it into the Abyss as a bomb.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Fourth Floor; Commandeered by Carl</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Nightmare Express on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Nightmare_Express</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Nine-Tier Attack</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Nine-Tier Attack</b> is a catastrophic, nine-part assault associated with <a href="bword://Scolopendra">Scolopendra</a>, the great beast said to slumber beneath the volcano. In the lore of the volcano levels it is remembered as a legendary cataclysm — a "poison cloud" that killed or horribly transformed nearly everyone it touched — and it survives in the region's myths and folklore.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Nine-Tier Attack on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Nine-Tier_Attack</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Nodling</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Nodling</b> are a race that has multiple heads they can have anywhere from two to six heads. When a nodling dies they split into a new creature for each head, these emerge as toddlers but quickly grow.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Nodling on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Nodling</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>NPCs</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>NPCs</b> (Non-Player Characters) are the living, biological creatures the <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> engineers or repurposes to populate the Dungeon, ranging from autonomous mobs and scripted elites to indentured former crawlers. Safe-zone guildmasters, guides, and merchants fall under the same heading, flagged by the system as non-combatants.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: NPCs on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/NPCs</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Nullian</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Nullians</b> (a.k.a. <b>Nulls</b> or <b>Grays</b>) look like typical "Roswell aliens," and are generally discriminated against in <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> space. Nulls are not a <a href="bword://Syndicate Council">Syndicate Council</a> race, and entire systems (illegally) refuse entry to their kind. As a result, many nulls live in communes in unfriendly systems; the Orcs recently raised the tax rate on the Null commune in the Filt System.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Nullian on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Nullian</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Obsidian Butterfly</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Obsidian Butterfly</b> is the race <a href="bword://Imani">Imani</a> chooses on the Third Floor, pairing with the Fire Spiritualist class to form a support build centered on healing and buffs delivered through her wings.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Obsidian Butterfly on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Obsidian_Butterfly</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Octo-Shark</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Octo-Shark</b> is a race of sharks with an octopus-like tail. Like a water centaur. <a href="bword://Lusca">Lusca</a> is one.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Octo-Shark on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Octo-Shark</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Odette</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Odette</b> is a former Crawler and the host of <i>Dungeon Crawler After Hours with Odette</i>. She is described as "the most-beloved interviewer and program host in the history of the galaxy."</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Unknown seeded world</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human (non-terrestrial)</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 28</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Odette on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Odette</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Odius Creeper</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Odius Creeper</b> are a mob on the Sixth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Odius Creeper on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Odius_Creeper</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ogre</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Ogre</b> are a race.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ogre on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ogre</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ogun</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Ogun</b> is a god who is part of the <a href="bword://Orisha">Orisha</a> pantheon, with <a href="bword://Legba">Legba</a>, <a href="bword://Shango">Shango</a>, <a href="bword://Oshun">Oshun</a>, <a href="bword://Asojano">Asojano</a>, <a href="bword://Inle">Inle</a>, and <a href="bword://Yemaya">Yemaya</a>.According to <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a>, a common god to worship. God of blacksmiths and protection.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Orisha Deity</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ogun on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ogun</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Oh shit! A country Boss! Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Oh shit! A country Boss! Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded for seeing a Country Boss. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives this when <a href="bword://Imogen">Imogen</a> shows up in the convoy on the way to the castle.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Oh shit! A country Boss! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Oh_shit%21_A_country_Boss%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>One Quadrillion! Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>One Quadrillion! Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> when he reaches one quadrillion views. <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> also received the achievement.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: One Quadrillion! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/One_Quadrillion%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ontario</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>A Hunter who set traps for crawlers in Zockau.</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 5, Book 5</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ontario on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ontario</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Oooh, Magic Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> donned on his <a href="bword://Enchanted Trollskin Shirt of Pummeling">Enchanted Trollskin Shirt of Pummeling</a> and <a href="bword://Enchanted Nightgaunt Cloak of Stoutness">Enchanted Nightgaunt Cloak of Stoutness</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Oooh, Magic Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Oooh%2C_Magic_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Oozy Form Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Oozy Form</b> is a spell that lets <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> temporarily transform into a slime that can traverse tight gaps, learned from a spellbook on the Tenth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Oozy Form Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Oozy_Form_Spell</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Open Intellect Pacifist Action Network</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Open Intellect Pacifist Action Network, Intergalactic NFC</b> is a small, tax-exempt organization operating in <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> space and the second sponsor of <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> on the Fifth Floor. Behind its charitable registration, the Network is an activist group of former crawlers working to bring the crawl to a permanent end, and it is later re-formed as an openly militant resistance movement.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> OIAN; Open Intellect Pacifist Network; The Pacifist Network; Open Intellect Action Network</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Open Intellect Pacifist Action Network on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Open_Intellect_Pacifist_Action_Network</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Long Haul Biological Waste Management Solutions</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Long Haul Biological Waste Management Solutions</b> is a DBA and front company for the <a href="bword://Open Intellect Pacifist Action Network">Open Intellect Pacifist Action Network</a> (OIPAN), an intergalactic NFC.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Open Intellect Pacifist Action Network</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Long Haul Biological Waste Management Solutions on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Long_Haul_Biological_Waste_Management_Solutions</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Opiee</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Opiee</b> is a small, floating <a href="bword://Bune">Bune</a> and the adjutant for the Madness, one of the Faction Wars adjutants who preside over formal rules disputes during the Faction Wars on the Ninth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Opiee on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Opiee</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Opposite Day Ring</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Opposite Day</b> looks like a "fat ring" studded with five small jewels that glow ominously like tiny <a href="bword://Soul Crystals">Soul Crystals</a>. When the wearer is struck by a powerful spell, the ring activates: one of the jewels burns out (or explodes or disappears), and the spell rebounds at the caster. The ring can only be used five times.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Opposite Day Ring on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Opposite_Day_Ring</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Orc</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Orc</b> are a race both in the Dungeon and in the <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a>. Within the Syndicate, the <a href="bword://Skull Empire">Skull Empire</a> is a part of the <a href="bword://Syndicate Council">Syndicate Council</a>. One of the citizen types of the Overcity are orcs. <a href="bword://GumGum">GumGum</a> is an orc NPC, but doesn't have the same skin color as <a href="bword://Maestro">Maestro</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Orc on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Orc</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Orchid of Eileithyia's Grace</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Orchid of Eileithyia's Grace</b> is a pink orchid contained inside the <a href="bword://Engaged Lock Box of the Night Wyrm">Engaged Lock Box of the Night Wyrm</a>. Before choosing to worship the goddess, the three boons are simply described as: "<i>Triple Constitution, You are an Attendant, You get Pregnant.</i>" These descriptions are expanded after worshipping her.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Celestial Loot Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Orchid of Eileithyia's Grace on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Orchid_of_Eileithyia%27s_Grace</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Orcish Supremacy</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>An Orcish government ruled by Tusklings, comparatively small when compared to the <a href="bword://Skull Empire">Skull Empire</a>. They are also regarded as a more "hedonistic" society.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Orcish Supremacy on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Orcish_Supremacy</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Orisha</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The Orisha pantheon are a group of former gods and goddess that attempt to get <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> to repair their shrine so that they can Ascend.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Orisha on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Orisha</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Orren</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Orren</b> is a <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> Liaison, an independent fact finder called in when the showrunners and the <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a> cannot agree on what happened. Orren is a parasitic worm and a citizen of the Valtay. He describes himself as an independent consultant retained by the Syndicate rather than an employee of Borant, working in concert with the showrunners, the Syndicate government, and the controlling System AI. When the kua-tin and the AI file contradictory or inconclusive reports on an incident, a liaison investigates and recommends a resolution; crawlers would not normally meet one.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Manager Orren, Orren the Liaison</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Knot</li><li><b>Race:</b> Gondii</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 19</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Orren on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Orren</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Orthrus</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Orthrus</b> is an adorable, floppy eared, impossibly massive two-headed puppy that was pulled into the Nothing after his former master, <a href="bword://Emberus">Emberus</a>'s son <a href="bword://Geyrun">Geyrun</a>, was murdered.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> God</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 29</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Orthrus on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Orthrus</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Oshun</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Oshun</b> is a god who is part of the <a href="bword://Orisha">Orisha</a> pantheon, with <a href="bword://Ogun">Ogun</a>, <a href="bword://Legba">Legba</a>, <a href="bword://Shango">Shango</a>, <a href="bword://Asojano">Asojano</a>, <a href="bword://Inle">Inle</a>, and <a href="bword://Yemaya">Yemaya</a>. During the Thorn Room Boss Battle, if her shrine is repaired: “Sweet, sweet Oshun. If you repair her shrine, you all will be protected from the next five fatal blows. Everyone will receive a fifty percent boost to their charisma. All will receive a level 10 <a href="bword://Heal Party">Heal Party</a> spell. Oshun will ascend.”</li><li><b>Race:</b> Orisha Deity</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Oshun on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Oshun</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ossie</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Ossie</b> is a former Crawler and author of the <i><a href="bword://Dungeon Anarchist&#x27;s Cookbook">Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook</a> (18th Edition)</i>. Ossie's Cookbook took the form of scrolls. &lt;Note Added by Crawler Ossie, 18th Edition&gt;</li><li><b>Race:</b> Unknown</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ossie on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ossie</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Osvaldo</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Osvaldo</b> is a Brazilian Crawler and a member of Team <a href="bword://Flamengo">Flamengo</a>. A <a href="bword://Curupira">Curupira</a> Ranger, he is known for his dispute with <a href="bword://Prepotente">Prepotente</a> over the <a href="bword://Memorial Crystal">Memorial Crystal</a> of <a href="bword://Apito">Apito</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Brazil</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Curupira</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 5, Chapter 69</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Osvaldo on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Osvaldo</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Pacifist Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Pacifist</b> is an <a href="bword://Achievement">Achievement</a> awarded when a crawler survives an entire floor without hurting a single mob. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives this achievement on the Eighth Floor because <a href="bword://Prepotente">Prepotente</a> broke the Seventh Floor, resulting in every crawler making it through that floor without killing a single mob.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Pacifist Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Pacifist_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Pacifist's Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Pacifist's Box</b> is a Loot Box given to crawlers for actions of non-violence. Residents of <a href="bword://Meadow Lark">Meadow Lark</a> that made it to the Third Floor without killing anything got <b>Legendary Pacifist's Boxes</b>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Actions of non-violence</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Pacifist's Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Pacifist%27s_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Pain Amplifier Jellyfish</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Pain Amplifier Jellyfish</b> are a mob on the Fifth Floor. They are small, white jellyfish located in the Water Quadrant of Bubble 593. They inflict the <b>Kill Me Now It Hurts</b> debuff and a one-minute healing block. The <b>Kill Me Now It Hurts</b> debuff can be removed by using the <b><a href="bword://Jellyfish Salve">Jellyfish Salve</a></b> lotion.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Pain Amplifier Jellyfish on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Pain_Amplifier_Jellyfish</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Panford</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Panford</b> is a Dreadnaught and the adjutant for the <a href="bword://Lemig Sortion">Lemig Sortion</a> (referred to in the official proceedings as the "Democratic Sortion"), one of many adjutants who preside over formal rules disputes during the Faction Wars on the Ninth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Panford on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Panford</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Panty Dropper Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Panty Dropper Spell</b> is a spell. The "Panty Dropper" spell is part of the NecroBard Class at level 3.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Panty Dropper Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Panty_Dropper_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Party Planner Vehicle</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Party Planner</b> is an airship that <a href="bword://Louis">Louis</a> receives in a <a href="bword://Celestial">Celestial</a> box for surviving being marked for death by <a href="bword://Ysalte">Ysalte</a> on the Eighth Floor. The Party Planner is a fifty-foot long, sleek, silver tube sitting on a pair of chopper-like landing skids with four rectangle-shaped protuberances on the top. The fuselage isn’t a perfect tube, but more like a squished oval. It looks like a submarine crossed with a bullet train car with a rounded nose made of heavily-tinted glass reminiscent of the nose of a B-29 bomber, though not nearly as big.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Celestial Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Party Planner Vehicle on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Party_Planner_Vehicle</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Pater Coal</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Pater Coal</b> is an NPC and the High Cleric Supreme of the <a href="bword://Emberus High Temple of the Ending Sun">Emberus High Temple of the Ending Sun</a>, <a href="bword://Emberus">Emberus</a>'s secret temple inside <a href="bword://Club Vanquisher">Club Vanquisher</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> Hobbledehoy</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 18</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Pater Coal on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Pater_Coal</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Patty Pump-It-Up</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Patty Pump-It-Up</b> is a <a href="bword://Dwarf">Dwarf</a> and an NPC in <a href="bword://Borant Corporation">Borant Corporation</a>'s Dungeon. She works as a stripper at the Bitches Room in the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Katia Grim">Katia Grim</a> meet Patty Pump-It-Up after completing the assassination quest for the <a href="bword://Guild of Suffering">Guild of Suffering</a>. She is one of the many strippers hiding from the Vorpals inside the Penis Parade.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Dwarf</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 33</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Patty Pump-It-Up on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Patty_Pump-It-Up</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Paulie</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Paulie</b> is the preferred name of <b><a href="bword://Goff">Goff</a></b>, and is a human occupied by a <a href="bword://Residual">Residual</a>. In the months before the transformation, he lived at the Shepherd's House, a homeless shelter near Miami, Florida.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Goff; Paulie</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Miami, FL</li><li><b>Race:</b> Residual</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 49</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Paulie on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Paulie</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Goff</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b><a href="bword://Paulie">Paulie</a></b> is the preferred name of <b>Goff</b>, and is a human occupied by a <a href="bword://Residual">Residual</a>. In the months before the transformation, he lived at the Shepherd's House, a homeless shelter near Miami, Florida.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Goff; Paulie</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Miami, FL</li><li><b>Race:</b> Residual</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 49</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Goff on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Goff</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Paw Patrol Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Paw Patrol</b> is a spell whose only appearance in the text is as the title of a scroll offered as a prize at the Butcher's Masquerade Ball. Nothing about what the spell actually does is ever revealed.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Paw Patrol Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Paw_Patrol_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Pawna's Cries</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>Similar but distinct from the <a href="bword://Pawna&#x27;s Tears">Pawna's Tears</a> <a href="bword://Potion">Potion</a>, the <b>Pawna's Cries</b> potion adds three levels to any spell or skill that the crawler chooses. Due to its "limited shelf life," it must be used before the Floor collapses.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Gold Benefactor Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Pawna's Cries on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Pawna%27s_Cries</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Pawna's Tears</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>Similar but distinct from the <a href="bword://Pawna&#x27;s Cries">Pawna's Cries</a> <a href="bword://Potion">Potion</a>, the <b>Pawna's Tears Potion</b> is an extremely high-value item that adds five levels to any spell or skill chosen by the imbiber. The potion does not expire.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Legendary Loot Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Pawna's Tears on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Pawna%27s_Tears</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Payload Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Payload Box</b> is a Loot Box given to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for dropping all the bombs in his inventory at the end of the Ninth Floor. He receives a Gold version of the box.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Bomb's Away Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Payload Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Payload_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Paz Lo</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>Paz Lo: race/species: <a href="bword://Human">Human</a>; class: Santero Class; first scene: Chapter 5, Book 6.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 5, Book 6</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Paz Lo on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Paz_Lo</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Pazuzu</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Pazuzu</b> are a half-human, half-scorpion race found in the land quadrant of the Fifth Floor of the Dungeon. They appear both as settled townsfolk, who keep the inns, taverns and shops of towns such as Pandinus, and as feral mobs that swarm the open desert after dark.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Pazuzu on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Pazuzu</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Peace Upgrade Patch</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Peace Upgrade Patch</b> is an <a href="bword://Upgrade Patch">Upgrade Patch</a> given to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> on the Eighth Floor in a Gold <a href="bword://Pacifist&#x27;s Box">Pacifist's Box</a> rewarded to him for the <a href="bword://Pacifist Achievement">Pacifist Achievement</a>. This patch is applied to the <a href="bword://Enchanted Anarchist&#x27;s Battle Rattle">Enchanted Anarchist's Battle Rattle</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Gold Pacifist's Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Peace Upgrade Patch on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Peace_Upgrade_Patch</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Pearson</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>One of the Changelings from Hump Town. He had been impersonating a <a href="bword://Dromedarian">Dromedarian</a> bartender. He meets <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> in the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a> to get the map and plan to evacuate the Changelings to the 9th Floor.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Changeling</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 58, Book 5</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Pearson on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Pearson</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Penelope</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Penelope</b> is a pig. A beloved and many married pig and magically protected pig.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Yorkshire Sow</li><li><b>First scene:</b> book 8, Chapter 19</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Penelope on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Penelope</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Penn</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Penn</b> is a former crawler who comes back to help the <a href="bword://Princess Posse">Princess Posse</a> in the Faction Wars (game) on the Ninth Floor. A tall, muscular human sergeant stood right there, carrying what looked like a steel H-beam for a building. The metallic beam had to be 20 feet long, and it looked as if it weighed two tons. The monster of a man held it on his shoulder.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Penn on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Penn</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Permacube</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>permacube</b> generates heat when combined with combustible material such as coal. It has an extremely long lifespan and goes dormant when it runs out of coal, but does not turn off. It reactivates a few minutes after the material is shoveled in.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Goblins</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Permacube on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Permacube</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Pestiferous Vine</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Pestiferous Vine</b> appear to be massive living vines that infect other mobs. Pestiferous Vines aren't really a plant, but rather a hybrid fungus with a type of plant parasitic worms.They really exist outside the Dungeon.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Pestiferous Vine on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Pestiferous_Vine</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Pet Biscuit</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>A regular <b>Pet Biscuit</b> is a small, round, crumbly hard pellet that can feed a pet or dungeon familiar for one full day. Pets find them delicious, so <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> advises only pulling out one biscuit at a time.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Pet Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Pet Biscuit on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Pet_Biscuit</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Pet Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Pet Box</b> is a Loot Box distributed for pet-related achievements. All tiers of the box have a hedgehog-like animal stenciled on them. The bronze Pet Box is about half the size of a military footlocker, bronze-colored and had a hegde-hog like animal stenciled on top.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Achievements</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Pet Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Pet_Box</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Pet Biscuit</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>A regular <b>Pet Biscuit</b> is a small, round, crumbly hard pellet that can feed a pet or dungeon familiar for one full day. Pets find them delicious, so <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> advises only pulling out one biscuit at a time.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Pet Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Pet Biscuit on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Pet_Biscuit</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Pet Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Pet Box</b> is a Loot Box distributed for pet-related achievements. All tiers of the box have a hedgehog-like animal stenciled on them. The bronze Pet Box is about half the size of a military footlocker, bronze-colored and had a hegde-hog like animal stenciled on top.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Achievements</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Pet Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Pet_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Pet Carrier</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Pet Carrier</b> is a magical pet carrier that is "the dungeon's equivalent of a pokeball." It allows bonded pets into a crawler's inventory without harming them.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Buy</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Pet Carrier on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Pet_Carrier</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>PETA Enthusiast Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>PETA Enthusiast Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded for removing the aggro of an opponent.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: PETA Enthusiast Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/PETA_Enthusiast_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Pharmaceutical Starter Kit</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Pharmaceutical Starter Kit</b> is a large chest filled to the brim with chemicals, herbs, and "everything you need to start your own pharmaceutical empire." <a href="bword://Quint">Quint</a> sells these in the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>, but crawlers typically can't afford them until the Fifth Floor.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Pharmacists</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Pharmaceutical Starter Kit on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Pharmaceutical_Starter_Kit</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Pierre</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Pierre</b> is a Porter for the Yellow line train on the Iron Tangle. Pierre is a quarter giant, similar looking to Lurch from the Addam's Family. He's described as having a wide pale face, and hair that looks like dying moss. He wears a porter outfit.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Grapple</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 5</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Pierre on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Pierre</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Pincushioned Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Pincushioned</b> is an <a href="bword://Achievement">Achievement</a> awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for having both eyeballs pierced at the same time. During a Deckmaster fight against Tom the <a href="bword://Turkey">Turkey</a> and <a href="bword://Sharp-Elbows">Sharp-Elbows</a> the <a href="bword://Ogre">Ogre</a> Necromancer Witch (Deckmasters Eight and Nine) on the Eighth Floor, Carl activates the Daughter's Kiss ability of his <a href="bword://Scavenger&#x27;s Daughter Upgrade Patch">Scavenger's Daughter Upgrade Patch</a> to kill Tom the Turkey. The resulting explosions destabilizes the barn where the fight had occurred and in the resulting tumult Carl secures himself to a concrete slab using his Sticky Feet Benefit.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Pincushioned Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Pincushioned_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ping Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>Also known as, “Here piggy, piggy,” or “The Night Dread,” Ping is a hunting and artillery-aiming tool for those who do not care if their quarry knows they’re coming.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ping Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ping_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Platinum Sharpening Stone</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> gets the <b>Platinum Sharpening Stone</b> as a reward for completing the Squeeze out the <a href="bword://Juice Box">Juice Box</a> Quest quest on the Fifth Floor. A little black rock.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Platinum Quest Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Platinum Sharpening Stone on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Platinum_Sharpening_Stone</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Plenty</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Plenty</b> are a caprid people who invented and control the modern tunneling system, the proprietary technology that carries real-time communication across the universe.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> The Herd</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Plenty on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Plenty</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Pocket Kuma</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Pocket Kuma</b> is the race <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> became on the Sixth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Pocket Kuma on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Pocket_Kuma</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Podophilia! Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> earned this achievement for stomping a goblin with his bare feet on the first floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Podophilia! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Podophilia%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Poison Antidote</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Poison Antidotes</b> are <i>presumably</i> potions that heal the Poisoned debuff. Crawlers may receive Poison Antidotes in low-tier Adventurer Boxes.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Loot Boxes</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Poison Antidote on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Poison_Antidote</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Poison Grapple Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Poison <a href="bword://Grapple">Grapple</a></b> is a spell whose only appearance in the text is as the title of a spellbook offered as a prize at the Butcher's Masquerade Ball. Nothing about what the spell actually does is ever revealed.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Poison Grapple Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Poison_Grapple_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Pollyslog</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Pollyslog</b> are a Fourth Floor mob that can be found at the Phantom Kangaroo station #84 on the Yellow Line. The Pollyslog look like large, green-skinned fish-like humanoids. They have massive milk white eyes.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Pollyslog on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Pollyslog</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Pontifex Shine</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Pontifex Shine</b> is a wealthy, external sponsor representing the religious faction known as the <a href="bword://Nebular">Nebular</a> Balance. Very little is known about the character personally, but they play a critical background role in sponsoring both crawlers and deadly deities during the events of the World Dungeon.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> The Syndicate (Outside the Dungeon)</li><li><b>Race:</b> Unknown (Nebulars consist of various species including Soothers, Humans, and Elves)</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 66</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Pontifex Shine on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Pontifex_Shine</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Pontiff</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Pontiff</b> is a level 83 Taurin mercenary and a former dancer. Originally introduced as hired help for the racing team One Fine Pig during the Tenth Floor, Pontiff eventually defects to aid <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and the <a href="bword://Princess Posse">Princess Posse</a>, acting as their driver and undercover operative.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Taurin</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 8, Chapter 19</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Pontiff on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Pontiff</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Pooka</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Pooka</b> on the Fourth Floor is a Neighborhood Boss, and part of the Iron Tangle political statement. They hand out the drugs that the <a href="bword://Krakaren Clone (Fourth Floor)">Krakaren Clone (Fourth Floor)</a> boss would make.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon - Fourth Floor</li><li><b>Race:</b> Plenty</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 12</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Pooka on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Pooka</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Popov Brothers</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>Fraternal twin brothers. The two of them speak with an eastern European accent. Dmitri had just brought a cat named Capitan Whiskers. Maxim has a meteor hammer.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Nodling</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 25, Book 3</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Popov Brothers on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Popov_Brothers_%28Maxim_%26_Dmitri%29</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Porky</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Porky</b> is one of the two split halves of the mantaur <a href="bword://Corcunda">Corcunda</a>, a Stage Performance Guildmaster reunited with his other half, Corky, over the course of the Tenth Floor's racing arc.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Porky on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Porky</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Porsuk</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Porsuk</b> are a badger-headed race. All the bartenders at the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a> are Porsuk.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Porsuk on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Porsuk</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Portal</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Portal</b> allow for teleport between two locations in the Dungeon. They were a common mechanic on the Fourth Floor. Portals are a Dungeon mechanic that allows for teleportation between one location to another. Portals can be key locked to prevent unauthorized individuals from passing through. Portals can pass inside each other without issue.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Portal on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Portal</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Porthus</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Dr. Porthus Hu</b> is a former crawler and the author of the <i><a href="bword://Dungeon Anarchist&#x27;s Cookbook">Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook</a> (2nd Edition)</i>. He is now CEO of the <a href="bword://Open Intellect Pacifist Action Network">Open Intellect Pacifist Action Network</a>.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Dr. Porthus Hu</li><li><b>Race:</b> Elf| High Elf</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Epilogue</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Porthus on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Porthus</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Princess Posse</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Princess Posse</b> is Team #3 in the Ninth Floor Faction Wars of <i>Dungeon Crawler World: Earth</i>, co-led by Crawlers <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and Princess <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> and crowd-funded by Donut's massive intergalactic fan club. Sponsored by the <a href="bword://Society for the Eradication of Cocker Spaniels">Society for the Eradication of Cocker Spaniels</a> (TSECS) and doing business as Princess Posse Enterprises, NFC, the team aims to survive the Ninth Floor, protect as many crawlers and <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a> as possible, and level the playing field by stripping the safety protections from the wealthy out-worlder combatants.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> The Princess Posse, sponsored by the Society for the Eradication of Cocker Spaniels (TSECS), NFC, DBA as Princess Posse Enterprises, NFC</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Princess Posse on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Princess_Posse</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Princess Posse Fan Club</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Princess Posse Fan Club</b> is the official fan club for Princess <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>. Donut refuses to acknowledge the unofficial fan club, the <a href="bword://Donut Holes">Donut Holes</a>. Zev lets Donut know that the <a href="bword://Princess Posse">Princess Posse</a> is winning out over the Donut Holes as a name for her fan club.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Princess Posse Fan Club on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Princess_Posse_Fan_Club</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Potion</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>In the Dungeon, <b>Potions</b> are single-use consumable items that produce a magical effect, usually a buff or debuff, and act on crawlers, pets, mobs, and <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a> alike. They can be drunk, triggered through the hotlist, or thrown as weapons.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Crafting, Loot, Loot Boxes, Store</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Potion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Potion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Potion of Bloodlust</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Potions of Bloodlust</b> make you go faster and hit harder, and every time you kill something you go even faster. That's the fun news. The bad news is it also makes you forget whose a friend and whose an enemy<b>.</b> <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> gets two as a reward for the <a href="bword://Milquetoast Achievement">Milquetoast Achievement</a> from a Silver Pacifist Box, which goes to show you that the AI loves a proper bit of irony.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Silver Pacifist Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Potion of Bloodlust on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Potion_of_Bloodlust</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Potion of Dinosaur Repellent</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives several <b>Potions of Dinosaur Repellent</b> in adventurer boxes on the Fifth Floor. <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> is immediately concerned by the appearance of these potions. After receiving several on the fifth floor, Carl receives another 10 on the Sixth Floor before their purpose starts to becomes clear. Carl makes sure all the crawlers attending the Masquerade have access to Dinosaur Repellent as he guesses that <a href="bword://Kiwi">Kiwi</a>'s herd are going to become hostile.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Adventurer Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Potion of Dinosaur Repellent on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Potion_of_Dinosaur_Repellent</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Potion of Half Splat</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Potion of Half Splat</b> is a potion that prevents you from dying from falling damage but leaves you at 5% health.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Potion of Half Splat on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Potion_of_Half_Splat</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Potion of Invisibility</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives his first <b>Potion of Invisibility</b> in a Reward Room prize case on the Fourth Floor. Turns the drinker invisible for 2 x intelligence seconds.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Reward Room prize case / Adventurer Box / Silver Lucky Bastard Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Potion of Invisibility on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Potion_of_Invisibility</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Potion of Phase Through Wall</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> receives a few <b>Potions of Phase Through Wall</b> at the start of the Eighth Floor. Allows the drinker to phase through wood, stone, or metal walls. According to <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> they're more complex that their description suggests and actually work on anything that is "solid and unnatural non-biological with empty space on both sides".</li><li><b>Source:</b> Adventurer Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Potion of Phase Through Wall on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Potion_of_Phase_Through_Wall</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Potion of Somnolent Embrace</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> brews the <b>Potion of Somnolent Embrace</b> for <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> to take while they expunge <a href="bword://Shi Maria">Shi Maria</a> on the Ninth Floor. Mordecai gives this potion to Carl so he can stay asleep during the process to get rid of Shi Maria.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Mordecai</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Potion of Somnolent Embrace on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Potion_of_Somnolent_Embrace</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Potsy</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Potsy</b> is an NPC that guards the front door of <a href="bword://Club Vanquisher">Club Vanquisher</a> on the Eighth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Potsy on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Potsy</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Pox Slug</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Pox Slug</b> are a horrifying slug mob that can start exploding from your skin if your infected with Slug Pox. Starts at level 1, each additional one becomes stronger by one level.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Pox Slug on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Pox_Slug</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Precious Elemental Reserves Code</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Precious Elemental Reserves Code</b> is a <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> law pertaining to the rights of planets to their mineral wealth.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Precious Elemental Reserves Code on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Precious_Elemental_Reserves_Code</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Precision Card</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Precision Card</b> is a utility T'Ghee card that increases a totems chance of landing an attack. If stacked they count as a single buff.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Precision Card on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Precision_Card</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Predator Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Predator Box</b> is a Loot Box given to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for the <a href="bword://Apex Predator Achievement">Apex Predator Achievement</a>. This is the first <a href="bword://Celestial">Celestial</a> box he receives. He opens this box on the Eighth Floor.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Apex Predator Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Predator Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Predator_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Premature Questjaculation Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Premature Questjaculation Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> killed <a href="bword://Claude Sludgington the Fourth">Claude Sludgington the Fourth</a>, a level 65 borough boss, before they received the quest for it because Carl recalled <a href="bword://Samantha">Samantha</a> when he dropped his xistera.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Premature Questjaculation Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Premature_Questjaculation_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Prepare for Trouble! Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The Prepare for Trouble! Achievement<b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for fighting two card opponents at the same time on the Eighth Floor.</b></li></ul><p class="source">Source: Prepare for Trouble! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Prepare_for_Trouble%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Prepotente</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Prepotente Lorenzo De La Rosa</b>, often called <b>Pony</b>, is a Crawler from Italy in Dungeon Crawler World: Earth. He entered the Dungeon as one of roughly fifteen brown-and-white Boer goats belonging to fellow crawler <a href="bword://Miriam Dom">Miriam Dom</a>, until an <a href="bword://Enhanced Pet Biscuit">Enhanced Pet Biscuit</a> transformed him into an intelligent, bipedal <a href="bword://Caprid">Caprid</a>. He quickly climbed into the dungeon's Top Ten Crawlers at Miriam's side as a Forsaken Aerialist.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Pony</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Italy</li><li><b>Race:</b> Boer Goat | Caprid</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2, Chapter 14</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Prepotente on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Prepotente</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Prepotente Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Prepotente Box</b> is a Loot Box distributed for A box that screams when it's opened, named after <a href="bword://Prepotente">Prepotente</a>. It appears to be a statue of Prepotente.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Prepotente Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Prepotente_Box</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Prepotente Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Prepotente Box</b> is a Loot Box distributed for A box that screams when it's opened, named after <a href="bword://Prepotente">Prepotente</a>. It appears to be a statue of Prepotente.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Prepotente Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Prepotente_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Priestly</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Priestly</b> is a former Crawler and author of the <i><a href="bword://Dungeon Anarchist&#x27;s Cookbook">Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook</a> (14th Edition)</i>. Priestly's contributions to the cookbook are the single best source of information about the Ninth Floor Faction Wars. He loved music and was charmed by the city of Larracos.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Unknown</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Priestly on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Priestly</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Primal</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Primal</b> is an ancient alien race that vanished after spreading across the galaxy. It survives in the Dungeon as a rare, blank-slate racial option available to Crawlers on the Third Floor, one that costs base stats but removes the training cap on every skill.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Primal on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Primal</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Primal Engine</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>Primal Engine</b> is an ancient planet-regulating computer with a basic operating system. A machine approximately the size of a grain of rice, <a href="bword://Primal">Primal</a> Engines can be found at the cores of some planets in multiple solar systems throughout the galaxy.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Primals</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Primal Engine on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Primal_Engine</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Primal Engine</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>Primal Engine</b> is an ancient planet-regulating computer with a basic operating system. A machine approximately the size of a grain of rice, <a href="bword://Primal">Primal</a> Engines can be found at the cores of some planets in multiple solar systems throughout the galaxy.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Primals</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Primal Engine on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Primal_Engine</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Princess Chonkalot</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Princess Chonkalot</b> is <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s grandmother, a celebrated, multiple-award-winning Persian show cat who originally belonged to Bea as a childhood pet.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Princess Chonkalot on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Princess_Chonkalot</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Princess Posse</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Princess Posse</b> is Team #3 in the Ninth Floor Faction Wars of <i>Dungeon Crawler World: Earth</i>, co-led by Crawlers <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and Princess <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> and crowd-funded by Donut's massive intergalactic fan club. Sponsored by the <a href="bword://Society for the Eradication of Cocker Spaniels">Society for the Eradication of Cocker Spaniels</a> (TSECS) and doing business as Princess Posse Enterprises, NFC, the team aims to survive the Ninth Floor, protect as many crawlers and <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a> as possible, and level the playing field by stripping the safety protections from the wealthy out-worlder combatants.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> The Princess Posse, sponsored by the Society for the Eradication of Cocker Spaniels (TSECS), NFC, DBA as Princess Posse Enterprises, NFC</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Princess Posse on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Princess_Posse</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Princess Posse Fan Club</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Princess Posse Fan Club</b> is the official fan club for Princess <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>. Donut refuses to acknowledge the unofficial fan club, the <a href="bword://Donut Holes">Donut Holes</a>. Zev lets Donut know that the <a href="bword://Princess Posse">Princess Posse</a> is winning out over the Donut Holes as a name for her fan club.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Princess Posse Fan Club on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Princess_Posse_Fan_Club</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Prism Industries Capacitating and Focusing Goggles</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Prism Industries Capacitating and Focusing Goggles</b> are sunglasses gifted to <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> by her sponsor Princess D'Nadia in a <a href="bword://Benefactor Box">Benefactor Box</a> on the Fourth Floor.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Benefactor Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Prism Industries Capacitating and Focusing Goggles on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Prism_Industries_Capacitating_and_Focusing_Goggles</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Prism Kingdom</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Prism Kingdom</b> is country of <a href="bword://Saccathian">Saccathian</a> ruled by Princess D'Nadia. It is small but known for its trade abilities. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> first meet Princess <a href="bword://D&#x27;nadia">D'nadia</a> while on the show Danger Zone with <a href="bword://Ripper Wonton">Ripper Wonton</a>. The program's director Evo described the Prism Kingdom as "rather small" but "a powerful force in certain trade circles." Following the attack by Prince <a href="bword://Stalwart">Stalwart</a> of the <a href="bword://Skull Empire">Skull Empire</a> that kills <a href="bword://Manasa">Manasa</a>, Princess D'nadia formally condemns the action on behalf of the Prism Kingdom.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Prism Kingdom on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Prism_Kingdom</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Enchanted Prison Tattoo Kit</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Enchanted Prison Tattoo Kit</b> allows someone to create a tattoo on a target, can potentially imbue magical buffs and upgrades if the artist is good enough.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Enchanted Prison Tattoo Kit on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Enchanted_Prison_Tattoo_Kit</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Prison Pocket</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Prison Pocket</b> is a boss on the Tenth Floor during the 2nd Heat.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Poppa</li><li><b>Race:</b> Macropus Dominus</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 8, Chapter 20</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Prison Pocket on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Prison_Pocket</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Prison Pocket</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Prison Pocket</b> is a boss on the Tenth Floor during the 2nd Heat.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Poppa</li><li><b>Race:</b> Macropus Dominus</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 8, Chapter 20</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Prison Pocket on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Prison_Pocket</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Prize Carousel</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Prize Carousel</b> is a time-restricted Dungeon minigame hosted by <a href="bword://Chaco">Chaco</a>. Crawlers can receive the ability to "play" if their fans select it as a <a href="bword://Fan Box">Fan Box</a> reward, but it is not particularly popular and only happens a few times each season.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Fan Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Prize Carousel on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Prize_Carousel</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Protective Shell Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Protective Shell</b> is a rare protection spell that creates a stationary, temporary sphere around the caster's position at time of casting. Red-tagged corporeal mobs and physical attacks cannot move through the sphere.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Protective Shell Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Protective_Shell_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Proximity Trigger</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>Proximity Trigger</b> is an expensive trap-building device that, when added to a trap at a <a href="bword://Sapper&#x27;s Table">Sapper's Table</a>, allows the user to set conditions for when the trap goes off.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Gold Sapper's Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Proximity Trigger on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Proximity_Trigger</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Psycho Sticker</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Psycho Sticker</b> are mobs that appear on the Fourth Floor. They attack the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a> at the start of the Fourth Floor. Hedgehog Ogres. Can be found on Mora Station #82 on the red line of The Iron Tangle.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Psycho Sticker on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Psycho_Sticker</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Pterolykos</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Pterolykos</b> are a wolf with wings.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Pterolykos on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Pterolykos</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Puddle Jumper Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><i><b>Puddle Jumper</b></i> is a teleportation spell that allows the caster to teleport themselves and up to three others to a location in line of sight. Due to its high cost, time delay, and long cooldown, it is not a practical combat spell.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Puddle Jumper Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Puddle_Jumper_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Pustule</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Pustule</b> is a hobgoblin NPC and the proprietor of the Hobgobs and Boom Sticks in the Silk Road at the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>. She sold <a href="bword://Hobgoblin Hob-Lobber">Hobgoblin Hob-Lobber</a> and <a href="bword://Goblin Dynamite">Goblin Dynamite</a> to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Hobgoblin</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2, Chapter 16</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Pustule on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Pustule</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>PVP Coupon</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>PVP Coupon</b> is an item that the first crawler in a Party to receive a Player Killer Skull gets. Other players in the party who get Player Killer Skulls do not receive them.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Player Killer Skull</li></ul><p class="source">Source: PVP Coupon on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/PVP_Coupon</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Quadruped Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>Quadruped Box</b> appears to be a type of Loot Box given to four-legged creatures for... being four-legged. The symbol on the front of the box is a lion.</li><li><b>Source:</b> achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Quadruped Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Quadruped_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Quan Ch</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Quan Ch</b> is an Earth Crawler and a Half-Elf Imperial Security Trooper, unaffiliated with the Royal Court. He is best known for surviving "The Fools Who Broke the Glass" on the Third Floor to claim one of Dungeon Crawler World's rare <a href="bword://Celestial">Celestial</a> prizes: an enchanted robe that lets him fly on ethereal wings, his left hand glowing blue with its power.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Half-Elf</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2, Chapter 24</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Quan Ch on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Quan_Ch</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Quarry Sees Another Spring Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Quarry Sees Another Spring</b> achievement is awarded to Crawlers who enter a stairwell while they are featured on the Dungeon's Leaderboard. The crawler's bounty multiplies every time they receive this achievement.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Quarry Sees Another Spring Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Quarry_Sees_Another_Spring_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Quasar</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Quasar</b> is a <a href="bword://Nullian">Nullian</a> advocate and <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s legal representative under <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> law. Carl gains him on the Sixth Floor by demanding a lawyer, far earlier in the crawl than counsel is normally available, and Quasar tells him at their first meeting that he represents Carl alone.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Franciscan Arm</li><li><b>Race:</b> Nullian</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 5, Chapter 3</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Quasar on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Quasar</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Queen Consort Ugloo</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Queen Consort Ugloo</b> is the wife of <a href="bword://King Rust">King Rust</a> and mother to Prince <a href="bword://Stalwart">Stalwart</a>, Prince <a href="bword://Maestro">Maestro</a>, and Princess <a href="bword://Formidable">Formidable</a>. Sister to <a href="bword://Victory">Victory</a>. The <a href="bword://Valtay Corporation">Valtay Corporation</a> destroys Prince Stalwart's space yacht in retaliation for his accidental killing of their pop singer <a href="bword://Manasa">Manasa</a>. Queen Consort Ugloo and former Prince Maestro were presumed to be on board and killed in the explosion.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Orc</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Queen Consort Ugloo on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Queen_Consort_Ugloo</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Quest Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>Quest Box</b> is a type of Loot Box awarded to crawlers for completing a Quest or for quest-related achievements. Quest boxes arrived with the Quests tab of the crawler interface, which unlocked for <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> on the Third Floor with their first quest. The <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a> generally determines a box's contents.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Completing a Quest; Surviving a group quest, which pays every qualifying participant; Quest-related achievements, such as the CockBlock Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Quest Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Quest_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Quetzalcoatlus</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Quetzalcoatlus</b> is a Wailing Shrieker that guards the Necropolis of <a href="bword://Anser">Anser</a>. As a wailing shrieker, she can be defeated by banishment, exorcism, electrocution or destruction of the corpse of her lover.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Quetzalcoatlus on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Quetzalcoatlus</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Quint</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Quint</b> is a Pharmacist at the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>. His race is a <a href="bword://Half-Djinn">Half-Djinn</a>, Half-Garbarge Scowl. He is a former Crawler and used to be an orc. He gives alchemy supplies to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and Mordicai in exchange for the three bottles of Rev up Moonshine.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Half-Djinn, Half-Garbarge Scowl Formerly Orc</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Quint on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Quint</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Qwist</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Qwist</b> is a <a href="bword://Bopca">Bopca</a> Protector who staffs the Big Shot Chicken safe room where <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> shelter early in their crawl. Like other Bopca Protectors, Qwist manages, cleans, and cooks for the safe room, addressing Donut as "Princess" and catering to her demands, including grooming her with a brush and fetching her custard on request.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Qwist on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Qwist</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Radoslav</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Radoslav</b> was a level 75 <a href="bword://Bugbear">Bugbear</a> <a href="bword://Jack">Jack</a> of All Trades and a member of Team Free Love, an NPC racing team that competed on the Tenth Floor of the World Dungeon.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> The World Dungeon (NPC)</li><li><b>Race:</b> Bugbear</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 8, Chapter 4</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Radoslav on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Radoslav</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ragazzaccia</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Ragazzaccia</b> is <a href="bword://Prepotente">Prepotente</a>'s "girlfriend" from before the Transformation. Ragazzaccia is never shown on-page. Lonely and missing his old friends, Prepotente asks <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> and <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for advice about using one of his special enhanced pet biscuits to turn a fellow goat, Ragazzaccia, complete with a "mind-control-sex-slave" benefit. Donut immediately and firmly shuts the idea down, telling Prepotente it isn't right no matter how lonely he is.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ragazzaccia on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ragazzaccia</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Rage Elemental</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Rage Elementals</b> are mobs drawn from the Thirteenth Floor of the Dungeon and deployed on lower floors as a penalty rather than as an encounter. On the Second Floor, the <a href="bword://Borant Corporation">Borant Corporation</a> announced that any human-born crawler who intentionally relieved themselves outside a designated bathroom area would have one summoned on the spot, promising it would kill the offender and their entire party.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Rage Elemental on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Rage_Elemental</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ralph</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Ralph</b> is a <a href="bword://Frenzied Gerbil">Frenzied Gerbil</a> and a Neighborhood Boss on the Second Floor. Ralph looks like a regular ("absurdly cute") Earth gerbil, except for its mouth. The mouth looks normal when closed, but opens wider than physically possible when it opens its mouth to scream. The mouth opens so wide that it obscures the rest of the body behind it.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Frenzied Gerbil</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ralph on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ralph</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Randall</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Randall</b> was a former patient of <a href="bword://Meadow Lark">Meadow Lark</a> Elder Care Facility. Either two patients shared the name "Randall," or he is a continuity error.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Wenatchee, WA</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 27</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Randall on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Randall</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ranged Weapon Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Ranged Weapon Box</b> is a Loot Box given to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for the <a href="bword://That&#x27;s not how you use arrows, dumbass Achievement">That's not how you use arrows, dumbass Achievement</a> when he stabs <a href="bword://Vrah">Vrah</a> with the <a href="bword://Arrow of Enthusiastic Double Gonorrhea">Arrow of Enthusiastic Double Gonorrhea</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> That's not how you use arrows, dumbass Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ranged Weapon Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ranged_Weapon_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Rapid Detox Potion</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> makes <a href="bword://Louis">Louis</a> and <a href="bword://Firas">Firas</a> Rapid Detox Potions which causes them to become violently ill. The potion is used to treat alcoholism and to torture prisoners. Mordecai adds sage beetle ichor to disguise the potions, but it makes it so they go bad after an hour. They are white with little frothy bubbles.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Rapid Detox Potion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Rapid_Detox_Potion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Rapture</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book {{{1}}}.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Rapture</b> is a Level 95 Lady Mantaur Dominator, one half of a pair of womantaur drivers (alongside <a href="bword://Genesis">Genesis</a>) racing for the Lady Dominators during the Tenth Floor's racing heats.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Rapture on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Rapture</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Rat-kin</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>In the Dungeon, <b>Rat-kin</b> are a First Floor mob and are <i>most likely</i> a race option that crawlers can choose on the Third Floor. <a href="bword://Rats">Rats</a> attacked <a href="bword://Frank Q">Frank Q</a>'s group shortly after they entered the Dungeon from Seattle, WA.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Rat-kin on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Rat-kin</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Rats</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Rats</b> are rats.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Rats on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Rats</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Raul the Crab</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Raul</b> is a Red Maníseros Land Crab who becomes one of Princess <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s primary Totem Cards during the card-battling event on the Eighth Floor.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Cuba (Eighth Floor)</li><li><b>Race:</b> Red Maníseros Land Crab</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 24</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Raul the Crab on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Raul_the_Crab</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Razor Fox</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Razor Fox</b> are a Fourth Floor mob that is suffering from the DTs. The normal version of this mob can be found on the Fifth Floor. The <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a> comes across this mob at station 75 during the End of the Line Rescue. They only see the mob when it is suffering from stage 3 of the DTs, which is very different than the base version of the mob.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Razor Fox on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Razor_Fox</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Reaper Spider Minion</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Reaper Spider Minions</b> are terrifying arachnid mobs with celestial blood and devastating special attacks. Although they are commonly found on the Fifteenth Floor, they may appear on other levels as traveling merchants.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Reaper Spider Minion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Reaper_Spider_Minion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Reaper Spider Minion Patch</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Reaper Spider Minion Patch</b> is an <a href="bword://Upgrade Patch">Upgrade Patch</a> given to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> in a Platinum <a href="bword://Hell In A Handbasket Box">Hell In A Handbasket Box</a> rewarded to him for the <a href="bword://Holy Hell Achievement">Holy Hell Achievement</a>. This patch is applied to the <a href="bword://Enchanted Anarchist&#x27;s Battle Rattle">Enchanted Anarchist's Battle Rattle</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Platinum Hell In A Handbasket Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Reaper Spider Minion Patch on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Reaper_Spider_Minion_Patch</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Reavers</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The Reavers are a megacorporation and system government that live on a dyson sphere. Originally several different races that enhanced themselves with machines until the only organic part remaining was their brain. Originally related to the Nebulars.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Reavers on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Reavers</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Rebecca W</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Rebecca W</b> was a crawler from somewhere near Seattle, WA, whose real name was most likely Rebecca Wong. The <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a> labels her corpse as: <i>Lootable Corpse. Crawler Rebecca W. Level 3. Killed by Crawler <a href="bword://Frank Q">Frank Q</a>.</i></li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Near Seattle, WA</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 12</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Rebecca W on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Rebecca_W</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Red Beret</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Red Beret</b> is an item</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Red Beret on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Red_Beret</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Reef Explorer</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Reef Explorer</b> is a boss on the Eighth Floor. It is flanked by two <a href="bword://Swordfish Interlopers">Swordfish Interlopers</a>. The Reef Explorer is wearing an etheral glowing deep dive suit.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Reef Explorer on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Reef_Explorer</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Remex</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Remex</b> is an NPC associated with the Sex Workers Who Fell from the Heavens Quest and the Fools Who Broke the Glass Quest. He's also a former crawler.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Skyfowl</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2, Chapter 24</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Remex on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Remex</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Reminiscence Hydra of Malicious Compliance</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Reminiscence Hydra of Malicious Compliance</b> is a Level 125 City Boss designed by the <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a>. <i>Most</i> but not all parties must fight a custom hydra to win a Key during the second phase of the Eighth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Reminiscence Hydra of Malicious Compliance on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Reminiscence_Hydra_of_Malicious_Compliance</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Residual</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Residuals</b> are a hyperspatial, collective-mind alien race without a home who secretly inhabit the bodies of a host species on worlds containing <a href="bword://Primal">Primal</a> Engines.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Residual on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Residual</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Rev-Up</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Rev-Up</b> is a running gag in <a href="bword://Borant Corporation">Borant Corporation</a>'s 18-Level World Dungeon created as a political satire of the <a href="bword://Apothecary">Apothecary</a> and the <a href="bword://Plenty">Plenty</a>. The <a href="bword://Bloom">Bloom</a> and Borant Corporation lost a ton of money in communication stocks when the Plenty released the tunnel system, and retaliated by spreading rumors that (a) the Apothecary is the true creator of the tunnel system, and (b) using the tunnel system will indoctrinate you into the collective mind.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Rev-Up on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Rev-Up</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Rev-Up Immunity Smoothie</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b><a href="bword://Rev-Up">Rev-Up</a> Immunity Smoothies</b> are a discontinued Rev-Up product originally manufactured on the Second Floor. Consuming the smoothie gives immunity to the Taint and Vigorous Measles.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Crafting</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Rev-Up Immunity Smoothie on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Rev-Up_Immunity_Smoothie</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Rev-Up Magic Hair Restoration Tonic</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>Produced by <a href="bword://Rev-Up">Rev-Up</a>, <b>Rev-Up Magic Hair Restoration Tonic</b> stimulates hair growth when applied to any surface. The tonic is packaged in a set that includes plastic gloves, cotton swabs, multiple trays of assorted size and brushes, and an extremely long paper fold-out pamphlet with convoluted instructions.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Gore-Gore's Corpse</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Rev-Up Magic Hair Restoration Tonic on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Rev-Up_Magic_Hair_Restoration_Tonic</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Rev-Up Toilet-Grade Moonshine</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Rev-Up Toilet-Grade Moonshine</b> is manufactured and dropped by Unvaccinated <a href="bword://Clurichaun">Clurichaun</a> <a href="bword://Rev-Up">Rev-Up</a> Consultants on the Second Floor. Rev-Up Moonshine Consultants sell this item to other mobs, but it's definitely not a pyramid scheme.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Unvaccinated Clurichaun Rev-Up Consultant</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Rev-Up Toilet-Grade Moonshine on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Rev-Up_Toilet-Grade_Moonshine</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Rev-Up Vitamin Shots</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Rev-Up Vitamin Shots</b> (officially known by the system as the <b><a href="bword://Rev-Up">Rev-Up</a> Amazing Cure-All Vitamin Immunity Shot</b>) are highly addictive, race-specific opiate painkillers distributed to mobs on the Fourth Floor of the World Dungeon.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Krakaren (Manufacturer) / Pookas (Distributors)</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Rev-Up Vitamin Shots on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Rev-Up_Vitamin_Shots</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Reverse Gravity Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><i><b>Reverse Gravity</b></i> is a limited range spell that does exactly what its name suggests: gravity pulls all creatures and objects in range in the opposite direction, so the floor becomes the ceiling and the ceiling becomes the floor. When cast, the targets "fall" upward and crash into the ceiling. The spell's boundaries are abrupt: if someone or something is pushed over the boundary, it falls to the actual floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Reverse Gravity Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Reverse_Gravity_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Rickard</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Rickard</b> is a former Crawler and author of the <i><a href="bword://Dungeon Anarchist&#x27;s Cookbook">Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook</a> (24th Edition)</i>. Rickard entered the Dungeon with his pregnant wife. She disappeared when they passed through the doors, and he never saw her again.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Unknown</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 25</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Rickard on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Rickard</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ring of Water Breathing</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> gets a <b>Ring of Water Breathing</b> on the Fifth Floor. A glowing blue ring that twinkles with little sparkles.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Gold I'm Wet Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ring of Water Breathing on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ring_of_Water_Breathing</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ripper Wonton</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Ripper Wonton</b> is the host of <i>Danger Zone with Ripper Wonton</i>. Ripper is known as a "good-hearted gentleman" with strong opinions that treats guests fairly but will push back if he disagrees with them.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Setonix</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ripper Wonton on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ripper_Wonton</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Rishi</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Rishi</b> is a four-armed <a href="bword://Naga">Naga</a> who serves as a representative for the <a href="bword://Blood Sultanate">Blood Sultanate</a> during the Ninth Floor's Faction Wars. He is legally married into the Naga royal family,</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Sultan Rishi the Usurper, First of his Name of the Naga Uprising</li><li><b>Origin:</b> The Naga System</li><li><b>Race:</b> Naga</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 21</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Rishi on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Rishi</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Robot Donut</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Robot Donut</b> is toy created by the <a href="bword://Veriluxx RealPet Companions">Veriluxx RealPet Companions</a> company and owned by <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> As a part of their sponsorship deal of Donut, Veriluxx RealPet Companions sends her a special prize box. <a href="bword://Loita">Loita</a>, instructs the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a> that they are expected to play with the toy and praise it. They are also informed they will be appearing on a special show where they will be asked their opinion on the toy.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Robot Donut on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Robot_Donut</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Rock Bottom Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Rock Bottom Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for diving more than 1000 meters under the water.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Rock Bottom Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Rock_Bottom_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Rockard's Ring of Sniping</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> takes <b>Rockard's Ring of Sniping</b> from <a href="bword://Quan Ch">Quan Ch</a> on the Fifth Floor. An amber-stoned ring.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Quan Ch's hand</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Rockard's Ring of Sniping on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Rockard%27s_Ring_of_Sniping</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Rory</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Rory</b> is a Level 7 <a href="bword://Goblin Shamanka">Goblin Shamanka</a> NPC who appears on the First Floor. Her name was assigned by <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>. She is also the protagonist of the first part of Backstage at the Pineapple Cabaret.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> Goblins</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 15</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Rory on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Rory</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Rosemarie</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Rosemarie</b> is an elderly female <a href="bword://Dwarf">Dwarf</a> NPC who runs the Meat Shields in the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>. Rosemarie is normally found in the Penis Parade, where she runs her Meat Shields location. She has a mole like creature named Bernie who sits on her shoulder. She likes to throw coins at the strippers and gets in trouble for aiming at their eyes.</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 23</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Rosemarie on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Rosemarie</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Rosetta Thagra</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Rosetta Thagra</b> is an alien, a former Crawler, and an anarchist, best known as the author of the ninth edition of the <i><a href="bword://Dungeon Anarchist&#x27;s Cookbook">Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook</a></i>. Her marginal notes, addressed throughout to "comrades," lean heavily toward demolitions and practical bomb-craft.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Rosie</li><li><b>Race:</b> Crest</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 13</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Rosetta Thagra on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Rosetta_Thagra</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Rot Stickers</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Rot Stickers</b> are a Dungeon mob found on the First Floor, where they're generally levels 1-2. Rot Stickers are small, round, "black-hued ravioli"-like monsters capable of running on walls and ceilings. They chitter loudly as they approach, and "suicide bomb" crawlers and attempt to attach to their target's body. Three seconds after attaching, they explode; each blast inflicts the Take Down Effect and feels like "getting hit with a sledgehammer."</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Rot Stickers on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Rot_Stickers</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Roth</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Mr. Roth</b> was the landlord of <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s Apartment in Seattle, WA, before the transformation. He lived alone in the basement apartment, and was collected during the collapse.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Seattle, WA</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 46</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Roth on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Roth</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Royal Court of Princess Donut</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Royal Court of Princess Donut</b> (or simply the <b>Royal Court</b>) is the crawler party of <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and his sapient cat, Princess <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>, on this season of <i>Dungeon Crawler World</i>. <a href="bword://Mongo">Mongo</a> joined on the Second Floor, and the party's manager, <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a>, one floor after that.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Royal Court</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Royal Court of Princess Donut on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Royal_Court_of_Princess_Donut</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Rubber Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Rubber Spell</b> is a damage transfer and protection spell that redirects an incoming attack to a selected target, while mitigating a large portion of the damage to the caster.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Rubber Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Rubber_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ruby</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>An orphan <a href="bword://Changeling">Changeling</a> child from Hump Town. She suffers from Compression Sickness, and has no arms, and a sunken in head when in her default form.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Changeling</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ruby on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ruby</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ruckus</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Ruckus</b> is a Borough Boss on the Fifth Floor.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Spring-operated Chicken Hawk Sentinel</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 9</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ruckus on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ruckus</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Rude-Dolph the Blood-Nosed Slay-Deer</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Rude-Dolph the Blood-Nosed Slay-Deer</b> is an arena boss on the Eighth Floor.</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 28</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Rude-Dolph the Blood-Nosed Slay-Deer on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Rude-Dolph_the_Blood-Nosed_Slay-Deer</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Run, Little Guenter, Run Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Run, Little Guenter, Run Spell</b> is a spell given to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> in a Legendary <a href="bword://1914 Box">1914 Box</a>. The book grows centipede legs and runs away from Carl. It leaks foul-smelling black liquid. The book starts shivering and whimpering and shrieking "Stay Away! Don't Touch Me!" While it can speak, Carl can still pull the book into his <a href="bword://Inventory">Inventory</a>, so it is not considered a pet.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Run, Little Guenter, Run Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Run%2C_Little_Guenter%2C_Run_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Saber-Toothed Void Leopard</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Saber-Toothed Void Leopard</b> is a powerful creature race that <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> could have transformed into early in the crawl, but never does. Nothing about the race's abilities or appearance is described in the text. It is mentioned only as an example of the kind of dramatic, powerful race change offered to popular crawlers on the early floors.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Saber-Toothed Void Leopard on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Saber-Toothed_Void_Leopard</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Saccathian</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Saccathian</b> (or <b>Sacs</b>) are a common race outside the dungeon. They are described by <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> as squid-like and also like human sized Cthulhu. They squid-like tentacles dangling from cephalopod-eque faces.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Saccathian on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Saccathian</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sadie</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>Part of <a href="bword://Hekla">Hekla</a>'s group of <a href="bword://Brynhild&#x27;s Daughters">Brynhild's Daughters</a>. She casts her <i>Glass Prison</i> spell on the <a href="bword://Kravyad">Kravyad</a> so the group could pass through in The Iron Tangle.</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 21, Book 3</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sadie on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sadie</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sadir</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Sadir</b> was an alien bounty hunter who was hired to find and kidnap a cat known Gravy Boat so she could be brought into the dungeon. He had a mate and multiple children, who lived in a null commune in the Filt System. His mate was unaware of his being a bounty hunter, believing instead that he worked on an elemental barge.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Nullian</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Epilogue of Book 4</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sadir on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sadir</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Safehome Yolanda</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Safehome Yolanda</b> is a Dungeon guild founded on the Sixth Floor and led by the Crawler <a href="bword://Imani">Imani</a>, with Team Meadowlark as its controlling party. Chartered so that several parties could pool their personal space upgrades without merging into a single party, it became the shared home, workshop, and barracks of the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a> and most of <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s closest allies.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Safehome Yolanda on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Safehome_Yolanda</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sally</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Beatrice">Beatrice</a> managed to get her fired after she messaged <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> asking him out for drinks. Bea contacted Carl's boss, <a href="bword://Dick">Dick</a>, and claimed that Sally was stalking Carl. Dick agreed to fire her in return for Tiffany sending him a picture of her boobs, this was really just a picture she found on the internet. Beatrice and her friends named this episode Operation Slut Stop.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sally on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sally</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Salvatore</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Salvatore</b> is a member of the <a href="bword://201st Security Group Militia">201st Security Group Militia</a>, a group of <a href="bword://Apito">Apito</a> worshiping elves on the Third Floor. Salvatore is one of three robed elves outside the 201st Security Group Militia headquarters. They attempt to bring people in by handing them sticks with acorns hanging off the end.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Salvatore on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Salvatore</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Samantha</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Psamathe</b>, better known as <b>Samantha</b>, is a banished minor deity and a Withering Spirit who possesses a decapitated latex doll head. She is an NPC who joins the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a> as a companion and officially hired "Trainer."</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Samantha; Psamathe; Lika Love Doll Head; Goddess of Unrequited Love; Goddess of Crazy Ex-Girlfriends</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Celestial Ascendency (Twelfth Floor)</li><li><b>Race:</b> Naiad | Minor Deity</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 24</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Samantha on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Samantha</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sapper's Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Sapper's Box</b> is a Loot Box that gives various trap supplies.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Achievements</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sapper's Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sapper%27s_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sapper's Table</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>Sapper's Table</b> is a Crafting Workbench that can be purchased from a Safe Room Marketplace or received from a <a href="bword://Sapper&#x27;s Box">Sapper's Box</a>, and installed in a crawler's Personal Space. It allows crawlers to create stable traps, explosive items, and poisons, or to modify existing explosives and traps with modules or triggers.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Marketplace; Loot Boxes</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sapper's Table on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sapper%27s_Table</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sappy Gold Ring</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Sappy Gold Ring</b> is a ring <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> took off <a href="bword://Quan Ch">Quan Ch</a>'s arm.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Quan Ch's Arm</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sappy Gold Ring on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sappy_Gold_Ring</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sasquatch</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Sasquatch</b> is a race offered to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> during Third Floor race selection. A Sasquatch looks like a stereotypical Big Foot humanoid creature with massive feet and covered in hair. It has fangs and a giant forehead.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sasquatch on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sasquatch</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Satan's Lil' Hedgehog</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Satan's Lil' Hedgehogs</b> were a Second Floor mobs, but were moved to a lower level during the first round of floor patches because the <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a> determined that their armor-piercing quill attack was too strong for the new crawlers.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Satan's Lil' Hedgehog on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Satan%27s_Lil%27_Hedgehog</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Satchel Bomb</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> gets a bunch of <b>Satchel Bombs</b> in a <a href="bword://Boss Box">Boss Box</a> from killing an Odious Creeper on the Sixth Floor. A little bag with leather handles containing explosive equivalent to three sticks of hobgoblin dynamite. Enough to level a small town.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Boss Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Satchel Bomb on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Satchel_Bomb</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Savage Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Savage Box</b> is a type of Loot Box given players for violence against other crawlers. When the first crawler in a party gets their first Player Killer Skull, they receive a booklet of PVP Coupons for every crawler in their party.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Violence against Crawlers</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Savage Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Savage_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Scab Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Scab Box</b> is a Loot Box distributed for <b>participation in a mass crawler movement</b> (unionizing or similar). Gold Scab Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Scab Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Scab_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Scar Tissue Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Scar Tissue</b> is a spell whose only appearance in the text is as the title of a spellbook offered as a prize at the Butcher's Masquerade Ball. Nothing about what the spell actually does is ever revealed.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Scar Tissue Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Scar_Tissue_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Scat Thug</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Scat Thugs</b> are level 3 First Floor mobs. They are bipedal racoon-headed monsters that stand approximately 2 ft tall, are roughly as strong as <a href="bword://Goblins">Goblins</a>, and are armed with spears.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Scat Thug on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Scat_Thug</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Scatterer</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Scatterers</b> are chittering, cockroach-like mobs found on the Dungeon's First Floor (specifically, in the <a href="bword://Hoarder">Hoarder</a> neighborhood). Brood Guardians are approximately cat-sized, and quickly charge at their targets. Stomping on their head almost always results in a critical hit, and they leak white goo when killed. They occasionally drop vials of Scatterer Hemolymph, which is tagged as a alchemy material.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Scatterer on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Scatterer</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Scavenger's Daughter Upgrade Patch</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Scavenger's Daughter Upgrade Patch</b> is a divine, unique, and fleeting back upgrade patch awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> on the Eighth Floor in a <a href="bword://Celestial">Celestial</a> <a href="bword://Predator Box">Predator Box</a>. It doubles the stat point benefit of every other patch on the garment it is affixed to, grants flat bonuses to Dexterity and Strength alongside three further benefits, and confers shifting temporary effects in the presence of deities and demons.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Celestial Predator Box, opened on the Eighth Floor; Reward for the Apex Predator Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Scavenger's Daughter Upgrade Patch on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Scavenger%27s_Daughter_Upgrade_Patch</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Scolopendra</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Scolopendra</b> is the colossal monster of dungeon legend — a sleeping beast said to lie at the very bottom of the great dormant volcano and blamed for the ancient nine-tier attack, the cataclysm that killed or monstrously transformed most of the volcano-world's inhabitants before the current crawl.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Dungeon Boss; "the big bad centipede thing"</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Scolopendra's Lair, at the bottom of the World Dungeon's volcano</li><li><b>Race:</b> Giant Centipede</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2, Chapter 3</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Scolopendra on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Scolopendra</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Scourge Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Scourge Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for killing the most <a href="bword://Hunters">Hunters</a> on the Sixth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Scourge Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Scourge_Achievement</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Scree</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>Similar to <a href="bword://Gondii">Gondii</a> and Intellect <a href="bword://Hunters">Hunters</a>, <b>Infiltrators</b> (AKA <b>Scree</b>) are an aquatic brain parasite that can take control of a living brain. Crawlers may choose the "<a href="bword://Infiltrator">Infiltrator</a>" race on the Third Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Scree on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Scree</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Infiltrator</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>Similar to <a href="bword://Gondii">Gondii</a> and Intellect <a href="bword://Hunters">Hunters</a>, <b>Infiltrators</b> (AKA <b><a href="bword://Scree">Scree</a></b>) are an aquatic brain parasite that can take control of a living brain. Crawlers may choose the "Infiltrator" race on the Third Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Infiltrator on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Infiltrator</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Screeching Death Manatee</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Miss Talulah. Level 90 Screeching Death Manatee.</b> This is a special guest creature for the 10th and 11th floors. You’re probably going to find this hard to believe, but not only are these things sort of real, but that name they have—Screeching Death Manatees—is the actual name of record for this particular species. They were regular manatees, not unlike the Trichechus manatus most people from your world know and love. These guys were added to a former Land War world undergoing reparative terraforming when the company in charge of the project suddenly went bankrupt.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Screeching Death Manatee on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Screeching_Death_Manatee</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Scroll of Build Trench</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives approximately 50 <b>Scrolls of Build Trench</b> during the Ghosts of Earth floor. These scrolls are central to Carl's plan to save crawlers who didn't manage to get keys by the end of the 8th floor.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Silver Spam Box/ Adventurer Boxs</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Scroll of Build Trench on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Scroll_of_Build_Trench</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Scroll of Meat Hooks</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Scrolls of Meat Hooks</b> are scrolls that attract all carnivorous pet-class mobs within range toward the caster. Once cast, rancid-smelling black smoke trails from the caster's hand.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Scroll of Meat Hooks on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Scroll_of_Meat_Hooks</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Scroll of Upgrade</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Scroll of Upgrade</b> is a scroll that upgrades a currently equipped item. It is a limited time item so crawlers can't bring it to lower floors and upgrade later. While a crawler can take every item off except for one, <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> mentions that the upgrade isn't as good.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Scroll of Upgrade on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Scroll_of_Upgrade</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Scroll of Water Breathing</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Scroll of Water Breathing</b> is a scroll that allows a crawler to breathe underwater for a limited amount of time.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Platinum That Wasn't Too Smart, Was It? Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Scroll of Water Breathing on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Scroll_of_Water_Breathing</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sebastian</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Sebastian</b> is a level 21 <a href="bword://Bopca">Bopca</a> Protector, and the proprietor a First Floor Safe Room located near the <a href="bword://Juicer">Juicer</a>'s neighborhood. Overwhelmed by <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s Charisma, he gifts her his personal hairbrush and enthusiastically brushes her.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Bopca Homeworld</li><li><b>Race:</b> Bopca</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 26</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sebastian on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sebastian</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Second Chance Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><i><b>Second Chance</b></i> is a necromancy spell that allows the caster to raise a lower-level monster from the dead and turn them into an undead minion. The minion's level is 1/3 of its previous level (minimum level 1) and it will fight on the caster's side for a number of minutes equal to the spell's level. As a minion, it can be targeted by minion spells such as <a href="bword://Clockwork Triplicate">Clockwork Triplicate</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Second Chance Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Second_Chance_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Secondary Gig Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Secondary Gig Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> upon recieving the <a href="bword://Guild of Suffering">Guild of Suffering</a> quest from the <a href="bword://Enchanted Lock Box of the Night Wyrm">Enchanted Lock Box of the Night Wyrm</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Secondary Gig Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Secondary_Gig_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Self-Immolation Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Self-Immolation Spell</b> is a spell given to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> by <a href="bword://Emberus">Emberus</a> for being in his good graces as a Devotee.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Self-Immolation Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Self-Immolation_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Senegal Production Systems</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Senegal Production Systems, Unlimited</b> is a <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> corporation that owns and operates Production Trailers, which it rents out to multiple tunnel productions during the crawl.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Senegal Production Systems on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Senegal_Production_Systems</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sensation Entertainment Inc</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Sensation Entertainment, Incorporated</b> is the <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> production company responsible for <i>Vengeance of the Daughter</i>. They are located in one of the Center Systems, and their employees include Saccathians.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sensation Entertainment Inc on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sensation_Entertainment_Inc</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sentry Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Sentry Spell</b> is a spell that <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> receives from the <a href="bword://Tserendolgor Box">Tserendolgor Box</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sentry Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sentry_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Setonix</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Setonix</b> (or <b>Quokkas</b>) are a race that appears as a cross between a wombat and ewok, they are around 4 feet tall and are extremely cute. According to Evo, most people call them Quokkas.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Setonix on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Setonix</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Seventh Floor Pole Position</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Seventh-Floor Pole Position</b> is a one-time "Future Floor Boon" that was sold at the prize counter of the Butcher's Masquerade Ball and guaranteed its buyer a protected, privileged start to the Seventh Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Seventh Floor Pole Position on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Seventh_Floor_Pole_Position</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sex Pervert Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Sex Pervert Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> pierced himself with the <a href="bword://Enchanted Nipple Ring of the Defiler">Enchanted Nipple Ring of the Defiler</a> while trying to convince <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> it wasn't weird and wouldn't make her a "whore".</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sex Pervert Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sex_Pervert_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Shadow Leaks</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Shadow Leaks</b> are level 14 are smoke-like ghost mobs that utilize a stinging cold attack. The can be found on the Third Floor inside the Medium <a href="bword://Skyfowl">Skyfowl</a> Settlement at night.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Shadow Leaks on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Shadow_Leaks</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Shambling Acid Impaler</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Shambling Acid Impalers</b> were a common Second Floor mob in previous <a href="bword://Borant Corporation">Borant Corporation</a>-hosted seasons of <i>Dungeon Crawler World</i>. They are hairy, green, four-legged monsters that spit acidic darts capable of melting a crawler's skin from their bones.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Shambling Acid Impaler on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Shambling_Acid_Impaler</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Shambling Berserker</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Shambling Berserker</b> are tall piles of body parts, all sewn together and acting like a typical zombie. The can be found on the Third Floor outside the Medium <a href="bword://Skyfowl">Skyfowl</a> Settlement.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Shambling Berserker on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Shambling_Berserker</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Shamus Chaindrive</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Shamus Chaindrive</b> is a deceased bugbear treasure hunter and submarine captain whose decades-long hunt for the <a href="bword://Gate of the Feral Gods">Gate of the Feral Gods</a> led him to the Necropolis of <a href="bword://Anser">Anser</a> on the Fifth Floor, where the automaton guardians he left behind are still active long after his death. He never appears on-page; everything known about him comes from the AI Descriptions of the constructs and <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a> tied to his story.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Shamus Chaindrive on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Shamus_Chaindrive</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Shango</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Shango</b> is a god who is part of the <a href="bword://Orisha">Orisha</a> pantheon, with <a href="bword://Ogun">Ogun</a>, <a href="bword://Legba">Legba</a>, <a href="bword://Oshun">Oshun</a>, <a href="bword://Asojano">Asojano</a>, <a href="bword://Inle">Inle</a>, and <a href="bword://Yemaya">Yemaya</a>. During the Thorn Room Boss Battle, if his shrine is repaired: “He’s a little shy. You will learn a level-15 Lightning spell if you repair it. You will gain the ability to train this spell to 20. Hint, hint that spell might come in handy later. Shango will ascend.”</li><li><b>Race:</b> Orisha Deity</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Shango on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Shango</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sharp-Elbows</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Sharp-Elbows</b> is an <a href="bword://Ogre">Ogre</a> Necromancer Witch, covered in spikes, who fights <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> on floor 8.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sharp-Elbows on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sharp-Elbows</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Shatter Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Shatter Spell</b> is a spell that disarms attackers. Any attack that lands upon the object imbued with this enchantment has a 1.5% chance to disarm the opponent. If the opponent is disarmed, there is a 90% chance the item will drop to the ground, a 5% chance the weapon will break, and a 5% chance the weapon will be immediately transferred to your inventory.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Shatter Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Shatter_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Shattering Train Bomb</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Shattering Train Bomb</b> is what the <a href="bword://Nightmare Express">Nightmare Express</a> turns into when there is no one driving the train. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> creates this bomb on the Fourth Floor by killing the train engineers on the Nightmare Express using his <a href="bword://Protective Shell Spell">Protective Shell Spell</a>. <a href="bword://Fire Brandy">Fire Brandy</a> helps him defuse the bomb by teaching him how to drive the train, earning him the <a href="bword://Kept A Rollin&#x27; Achievement">Kept A Rollin' Achievement</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Nightmare Express (Fourth Floor</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Shattering Train Bomb on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Shattering_Train_Bomb</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sheet Music</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Sheet Music</b> is similar to a scroll or magic book but exclusive to bard classes. It allows bards to sing a song they normally couldn’t, the system helped them perform if they had the music in front of them making it easier to pull off but with a chance of failure if the performance was out of key. If sung badly the sheet music tears a little bit and with too many tears, it’s ruined. If sung perfectly and in the correct pitch the spell is added to your bard repertoire, when this happens the sheet music isn’t consumed and can be sold or given to someone else.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sheet Music on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sheet_Music</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sheol Bricks</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Sheol Bricks</b> are the hardened, shriveled, blackened corpses of <a href="bword://Lesser Demon">Lesser Demon</a> infants. Common on the Fifteenth Floor, these coal-like bricks are a valuable resource that burn long and hot when exposed to fire.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Lesser Demon MILF; Fifteenth Floor</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sheol Bricks on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sheol_Bricks</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sheol Fire</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Sheol Fire</b> is an extremely destructive fire native to Sheol, the Fifteenth Floor, hot enough to turn wood instantly to ash and rock to lava. Unlike ordinary fire, it also empowers any demon it touches instead of harming it.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sheol Fire on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sheol_Fire</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sheol Glass Reaper Case</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Sheol Glass Reaper Case</b> is a case that can contain extreme things and stop them in time, such as a crystal nuke that is a millisecond away from exploding.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sheol Glass Reaper Case on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sheol_Glass_Reaper_Case</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Shi Maria</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Shi Maria</b> is a demi-god, <a href="bword://Reaper Spider Minion">Reaper Spider Minion</a>, and Level 140 City Boss encountered in the Cuba region of the Eighth Floor. Also known as the Screamer, the Bedlam Bride, the Widow Endless, and MaeMae, she briefly serves as a powerful Totem <a href="bword://T&#x27;Ghee Card">T'Ghee Card</a> in Princess <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s deck before binding herself to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> as a living tattoo.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> The Screamer, The Reviled, Kwaku's Love, The Corrupted Paramour, The Bedlam Bride, The Widow Endless, MaeMae</li><li><b>Origin:</b> The Celestial Realm (banished to the Eighth Floor)</li><li><b>Race:</b> Reaper Spider Minion (Demi-god)</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 8</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Shi Maria on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Shi_Maria</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Shield Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><i><b>Shield</b></i> is a popular protection spell that creates a translucent sphere around the caster, and repels corporeal red-tagged mobs and physical attacks. Unlike <i>Protective Shell</i>, <i>Shield</i> moves with the caster.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Shield Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Shield_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Shock Chomper</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Shock Chomper</b> are a Fourth Floor mob that looks like a lion-headed naga with an electrical attack that can be found on the Yellow Line. No full description is given other than <b>"lesser nagas with mommy issues."</b> Given that this whole floor is a political parody, this is most likely in reference to the <a href="bword://Naga">Naga</a> and the story of the Sepsis Whore.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Shock Chomper on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Shock_Chomper</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Shoe Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Shoe Box</b> are <a href="bword://Loot Boxes">Loot Boxes</a> awarded for foot related achievements.</li><li><b>Source:</b> This Little Piggy Went to Market! Achievement (Platinum)</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Shoe Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Shoe_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Shrink Wand</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Shrink Wand</b> is a wand that causes items to shrink in size. Has 10 charges. The effect can be <b>prematurely stopped.</b></li></ul><p class="source">Source: Shrink Wand on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Shrink_Wand</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Siege Master Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Siege Master Box</b> is a Loot Box distributed for <b>participating in large-scale warfare</b>. <b>Contents:</b> Unclear, but <b><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> obtained powerful explosives and siege-based gear</b>​</li><li><b>Source:</b> B'sieging Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Siege Master Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Siege_Master_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sierra</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Sierra - Northropi <a href="bword://Vampire">Vampire</a></b>. This is a Bereft Minion of Viscount Fog</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sierra on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sierra</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sigmund Textiles Foundry</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The Sigmund Textiles Foundry is a publicly traded company based in the <a href="bword://Skull Empire">Skull Empire</a>. It's shares are valued at 10.422 credits.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sigmund Textiles Foundry on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sigmund_Textiles_Foundry</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Silfa</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Silfa</b> is a fairy class healer crawler who is a part of <a href="bword://Brynhild&#x27;s Daughters">Brynhild's Daughters</a>. She has two daughters who came into the dungeon with her. Silfa has at least three spells, a healing spell, a map hiding skill, and an ice spell.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Wisteria Fairy</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 22, Book 3</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Silfa on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Silfa</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Silver Ring</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Silver Ring</b> is simple rings that, when equipped on a crawler's finger, boost a specific stat by a set value. They can be found in Silver <a href="bword://Loot Boxes">Loot Boxes</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Silver Loot Boxes</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Silver Ring on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Silver_Ring</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Simoom</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Simoom</b> is a rhino that <a href="bword://Ferdinand">Ferdinand</a> uses as a mount on the Sixth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Simoom on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Simoom</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sinjin</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Sinjin</b> is a former Crawler and author of the <i><a href="bword://Dungeon Anarchist&#x27;s Cookbook">Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook</a> (15th Edition)</i>. Sinjin came from a race with paws. They were most likely killed by the Dungeon goddess Kuraokami after trying to leave the faith.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Unknown</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sinjin on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sinjin</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sister Ines</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Sister Ines Quiteria</b> is a Cuban nun and a Crawler from Earth who leads a three-crawler squad alongside Anton and <a href="bword://Paz Lo">Paz Lo</a>. Her squad allies briefly with the Royal Court on the Eighth Floor.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Sister Ines; El Segador de La Habana</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Cuba</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Cat Girl</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 5</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sister Ines on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sister_Ines</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Size-Up Potion</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Size-Up Potion</b> is a potion that gives detail about mobs including their stats and skills.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Size-Up Potion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Size-Up_Potion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Skarn</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>A juvenile changeling, about eight years old. Orphaned and living in Hump Town after the Gnomes bombed their town. Operates the telescope. Currently being looked after by <a href="bword://Flint">Flint</a>.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Changeling</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 2, Book 4</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Skarn on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Skarn</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Skellie</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Skellies</b> are "your typical, run-of-the-mill reanimated skeleton," and may be created by the <i>Boned</i> spell. In the Dungeon, several <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a> share this race, but Skellies may also appear as "weak undead" mobs.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Skellie on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Skellie</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Skewer Belle</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Skewer Belle</b> is a mushroom that, upon touching the top, extrudes a spike and causes skin to boil if it pierces you, The spike only activates if you touch the top, therefore it is advised that you should only touch the stem of this mushroom. The <b>Skewer Belle</b> has useful alchemical properties.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Sixth Floor</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Skewer Belle on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Skewer_Belle</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Skill Potion</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>Skill Potion</b> is a special potion that, when consumed, adds a single level to a skill specified in the item's description. Typically received in <a href="bword://Loot Boxes">Loot Boxes</a>, Skill Potions may be the only way to unlock certain Crawler Menu options such as sorting inventory by value.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Loot Boxes</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Skill Potion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Skill_Potion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Skull Empire</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Skull Empire</b> is one of the largest and oldest system governments in the <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a>, ruled by an orcish royal family that claims descent from gods and royalty. The family owns the Death Watch Extreme Dungeon Mayhem production and fields the Skull Clan in Faction Wars on the Ninth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Skull Empire on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Skull_Empire</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Skydiver's Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Skydiver's Box</b> is a Loot Box distributed the <a href="bword://Cannonball! Achievement">Cannonball! Achievement</a> for falling from a great height.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Cannonball! Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Skydiver's Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Skydiver%27s_Box</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Skyfowl</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Skyfowl</b> are a race of flying, eagle-headed humanoids and the birth race of <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a>. Before the Cataclysm, they ruled the Third Floor's Over City, and they still govern several of its settlements.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Skyfowl on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Skyfowl</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Skyfowl Upgrade Patch</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Skyfowl Upgrade Patch</b> is an <a href="bword://Upgrade Patch">Upgrade Patch</a> given to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> on the Sixth Floor in a Gold <a href="bword://Ranged Weapon Box">Ranged Weapon Box</a> rewarded to him for the <a href="bword://That&#x27;s not how you use arrows, dumbass Achievement">That's not how you use arrows, dumbass Achievement</a>. This patch is applied to the <a href="bword://Enchanted Anarchist&#x27;s Battle Rattle">Enchanted Anarchist's Battle Rattle</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Gold Ranged Weapon Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Skyfowl Upgrade Patch on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Skyfowl_Upgrade_Patch</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Skyfowl Upgrade Patch</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Skyfowl Upgrade Patch</b> is an <a href="bword://Upgrade Patch">Upgrade Patch</a> given to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> on the Sixth Floor in a Gold <a href="bword://Ranged Weapon Box">Ranged Weapon Box</a> rewarded to him for the <a href="bword://That&#x27;s not how you use arrows, dumbass Achievement">That's not how you use arrows, dumbass Achievement</a>. This patch is applied to the <a href="bword://Enchanted Anarchist&#x27;s Battle Rattle">Enchanted Anarchist's Battle Rattle</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Gold Ranged Weapon Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Skyfowl Upgrade Patch on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Skyfowl_Upgrade_Patch</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Skylar Spinach</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Skylar Spinach</b> is a Totem <a href="bword://T&#x27;Ghee Card">T'Ghee Card</a> on the Eighth Floor. This card is held by the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Eighth Floor Cuba</li><li><b>Race:</b> Monk Seal</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 9</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Skylar Spinach on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Skylar_Spinach</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sledge</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Sledge</b> is a <a href="bword://Cretin">Cretin</a> NPC employed as a bodyguard at the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a> and later assigned to the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a> as permanent security. He works alongside <a href="bword://Bomo">Bomo</a>, a fellow cretin bodyguard.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Sledgie</li><li><b>Race:</b> Cretin</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 8</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sledge on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sledge</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Slime</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Slimes</b> are toxic, arm-less mobs found on <i>at least</i> the First Floor and Seventh Floor of the Dungeon. Level 2 Green Slimes are roughly pig-sized gelatinous green blobs that occupy at least one neighborhood on the First Floor. Their flesh is acidic and burns on contact.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Slime on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Slime</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Slingshot</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Slingshots</b> are small, handheld, hand-powered projectile weapons typically made with a Y-shaped frame with an elastic strip tied to the ends of each prong. On Earth, slingshots are common toys but have also been used as military weapons by guerilla forces. During the Siege of Marawi in 2017, the Philippine Army's elite Scout Rangers used slingshots to hurl grenades at opposing forces.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Mobs</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Slingshot on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Slingshot</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Slit</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Slit</b> is a Feral Minor Demon who was banished to the Nothing a very, very long time ago. Slit and her sisters, including <a href="bword://Gash">Gash</a>, are members of a demon harem living in the Nothing. <a href="bword://Samantha">Samantha</a>, while banished there, talked about her sexual exploits with her king, and Slit thought that Samantha had had sex with <i>their</i> king. Naturally, Samantha trolled them with made-up stories about her wild sexcapades with <i>their</i> king. Now, Slit and her sisters hate Samantha.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> Lesser Demon</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 34</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Slit on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Slit</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sluggalo</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Sluggalos</b>, initially identified by the system as <b>Pox Slugs</b>, are a bizarre, juggalo-themed species of slug monsters born from the infectious boils of the SlugPox disease. They exhibit a crude, rowdy culture and serve as highly enthusiastic, albeit expendable, combatants for the <a href="bword://Princess Posse">Princess Posse</a> during the Faction Wars.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sluggalo on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sluggalo</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Smeat Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Smeat Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> on the Eighth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Smeat Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Smeat_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Smoke Form Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Smoke Form</b> is a Phase-style travel spell granted by <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s Assassin of Sekhmet class, letting her slip through and around obstacles. Unlike <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s Gloom Wraith Phase, which is an attack that forces movement in a single direction, Smoke Form is purely a travel spell, letting the caster equally slip through and around obstacles without a fixed direction.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Smoke Form Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Smoke_Form_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Smushed for Daddy Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Smushed for Daddy Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for being stepped on by <a href="bword://Grull">Grull</a>. Carl opens this box in a safe room on the Fifth Floor</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Smushed for Daddy Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Smushed_for_Daddy_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Snail Trail</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Snail Trail</b> is a goblin dancer at Bitches, a club inside the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>, and the wife of <a href="bword://Splash Zone">Splash Zone</a>. Snail Trail works the early shift at Bitches, alongside her mother, <a href="bword://Grandma Sticky">Grandma Sticky</a>, who works the later shift. Splash Zone, her husband, speaks fondly and proudly of her pole routine.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Snail Trail on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Snail_Trail</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Snare Trap</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Snare Traps</b> activate when stepped on, and hold the target in place. During the second phase of the Eighth Floor, <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s snare traps hold targets in place for fifteen seconds.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Market</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Snare Trap on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Snare_Trap</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sniper's Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Sniper's Box</b> is a Loot Box distributed for <b>long-range combat proficiency</b>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Hail Mary Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sniper's Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sniper%27s_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Social Media Board</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Social Media Board</b> is a tier-1 Personal Space Social Upgrade that allows crawlers to view a running log of social media comments. It is heavily moderated by the <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a> and fully replaces your appointed <a href="bword://Borant Corporation">Borant Corporation</a> Social Media Manager. The board beeps and clicks as the feed updates.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Social Media Board on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Social_Media_Board</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Society for the Eradication of Cocker Spaniels</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Society for the Eradication of Cocker Spaniels (TSECS), NFC</b><b>, dba</b> <b>as <a href="bword://Princess Posse">Princess Posse</a> Enterprises, NFC</b> is a nonprofit <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> organization and NFC taking legal action to prevent the Syndicate from preserving Cocker Spaniel DNA. It also sponsors the Princess Posse faction on the Ninth Floor.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> TSECS; Princess Posse Enterprises</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Society for the Eradication of Cocker Spaniels on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Society_for_the_Eradication_of_Cocker_Spaniels</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Soft Vore Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Soft Vore</b> is an <a href="bword://Achievement">Achievement</a> awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> after he got eaten by <a href="bword://Lusca">Lusca</a> the <a href="bword://Octo-Shark">Octo-Shark</a> Brood <a href="bword://Mother">Mother</a> Queen. Carl receives this achievement on the Fifth Floor after getting eaten whole by Lusca. No one else that participated in the fight got this achievement.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Soft Vore Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Soft_Vore_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Soul Crystals</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Soul Crystals</b> is a power source that elves use. They are created when certain types of people die and their souls are filtered through <a href="bword://Scolopendra">Scolopendra</a>'s body. They are powered by and run off actual souls.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Souls dying in a set area to charge the crystal</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Soul Crystals on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_Crystals</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Spam Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>A Silver <b>Spam Box</b> is awarded to "most everyone in the dungeon" after the first card battles on the eight floor. TBA</li><li><b>Source:</b> Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Spam Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Spam_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Special Play</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> come up with Special Plays as a system for quickly taking specific actions on the battlefield. Each play is supposed to be followed immediately and without question upon being called.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Special Play on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Special_Play</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Spicy Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Spicy Box</b> is a type of Loot Box given to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for achievements the <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a> <i>really</i> likes. Due to the individual nature of each awarded box, this page is broken up by book.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Achievements</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Spicy Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Spicy_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Spider Stalker</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Spider Stalkers</b> (also frequently referred to as spider automatons or seeker spiders) are small, crafted robotic devices that function as mechanical versions of the explosive "rot sticker" mobs. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> uses them as mobile delivery systems for bombs, traps, and potions.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Crafted by Carl (Requires a Main Driveshaft and automaton components)</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Spider Stalker on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Spider_Stalker</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Spike Module</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>Spike Module</b> is a type of trap that produces spikes that move up and down off the surface that it is placed on. “The spike module had a similar description (to Alarm Module), but it would cause 50-centimeter spikes to pop out of the ground at two second intervals in a one meter-square area. Friendly <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a> and crawlers wouldn’t set it off, but once triggered, it would keep spiking up and down forever, so we had to be careful.”</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Spike Module on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Spike_Module</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Splash Zone</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Splash Zone</b> is an NPC otter and former stripper at the Penis Parade who serves as a mercenary and loyal ally to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>, Princess <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>, and their faction.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Splashy, Splash</li><li><b>Origin:</b> The Dungeon (Desperado Club)</li><li><b>Race:</b> Otter</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 23</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Splash Zone on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Splash_Zone</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Split Personality Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Split Personality</b> is a spell that cuts a living creature vertically in half, leaving both resulting halves alive and functional. Victims of Split Personality are severed exactly down the center, from between the eyes through the groin, left standing on a single leg with one arm and a second arm above it. Split victims rarely survive more than a few minutes after the casting, and the two halves normally must wear supportive suits to keep their organs from spilling out. Reuniting the two halves afterward requires a fleshmancer.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Split Personality Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Split_Personality_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sprout Forest Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Sprout Forest</b> is an ability of <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s that lets her grow a wide variety of plants, not limited to trees despite the name. Despite its name, Sprout Forest isn't restricted to growing trees; it lets Donut choose from a wide array of plant types. She uses it in consultation with <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> to select a specific flower for decoration purposes.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sprout Forest Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sprout_Forest_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Spunky Jefferson the Enchanted Nickel Sock of the Elderly Miser</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Spunky Jefferson the Enchanted Nickel Sock of the Elderly Miser</b> is a weapon. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> gets the <a href="bword://Uh oh. It talks. Achievement">Uh oh. It talks. Achievement</a> for examining this weapon.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Spunky Jefferson the Enchanted Nickel Sock of the Elderly Miser on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Spunky_Jefferson_the_Enchanted_Nickel_Sock_of_the_Elderly_Miser</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Squim Conglomerate</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Squim Conglomerate</b> is a <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> Corporation that mines planets. They ran the crawl before Dungeon Crawler World: Earth, a battle royale style season called Battle for Planet Aryl. The entire planet battles down to one champion. It makes good television but does not earn them a lot of money. The season does not include Faction Wars or <a href="bword://Celestial">Celestial</a> Ascendency segments.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Squim Conglomerate on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Squim_Conglomerate</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Squonk</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Squonk</b> are a mob on the Eighth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Squonk on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Squonk</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Stairwells</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Stairwells</b> are a feature of the Dungeon that allows for passage between floors. Different floors of the dungeon may have different rules governing how their stairwells are accessed.</li><li><b>Source:</b> World Dungeon / System AI</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Stairwells on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Stairwells</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Stalwart</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Stalwart</b> is an orc and the crown prince of the <a href="bword://Skull Empire">Skull Empire</a>, one of the largest and oldest governments in the <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a>. He orders the execution of <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> after Carl insults his father, <a href="bword://King Rust">King Rust</a>, on live television.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Captain Enormous (proposed by Donut)</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Skull Empire</li><li><b>Race:</b> Orc</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 44</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Stalwart on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Stalwart</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Standing Ovation</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Standing Ovation</b> is a bard spell that increases the party's dexterity and make their regular spells more powerful.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Standing Ovation on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Standing_Ovation</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Station Mimic</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Station Mimic</b> is a City Boss on the Fourth Floor. They are at station 433, Terminous station. Mimics are shapeshifting creatures that can turn into inanimate objects to fool crawlers into coming close enough to be eaten. If a part of a mimic is chopped off, the removed part turns into a spidery creature and crawls back to join the whole. Bashing weapons and magic do nothing against it. If more than 50% of the body mass is removed, it can no longer heal or transform. The sliced pieces can't be killed and won't die until the entire thing dies.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> Mimic</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 17</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Station Mimic on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Station_Mimic</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Stock Certificate</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The bearer of this instrument now holds one share of common stock in the <a href="bword://Sigmund Textiles Foundry">Sigmund Textiles Foundry</a>, a publicly-traded company based in the Gun-ya system within the <a href="bword://Skull Empire">Skull Empire</a> and traded via the I.R.F.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Stock Certificate on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Stock_Certificate</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Stone Hawk</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Stone Hawks</b> are a pet-class mob that can be found in the Dungeon. Stone Hawks resemble standard American brown hawks, but their underwing coverts are opalescent. These hawks have the ability to transform their targets into stone through unspecified means; the target can then be shattered.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Stone Hawk on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Stone_Hawk</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Stranger Danger Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Stranger Danger Box</b> is a Loot Box distributed for <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> unknowingly inviting a red-tagged NPC boss into a saferoom. <b>Bronze Stranger Danger Box</b></li></ul><p class="source">Source: Stranger Danger Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Stranger_Danger_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Street Urchin</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Street Urchin</b> are the janitor mobs of the Third Floor. They appear to consume trash. Street Urchins look like knee high tumbleweeds, covered in black spikes about 15 inches long.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Street Urchin on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Street_Urchin</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Stuffed Figure</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Stuffed Figure</b> is a summoning device that looks like a beanie baby in the shape of a race of creature or a specific figure. Removing the tag summons the creature, having them fight on behalf of the summoner. The stuffed figures are made by <a href="bword://Jaxbrin Amusements, Limited">Jaxbrin Amusements, Limited</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Jaxbrin Amusements, Limited</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Stuffed Figure on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Stuffed_Figure</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Stuffed Grulke Infantry Figure</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Stuffed Grulke Infantry Figure</b> is a <a href="bword://Stuffed Figure">Stuffed Figure</a> of a <a href="bword://Grulke">Grulke</a> wearing a spiked helmet made by <a href="bword://Jaxbrin Amusements, Limited">Jaxbrin Amusements, Limited</a>. <a href="bword://Bautista">Bautista</a> acquired this from <a href="bword://Miss Quill">Miss Quill</a>'s apartment on the Third Floor. He gives the stuffed animal to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> after the End of the Line Rescue.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Miss Quill's apartment</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Stuffed Grulke Infantry Figure on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Stuffed_Grulke_Infantry_Figure</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Stuffed Kimaris Figure</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Stuffed Kimaris Figure</b> is a <a href="bword://Stuffed Figure">Stuffed Figure</a> made by <a href="bword://Jaxbrin Amusements, Limited">Jaxbrin Amusements, Limited</a>. It is a "Unique" Item, and one of the most valuable items in <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s <a href="bword://Inventory">Inventory</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Miss Quill's collection</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Stuffed Kimaris Figure on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Stuffed_Kimaris_Figure</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Kimaris</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b><a href="bword://Stuffed Kimaris Figure">Stuffed Kimaris Figure</a></b> is a <a href="bword://Stuffed Figure">Stuffed Figure</a> made by <a href="bword://Jaxbrin Amusements, Limited">Jaxbrin Amusements, Limited</a>. It is a "Unique" Item, and one of the most valuable items in <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s <a href="bword://Inventory">Inventory</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Miss Quill's collection</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Kimaris on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Kimaris</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Stuffed Slate Butterfly Figure</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Stuffed Slate Butterfly Figure</b> is a <a href="bword://Stuffed Figure">Stuffed Figure</a> of a Slate Butterfly made by <a href="bword://Jaxbrin Amusements, Limited">Jaxbrin Amusements, Limited</a>. See also: <a href="bword://Talisman of the Slate Butterfly">Talisman of the Slate Butterfly</a> (Book 1)</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Stuffed Slate Butterfly Figure on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Stuffed_Slate_Butterfly_Figure</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Succubus</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Succubus</b> are the female equivalent of an <a href="bword://Incubus">Incubus</a>. <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> warns <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> about staying away from girls with horns who would be attracted to his increased charisma.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Succubus on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Succubus</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sugar Cube</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>Sugar Cube is a persian cat and one of <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s cousin and half aunt. She was used for <a href="bword://Reminiscence Hydra of Malicious Compliance">Reminiscence Hydra of Malicious Compliance</a> on the Eighth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sugar Cube on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sugar_Cube</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Summary Judgement Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Summary Judgement Box</b> is a Loot Box distributed for <a href="bword://Fight the Power Achievement">Fight the Power Achievement</a>. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> won seven of these for winning seven court cases.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Fight the Power Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Summary Judgement Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Summary_Judgement_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Summon Guard Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Summon Guard</b> is a summoning spell that instantly teleports backup to the caster's location. It appears both as an innate ability of the fairy <a href="bword://Astrid">Astrid</a> and, separately, as a type of preset trap module planted in contested territory.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Summon Guard Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Summon_Guard_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sun Shrine</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Sun Shrine</b> appears in a crawler's Personal Space if they choose to worship <a href="bword://Emberus">Emberus</a>. The shrine is a bubbling fountain consisting of a sun disk, a cup, and a skull; the blessed water runs red, and can be used in crafting.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Worshipping Emberus</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sun Shrine on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sun_Shrine</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Superb Constitution Buff Potion</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> brews <b>Superb Constitution Buff Potion</b> on the Fourth Floor using the level 3 <a href="bword://Alchemy Table">Alchemy Table</a>. The <a href="bword://Potion">Potion</a> buffs a player's Constitution by a random number between 1 and 4 and the crawler can only take two total potions.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Mordecai's Alchemy Table</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Superb Constitution Buff Potion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Superb_Constitution_Buff_Potion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Superior Fire Demon</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>These bitches are three pugs short of a grumble. <b>Superior Fire <a href="bword://Demons">Demons</a></b> are notorious for their power, instability, and ability to wreak havoc.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Superior Fire Demon on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Superior_Fire_Demon</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Suppurating Eye Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Suppurating Eye Spell</b> is a common lich spell that allows the caster to see or overhear anything going on while the spell is active. Commonly attached to Scrolls.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Suppurating Eye Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Suppurating_Eye_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Surefire</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>A Surefire adds the “Guided” status to any projectile, powered or not. It may be utilized on a vast array of crafting tables. If added to an arrow or bolt, you must choose a target prior to unleashing the weapon, and the projectile will seek that target.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Sniper's Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Surefire on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Surefire</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Survivor's Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>Survivor's Box</b> is a Loot Box awarded to crawlers who only just barely survive a battle. <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> receives this box on the First Floor after the fight with the <a href="bword://Juicer">Juicer</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Achievements</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Survivor's Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Survivor%27s_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sushi Smoothie Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Sushi Smoothie Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for using the Soul Reaper Skill on a <a href="bword://Concierge Shark">Concierge Shark</a> to cure his Soul Poisoning debuff.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sushi Smoothie Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sushi_Smoothie_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Svern</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Svern</b> is a <a href="bword://Changeling">Changeling</a> impersonating a <a href="bword://Dromedarian">Dromedarian</a> in Hump Town.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Changeling Principal</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 6</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Svern on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Svern</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Swordfish Interlopers</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Swordfish Interlopers</b> are a bipedal swordfish mob.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Swordfish Interlopers on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Swordfish_Interlopers</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Sydnee Iglacia</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Sydnee Iglacia</b> is a <a href="bword://Saccathian">Saccathian</a> author and self-described crawl historian. A civilian rather than a crawler, she first appears as a panelist at CrawlCon, where she is largely overlooked despite her passion for chronicling the dungeon's history.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Makoka Cloud (SCC 5 / "Observation Deck")</li><li><b>Race:</b> Saccathian</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 5, Chapter 33</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Sydnee Iglacia on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Sydnee_Iglacia</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Syndicate</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Syndicate</b> is a massive intergalactic governing body composed of over three billion independent star systems and quintillions of citizens of various races. It orchestrates the seizure and mining of seeded planets, running the World Dungeon broadcasts—the Crawl—as a lucrative source of entertainment and resources.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Syndicate on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Syndicate</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Syndicate Council</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Syndicate Council</b> is the governing body of the <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a>, the interstellar government whose member states set and enforce law across more than three billion independent star systems. Races apply to the council for membership.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> The Council</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Syndicate Council on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Syndicate_Council</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>System AI</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>System AI</b> is the artificial intelligence that generates, narrates, and enforces the rules of the World Dungeon on <i>Dungeon Crawler World: Earth</i>. When <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> is involved, it frequently refers to itself as "Daddy."</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> "Daddy" (self-applied, with Carl)</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Hive Home (Mantis system); installed in Earth's Primal Engine</li><li><b>Race:</b> Macro AI</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 1</li></ul><p class="source">Source: System AI on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/System_AI</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>T'Ghee Card</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>T'Ghee cards</b> are the playing pieces of T'Ghee, the deck-building game the dungeon imposed on every crawler for the length of the eighth floor.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Flagging a creature at 5% health or below; Looted from defeated opponents</li></ul><p class="source">Source: T'Ghee Card on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/T%27Ghee_Card</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Take That Shit Off Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Take That Shit Off Spell</b> is a theorized spell capable of stripping away biological armor, meaning it could, in theory, be used to forcibly remove an alien pilot from inside a god's Soul Armor body.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Take That Shit Off Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Take_That_Shit_Off_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Talent</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>He was killed after firing a lightning bolt too close to the All Tree. He has three scrolls of lightning and almost 70,000 piece of gold on him.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Orc</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Talent on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Talent</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Talisman of the Slate Butterfly</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Talisman of the Slate Butterfly</b> is a small silver butterfly charm on a small silver ring, so it can be attached to collars or other jewelry. It jingles when it moves.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Gold Magic Item Loot Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Talisman of the Slate Butterfly on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Talisman_of_the_Slate_Butterfly</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Talk of the Town Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Talk of the Town Box</b> is a Loot Box distributed for <b>gaining significant public attention</b> due to strategic actions. Gold Talk of the Town Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Talk of the Town Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Talk_of_the_Town_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Tally</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Tally</b> is the first <a href="bword://Bopca">Bopca</a> Protector that <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> meet inside the Dungeon. Tally agreed to work for <a href="bword://Borant Corporation">Borant Corporation</a> to save his own home world from a transformation. He has worked for Borant Corporation for many cycles, and has spent years learning to make Earth food. He makes an <i>awesome</i> <a href="bword://Murgh Vindaloo">Murgh Vindaloo</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Unspecified Bopca Planet</li><li><b>Race:</b> Bopca Protector</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 9</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Tally on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Tally</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Tami-Lynn</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Tami-Lynn</b> is <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>'s <a href="bword://Father">Father</a>'s second wife and <a href="bword://Asher">Asher</a>'s mom. She has a tattoo of a pitbull on her neck and smokes cigerettes.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Tami-Lynn on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Tami-Lynn</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Taranis</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The god of thunder. Older brother of <a href="bword://Emberus">Emberus</a> and his twin brother <a href="bword://Hellik">Hellik</a>. Half sister of <a href="bword://Eris">Eris</a> Hellik seeks to kill Emberus and Taranis. The wife of Taranis is the goddess <a href="bword://Apito">Apito</a>. Together, Apito and Taranis held the first Butchers Masquerade in the Halls of Ascendency. They are also the parents of many children including the war god <a href="bword://Grull">Grull</a> and the lust god <a href="bword://Yarilo">Yarilo</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Taranis on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Taranis</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Team Katia</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>Team Katia is a group of crawlers centred around <a href="bword://Katia Grim">Katia Grim</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Team Katia on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Team_Katia</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Team Li Na</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>A team of Crawlers.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Team Li Na on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Team_Li_Na</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Team Retribution</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Team Retribution</b> is the NPC faction recognized as the defending team during the ninth-floor Faction Wars (game), headquartered in the funnel city of Larracos.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Team Retribution on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Team_Retribution</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Teleport Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><i><b>Teleport</b></i> is "one of the most powerful, most important spells to have in this dungeon." <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> describes a level 15 <a href="bword://Puddle Jumper Spell">Puddle Jumper Spell</a> as "almost as good as <b>Teleport Spell</b>."</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Teleport Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Teleport_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Teleport to Stairwell Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Teleport to Stairwell Spell</b> is a spell that At level 15, the spell <i>Teleport to Stairwell</i> allows a user to pick a stairwell from a list and teleport there. The list of stairwells show all stairwells on the entire floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Teleport to Stairwell Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Teleport_to_Stairwell_Spell</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Teleport Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><i><b>Teleport</b></i> is "one of the most powerful, most important spells to have in this dungeon." <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> describes a level 15 <a href="bword://Puddle Jumper Spell">Puddle Jumper Spell</a> as "almost as good as <b>Teleport Spell</b>."</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Teleport Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Teleport_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Teleport to Stairwell Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Teleport to Stairwell Spell</b> is a spell that At level 15, the spell <i>Teleport to Stairwell</i> allows a user to pick a stairwell from a list and teleport there. The list of stairwells show all stairwells on the entire floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Teleport to Stairwell Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Teleport_to_Stairwell_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Temple Defiler Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Temple Defiler Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> fell through the roof and broke the shrine in temple of <a href="bword://Diwata">Diwata</a> which <a href="bword://Lucia Mar">Lucia Mar</a> had previously desecrated. As a reward he recieved an <a href="bword://Enemy of the Church Tattoo">Enemy of the Church Tattoo</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Temple Defiler Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Temple_Defiler_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Terror the Clown</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>Once clowns-on-stilts performing at <a href="bword://Grimaldi">Grimaldi</a>'s Traveling Circus on the third floor, <a href="bword://Scolopendra">Scolopendra</a>'s curse transformed the <b>stilt clowns</b> into long-limbed monsters likened to "Slender Man dressed as a clown."</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Terror the Clown on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Terror_the_Clown</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>That was Disgusting Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>That-Was-Disgusting Box!</b> is a type of loot box awarded by the <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a> for achievements that are (presumably) very disgusting. <b>Platinum Tier</b></li><li><b>Source:</b> Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: That was Disgusting Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/That_was_Disgusting_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>That Wasn't Too Smart, Was It? Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>That Wasn't Too Smart, Was It? Box</b> is a Loot Box distributed for attacking a Province Boss. <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> receives a Platinum version this box for attacking a boss on the Fourth Floor and opens it in a safe room on the Fifth Floor. The contents of the box are not specified.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: That Wasn't Too Smart, Was It? Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/That_Wasn%27t_Too_Smart%2C_Was_It%3F_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>That's not how you use arrows, dumbass Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>That's not how you use arrows, dumbass</b> is an <a href="bword://Achievement">Achievement</a> awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> after stabbing <a href="bword://Vrah">Vrah</a> with the <a href="bword://Arrow of Enthusiastic Double Gonorrhea">Arrow of Enthusiastic Double Gonorrhea</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: That's not how you use arrows, dumbass Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/That%27s_not_how_you_use_arrows%2C_dumbass_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>That's the Spirit Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>That's the Spirit Box</b> is a Loot Box.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Killing family member</li></ul><p class="source">Source: That's the Spirit Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/That%27s_the_Spirit_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>The Bloc</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Bloc</b> is a formal truce and military alliance formed at the start of the Ninth Floor Faction Wars, uniting eight crawler and NPC teams against <a href="bword://Team Retribution">Team Retribution</a> and the <a href="bword://Princess Posse">Princess Posse</a>. It fractures steadily over the course of the war through both desertion and elimination.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: The Bloc on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/The_Bloc</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Theia</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Theia</b> is a light based deity that is a god of something. She is <a href="bword://Samantha">Samantha</a>'s mother, whom she has a complicated relationship with. Shows up to kill <a href="bword://Slit">Slit</a>.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Rectrix (sponsor)</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> God</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Theia on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Theia</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>They like me! They really like me! Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>They like me! They really like me! Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> on the Fourth Floor for gaining 500 trillion followers.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: They like me! They really like me! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/They_like_me%21_They_really_like_me%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>This Little Piggy Made a Boom Boom! Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>This Little Piggy Made a Boom Boom!</b> is an exclusive achievement that the <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a> awards to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> on the Sixth Floor. The name might be related to the First Floor <a href="bword://This Little Piggy Went to Market! Achievement">This Little Piggy Went to Market! Achievement</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: This Little Piggy Made a Boom Boom! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/This_Little_Piggy_Made_a_Boom_Boom%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>This Little Piggy Went to Market! Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>This Little Piggy Went to Market!</b> is the logical follow-up to the <a href="bword://Podophilia! Achievement">Podophilia! Achievement</a> and Smush Skill. It is most likely a unique achievement only awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>. It's also the first time that the <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a> refers to itself as "Daddy."</li></ul><p class="source">Source: This Little Piggy Went to Market! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/This_Little_Piggy_Went_to_Market%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Three Cheers for Slaughter Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Three Cheers for Slaughter Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for killing three neighborhood bosses with his <a href="bword://Protective Shell Spell">Protective Shell Spell</a> on the <a href="bword://Nightmare Express">Nightmare Express</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Three Cheers for Slaughter Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Three_Cheers_for_Slaughter_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Tiara of a Thousand Lights</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Tiara of a Thousand Lights</b> is a unique item created for <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> by her sponsor <a href="bword://Long Haul Biological Waste Management Solutions">Long Haul Biological Waste Management Solutions</a> and given to her in a <a href="bword://Celestial">Celestial</a> <a href="bword://Benefactor Box">Benefactor Box</a>. It is an upgradable tiara, with 99 slots to upgrade.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Celestial Benefactor Box from Long Haul Biological Waste Management Solutions to Donut</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Tiara of a Thousand Lights on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Tiara_of_a_Thousand_Lights</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Tigran</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Tigran</b> is an orange, furry humanoid race. race a crawler can choose upon entry to the Third Floor. Tigrans are bipedal humanoid / big cat hybrid, covered in lots of fur. The fur color is a very vibrant orange. Tigrans have a long shaggy tail.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Tigran on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Tigran</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Tin</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Tin</b> is a former Crawler and author of the <i><a href="bword://Dungeon Anarchist&#x27;s Cookbook">Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook</a> (21st Edition)</i>. &lt;Note added by Crawler Tin, 21st Edition&gt;</li><li><b>Race:</b> Unknown</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 32</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Tin on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Tin</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Tipid</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Tipid</b> is a veteran former crawler who authored the fourth edition of the <a href="bword://Dungeon Anarchist&#x27;s Cookbook">Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook</a>. He returns to the Dungeon during the Ninth Floor's Faction Wars as a Level 60 mercenary, serving as a Colonel and key tactician for the <a href="bword://Princess Posse">Princess Posse</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Crest System</li><li><b>Race:</b> Crest</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Epilogue</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Tipid on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Tipid</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Titan Conglomerate</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Titan Conglomerate</b> is the <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> production company primarily responsible for <i>Dungeon Crawler After Hours with <a href="bword://Odette">Odette</a></i> and <i>Planet Beautiful</i>, as well as other popular programs.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Titan Entertainment</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Titan Conglomerate on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Titan_Conglomerate</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Tito</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Tito</b> is a croupier for the Wheel of Fortune game at the Casino in the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>. One of the spots on the game has an option for “Get stabbed in the stomach by the croupier.” Tito is the croupier.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 9</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Tito on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Tito</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Tizquick</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Tizquick</b> is a <a href="bword://Dwarf">Dwarf</a> train conductor of the <i>Mango Line</i> on the Fourth Floor Iron Tangle. He was given false memories of a daughter that never existed.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> NPC</li><li><b>Race:</b> Dwarf</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 21</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Tizquick on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Tizquick</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Toad Cudgel</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Toad Cudgel</b> is a wooden stick about 3/4 the length of a baseball bat. The toad cudgel is the first unenchanted weapon <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives after entering the Dungeon; it comes in a Bronze <a href="bword://Weapon Box">Weapon Box</a> awarded for the <a href="bword://Unarmed Combat Achievement">Unarmed Combat Achievement</a>. Carl attempts to use it in combat exactly one time before putting it back in his inventory.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Bronze Weapon Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Toad Cudgel on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Toad_Cudgel</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Tom</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Tom</b> is a boss on the Eighth Floor.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Turkey</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 42</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Tom on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Tom</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Toraline</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>Toraline Root Vegetable</b> is essentially a sweet potato with alchemical uses. Toraline looks a like a sweet potato and only grows in volcanic soil. The <a href="bword://Inventory">Inventory</a> flags it as as "Very Rare," but its sell value is low. It can be used to create special ink for scrolls or for various lava-themed potions, including a Phase Lava Rock <a href="bword://Potion">Potion</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Benefactor Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Toraline on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Toraline</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Torch</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Torches</b> are single-use utility items frequently and abundantly received in <a href="bword://Loot Boxes">Loot Boxes</a> on the First Floor. They look like short, tapered sticks, approximately the diameter of a cork.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Loot Boxes</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Torch on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Torch_%28Item%29</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Torch Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><i>This article is about the spell. For the item, see <a href="bword://Torch">Torch</a> (Item).</i> <b>Torch</b> is a utility spell that creates an orb of flaming light that follows the crawler around. It works underwater.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Torch Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Torch_Spell</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Torch Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><i>This article is about the spell. For the item, see <a href="bword://Torch">Torch</a> (Item).</i> <b>Torch</b> is a utility spell that creates an orb of flaming light that follows the crawler around. It works underwater.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Torch Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Torch_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Torn Book Page</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Torn Book Page</b> is an item on the Fifth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Torn Book Page on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Torn_Book_Page</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Total, Utter Failure Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Total, Utter Failure Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for failing the quest Free <a href="bword://Wynne">Wynne</a> from His Bondage Quest.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Total, Utter Failure Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Total%2C_Utter_Failure_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Touched by a Demon Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Touched by a Demon Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for being touched by the demon lord <a href="bword://Amayon">Amayon</a> during the Eighth Floor. Carl opens this achievement in a safe room on the Ninth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Touched by a Demon Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Touched_by_a_Demon_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Toyotomi</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li>Toyotomi: race/species: Sai; occupation: Guard at <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a> (formerly)Mercenary During Faction Wars; first scene: Book 7, Chapter 28.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Sai</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 7, Chapter 28</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Toyotomi on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Toyotomi</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Tracked All-Terrain Suicide Machine. The Royal Chariot</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Tracked All-Terrain Suicide Machine. The Royal Chariot</b> is a vehicle constructed by <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> on the Fifth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Tracked All-Terrain Suicide Machine. The Royal Chariot on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Tracked_All-Terrain_Suicide_Machine._The_Royal_Chariot</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Trailblazing Crazy Cat Lady Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b><i>Trailblazing</i> Crazy Cat Lady</b> is a unique achievement awarded to the <i>first</i> crawler to enter the Dungeon with a cat.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Trailblazing Crazy Cat Lady Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Trailblazing_Crazy_Cat_Lady_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Train Conductor's Souvenir Hat</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>All crawlers receive the Train Conductor's Souvenir Hat upon entry to the Fourth Floor from the <a href="bword://I&#x27;m on a train Achievement">I'm on a train Achievement</a>. A simple, non-magical, blue and white hat with the words “I rode the Iron Tangle” embroidered on it.”</li><li><b>Source:</b> I'm on a train Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Train Conductor's Souvenir Hat on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Train_Conductor%27s_Souvenir_Hat</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Training Room</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Training Room</b> is a Personal Space upgrade that allows crawlers to train specific skills and spells. At level 1, it allows for one hour a day on a specific non-magical skill. It won't train anything explosives based until level 2 which has a Bomber's Studio.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Dungeon Market</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Training Room on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Training_Room</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Tran</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Tran</b> is a human Crawler from Earth and a Swashbuckler who fought with Gwen's team in the land quadrant of the Fifth Floor. Tran is quiet, dry, and willing to volunteer for dangerous work, joking that he should put on a red shirt before the dive to the Akula and then asking himself aloud why he had volunteered. He defers to his own team's leadership, checking with Gwen before acting on instructions from a crawler he had only just met.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth (Da Nang, Vietnam)</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 20</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Tran on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Tran</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Trapmaster Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Trapmaster Box</b> is a Loot Box distributed for <b>expert use of traps in battle</b>. <a href="bword://Insurgent Achievement">Insurgent Achievement</a> <b>Not yet fully documented</b>, but <b><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> received multiple Phase Through Wall scrolls</b>, possibly related​</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Trapmaster Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Trapmaster_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Travis Priest</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Travis Priest</b> is a strong and addictive painkiller.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Travis Priest on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Travis_Priest</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Treasure Map</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Treasure Map</b> is a persistent item dropped by a slain Country Boss, meaning that any crawler can loot it from the boss's corpse. It shows the location and quality of all magical equipment in the area.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Country Boss</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Treasure Map on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Treasure_Map</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Tripper</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Tripper</b> is a spell that triggers all passage-, motion-, heat-, and weight-triggered traps in a Crawler's radius. At level 15, the radius is massive.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Tripper on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Tripper</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Troglodyte</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Troglodytes</b> are humanoid, unintelligent mobs. On the First Floor, they occupy the <a href="bword://Juicer">Juicer</a>'s neighborhood. Troglodytes are muscular, humanoid mobs dressed in loincloths. Their head and torsos resemble Komodo dragons, but their scaly legs are long and bent, almost kangaroo-like. Their attacks may inflict a devastatingly painful Poison Debuff.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Troglodyte on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Troglodyte</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Troglodyte Pygmy</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Troglodytes</b> are humanoid, unintelligent mobs. On the First Floor, they occupy the <a href="bword://Juicer">Juicer</a>'s neighborhood. Troglodytes are muscular, humanoid mobs dressed in loincloths. Their head and torsos resemble Komodo dragons, but their scaly legs are long and bent, almost kangaroo-like. Their attacks may inflict a devastatingly painful Poison Debuff.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Troglodyte Pygmy on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Troglodyte_Pygmy</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Troglodyte</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Troglodytes</b> are humanoid, unintelligent mobs. On the First Floor, they occupy the <a href="bword://Juicer">Juicer</a>'s neighborhood. Troglodytes are muscular, humanoid mobs dressed in loincloths. Their head and torsos resemble Komodo dragons, but their scaly legs are long and bent, almost kangaroo-like. Their attacks may inflict a devastatingly painful Poison Debuff.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Troglodyte on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Troglodyte</p></div></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Troglodyte</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Troglodytes</b> are humanoid, unintelligent mobs. On the First Floor, they occupy the <a href="bword://Juicer">Juicer</a>'s neighborhood. Troglodytes are muscular, humanoid mobs dressed in loincloths. Their head and torsos resemble Komodo dragons, but their scaly legs are long and bent, almost kangaroo-like. Their attacks may inflict a devastatingly painful Poison Debuff.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Troglodyte on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Troglodyte</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Troglodyte Pygmy</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Troglodytes</b> are humanoid, unintelligent mobs. On the First Floor, they occupy the <a href="bword://Juicer">Juicer</a>'s neighborhood. Troglodytes are muscular, humanoid mobs dressed in loincloths. Their head and torsos resemble Komodo dragons, but their scaly legs are long and bent, almost kangaroo-like. Their attacks may inflict a devastatingly painful Poison Debuff.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Troglodyte Pygmy on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Troglodyte_Pygmy</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Troll Smoke Mantel</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Troll Smoke Mantel</b> is a smoke bomb, costs 30,000 gold for a set of twelve.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Troll Smoke Mantel on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Troll_Smoke_Mantel</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Tsarina Signet</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Tsarina Signet</b> is a level 60 Elite NPC and the star of the <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> program <i>Vengeance of the Daughter</i>. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> first encounter her on the Third Floor near <a href="bword://Grimaldi">Grimaldi</a>'s Traveling Circus.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Signet the Bastard</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Hunting Grounds, Liana Sector</li><li><b>Race:</b> Half-Naiad, half-High Elf</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2, Chapter 6</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Tsarina Signet on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Tsarina_Signet</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Tserendolgor</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Tserendolgor</b> ("Ren") is a crawler from Earth. Despite <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s constant harassment due to her dog-themed race, Ren becomes a close ally of <a href="bword://Meadow Lark">Meadow Lark</a> and the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a> after fighting beside them on the Fourth Floor.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Ren</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Mongolia</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Dog Soldier</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 31</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Tserendolgor on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Tserendolgor</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Tserendolgor Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Tserendolgor Box</b> is a Loot Box distributed for the <a href="bword://Chickenshit Exploit Achievement">Chickenshit Exploit Achievement</a>. Both <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> receive a Platinum version of this box.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Chickenshit Exploit Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Tserendolgor Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Tserendolgor_Box</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Tserendolgor Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Tserendolgor Box</b> is a Loot Box distributed for the <a href="bword://Chickenshit Exploit Achievement">Chickenshit Exploit Achievement</a>. Both <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> receive a Platinum version of this box.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Chickenshit Exploit Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Tserendolgor Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Tserendolgor_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Tucker</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Tucker</b> is one of the guests on Danger Zone with <a href="bword://Ripper Wonton">Ripper Wonton</a>. A stuffy looking middle-aged human with a stupid grin.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 2 Chapter 19</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Tucker on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Tucker</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Tuesday Two For One</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Tuesday Two For One</b> is a heavily pierced goblin female stripper in the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Goblin</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Tuesday Two For One on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Tuesday_Two_For_One</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Tummy Acher</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>Tummy Acher</b> is a type of pet-class mobs. <a href="bword://Garret">Garret</a> is a Tummy Acher owned by <a href="bword://Tserendolgor">Tserendolgor</a>. Tummy Achers are known for their abilities to be excellent melee tanks.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Tummy Acher on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Tummy_Acher</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Garret</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Garret</b> is a <a href="bword://Tummy Acher">Tummy Acher</a> pet that originally belonged to the crawler <a href="bword://Tserendolgor">Tserendolgor</a> (nicknamed "Ren" by her fellow crawlers, since nobody could pronounce her name), who received him as a gift for attending Crawl Con.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Rend, Garret, Bam-Bam, Cousin Oliver, Tummy Acher, Belly Acher</li><li><b>Origin:</b> The World Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> Tummy Acher / Belly Acher</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Garret on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Garret</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Turkey</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Turkey</b> are a race of mob on the Eighth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Turkey on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Turkey</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Turn Undead Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Turn Undead Spell</b> is a bard spell that turns undead. The "Turn Undead" spell is part of the NecroBard Class at level 3.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Turn Undead Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Turn_Undead_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Tuskling</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>In the <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a>, <b>Tusklings</b> are pig-like orcs and the ruling class of the <a href="bword://Orcish Supremacy">Orcish Supremacy</a>. They appear in the Dungeon as part of the <a href="bword://Ball of Swine">Ball of Swine</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Tuskling on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Tuskling</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Twinkle Toes</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>A cheap spell that makes a minion run really fast for as many seconds as the caster's intelligence level. Obtained by <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> in a platinum quest box on Floor 5.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Twinkle Toes on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Twinkle_Toes</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Twister</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The original Twister, is the roofless Chevy Astrovan driven by <a href="bword://Louis">Louis</a>, which became famous when he accidentally drove it into one of the first dungeon stairwells during the collapse.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Earth</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Twister on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Twister</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Two Chicks at the Same Time Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Two Chicks at the Same Time</b> is an achievement awarded to crawlers who use one mob's body to beat another's, and kills both mobs in the process.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Two Chicks at the Same Time Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Two_Chicks_at_the_Same_Time_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Tyler Storm</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>One of the crawlers in the Subterranean Quadrant of Bubble #543.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 6, Book 4</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Tyler Storm on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Tyler_Storm</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Tyrant Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Tyrant Box</b> is a Loot Box distributed for <b>killing a mayor</b> in the dungeon.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Killing a mayor of a settlement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Tyrant Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Tyrant_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ugly Ass Backpack With a Completely Useless Design that Only an Idiot Would Wear</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> crafts the <b>Ugly Ass Backpack With a Completely Useless Design that Only an Idiot Would Wear</b> for <a href="bword://Katia Grim">Katia Grim</a> at his <a href="bword://Armorer&#x27;s Workshop">Armorer's Workshop</a> during the Fourth Floor. The idea is to take advantage of her <a href="bword://Doppelgänger">Doppelgänger</a> race's ability to assimilate and shape equipped gear by making an equippable item that can store variable amounts of mass.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Carl Armorer's Workshop</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ugly Ass Backpack With a Completely Useless Design that Only an Idiot Would Wear on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ugly_Ass_Backpack_With_a_Completely_Useless_Design_that_Only_an_Idiot_Would_Wear</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Uh oh. It talks. Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Uh oh. It talks. Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for discovering a Sapient weapon, Spunky Jeffery the Enchanted Nickel Sock of the Elderly Miser and giving it to <a href="bword://Dong Quixote">Dong Quixote</a> on the Eighth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Uh oh. It talks. Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Uh_oh._It_talks._Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ultimate Extreme Power Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Ultimate Extreme Power Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for killing <a href="bword://Miss Quill">Miss Quill</a> and gained control of a Medium <a href="bword://Skyfowl">Skyfowl</a> Settlement.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ultimate Extreme Power Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ultimate_Extreme_Power_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ultra-Stabilized Size-Adjustable Race-Adjustable Alleviating Sleep Apparatus</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Ultra-Stabilized, Size-Adjustable, Race-Adjustable Alleviating Sleep Apparatus</b> is a Tier-1 Personal Space Bed Upgrade available on the Fourth Floor.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Dungeon Market</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ultra-Stabilized Size-Adjustable Race-Adjustable Alleviating Sleep Apparatus on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ultra-Stabilized_Size-Adjustable_Race-Adjustable_Alleviating_Sleep_Apparatus</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Unarmed Combat Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Unarmed Combat</b> is an achievement awarded to crawlers who enter the First Floor without a weapon. This is the sixth achievement <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives after entering the Dungeon wearing only boxers and a leather jacket.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Unarmed Combat Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Unarmed_Combat_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Unbirthing Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Unbirthing Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for teleporting into <a href="bword://Samantha">Samantha</a>'s neck hole on the Eighth Floor. The <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a> is a big fan of this achievement.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Unbirthing Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Unbirthing_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Uncle Morty’s Insta Lawn-Kill and Undead Repellant, Extra-Strength Edition</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Uncle Morty’s Insta Lawn-Kill and Undead Repellant, Extra-Strength Edition</b> is a potion made by <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> on the Sixth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Uncle Morty’s Insta Lawn-Kill and Undead Repellant, Extra-Strength Edition on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Uncle_Morty%E2%80%99s_Insta_Lawn-Kill_and_Undead_Repellant%2C_Extra-Strength_Edition</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Uncooked Llama steaks</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Uncooked Llama steaks</b> is a food item that are received as a loot drop after killing Bad Llamas. The system AI automatically adds these to the Food Items tab when <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> adds them to his inventory.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Uncooked Llama steaks on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Uncooked_Llama_steaks</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Unk Tehi</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Unk Tehi</b> is a deity of unrecorded domain. Enemies calling themselves Unk Tehi Temple Guards appear as level 85 <a href="bword://T&#x27;Ghee Card">T'Ghee Card</a> opponents: large lizard-headed humanoids wearing turkey-feather headdresses and carrying bows, arrows, or spears, announced with black-and-yellow confetti and a "these lizards" tagline.</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Bedlam Bride</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Unk Tehi on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Unk_Tehi</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Unvaccinated Clurichaun Rev-Up Consultant</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b><a href="bword://Clurichaun">Clurichaun</a></b> are a fairy-class mob on the Second Floor. Small and troll-like with humanoid bodies and oversized heads, Clurichaun are marked by curly black hair, hooked noses, small feet, and very few teeth. They make a puglike gurgling noise when attack.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Unvaccinated Clurichaun Rev-Up Consultant on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Unvaccinated_Clurichaun_Rev-Up_Consultant</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Clurichaun</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Clurichaun</b> are a fairy-class mob on the Second Floor. Small and troll-like with humanoid bodies and oversized heads, Clurichaun are marked by curly black hair, hooked noses, small feet, and very few teeth. They make a puglike gurgling noise when attack.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Clurichaun on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Clurichaun</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Unwashed</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li>Unwashed: race/species: Unknown; first scene: Chapter 43, The Inevitable Ruin.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> The Stalker, The Last Light, The Thirst, The Fell, The Inexorable, The Beautiful Place</li><li><b>Race:</b> Unknown</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 43, The Inevitable Ruin</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Unwashed on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Unwashed</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Upgrade Coupon</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>Coupons for upgrading Crafting tables. Came in the <a href="bword://It&#x27;s Not My Fault You Fish-Headed Assholes Don&#x27;t Properly Program Your Quests Box">It's Not My Fault You Fish-Headed Assholes Don't Properly Program Your Quests Box</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Upgrade Coupon on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Upgrade_Coupon</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Upgrade Patch</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><i>Warning: Upgrade patches are fleeting items. You may remove them, but they will be destroyed in the process.</i></li></ul><p class="source">Source: Upgrade Patch on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Upgrade_Patch</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Upgraded Shower</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>Automatic shower in the Royal Palace that adds +10% to all base stats and lowers "Detectability" for 30 hours. It is one of the party's daily buffs.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Dungeon Market</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Upgraded Shower on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Upgraded_Shower</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Uprooted Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Uprooted Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> used his <a href="bword://Protective Shell Spell">Protective Shell Spell</a> to launch <a href="bword://Claude Sludgington the Fourth">Claude Sludgington the Fourth</a>, a Level 65 Borough Boss Eryops Gigantis.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Uprooted Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Uprooted_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Uptown Hal</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Uptown Hal</b> is a slate, which is an orange alien shaped like a piece of chewing gum. He was never a crawler, but was a game guide and occasional manager for 200 seasons before the crawl starting using ex-crawlers. He runs a talk show called <i>Uptown Hal Talks Tactics</i>. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> meets him on the panel Crawling Through the Ages at CrawlCon!</li><li><b>Race:</b> slate</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Uptown Hal on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Uptown_Hal</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Urgyle</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Urgyles</b> are a small, winged, demon-like race. They populated at least one of the seeded planets featured on <i>Dungeon Crawler World</i>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Urgyle on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Urgyle</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ursensus</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><i>Ursensus'</i> is a race that is a combination of a <a href="bword://Mongoliensis">Mongoliensis</a> and a <a href="bword://Ursine">Ursine</a>, mixed up with the results of <a href="bword://Scolopendra">Scolopendra</a>'s Nine Tier Attack. <a href="bword://Mongo">Mongo</a> and <a href="bword://Kiwi">Kiwi</a> have two girls.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ursensus on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ursensus</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ursine</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Ursine</b> are a race of bear-like <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a> on the Sixth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ursine on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ursine</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Used Pet Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Used Pet Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for adopting a pet that belonged to someone else. He received this on the Eighth Floor when he received <a href="bword://Garret">Garret</a> from <a href="bword://Tserendolgor">Tserendolgor</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Used Pet Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Used_Pet_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Utter Annihilation Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Utter Annihilation</b> is a destructive spell channeled through a wand, whose only appearance in the text is as an incidental durability test rather than a combat encounter.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Utter Annihilation Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Utter_Annihilation_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Uzzi</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Uzzi</b> was Mordecia's brother and former team mates along with <a href="bword://Chaco">Chaco</a> and <a href="bword://Hold Steady">Hold Steady</a>. <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> mentions his brother choose the Storm Commander Class during their crawl.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Skyfowl</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Uzzi on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Uzzi</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Vadim</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>Also known as Doctor Vadim. Was a cosmetic surgeon with lots of billboards and TV commercials. He was infamous for having impregnated many of his clients, and is rumored to have 50 children.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Ukraine</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human | Kuhli</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Vadim on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Vadim</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Valtay Corporation</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Valtay Corporation</b> is a corporate system government within the <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a>, at once a business and a nation. Its people are a parasitic species that pilots the bodies of other races, and the corporation holds the debt of the <a href="bword://Borant System">Borant System</a>.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> The Valtay ; The Brain Worms</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Valtay Corporation on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Valtay_Corporation</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Vampire</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4 and 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Vampire</b> are a race that are required to drink large amounts of blood to survive. If a crawler is infected by vampirism and makes it to a staircase the infection becomes permanent and they gain a title.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Vampire on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Vampire</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Varg Vikernes Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Varg Vikernes Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for defiling <a href="bword://Club Vanquisher">Club Vanquisher</a> while he was attacking <a href="bword://Vinata">Vinata</a>. Presumably the following crawlers also got this achievement: <a href="bword://Katia Grim">Katia Grim</a>, <a href="bword://Prepotente">Prepotente</a>, <a href="bword://Li Jun">Li Jun</a>, <a href="bword://Zhang">Zhang</a> and <a href="bword://Li Na">Li Na</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Varg Vikernes Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Varg_Vikernes_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Veeka</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Veeka</b> is a hunter, she got called out by the <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a> because she locked herself in a saferoom crying and masturbating.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Veeka on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Veeka</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Velma the Flamethrower</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Velma</b> is <a href="bword://Tserendolgor">Tserendolgor</a>'s enchanted flamethrower, which was upgraded once at the end of the Fifth Floor. Part weapon and part breast plate, it looks like a <i>Ghostbusters</i>-esque backpack that also wraps around the wearer's torso like a shirt.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Velma the Flamethrower on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Velma_the_Flamethrower</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Venison Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Venison Box</b> is a Loot Box given to crawlers on the Leaderboard upon entry to the next floor. Due to the individual nature of each awarded box, this page is broken up by book.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Quarry Sees Another Spring Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Venison Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Venison_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Veriluxx RealPet Companions</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>Verlluxx real pet Companions are a company that manufactures pet robots. They're linked to a soother lending fund named Veritan Linkage that advocates for the enslavement for those that can't afford their taxes. Closely allied to Borant and the <a href="bword://Bloom">Bloom</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Veriluxx RealPet Companions on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Veriluxx_RealPet_Companions</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Veriluxx RealPet Dungeon Crawl Special Edition Exclusive</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Veriluxx RealPet Dungeon Crawl Special Edition Exclusive</b> is kids toy version of Princess <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>, except filled with creepiness.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Veriluxx RealPet Dungeon Crawl Special Edition Exclusive on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Veriluxx_RealPet_Dungeon_Crawl_Special_Edition_Exclusive</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Vernon</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Vernon</b> is a train conductor for the Yellow line train on the Iron Tangle. The <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a> takes time between stations 84 and 85 on the Yellow Line to explore the train. They enter the Employee Break Room and talk to Vernon. Due to <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s high Charisma he is very talkative and explains a lot of the mechanics of how trains circle back to the beginning of the line. Vernon also talks about his wife and how he's excited to go back to her.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Dwarf</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 5</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Vernon on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Vernon</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Very Sullen</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Very Sullen</b> is a cretin working as a bodyguard in the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>. His face is thinner than the other cretin guards' faces, and his eyes are tiny emotionless dots. He rarely (if ever) speaks. Although not verified in the text, he is most likely 7 foot tall, level 35, and wearing a tuxedo, like the other cretin guards.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Cretin</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 7</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Very Sullen on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Very_Sullen</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Viceroys</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>The Viceroys</b> are a <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> race and government. They regularly participate in the Faction Wars (game) as the Madness. Marked by featureless white masks, Viceroys specialize in horrific battlefield spells and necromancy. They regularly join the Ninth Floor Faction Wars as "The Madness," and although they have not won in a few years, they often claim victory. They won in Rosetta's year. Another contributor to the <a href="bword://Dungeon Anarchist&#x27;s Cookbook">Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook</a> wondered if the viceroys were biological, as no one had seen one die.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> The Madness</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Viceroys on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Viceroys</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Victory</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Victory</b> is an Orc attorney and judge from the <a href="bword://Skull Empire">Skull Empire</a> who serves as Adjutant to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>. She is the half-sister of <a href="bword://Queen Consort Ugloo">Queen Consort Ugloo</a>.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Baroness Victory, esquire ; Judge Victory ; Prime Minister Victory</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Skull Empire</li><li><b>Race:</b> Orc</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 36</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Victory on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Victory</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Village Guard Swordsman</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Village Guard Swordsman</b> are a guard type NPC / mob on the Third Floor. Village guards are decked head to toe in plate mail and carry a long, steel blade. They are bulky and tall, with indeterminant race characteristics.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Village Guard Swordsman on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Village_Guard_Swordsman</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Vinata</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Vinata</b> is a <a href="bword://Naga">Naga</a> princess and member of the ruling class of the Nagas in <a href="bword://Syndicate">Syndicate</a> space. She is also the warlord of her faction in the Ninth Floor Faction Wars.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Sepsis Whore</li><li><b>Race:</b> Naga</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 7, Chapter 42</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Vinata on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Vinata</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Vine Creepers</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Vine Creepers</b> are a plant-type mob found on the First Floor. They are thorny, creeping plants that emerge from giant pods and consume crawlers whole.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Vine Creepers on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Vine_Creepers</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Visitor</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Visitor</b> are a type of mob on the Eighth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Visitor on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Visitor</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Vocal Coach Training Room</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>A <b>Vocal Coach</b> is a special training room that can be installed inside a crawler's Personal Space. The room is roughly the size of a closet, and includes a microphone behind a glass panel (à la a recording studio). A holographic NPC named Lover Illiana teaches the crawler throat exercises that train up the crawler's Singing Skill, which helps Bard class crawlers cast spells and create substantial illusions.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Loot Boxes; Marketplace</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Vocal Coach Training Room on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Vocal_Coach_Training_Room</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Volteeg</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Volteeg</b> is a former crawler and author of the <i><a href="bword://Dungeon Anarchist&#x27;s Cookbook">Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook</a></i> (7th Edition). They contributed only a single entry to the cookbook, in which they lamented the loss of a loved one.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Sturnus | Gargoyle</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 5, Chapter 47</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Volteeg on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Volteeg</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Voting Admin Mass Number Three</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Voting Admin Mass Number Three</b> is the warlord in charge of the Operatic Collective for Faction Wars. They are a collective entity made up of three individuals, one of whom is Hortense.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Voting Admin Mass Number Three on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Voting_Admin_Mass_Number_Three</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Vrah</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Vrah</b> is a <a href="bword://Mantis">Mantis</a> Hunter and the top hunter of the <a href="bword://Dark Hive">Dark Hive</a> who hunts crawlers on the Sixth Floor. She pursues <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>, <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>, and the Royal Court after Carl kills her sister, <a href="bword://Xindy">Xindy</a>.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Mantis</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 5, Chapter 5</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Vrah on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Vrah</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Wait, Bosses Can Leave Their Rooms? Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Wait, Bosses Can Leave Their Rooms? Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> when they get ambushed by the <a href="bword://Krakaren Clone (Second Floor)">Krakaren Clone (Second Floor)</a> boss while standing outside the room.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Wait, Bosses Can Leave Their Rooms? Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Wait%2C_Bosses_Can_Leave_Their_Rooms%3F_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Waldrip Chris</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Waldrip Chris</b> is a Gremlin animal trainer available to crawlers on the Tenth Floor. He is assigned to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s garage. Waldrip Chris is one of two choices for mechanic or animal trainer for the Tenth Floor races. His specialty is Animal Trainer, whereas <a href="bword://Hedy">Hedy</a> is another gremlin that specializes as a Vehicle Mechanic.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Gremlin</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Waldrip Chris on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Waldrip_Chris</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Wall Monitor</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Wall Monitor</b> is a lizard class mob that is located in the Abyss Station #436 of the Iron Tangle. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> first sees the Wall Monitor Lizards when he explores the Abyss Station #436 shortly after stealing the <a href="bword://Nightmare Express">Nightmare Express</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Wall Monitor on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Wall_Monitor</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Wall of Fire Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Wall of Fire Spell</b> is a spell obtained by <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> on Floor 5. <b>Cost</b>: 15 mana</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Wall of Fire Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Wall_of_Fire_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Walter</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>Walter: race/species: Sai; occupation: Firefighter; first scene: Chapter 32, Book 6.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Sai</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 32, Book 6</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Walter on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Walter</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Wand of Nighty Night</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Wand of Nighty Night</b> is a wand that casts level 10 sleep on single opponent.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Wand of Nighty Night on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Wand_of_Nighty_Night</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Wand Recharge Scroll</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Wand Recharge Scroll</b> is a scroll that recharges a wand.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Wand Recharge Scroll on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Wand_Recharge_Scroll</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>War Crimes Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>War Crimes Spell</b> is a spell given to <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> in a Legendary <a href="bword://1914 Box">1914 Box</a>. The spell book itself is described as bleeding and crying before the user reads it.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: War Crimes Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/War_Crimes_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>War Criminal Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>War Criminal</b> is an achievement awarded when a crawler kills 21+ non-combatant <a href="bword://NPCs">NPCs</a> in a single attack. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> receive the You Monster! and <b>War Criminal Achievement</b> on the First Floor after launching a cart laden with explosives and <a href="bword://Hobgoblin Pus">Hobgoblin Pus</a> into the Goblin War Chieftan's boss room... which also happened to contain a lot of babies, pregnant goblins, and elderly goblins.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: War Criminal Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/War_Criminal_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>War Lord Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>War Lord</b> is a spell whose only appearance in the text is as the title of a spellbook offered as a prize at the Butcher's Masquerade Ball. Beyond its mana cost, nothing about what the spell actually does is ever revealed. It is not to be confused with Warlord, the rank held by a leader of the Faction Wars.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: War Lord Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/War_Lord_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>War Mage</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>War Mages</b> are a race / class of magic-users known for casting brutal dark magic such as <i><a href="bword://You&#x27;re Not Done Yet Spell">You're Not Done Yet Spell</a></i>. War mages are symbiotes who survived at least 12 resleeving <a href="bword://Flesher">Flesher</a> attacks.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: War Mage on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/War_Mage</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Warrior's Gold Helmet of Resistance</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Warrior's Gold Helmet of Resistance</b> is a piece of magical head armor obtained by <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> on the Eighth Floor of the World Dungeon. This helmet is a piece of magical armor designed to offer resistance to the wearer. However, because the item features the word "Warrior's" in its title, it carries a strict equipment condition: the item only works if the person wearing it is actively wielding a sword.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Boss Box (Eighth Floor)</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Warrior's Gold Helmet of Resistance on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Warrior%27s_Gold_Helmet_of_Resistance</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Wastrel Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Wastrel Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for feeding the <a href="bword://Enchanted Night Wyrm&#x27;s Ring of Divine Suffering">Enchanted Night Wyrm's Ring of Divine Suffering</a> to <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> at the end of the Ninth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Wastrel Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Wastrel_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Watch where you're waving that thing, big boy. Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Watch where you're waving that thing, big boy. Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> after he uses a Wand in combat against the <a href="bword://Reminiscence Hydra of Malicious Compliance">Reminiscence Hydra of Malicious Compliance</a> on the Eighth Floor</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Watch where you're waving that thing, big boy. Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Watch_where_you%27re_waving_that_thing%2C_big_boy._Achievement</p></div><div class="multi-lookup"><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ring of Water Breathing</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> gets a <b>Ring of Water Breathing</b> on the Fifth Floor. A glowing blue ring that twinkles with little sparkles.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Gold I'm Wet Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ring of Water Breathing on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ring_of_Water_Breathing</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Scroll of Water Breathing</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Scroll of Water Breathing</b> is a scroll that allows a crawler to breathe underwater for a limited amount of time.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Platinum That Wasn't Too Smart, Was It? Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Scroll of Water Breathing on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Scroll_of_Water_Breathing</p></div></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Water Lily Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Water Lily</b> is powerful <a href="bword://Naiad">Naiad</a> heirloom magic spell that renders the target Unconscious until the caster cancels the spell. If the caster dies, the target will never wake up. If someone attempts to move the target, the target's health rapidly decreases.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Water Lily Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Water_Lily_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>We Want Meat! We Want Meat! Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>"We Want Meat! We Want Meat!" <a href="bword://Achievement">Achievement</a></b> is awarded the first time a crawler enters the Penis Parade at the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> received the "We want meat! We want meat!" achievement on the Eighth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: We Want Meat! We Want Meat! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/We_Want_Meat%21_We_Want_Meat%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Weapon Box</b></p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Weapon Box</b> is a Loot Box common on the First Floor. Although a Ranged Weapons Box is given out on the Sixth Floor, the basic "Weapon Box" is never mentioned again after the first book; instead, unenchanted weapons are distributed to crawlers on deeper floors in low-tier Adventurer Boxes.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Achievements; PVP Coupon</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Weapon Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Weapon_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Weapon Oil: Weeping Wound</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Weapon Oil: Weeping Wound</b> is a type of potion that can be applied to edged weapons to cause wounds inflicted with the weapon to "bleed longer."</li><li><b>Source:</b> Silver Asshole's Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Weapon Oil: Weeping Wound on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Weapon_Oil%3A_Weeping_Wound</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Welcome to the Neighborhood! Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><i>Welcome to the neighborhood!</i> is an <a href="bword://Achievement">Achievement</a> awarded for purchasing a Personal Space. The doorway to the personal space opens as soon as the achievement fades away. If multiple party members purchase a personal space, the space is titled "Conjoined Personal Space of Team [Name]."</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Welcome to the Neighborhood! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Welcome_to_the_Neighborhood%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Well-Rested! Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Well-Rested</b> is an achievement for receiving the "Good Rest Buff" for the first time. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives this achievement on the Fourth Floor after sleeping on the <a href="bword://Ultra-Stabilized Size-Adjustable Race-Adjustable Alleviating Sleep Apparatus">Ultra-Stabilized Size-Adjustable Race-Adjustable Alleviating Sleep Apparatus</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Well-Rested! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Well-Rested%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Wendita</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li>'<i>Wendita</i> is a <a href="bword://Bopca">Bopca</a> in the safe room at Station #83 in the Iron Tangle. She is describes as a shaggy female, Bopca gnome.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Unspecified Bopca Planet</li><li><b>Race:</b> Bopca</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Wendita on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Wendita</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Wetware</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Wetware</b> refers to a biological lifeform's brain and the "data" it contains. On Earth, the term "wetware" was popularized by Bruce Sterling's 1985 Nebula Award-winning cyberpunk novel <i>Schismatrix.</i> Rudy Rucker, who won the PKD award for his (frankly kind of weird) 180-page novel <i>Wetware</i> (1988), neatly summarized the term as "the whole bio-cybernetic software of the mind." In 2007, Rucker wrote a blog post explaining:</li><li><b>Source:</b> Inherent</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Wetware on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Wetware</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>What Big Muscles You Have! Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>What big muscles you have!</b> is an achievement awarded for reaching a base Strength of 100. Regardless of which option a crawler chooses, they immediately look more muscular.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: What Big Muscles You Have! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/What_Big_Muscles_You_Have%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>What Goes Up Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>What goes up...</b> is an achievement for surviving the <a href="bword://Reverse Gravity Spell">Reverse Gravity Spell</a>. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> receive this achievement on the Second Floor after their fight with the <a href="bword://Rage Elemental">Rage Elemental</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: What Goes Up Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/What_Goes_Up_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Who Let the Gods Out This Time? Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Who Let the Gods Out This Time? Box</b> is a Loot Box given to crawlers for the <a href="bword://Charge of the Light Brigade Achievement">Charge of the Light Brigade Achievement</a>. <a href="bword://Li Jun">Li Jun</a>, <a href="bword://Zhang">Zhang</a>, <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>, <a href="bword://Prepotente">Prepotente</a>, and <a href="bword://Katia Grim">Katia Grim</a> all received a <a href="bword://Celestial">Celestial</a> version of this box.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Celestial Orgy of Chaos Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Who Let the Gods Out This Time? Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Who_Let_the_Gods_Out_This_Time%3F_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Who Let the Gods Out? Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Who Let the <a href="bword://Gods">Gods</a> Out?</b> is an <a href="bword://Achievement">Achievement</a> awarded for unleashing a Feral God. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives this achievement on the Fifth Floor after using the <a href="bword://Gate of the Feral Gods">Gate of the Feral Gods</a> for the first time.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Who Let the Gods Out? Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Who_Let_the_Gods_Out%3F_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Why Are You Hitting Yourself Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Why Are You Hitting Yourself Spell</b> is a spell that makes target attack themselves.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Why Are You Hitting Yourself Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Why_Are_You_Hitting_Yourself_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Why Aren't You Wearing Pants? Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Why aren't you wearing pants?</b> is an achievement awarded for entering the Dungeon without pants. This is the fifth achievement that <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives after entering the First Floor wearing only his boxers and a leather coat. The Gold <a href="bword://Apparel Box">Apparel Box</a> contains the <a href="bword://Enchanted Nightgaunt Cloak of Stoutness">Enchanted Nightgaunt Cloak of Stoutness</a> and the <a href="bword://Enchanted Trollskin Shirt of Pummeling">Enchanted Trollskin Shirt of Pummeling</a>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Why Aren't You Wearing Pants? Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Why_Aren%27t_You_Wearing_Pants%3F_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Widget</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Widget</b> is an Steam Engine Train Technician on the Iron Tangle who works in Trainyard E. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> describes his accent as "Creole guy poorly attempting a cockney accent." Widget is very accommodating and friendly, though that might be due to <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s high Charisma.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> Grease Gremlin</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Widget on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Widget</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Wild Goose Chase! Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>Wild Goose Chase! Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> after he drank a trick pitcher of lemonade <a href="bword://Bonnie">Bonnie</a> made thinking it would help him fight <a href="bword://Denise">Denise</a> the goose.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Wild Goose Chase! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Wild_Goose_Chase%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Wings of the Pixie Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Wings of the Pixie Spell</b> is an escape spell availible to Bards. <a href="bword://Chaco">Chaco</a> had access to the spell during his crawl. <a href="bword://Mordecai">Mordecai</a> tells <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> to ask Chaco at the Butcher's Masquerade if he has anything like his <b>Wings of the Pixie Spell</b>.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Wings of the Pixie Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Wings_of_the_Pixie_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Wisp Armor Spell</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><i><b>Wisp Armor</b></i> is a protective spell that blocks a percentage of magical attack damage and makes the caster temporarily immune to mind control effects. When cast, the crawler sees a countdown timer and sparkling lights twirling around them like comets.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Wisp Armor Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Wisp_Armor_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Wrap of Sekhmet’s Compassion</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 8.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Wrap of Sekhmet’s Compassion</b> is an item <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> receives as part of her Assassin of Sekhmet Class. She gives it to Rend.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Assassin of Sekhmet Class</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Wrap of Sekhmet’s Compassion on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Wrap_of_Sekhmet%E2%80%99s_Compassion</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Wrath Ghouls</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Wrath Ghouls</b> are a mob on the Fourth Floor. They are created by a mob having the infliction of the DTs and not surviving the second of three stages.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Wrath Ghouls on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Wrath_Ghouls</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Wynne</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Wynne</b> is a <a href="bword://Dirigible Gnome">Dirigible Gnome</a> being held hostage and used as collateral to prevent the Dirigible Gnomes from bombing Hump Town.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Dirigible Gnome</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 6</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Wynne on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Wynne</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Xindy</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>Zindy was a hunter that was killed by <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>, her mother, Circe, hosted a panel at CrawlCon. She was meant to take over from her sister and become the hives next top hunter.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Mantis</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Chapter 5, Book 5</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Xindy on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Xindy</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Xistera</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> gets a <b>Xistera</b> in a <a href="bword://Fan Box">Fan Box</a>. It's an equippable scoop that allows him to throw things farther, particularly round shaped things. It is used in the sport Cesta Punta, the skill Carl got from the <a href="bword://Earth Hobby Potion">Earth Hobby Potion</a>.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Fan Box for One Quadrillion! Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Xistera on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Xistera</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Yago</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Yago</b> is a <a href="bword://Monk Seal">Monk Seal</a> Picket Sentry, an aquatic, melee tank mob and a Totem <a href="bword://T&#x27;Ghee Card">T'Ghee Card</a> on the Eighth Floor. This card was originally held by the Team <a href="bword://Sister Ines">Sister Ines</a>/Team Quiteria and later held by <a href="bword://Ysalte">Ysalte</a> after Sister Ines's death.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Monk Seal Picket Sentry</li><li><b>Race:</b> Monk Seal</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Yago on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Yago</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Yarilo</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Yarilo</b> is the banished god of lust, and the son of <a href="bword://Taranis">Taranis</a>. Yarilo was once known for hosting orgies (which <a href="bword://Samantha">Samantha</a> attended even though he skimped on catering), but is now trapped in the Nothing.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Twelfth Floor</li><li><b>Race:</b> Deity</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 21</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Yarilo on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Yarilo</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Yellow-Bellied Chickenshit! Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Yellow-Bellied Chickenshit!</b> is an <a href="bword://Achievement">Achievement</a> distributed to crawlers who end a boss battle without dying or killing the boss. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives this achievement after entering an encounter with the Level 85 Elite City Boss Ringmaster Grimadli - <a href="bword://Pestiferous Vine">Pestiferous Vine</a> on the Third Floor, and then talked his way out of it.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Yellow-Bellied Chickenshit! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Yellow-Bellied_Chickenshit%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Yemaya</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Yemaya</b> is a deity that is a god of rivers, but also the queen of love and bringer of life. She is a retainer of the goddess <a href="bword://Eileithyia">Eileithyia</a>. She is part of the <a href="bword://Orisha">Orisha</a> pantheon along with <a href="bword://Ogun">Ogun</a>, <a href="bword://Legba">Legba</a>, <a href="bword://Oshun">Oshun</a>, <a href="bword://Asojano">Asojano</a>, <a href="bword://Shango">Shango</a>, and <a href="bword://Inle">Inle</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Dungeon</li><li><b>Race:</b> God</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Yemaya on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Yemaya</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Yenk</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Yenk</b> are a race with three genders, all three of which are required to reproduce. The women, children and unintelligent third gender live together. The males are forced out when they reach maturity, they often work as mercenaries or bounty hunters but can't work with others of their kind lest they fight. Some of the males are castrated.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Yenk on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Yenk</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Yog's Special Chain</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><i><b>Yog's Special Chain</b></i> is a Scroll that allows the caster to summon and use any length (up to 1,000' or 304.8m) of glowing magical chain for 30 hours. The chain is "light as a feather" but at least as strong as regular chain.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Gold Loot Box</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Yog's Special Chain on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Yog%27s_Special_Chain</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Yolanda Martinez</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Yolanda Martinez</b> was a crawler from Wenatchee, WA, and a member of the <a href="bword://Meadow Lark">Meadow Lark</a> party on the first and second floors. Her death had a profound impact on both <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Imani">Imani</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Earth: Wenatchee, WA</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 22</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Yolanda Martinez on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Yolanda_Martinez</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>York</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>York</b> is a Tenodera former crawler and the author of the tenth edition of the <i><a href="bword://Dungeon Anarchist&#x27;s Cookbook">Dungeon Anarchist's Cookbook</a></i>. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> first meets York not as a person but as a voice on the page. While resting during his crawl, Carl reads York's contributions to the cookbook — pages of rambling, philosophical essays he can barely parse, though one passage refuses to leave him. The entries reveal a being who came from a hive yet spent his life feeling utterly alone, and who took a strange comfort in the idea that the cookbook could become a hive of its own: a fellowship of crawlers who would never actually meet.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> A Tenodera hive</li><li><b>Race:</b> Tenodera</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 3, Chapter 15 (mentioned); Book 7, Epilogue (in person)</li></ul><p class="source">Source: York on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/York</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>You Call That a Trap? Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>You call that a trap?</b> is an achievement awarded the first time a crawler sets a trap that deals damage to a mob. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> both receive the "You call that a trap?" achievement after their final battle against the <a href="bword://Rage Elemental">Rage Elemental</a> on the Second Floor. Although Carl isn't sure how they earned the achievement and specifically notes that bombs are categorized separately from traps, he guesses that they received it by tripping the Elemental with the remnants of <a href="bword://Yog&#x27;s Special Chain">Yog's Special Chain</a> or spilling <a href="bword://Goblin Oil">Goblin Oil</a> on the Dungeon floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: You Call That a Trap? Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/You_Call_That_a_Trap%3F_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>You Can't Fight City Hall! Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>You Can't Fight City Hall!</b> is an <a href="bword://Achievement">Achievement</a> distributed to crawlers who discover a City Boss. This special achievement <i>cannot</i> be minimized in the Heads-Up Display (HUD).</li></ul><p class="source">Source: You Can't Fight City Hall! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/You_Can%27t_Fight_City_Hall%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>You Crossed a Line You Didn't Even Know Was There Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>You Crossed a Line You Didn't Even Know Was There</b> is an <a href="bword://Achievement">Achievement</a> granted the first time a Crawler uses an artifact of Divine Suffering. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives this achievement after using the Enchanted Night Wyrm’s Ring of Divine Suffering to kill <a href="bword://Chin&#x27;Dua">Chin'Dua</a> shortly after arriving on the Sixth Floor. The <a href="bword://Junkie&#x27;s Box">Junkie's Box</a> contains the Night Wyrm's Nasty Little Web of Suffering.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: You Crossed a Line You Didn't Even Know Was There Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/You_Crossed_a_Line_You_Didn%27t_Even_Know_Was_There_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>You Found Stairs! Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>You found stairs!</b> is an achievement awarded the first time a crawler finds an accessible stairwell. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives this achievement after defeating the <a href="bword://Ball of Swine">Ball of Swine</a> on the First Floor, and gaining access to and seeing the staircase to the Second Floor. He does <i>not</i> receive this achievement for simply locating a staircase inside the Dungeon.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: You Found Stairs! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/You_Found_Stairs%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>You have discovered a Celestial Thorn Room! Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>You have discovered a Celestial Thorn Room! Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> on the Eighth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: You have discovered a Celestial Thorn Room! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/You_have_discovered_a_Celestial_Thorn_Room%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>You in my house now boy Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>You in my house now boy Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for confronting <a href="bword://Khepri">Khepri</a> in his own temple during the Operation Snake Pit. Both <a href="bword://Katia Grim">Katia Grim</a> and <a href="bword://Prepotente">Prepotente</a> had received the same achievement.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: You in my house now boy Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/You_in_my_house_now_boy_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>You Know Everybody Can See You Right? Box</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>You Know Everybody Can See You Right? Box</b> is a Loot Box distributed for...reasons. Whatever the crawler was doing, where everybody could see them, they were doing it to such an extent that it was deemed worthy of a Legendary loot box.. The loot box is mentioned as part of the AI's description for Spunky Jeffery the Enchanted Nickel Sock of the Elderly Miser.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Achievement</li></ul><p class="source">Source: You Know Everybody Can See You Right? Box on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/You_Know_Everybody_Can_See_You_Right%3F_Box</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>You Monster! Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>You Monster!</b> is an achievement awarded when a crawler kills an infant. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a> receive the <b>You Monster!</b> and <a href="bword://War Criminal Achievement">War Criminal Achievement</a> on the First Floor after launching a cart laden with explosives and <a href="bword://Hobgoblin Pus">Hobgoblin Pus</a> into the Goblin War Chieftan's boss room... which also happened to contain a lot of babies, pregnant goblins, and elderly goblins.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: You Monster! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/You_Monster%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>You now tread in the realm of gods Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li>The <b>You now tread in the realm of gods Achievement</b> is an achievement awarded to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> for training his Mind Balance Skill over level 15 while being hit with a barrage of psionic attacks while storming the Madness stronghold during Faction Wars (game).</li></ul><p class="source">Source: You now tread in the realm of gods Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/You_now_tread_in_the_realm_of_gods_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>You're Not Done Yet Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><i><b>You're Not Done Yet</b></i> is a brutal necromancy spell that rips the flesh from the dead, creating a <a href="bword://Flesher">Flesher</a>. A flesher's goal is to find a new body to wrap itself around. This spell is associated with War Mages and often used on the Ninth Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: You're Not Done Yet Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/You%27re_Not_Done_Yet_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>You're the Reason Why Daddy Drinks! Achievement</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>You're the reason why daddy drinks!</b> is an achievement that the <a href="bword://System AI">System AI</a> awards to <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a>, and only Carl, on the Fifth Floor. After Carl, <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>, and <a href="bword://Katia Grim">Katia Grim</a> destroy the <i>Wasteland</i>, the System AI throws a hissy fit that includes the <a href="bword://Cannonball! Achievement">Cannonball! Achievement</a> and tagging the <a href="bword://Dirigible Gnome">Dirigible Gnome</a> corpses as, "<b>Killed by falling from a great height with an assist by the Crawler Bitch Boy Carl.</b>" Katia asks Carl what he did to piss off the System AI, and Carl, clueless, looks up to the air and says, "I don’t know what I did, but I promise it wasn’t on purpose."</li></ul><p class="source">Source: You're the Reason Why Daddy Drinks! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/You%27re_the_Reason_Why_Daddy_Drinks%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>You've Discovered and Read an Official Dungeon Sign Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>You've Discovered and Read an Official Dungeon Sign</b> is an achievement awarded to crawlers the first time they see a legitimate sign advertising a Tutorial Guild Hall, which will presumably happen on the First Floor. The reward upgrades the crawler's Heads-Up Display (HUD) and Minimap.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: You've Discovered and Read an Official Dungeon Sign Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/You%27ve_Discovered_and_Read_an_Official_Dungeon_Sign_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>You've Entered a Guildhall! Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> earns this achievement after finding and entering a Tutorial Guild Hall on the first floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: You've Entered a Guildhall! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/You%27ve_Entered_a_Guildhall%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>You've Inflicted Damage on a Mob Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>You've inflicted damage on a mob</b> is an achievement awarded the first time a crawler deals damage to a mob. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives this achievement after fighting the goblins for the first time on the First Floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: You've Inflicted Damage on a Mob Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/You%27ve_Inflicted_Damage_on_a_Mob_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>You've Killed a Mob a Higher Level than Yourself! Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>You've Killed A Mob Higher Level than Yourself!</b> is an <a href="bword://Achievement">Achievement</a> awarded the first time a crawler defeats a mob of a higher level. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> earns this achievement after his first goblin encounter on the first floor.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: You've Killed a Mob a Higher Level than Yourself! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/You%27ve_Killed_a_Mob_a_Higher_Level_than_Yourself%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>You've Killed a Mob! Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>You've Killed a Mob!</b> is an achievement awarded the first time a crawler kills a mob. This achievement is required to begin earning experience points in the Dungeon.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: You've Killed a Mob! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/You%27ve_Killed_a_Mob%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>You've Killed an Armed Mob with Your Bare Fucking Hands! Achievement</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>You've killed an armed mob with your bare fucking hands!</b> is an achievement for killing an armed mob without a weapon. <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> receives this achievement on the First Floor, at the same time he receives the <a href="bword://You&#x27;ve Killed a Mob! Achievement">You've Killed a Mob! Achievement</a>, after killing a goblin with his fists.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: You've Killed an Armed Mob with Your Bare Fucking Hands! Achievement on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/You%27ve_Killed_an_Armed_Mob_with_Your_Bare_Fucking_Hands%21_Achievement</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Ysalte</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 4.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Ysalte</b>, also called the <b>Vinegar Bitch</b>, is a deity who can be pulled into the Dungeon as a secondary summoning when a feral god is released. The <a href="bword://Borant Corporation">Borant Corporation</a> announced that Ysalte was one of the deities that could be produced as a secondary summoning by the <a href="bword://Gate of the Feral Gods">Gate of the Feral Gods</a>, and that her arrival would have been an extinction-level event for the fifth and sixth floors. Rather than allow it before another floor of sponsorship bidding was complete, Borant blocked some, but not all, of the secondary summonings.</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> The Vinegar Bitch; The Downward Spiral</li><li><b>Race:</b> Deity</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 4, Chapter 33</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Ysalte on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Ysalte</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Yvette</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Yvette</b> is the daughter of <a href="bword://Maggie My">Maggie My</a> and <a href="bword://Frank Q">Frank Q</a>. She entered the dungeon with her parents after running away the night of the collapse. Yvette is reluctant to kill things in the Dungeon.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Seattle</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1 Chapter 43</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Yvette on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Yvette</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Zabit</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li>Hunter, killed by his own traps when <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> cast <i><a href="bword://Tripper">Tripper</a></i>. He was the final Hunter on floor 6. He hunts for the survival of the <a href="bword://Atoll">Atoll</a>, using the money to pay for the upkeep of his habitat as their race has limited employment opportunities. Without the money from hunting crawlers his community would have to agree to an indentureship with another system.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Atoll</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Zabit on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Zabit</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Zebani</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Zebani</b> is a race very similar to human, but with a blue tinge to the skin. The only recorded Zebani encountered so far is the Earth Crawler <a href="bword://Emir Akbas">Emir Akbas</a> who <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> meets in the <a href="bword://Desperado Club">Desperado Club</a>. Carl comments that he "looked human at first" but had a "blue tinge to his skin".</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Zebani on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Zebani</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Zentix</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Zentix</b> is a reactive, tamper-proof polymer that feels like cheap plastic. As a smart polymer, it can be programmed with security settings that cause it to fail under certain conditions (such as when tampered with or used by unauthorized users).</li><li><b>Source:</b> Veriluxx</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Zentix on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Zentix</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Zerzura Spell</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 5.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Zerzura</b> is a once-per-floor spell which transfers a Dungeon settlement to a deeper floor. It's extremely popular among watchers of <i>Dungeon Crawler World</i> due to the chaos it causes.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Zerzura Spell on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Zerzura_Spell</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Zev</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Zev</b> is a <a href="bword://Kua-Tin">Kua-Tin</a> and low-ranked employee in the <a href="bword://Borant Corporation">Borant Corporation</a> Communications Department. After <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> and <a href="bword://Donut">Donut</a>'s first appearance on <i>Dungeon Crawler After Hours with <a href="bword://Odette">Odette</a></i>, she was appointed as the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a>'s "Outreach Associate."</li><li><b>Aliases:</b> Mudskipper, Fish Sticks</li><li><b>Origin:</b> Borant System</li><li><b>Race:</b> Kua-Tin</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 36</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Zev on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Zev</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Zeynep</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 6.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Zeynep</b> is a crawler from the middle east. She and <a href="bword://Carl">Carl</a> trade fist bumps on the Eighth Floor. Zeynep is a middle aged middle eastern woman whose crawler ID is similar enough to those of her three other party members that Carl suspects they entered the Dungeon together. She may also be in a party with <a href="bword://Burcu">Burcu</a>.</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 6, Chapter 32</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Zeynep on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Zeynep</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Zhang</b></p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Zhang</b> is a Crawler from China on Dungeon Crawler World: Earth. He entered the Dungeon with his best friend <a href="bword://Li Jun">Li Jun</a> and Li Jun's sister <a href="bword://Li Na">Li Na</a>, and the three of them form the core of <a href="bword://Team Li Na">Team Li Na</a>, allies of the <a href="bword://Royal Court of Princess Donut">Royal Court of Princess Donut</a>.</li><li><b>Origin:</b> China, Earth</li><li><b>Race:</b> Human</li><li><b>First scene:</b> Book 1, Chapter 42</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Zhang on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Zhang</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Zhang's Cape of Odds</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 7.</p><ul class="definition"><li><a href="bword://Zhang">Zhang</a> receives the <b>Zhang's Cape of Odds</b> in a <a href="bword://Celestial">Celestial</a> Who Let the <a href="bword://Gods">Gods</a> Out This Time Box for the <a href="bword://Celestial Orgy of Chaos Achievement">Celestial Orgy of Chaos Achievement</a>. The cape is white with the standard black, red, and yellow archery target on the back. When it isn't activated, it gives 15% to all stats plus a level 10 Dodge Skill. Once an hour, it gives access to the Roll the Dice Skill.</li><li><b>Source:</b> Who Let the Gods Out This Time Box; Celestial Orgy of Chaos Achievement.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Zhang's Cape of Odds on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Zhang%27s_Cape_of_Odds</p></div><div class="entry"><p class="headword"><b>Zlurpies</b></p><p class="spoiler-note"><b>Spoiler note:</b> This article contains unmarked spoilers for Book 3.</p><ul class="definition"><li><b>Zlurpies</b> are a Fourth Floor mob that can be found on the Yellow Line of the Iron Tangle. Zlurpies are waist-high, semi-intelligent warrior armadillo things that roll into armored balls when they take damage, but they were small enough to be eaten whole by <a href="bword://Mongo">Mongo</a>, who would pick them up and crunch them like juice-filled hard candies.</li></ul><p class="source">Source: Zlurpies on Dungeon Crawler Carl Wiki<br />https://dungeon-crawler-carl.fandom.com/wiki/Zlurpies</p></div>